[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    So the inequality becomes:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    7 < 4x < \frac{28}{3}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 4. **Isolate \(x\) by dividing all parts of the inequality by 4:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \frac{7}{4} < x < \frac{28}{12}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 5. **Simplify the fractions:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \frac{7}{4} = 1.75
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \frac{28}{12} = \frac{7}{3} \approx 2.33
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    So the inequality becomes:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    1.75 < x < 2.33
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 6. **Since \(x\) must be an integer, we look for the integer values within this range. The integers between 1.75 and 2.33 are 2 and 3.**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
