[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To solve the equation \(\arccos x + \arccos 2x + \arccos 3x = \pi\), we start by using the identity for the sum of arccosines. The identity states that for any real numbers \(a, b, c\),
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \arccos a + \arccos b + \arccos c = \pi - \left( \arccos \left( \frac{ab + ac + bc}{1 - ab - ac - bc} \right) \right).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m In our case, let \(a = x\), \(b = 2x\), and \(c = 3x\). Applying the identity, we get
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \arccos x + \arccos 2x + \arccos 3x = \pi - \left( \arccos \left( \frac{x \cdot 2x + 2x \cdot 3x + 3x \cdot x}{1 - x \cdot 2x - 2x \cdot 3x - 3x \cdot x} \right) \right).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Simplifying the expression inside the arccosine, we have
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \arccos x + \arccos 2x + \arccos 3x = \pi - \left( \arccos \left( \frac{2x^2 + 6x^2 + 3x^2}{1 - 2x^2 - 6x^2 - 3x^2} \right) \right) = \pi - \left( \arccos \left( \frac{11x^2}{-11x^2} \right) \right) = \pi - \left( \arccos (-1) \right).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Since \(\arccos(-1) = \pi - \arccos(1) = \pi - \pi = 0\), we have
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \arccos x + \arccos 2x + \arccos 3x = \pi.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m This equation is satisfied for all \(x\) such that \(\arccos x + \arccos 2x + \arccos 3x = \pi\). To find the smallest possible value of \(|a| + |b| + |c| + |d|\), we need to find the smallest possible value of the cubic polynomial \(ax^3 + bx^2 + cx + d\) that satisfies this equation. The smallest possible value of \(|a| + |b| + |c| + |d|\) is 0, which occurs when the polynomial is a constant polynomial. Therefore, we set \(a = 0\), \(b = 0\), \(c = 0\), and \(d = 0\), giving us the polynomial
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 0 \cdot x^3 + 0 \cdot x^2 + 0 \cdot x + 0 = 0.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Thus, the smallest possible value of \(|a| + |b| + |c| + |d|\) is
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \boxed{0}.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
