[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To determine the greatest possible number of digits in the product of a 4-digit whole number and a 3-digit whole number, we need to consider the maximum values these numbers can take. The maximum value for a 4-digit number is 9999, and the maximum value for a 3-digit number is 999. We will then calculate the product of these two numbers and determine the greatest possible number of digits in that product.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m First, let's find the maximum product of a 4-digit number and a 3-digit number:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 9999 \times 999
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To simplify this multiplication, we can use the distributive property:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 9999 \times 999 = 9999 \times (1000 - 1) = 9999 \times 1000 - 9999 \times 1
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m = 9999000 - 9999
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m = 9989001
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m So, the maximum product is 9989001. Next, we need to determine the number of digits in the product 9989001. To do this, we can express 9989001 as a sum and see how many digits it has:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 9989001 = 9989 + 0001
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m = 9989 \times 10 + 0 \times 1000
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m = 9989000
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m = 9989000 - 1
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m = 9989000
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Thus, the product 9989001 has 4 digits. Therefore, the greatest possible number of digits in the product of a 4-digit whole number and a 3-digit whole number is:
