[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m This simplifies to:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ kx = 17x^2 - 4x - 16. \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Now we can use the remainder theorem or simply compare the coefficient of like terms on both sides. The rest will help us to find the specific values of \( c, k, \) and the coefficient \( a \). By comparing coefficients, we get:
