[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. **Total Food Choices**:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    The user must choose one meat, two different vegetables, and one dessert.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. **Meat Choices**:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    There are 3 different meats available:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - Beef
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - Chicken
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - Pork
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    Therefore, the number of ways to choose the meat is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - Beef: \(1\) way
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - Chicken: \(1\) way
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - Pork: \(1\) way
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    Considering the order seems random, the number of ways to choose 1 meat without considering the options within it is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    3 \text{ meats} \times (3! \text{ ways to choose vegetables}) = 3 \times 6 = 18 \text{ ways}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    (where the factorial of 3! is \(3 \times 2 \times 1 = 6\))
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3. **Vegetable Choices**:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    There are 4 different vegetables:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - Baked beans
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - Corn
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - Potatoes
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - Tomatoes
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    If the user chooses vegetables, they must include the given vegetables in their set.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    Therefore, the number of ways to choose the vegetables is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - Baked beans, Corn, Potatoes, Tomatoes
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - Total vegetables: 4 ways
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 4. **Dessert Choices**:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    There are 3 different desserts:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - Brownies
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - Chocolate cake
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - Chocolate pudding
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    If the user chooses desserts, they need to include these in their set.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    Therefore, the number of ways to choose the dessert is:
