[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To eliminate the repeating decimal, we multiply both sides of the equation by 10:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[10x = 5.555\ldots\]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Now, we already know that \(10x = 0.555\ldots\), which we can rewrite as:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[10x = 0.5555\ldots\]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m We subtract the original equation \(x = 0.555\ldots\) from this new equation:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[10x - x = 0.5555\ldots - 0.555\ldots\]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m This simplifies to:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[9x = 0.000\ldots\]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To solve for \(x\), we divide both sides of the equation by 9:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
