[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To expand the expression \(16(2x + 5)\), we need to distribute the 16 to each term inside the parentheses. This can be done using the distributive property, which states that \(a(b + c) = ab + ac\). In this case, \(a = 16\), \(b = 2x\), and \(c = 5\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Here are the steps:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. Distribute the 16 to the first term \(2x\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    16 \cdot 2x = 32x
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. Distribute the 16 to the second term \(5\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    16 \cdot 5 = 80
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3. Combine the results from the two distributions:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    16(2x + 5) = 32x + 80
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m So, the expanded form of the expression is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \boxed{32x + 80}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
