[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Let $\mathbf{a} = \begin{pmatrix} -3 \\ 10 \\ 1 \end{pmatrix},$ $\mathbf{b} = \begin{pmatrix} 5 \\ \pi \\ 0 \end{pmatrix},$ and $\mathbf{c} = \begin{pmatrix} -2 \\ -2 \\ 7 \end{pmatrix}.$  Compute
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[(\mathbf{a} - \mathbf{b}) \cdot [(\mathbf{b} - \mathbf{c}) \times (\mathbf{c} - \mathbf{a})].\]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To solve this problem, we need to compute the expression \(\mathbf{a} - \mathbf{b}\), \((\mathbf{b} - \mathbf{c}) \times (\mathbf{c} - \mathbf{a})\), and then find the dot product of the resulting vectors.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Let's break it down step by step:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. Calculate \(\mathbf{a} - \mathbf{b}\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \mathbf{a} - \mathbf{b} = \begin{pmatrix} -3 \\ 10 \\ 1 \end{pmatrix} - \begin{pmatrix} 5 \\ \pi \\ 0 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} -3 - 5 \\ 10 - \pi \\ 1 - 0 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} -8 \\ 10 - \pi \\ 1 \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. Calculate \((\mathbf{b} - \mathbf{c}) \times (\mathbf{c} - \mathbf{a})\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \mathbf{b} - \mathbf{c} = \begin{pmatrix} 5 \\ \pi \\ 0 \end{pmatrix} - \begin{pmatrix} -2 \\ -2 \\ 7 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 5 + 2 \\ \pi + 2 \\ 0 - 7 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 7 \\ \pi + 2 \\ -7 \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \mathbf{c} - \mathbf{a} = \begin{pmatrix} -2 \\ -2 \\ 7 \end{pmatrix} - \begin{pmatrix} -3 \\ 10 \\ 1 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} -2 + 3 \\ -2 - 10 \\ 7 - 1 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ -12 \\ 6 \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    Now, compute the cross product of \(\begin{pmatrix} 7 \\ \pi + 2 \\ -7 \end{pmatrix}\) and \(\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ -12 \\ 6 \end{pmatrix}\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    (\mathbf{b} - \mathbf{c}) \times (\mathbf{c} - \mathbf{a}) = \begin{vmatrix} \mathbf{i} & \mathbf{j} & \mathbf{k} \\ 7 & \pi + 2 & -7 \\ 1 & -12 & 6 \end{vmatrix} = \mathbf{i}((-12)(6) - (-7)(-12)) - \mathbf{j}(7(6) - (-7)(1)) + \mathbf{k}(7(-12) - 7(1))
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    = \mathbf{i}(-72 - 84) - \mathbf{j}(42 + 7) + \mathbf{k}(-84 - 7) = \mathbf{i}(-156) - \mathbf{j}(49) + \mathbf{k}(-91) = \begin{pmatrix} -156 \\ -49 \\ -91 \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3. Compute the dot product of \(\begin{pmatrix} -8 \\ 10 - \pi \\ 1 \end{pmatrix}\) and \(\begin{pmatrix} -156 \\ -49 \\ -91 \end{pmatrix}\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    (-8)(-156) + (10 - \pi)(-49) + (1)(-91) = 1248 - 49(10 - \pi) - 91 = 1248 - 490 + 49\pi - 91 = 777 + 49\pi
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m So the final answer is:
