[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The average age of the three Wilson children is 7 years. If the two younger children are 4 years old and 7 years old, how many years old is the oldest child?
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To determine the age of the oldest Wilson child, we start with the information given: the average age of the three Wilson children is 7 years. This means the total age of all three Wilson children is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ 3 \times 7 = 21 \text{ years} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m We know the ages of the two younger children are 4 years and 7 years. Let's denote the age of the oldest child as \( x \). Therefore, the total age of the three children can also be expressed as:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ 4 + 7 + x = 21 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Simplifying the left side of the equation, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ 11 + x = 21 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To find \( x \), we subtract 11 from both sides of the equation:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ x = 21 - 11 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ x = 10 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Thus, the age of the oldest child is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \boxed{10}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
