[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Okay, let's determine the form of the function \( g(x) \) step by step by analyzing the given equation:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ 8x^4 - 7x^2 + 8x - 7 + g(x) = x + 1. \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m First, we'll rewrite the right-hand side so it looks all in one term on one side:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ g(x) = x + 1 + 8x^4 - 7x^2 - 7. \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Now, we'll combine like terms to simplify \( g(x) \):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ g(x) = -7x^2 + 8x + x + 1 - 7 + 1, \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ g(x) = -7x^2 + 9x - 5. \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Thus, the function \( g(x) \) with terms in order of decreasing degree as requested is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ g(x) = -7x^2 + 9x - 5. \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m boxed{-7x^2 + 9x - 5}<|endoftext|>
