[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To solve the inequality \(5 - 4x > 17\), we will follow a step-by-step approach.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. **Start with the given inequality:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    5 - 4x > 17
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. **Isolate the term involving \(x\):**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    Subtract 5 from both sides of the inequality:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    5 - 4x - 5 > 17 - 5
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    Simplifying this, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
