[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3. **Solve for \(x\):**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    To isolate \(x\), divide both sides of the inequality by \(-4\). Remember that dividing by a negative number reverses the inequality sign:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    x < \frac{12}{-4}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    Simplify the right-hand side:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    x < -3
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 4. **Determine the location of the solution:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    The inequality \(x < -3\) means that \(x\) can be any value less than \(-3\). This includes all real numbers to the left of \(-3\) on a number line.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
