[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    We see that after the first six digits, the decimal repeats.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. **Identify the repeating block:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    The repeating block is "02727272727272". The length of the repeating block is 6 digits.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3. **Determine the position of the \(291^{\text{st}}\) digit:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    291^{\text{st}} \mod 6
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    We need to find the remainder when 291 is divided by 6.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
