[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    This tells us that:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    291^{\text{st}} \equiv 3 \mod 6
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    Therefore, the \(291^{\text{st}}\) digit is the same as the \(3^{\text{st}}\) digit in the repeating block "027272727272727272727272727".
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 4. **Extract the \(3^{\text{st}}\) digit from the repeating block:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    The repeating block starts with "027", which has two 7s. The digits in the blocks "027" repeat every 6 units. The \(3^{\text{st}}\) digit corresponds to the 4th digit in the sequence (since 3 is the 1st digit and the block "027" has 3 digits).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
