[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To determine by how much \( x+10 \) exceeds \( 10-x \) when \( x \) is a positive number, we start by setting up the expression for the difference between the two quantities:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m (x+10) - (10-x)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Next, we simplify the expression by distributing the negative sign and combining like terms:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m x + 10 - 10 + x
