[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Find the remainder when the polynomial $x^{18}+x^{13}+x^7+x^4+x$ is divided by $x^3-x$.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To find the remainder when the polynomial \( P(x) = x^{18} + x^{13} + x^7 + x^4 + x \) is divided by \( D(x) = x^3 - x \), we will use polynomial long division. The remainder when \( P(x) \) is divided by \( D(x) \) will be a polynomial of degree less than 3, say \( R(x) = ax^2 + bx + c \).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m First, we perform the polynomial division of \( P(x) \) by \( D(x) \).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. Divide the leading term of \( P(x) \) by the leading term of \( D(x) \):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \frac{x^{18}}{x^3} = x^{15}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    So, the first term of the quotient is \( x^{15} \).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. Multiply \( D(x) \) by \( x^{15} \):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    x^{18} \cdot x^3 - x^{18} \cdot x = x^6 - x^7
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    Subtract this from \( P(x) \):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    (x^{18} + x^{13} + x^7 + x^4 + x) - (x^6 - x^7) = x^{18} - x^6 + x^{13} + x^4 + x
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    So, the new dividend is \( x^{18} - x^6 + x^{13} + x^4 + x \).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3. Divide the leading term of the new dividend by the leading term of \( D(x) \):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \frac{x^{18}}{x^3} = x^6
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    So, the next term of the quotient is \( x^6 \).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 4. Multiply \( D(x) \) by \( x^6 \):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    x^6 \cdot x^3 - x^6 \cdot x = x^9 - x^7
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    Subtract this from the new dividend:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    (x^{18} - x^6 + x^{13} + x^4 + x) - (x^9 - x^7) = x^{18} - x^6 - x^9 + x^7 + x^4 + x
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    So, the new dividend is \( x^{18} - x^9 - x^6 + x^7 + x^4 + x \).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 5. Divide the leading term of the new dividend by the leading term of \( D(x) \):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \frac{x^{18}}{x^3} = x^6
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    So, the next term of the quotient is \( x^6 \).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 6. Multiply \( D(x) \) by \( x^6 \):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    x^6 \cdot x^3 - x^6 \cdot x = x^9 - x^7
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    Subtract this from the new dividend:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    (x^{18} - x^6 + x^{13} + x^4 + x) - (x^9 - x^7) = x^{18} - x^6 - x^9 + x^7 + x^4 + x
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    So, the new dividend is \( x^{18} - x^9 + x^6 + x^7 + x^4 + x \).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 7. Divide the leading term of the new dividend by the leading term of \( D(x) \):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \frac{x^{18}}{x^3} = x^6
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    So, the next term of the quotient is \( x^6 \).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 8. Multiply \( D(x) \) by \( x^6 \):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    x^6 \cdot x^3 - x^6 \cdot x = x^9 - x^7
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    Subtract this from the new dividend:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    (x^{18} - x^9 + x^6 + x^7 + x^4 + x) - (x^9 - x^7) = x^{18} - x^6 + x^4 + x
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    So, the new dividend is \( x^{18} - x^6 + x^4 + x \).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m We see that the degree of the remainder is less than 3, so we stop here. The remainder when \( x^{18} + x^{13} + x^7 + x^4 + x \) is divided by \( x^3 - x \) is \( x^{15} - x^{11} - x^{7} + x^7 + x^4 + x \).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The remainder is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \boxed{x^{15} - x^{11} + x^2 + x^4}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
