[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m First, we perform the prime factorization of 4125.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ 4125 = 5^5 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m This tells us that the prime factorization of 4125 is simply \( 5 \) raised to the power of 5. This means that \( 4125 \) is a factor of \( 5^5 \).
