[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To find the projection of the vector $\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ -2 \end{pmatrix}$ onto the vector $\begin{pmatrix} 8 \\ 1 \end{pmatrix}$, we can use the formula for the projection of a vector $\mathbf{a}$ onto a vector $\mathbf{b}$:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \text{proj}_{\mathbf{b}} \mathbf{a} = \frac{\mathbf{a} \cdot \mathbf{b}}{\mathbf{b} \cdot \mathbf{b}} \mathbf{b}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Here, $\mathbf{a} = \begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ -2 \end{pmatrix}$ and $\mathbf{b} = \begin{pmatrix} 8 \\ 1 \end{pmatrix}$.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m First, we need to compute the dot product $\mathbf{a} \cdot \mathbf{b}$:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \mathbf{a} \cdot \mathbf{b} = 1 \cdot 8 + (-2) \cdot 1 = 8 - 2 = 6
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Next, we compute the dot product $\mathbf{b} \cdot \mathbf{b}$:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \mathbf{b} \cdot \mathbf{b} = 8 \cdot 8 + 1 \cdot 1 = 64 + 1 = 65
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Now, we can find the scalar projection factor:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \frac{\mathbf{a} \cdot \mathbf{b}}{\mathbf{b} \cdot \mathbf{b}} = \frac{6}{65}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Finally, we multiply this scalar by the vector $\mathbf{b}$ to get the projection:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \text{proj}_{\mathbf{b}} \mathbf{a} = \frac{6}{65} \begin{pmatrix} 8 \\ 1 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} \frac{48}{65} \\ \frac{6}{65} \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m So the projection of the vector $\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ -2 \end{pmatrix}$ onto the vector $\begin{pmatrix} 8 \\ 1 \end{pmatrix}$ is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \boxed{\begin{pmatrix} \frac{48}{65} \\ \frac{6}{65} \end{pmatrix}}
