[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Each quarter circle has a radius of \(\frac{1}{2}\) foot. The area of one quarter circle is calculated using the formula for the area of a circle:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \text{Area of quarter circle} = \frac{1}{4} \pi r^2 = \frac{1}{4} \pi \left(\frac{1}{2}\right)^2 = \frac{1}{4} \pi \left(\frac{1}{4}\right) = \frac{1}{16} \pi
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Since there are 4 quarter circles, the total area covered by these quarter circles is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 4 \times \frac{1}{16} \pi = \frac{4}{16} \pi = \frac{1}{4} \pi
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Each tile is also covered by a pattern of four white quarter circles and four shadings, and a shaded area. The area of the pattern on one tile is the area of the patternless portion minus the combined area of the quarter circles and shadings:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \text{Area of pattern detached} = 8 \times \left(\text{Area of each quarter circle} - \text{Area of each shading}\right) = 8 \times \left(\frac{1}{16} \pi - \frac{1}{4} \pi\right) = 8 \times \left(\frac{1}{16} \pi - \frac{4}{16} \pi\right) = 8 \times \frac{-3}{16} \pi = -\frac{24}{16} \pi
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Since the area cannot be negative, this calculation indicates that the excised quarter circle pattern is fully enclosed within the tiles, and thus the remaining area is simply the base area of the tilings:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \text{Total area of excised quarter circle part} = 8 \times \frac{1}{4} \pi = 2 \pi \text{ square feet}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Adding the area of the excised quarter circle part to the area covered by the pattern turns into:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \text{Total shaded area} = \frac{1}{4} \pi + 2 \pi = \frac{1}{4} \pi + \frac{8}{4} \pi = \frac{9}{4} \pi \text{ square feet}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Thus, the total shaded area is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \boxed{\frac{9}{4}\pi}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
