[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The dot product of two vectors \(\begin{pmatrix} a \\ b \end{pmatrix}\) and \(\begin{pmatrix} c \\ d \end{pmatrix}\) is given by \(a \cdot c + b \cdot d\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Let \(\begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ 5 \end{pmatrix}\) be the first vector and \(\begin{pmatrix} x \\ -3 \end{pmatrix}\) be the second vector. The dot product of these vectors is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2 \cdot x + 5 \cdot (-3) = 0
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Simplifying the equation, we get:
