[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Let's solve the problem step by step.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. First, we need to find the measure of the largest interior angle of the isosceles triangle \(ABC\). Since \(AB\) and \(AC\) are the equal sides, the angle opposite to the base \(\angle BAC\) will be \(\text{angle} \angle BAC = \angle BAC\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. We know that angle \(A = 20^\circ\). Therefore, \(\angle BAC = 20^\circ\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3. Since \(AB = AC\) and triangles \(ABC\) and \(ACD\) are isosceles triangles (with \(BD\) as their altitude), the angles at base \(D\) of triangles \(ACD\) and \(ABC\) will also be equal to \(20^\circ\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 4. According to the properties of a triangle, the sum of the interior angles is equal to \(180^\circ\). Therefore, we can find the smallest interior angle of the triangle by subtracting the angles of triangles \(ABC\) and \(ACD\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[\text{Smallest angle} = 180^\circ - (\text{Angle} \angle ABC + \text{Angle} \angle BAC) - (\text{Angle} \angle CDA + \text{Angle} \angle ADC)\]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 5. We don't know the exact measures of \(\text{Angle} \angle BDC\) and \(\text{Angle} \angle CDA\), but we know that the sum of these angles must be equal to \(180^\circ - \text{Angle} \angle BAC - \text{Angle} \angle CDA = 180^\circ - 20^\circ - \text{Angle} \angle CDA = 160^\circ - \text{Angle} \angle CDA\). However, since we only need the smallest angle, we can use the fact that \(\angle BAC = \text{Angle} \angle BDC\) and \(\angle CDA = \text{Angle} \angle CDA\) (which must be the same as the angle opposite to the base angle).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 6. Therefore, the smallest angle of the triangle \(ABC\) is \(20^\circ\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m So, the measure of the largest interior angle of triangle \(ABC\) is \(\boxed{60}\).
