[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. **Compare with the given equation:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - The given equation is \( y = 2 \sin(3x + \pi) + 1 \).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - We can see that \( a = 2 \) and \( b = 3 \).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3. **Determine \( d \):**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - The vertical shift \( d \) is the value of the constant term on the right-hand side of the equation when \( x = 0 \).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - Substituting \( x = 0 \) into the equation, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      y = 2 \sin(3(0) + \pi) + 1
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - Simplifying inside the sine function:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      \[
