[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Calculate the volume of the parallelepiped formed by vectors $\mathbf{i} + 2\mathbf{j} + 3\mathbf{k}$, $\mathbf{k} - \mathbf{i}$, and $\mathbf{j} + 2\mathbf{k}$.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To find the volume of the parallelepiped formed by the vectors \(\mathbf{a} = \mathbf{i} + 2\mathbf{j} + 3\mathbf{k}\), \(\mathbf{b} = \mathbf{k} - \mathbf{i}\), and \(\mathbf{c} = \mathbf{j} + 2\mathbf{k}\), we need to calculate the scalar triple product \(\mathbf{a} \cdot (\mathbf{b} \times \mathbf{c})\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m First, we find the cross product \(\mathbf{b} \times \mathbf{c}\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \mathbf{b} \times \mathbf{c} = \begin{vmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \mathbf{i} & \mathbf{j} & \mathbf{k} \\
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1 & -1 & -1 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1 & 1 & 2
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \end{vmatrix} = \mathbf{i} \left((-1)(2) - (-1)(1)\right) - \mathbf{j} \left((1)(2) - (-1)(1)\right) + \mathbf{k} \left(1(-1) - (-1)(1)\right)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m = \mathbf{i} (-2 + 1) - \mathbf{j} (2 + 1) + \mathbf{k} (-1 + 1) = -\mathbf{i} - 3\mathbf{j} + 0\mathbf{k} = -\mathbf{i} - 3\mathbf{j}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m So, \(\mathbf{b} \times \mathbf{c} = -\mathbf{i} - 3\mathbf{j}\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Next, we calculate the dot product \(\mathbf{a} \cdot (\mathbf{b} \times \mathbf{c})\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \mathbf{a} \cdot (\mathbf{b} \times \mathbf{c}) = (\mathbf{i} + 2\mathbf{j} + 3\mathbf{k}) \cdot (-\mathbf{i} - 3\mathbf{j})
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m = 1(-1) + 2(0) + 3(1) = -1 + 0 + 3 = 2
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The volume of the parallelepiped is the absolute value of the scalar triple product:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \boxed{2}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m What number must multiply by 3 to result in $0.03$?
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To find the number that must multiply by 3 to result in \( 0.03 \), we can set up the following equation:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3x = 0.03
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To isolate \( x \), we need to divide both sides of the equation by 3:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m x = \frac{0.03}{3}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Next, we perform the division:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \frac{0.03}{3} = 0.01 = 0.01
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Thus, the number that must multiply by 3 to result in \( 0.03 \) is \( 0.01 \).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Therefore, the final answer is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \boxed{0.01}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
