[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To solve for \( x \) in the equation \( 5 - x = 8 \), we need to isolate \( x \) on one side of the equation. Here are the steps to do that:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. Start with the given equation:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    5 - x = 8
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. To isolate \( x \), we need to get rid of the 5 on the left side of the equation. We can do this by subtracting 5 from both sides of the equation:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    5 - x - 5 = 8 - 5
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3. Simplify both sides of the equation:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    -x = 3
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 4. To solve for \( x \), we need to get rid of the negative sign in front of \( x \). We do this by multiplying both sides of the equation by -1:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    -1 \cdot (-x) = -1 \cdot 3
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 5. Simplify both sides of the equation:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    x = -3
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m So, the solution to the equation \( 5 - x = 8 \) is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \boxed{-3}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
