[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m When \( x = 0 \):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ y = a \sin(2 \cdot 0 + c) = a \sin(c) \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m We need to check if the amplitude is consistent. The general form \( y = a \sin(bx + c) \) generally means the amplitude \( a \) is \( 2 \) because it looks like \( 2 \) in the problem statement. Hence, the phase shift tells us that the function is shifted to the left by \( \frac{\pi}{2} \) because it is vertically displaced shifted to the right by \( \frac{\pi}{2} \).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Therefore, the value of \( b \) is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ \boxed{2} \]<|endoftext|>
