[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To find the remainder when \( N = 3 \times 13 \times 23 \times 33 \times \ldots \times 183 \times 193 \) is divided by 5, we can use modular arithmetic. Specifically, we'll compute the product modulo 5.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m First, let's observe the pattern in the powers of 3 modulo 5:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3^1 \equiv 3 \pmod{5}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3^2 \equiv 9 \equiv 4 \pmod{5}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3^3 \equiv 3 \times 4 \equiv 12 \equiv 2 \pmod{5}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3^4 \equiv 3 \times 2 \equiv 6 \equiv 1 \pmod{5}
