[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To determine how long it will take my friend to read the same novella, we need to follow these steps:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. **Understand the given information:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - My friend reads three times as fast as I do.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - If it takes me 2 hours to read the novella, we need to find out how many minutes it will take for my friend.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. **Convert the time my friend reads into minutes:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - Since there are 60 minutes in an hour, 2 hours is equal to:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      2 \text{ hours} \times 60 \text{ minutes per hour} = 120 \text{ minutes}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3. **Determine my reading speed:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - If my friend reads three times as fast as I do, then my reading speed is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      3 \times \text{my reading speed} = \text{amplitude of the sine wave in one cycle}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 4. **Relate the conversion time to the amplitude:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - According to this setup, the conversion time (120 minutes) corresponds to the half period of a sine wave with an amplitude of 1 (since my friend is reading three times as fast):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      \text{Half period} = \frac{120 \text{ minutes}}{2} = 60 \text{ minutes}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 5. **Conclusion:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - The conversion time, which is half the period of the sine wave, means my friend has a similar conversion of time to my own reading time.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - Therefore, it will take my friend:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      60 \text{ minutes}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - to read the same novella.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \boxed{60}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
