[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To determine how many ordered pairs \((x, y)\) of positive integers satisfy the equation \(xy = 144\), we need to find all pairs \((x, y)\) such that \(x \times y = 144\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m First, let's list the factor pairs of 144:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[1 \times 144, \quad 2 \times 72, \quad 3 \times 48, \quad 4 \times 36, \quad 6 \times 24, \quad 8 \times 18, \quad 9 \times 16, \quad 12 \times 12\]
