[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2x - 14 & \text{if } x \ge 2,
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \end{cases} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m we need to consider the two cases that match the given \( f(x) = -2 \).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. **Case 1: \( x < 2 \)**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    In this case, the function is \( f(x) = 9x + 16 \). Setting this equal to \(-2\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    9x + 16 = -2
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    Subtracting 16 from both sides:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
