[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    Simplifying:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    9x = -18
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    Dividing both sides by 9:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    x = -2
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    Since \(-2 < 2\), this solution is valid.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. **Case 2: \( x \ge 2 \)**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    In this case, the function is \( f(x) = 2x - 14 \). Setting this equal to \(-2\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    2x - 14 = -2
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    Adding 14 to both sides:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    2x = -2 + 14
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    Simplifying:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    2x = 12
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    Dividing both sides by 2:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    x = 6
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    Since \(6 \ge 2\), this solution is valid.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Thus, the possible values of \( x \) that satisfy \( f(x) = -2 \) are \( x = -2 \) and \( x = 6 \). The sum of these values is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m -2 + 6 = 4
