[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To find the \(15^{\text{th}}\) term in the arithmetic sequence \(1, 4, 7, 10, 13, \ldots\), we need to identify the pattern and use the formula for the \(n^{\text{th}}\) term of an arithmetic sequence.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The general formula for the \(n^{\text{th}}\) term of an arithmetic sequence is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m a_n = a_1 + (n-1)d
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m where:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - \(a_n\) is the \(n^{\text{th}}\) term,
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - \(a_1\) is the first term,
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - \(d\) is the common difference,
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - \(n\) is the term number.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m From the given sequence:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - The first term \(a_1 = 1\),
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - The common difference \(d = 4 - 1 = 3\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m We need to find the \(15^{\text{th}}\) term (\(a_{15}\)). Plugging in the values, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m a_{15} = 1 + (15-1) \cdot 3
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m First, calculate \(15-1\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 15-1 = 14
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Next, multiply 14 by the common difference 3:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 14 \cdot 3 = 42
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Finally, add this product to the first term:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1 + 42 = 43
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Therefore, the \(15^{\text{th}}\) term in the sequence is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \boxed{43}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
