[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m ### Step 3: Degrees of the Polynomial and Coefficients
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Since \(P(z)\) and \(Q(z)\) are monic polynomials of degree 4, their product \(R(z) = P(z) \cdot Q(z)\) is also a polynomial of degree 8.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m ### Step 4: Degree of \(Q(z)\)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Because \(P(z) = (z-1)^4 Q(z)\), the degree of \(P(z)\) is 4, which implies \(Q(z)\) must be a polynomial of degree 8. Therefore, \(a + b + c + d + e + f + g + h = 8\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m ### Step 5: Using the Given Information about \(a\) and \(b\)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
