[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Given that \(P(z) = (z-1)^4 Q(z)\), the constant term of \(P(z)\) is the same as the constant term of \(Q(z)\). Therefore, the constant term of Jaclyn's polynomial \(Q(z)\) is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m c + d + e + f + g + h = \text{constant term of } Q(z) = 3
