[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Let $\mathbf{A} = \begin{pmatrix} 2 & 3 \\ 0 & 1 \end{pmatrix}.$  Find $\mathbf{A}^{20} - 2 \mathbf{A}^{19}.$
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To solve the problem \(\mathbf{A}^{20} - 2 \mathbf{A}^{19}\), where \(\mathbf{A} = \begin{pmatrix} 2 & 3 \\ 0 & 1 \end{pmatrix}\), we will first need to compute the powers of the matrix \(\mathbf{A}\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m ### Step 1: Compute \(\mathbf{A}^2\)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \mathbf{A}^2 = \mathbf{A} \cdot \mathbf{A} = \begin{pmatrix} 2 & 3 \\ 0 & 1 \end{pmatrix} \cdot \begin{pmatrix} 2 & 3 \\ 0 & 1 \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m = \begin{pmatrix} 2 \cdot 2 + 3 \cdot 0 & 2 \cdot 3 + 3 \cdot 1 \\ 0 \cdot 2 + 1 \cdot 0 & 0 \cdot 3 + 1 \cdot 1 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 4 & 9 \\ 0 & 1 \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m So, \(\mathbf{A}^2 = \begin{pmatrix} 4 & 9 \\ 0 & 1 \end{pmatrix}\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m ### Step 2: Compute \(\mathbf{A}^3\)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \mathbf{A}^3 = \mathbf{A} \cdot \mathbf{A}^2 = \begin{pmatrix} 2 & 3 \\ 0 & 1 \end{pmatrix} \cdot \begin{pmatrix} 4 & 9 \\ 0 & 1 \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m = \begin{pmatrix} 2 \cdot 4 + 3 \cdot 0 & 2 \cdot 9 + 3 \cdot 1 \\ 0 \cdot 4 + 1 \cdot 0 & 0 \cdot 9 + 1 \cdot 1 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 8 & 21 \\ 0 & 1 \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m So, \(\mathbf{A}^3 = \begin{pmatrix} 8 & 21 \\ 0 & 1 \end{pmatrix}\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m ### Step 3: Compute \(\mathbf{A}^4\)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \mathbf{A}^4 = \mathbf{A}^3 \cdot \mathbf{A}^2 = \begin{pmatrix} 8 & 21 \\ 0 & 1 \end{pmatrix} \cdot \begin{pmatrix} 4 & 9 \\ 0 & 1 \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m = \begin{pmatrix} 8 \cdot 4 + 21 \cdot 0 & 8 \cdot 9 + 21 \cdot 1 \\ 0 \cdot 4 + 1 \cdot 0 & 0 \cdot 9 + 1 \cdot 1 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 32 & 105 \\ 0 & 1 \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m So, \(\mathbf{A}^4 = \begin{pmatrix} 32 & 105 \\ 0 & 1 \end{pmatrix}\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m ### Step 4: Generalize for \(\mathbf{A}^n\)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m We observe a pattern that \(\mathbf{A}^n = \begin{pmatrix} 2^n & 3^n \\ 0 & 1 \end{pmatrix}\). To verify this, we can use induction.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m **Base case:** For \(n=1\),
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \mathbf{A}^1 = \begin{pmatrix} 2 & 3 \\ 0 & 1 \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m which is true.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m **Inductive step:** Assume \(\mathbf{A}^k = \begin{pmatrix} 2^k & 3^k \\ 0 & 1 \end{pmatrix}\). Then,
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \mathbf{A}^{k+1} = \mathbf{A} \cdot \mathbf{A}^k = \begin{pmatrix} 2 & 3 \\ 0 & 1 \end{pmatrix} \cdot \begin{pmatrix} 2^k & 3^k \\ 0 & 1 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 2^{k+1} & 3^{k+1} \\ 0 & 1 \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m So, \(\mathbf{A}^n = \begin{pmatrix} 2^n & 3^n \\ 0 & 1 \end{pmatrix}\) for all \(n\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m ### Step 5: Compute \(\mathbf{A}^{20} - 2 \mathbf{A}^{19}\)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Since \(\mathbf{A}^n = \begin{pmatrix} 2^n & 3^n \\ 0 & 1 \end{pmatrix}\), we have
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \mathbf{A}^{20} = \begin{pmatrix} 2^{20} & 3^{20} \\ 0 & 1 \end{pmatrix} \quad \text{and} \quad 2 \mathbf{A}^{19} = 2 \cdot \begin{pmatrix} 2^{20} & 3^{20} \\ 0 & 1 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 2^{21} & 3^{21} \\ 0 & 2 \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \mathbf{A}^{20} - 2 \mathbf{A}^{19} = \begin{pmatrix} 2^{20} & 3^{20} \\ 0 & 1 \end{pmatrix} - \begin{pmatrix} 2^{21} & 3^{21} \\ 0 & 2 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 2^{20} - 2^{21} & 3^{20} - 3^{21} \\ 0 & 1 - 2 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 2^{20} - 2^{21} & 3^{20} - 3^{21} \\ 0 & -1 \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Thus, the answer is \(\boxed{\begin{pmatrix} 2^{20} - 2^{21} & 3^{20} - 3^{21} \\ 0 & -1 \end{pmatrix}}\).<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
