[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To compute \((3^2)(2^4)(37)(5^3)\), we will break it down step by step.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m First, let's calculate \(3^2\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3^2 = 3 \times 3 = 9
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Next, we calculate \(5^3\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 5^3 = 5 \times 5 \times 5 = 125
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Now, substitute these results back into the original expression:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m (3^2)(2^4)(37)(5^3) = 9 \times 2^4 \times 37 \times 125
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Next, we will compute the raised powers:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2^4 = 2 \times 2 \times 2 \times 2 = 16
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m So the expression now is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 9 \times 2^4 \times 37 \times 125 = 9 \times 16 \times 37 \times 125
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Now, let's multiply these numerators:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 9 \times 16 = 144
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Next, we need to multiply this result by \(37\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 144 \times 37
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To do this multiplication, we can break it down into simpler steps:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 144 \times 37 = 144 \times (30 + 7) = (144 \times 30) + (144 \times 7)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 144 \times 30 = 4320
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 144 \times 7 = 936
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m So we have:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m (144 \times 30) + (144 \times 7) = 4320 + 936 = 5256
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Now, multiply this result by 37:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 5256 \times 37
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To do this multiplication, we can use the distributive property:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 5256 \times 37 = 5256 \times (30 + 7) = 5256 \times 30 + 5256 \times 7
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 5256 \times 30 = 157680
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 5256 \times 7 = 36792
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m So we have:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 157680 + 36792 = 194472
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Finally, we need to multiply this result by 125:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 194472 \times 125
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To do this multiplication, we can use the distributive property:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
