[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Find the ordered pair $(x,y)$ if
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m x+y&=(5-x)+(5-y),\\
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m x-y&=(x-1)+(y-1).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To solve the given system of equations, we will start by adding the two equations together. The first equation is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[x + y = (5 - x) + (5 - y)\]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Simplify the right side:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[x + y = 5 - x + 5 - y\]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[x + y = 10 - x - y\]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[x + x + y + y = 10\]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[2x + 2y = 10\]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[x + y = 5 \quad \text{(Equation 1)}\]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The second equation is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[x - y = (x - 1) + (y - 1)\]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Simplify the right side:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[x - y = x - 1 + y - 1\]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[x - y = x + y - 2\]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[0 = y - 2\]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[y = 2\]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Now that we have \(y = 2\), we can substitute this value back into Equation 1 to find \(x\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[x + 2 = 5\]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[x = 5 - 2\]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[x = 3\]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Therefore, the ordered pair \((x, y)\) is \(\boxed{(3, 2)}\).
