[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m William is taking the 25-question, multiple choice American Mathematics Competition. Each question has five answer choices. William guesses random answers for the last four questions. What is the probability that he will get at least one of these final four questions right?
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To determine the probability that William will get at least one of the last four questions right, we can model this problem using the complement rule. The complement rule states that the probability of an event happening is 1 minus the probability of the event not happening.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m First, let's calculate the probability that William fails exactly one of the last four questions. We will use the binomial probability formula for this calculation. The binomial probability formula is given by:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ P(X = k) = \binom{n}{k} p^k (1-p)^{n-k} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m where:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - \( n \) is the number of trials (questions), which is 4 in this case.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - \( k \) is the number of successful trials (correct answers), which is 1 (because we need at least one question wrong).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - \( p \) is the probability of success on an individual trial, which is the probability that a question is answered correctly, which is \( \frac{5}{6} \).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - \( \binom{n}{k} \) is the binomial coefficient, calculated as \( \binom{n}{k} = \frac{n!}{k!(n-k)!} \).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Plugging in the values, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ P(\text{fail exactly one}) = \binom{4}{1} \left( \frac{5}{6} \right)^1 \left( \frac{1}{6} \right)^3 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ P(\text{fail exactly one}) = 4 \cdot \frac{5}{6} \cdot \frac{1}{6^3} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ P(\text{fail exactly one}) = 4 \cdot \frac{5}{6^4} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ P(\text{fail exactly one}) = 4 \cdot \frac{5}{1296} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ P(\text{fail exactly one}) = \frac{20}{1296} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ P(\text{fail exactly one}) = \frac{5}{324} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The complement of this event is that William gets all four questions wrong. We now calculate this probability:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ P(\text{all wrong}) = \binom{4}{4} \left( \frac{5}{6} \right)^4 \left( \frac{1}{6} \right)^0 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ P(\text{all wrong}) = 1 \cdot \frac{5}{6^4} \cdot 1 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ P(\text{all wrong}) = \frac{5}{6^4} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ P(\text{all wrong}) = \frac{5}{1296} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Using the complement rule, the probability that William gets at least one question right is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ P(\text{at least one right}) = 1 - P(\text{all wrong}) \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ P(\text{at least one right}) = 1 - \frac{5}{1296} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ P(\text{at least one right}) = \frac{1296}{1296} - \frac{5}{1296} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ P(\text{at least one right}) = \frac{1291}{1296} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Therefore, the probability that William will get at least one of the last four questions right is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \boxed{\frac{1291}{1296}}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m [Ground Truth]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \frac{369}{625}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m [Is Boxed Matched]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m True
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m [Extracted Answer]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \frac{1291}{1296}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
