[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The given task involves determining the roles of variables, calculating the gains and losses of these variables, and then using these outcomes to compute the arithmetic mean. The variables to be allocated are as follows:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - Number of Prime Forenas (P)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - Type of Stock (X)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - Number of Stocks traded (N)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Here are the detailed calculations for each operation:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. **Gain (G):**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    G = P \times (1 - \delta) \times (1 + Pr(x < y)) - (\sum a_ix_i) \times \left(P - \sum a_i\right)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    where \(P\) is the product of all Prime Forenas, \(Pr(x < y)\) is PrXx (the probability that a Forena exits at \(x\)) and \(\sum a_i\) is the sum of all Forenas.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    For the gain expression:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    G = P(v_x - P)\times(1-P)\*(1-Pr(x < y)p(y-x)) = P(\delta v_x) \*(1-\delta)\*(1+Pr(x < x)), = P (\delta v_x)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    This expression gives the loss of forenas (losing value) from the dating house in the game.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. The loss is the gain with respect to the fixed premium. If you have a gain, or a loss, you need to explicitly calculate the gain or loss unless otherwise specified.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3. **Maximum Profit (MIN):**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    MIN = P v + v x + z
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    This expression gives the maximum profit (money) invested in a Prime Forena if all Forenas are bought and sold at auction, making a profit of higher value each time a Forena is sold.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 4. **Minimum Loss:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    MIN = 0
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    This expression is generally understood to hold for a Forena because investing in it and not losing it results in a loss of no value. It helps stabilize calculations and ensures the game can account for an unlimited number of Forenas.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m   
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \boxed{
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \begin{aligned}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m     G &= P(\delta v_x) \\
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m     MIN &= P v + v_x + z
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \end{aligned}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m }
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m   
