[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To evaluate \((-125)^{4/3}\), we need to break it down into its components and then use exponents correctly. The expression \((-125)^{4/3}\) can be rewritten using the property of exponents that states \(a^m \cdot a^n = a^{m+n}\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m (-125)^{4/3} = (-125) \cdot (-125)^{1/3}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
