[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m (-125)^{4/3} = (-125)^{1/3} \cdot (-125)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Next, we need to evaluate \((-125)^{1/3}\). The exponent \(1/3\) means we are only concerned with the cube root of \(-125\). The cube root of \(-125\) is also \(-5\) (since \((-5)^3 = -125\)):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m (-125)^{1/3} = -5
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Now we substitute this back into our expression:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m (-125)^{4/3} = -5 \cdot (-125)
