[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To determine which integer is not in the range of \(f(x)\), we need to analyze the behavior of the function \(f(x)\) based on the given piecewise condition:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m f(x) = \left\lceil\dfrac{1}{x+2}\right\rceil \quad \text{for} \quad x > -2
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m f(x) = \left\lfloor\dfrac{1}{x+2}\right\rfloor \quad \text{for} \quad x < -2
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m ### Step 1: Find the Domain of \(f(x)\)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - For \(x > -2\), \(f(x) = \left\lceil\dfrac{1}{x+2}\right\rceil\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - For \(x < -2\), \(f(x) = \left\lfloor\dfrac{1}{x+2}\right\rfloor\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m We need to determine the values of \(x\) for which these expressions are defined.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - For \(x > -2\), \(\frac{1}{x+2}\) must be greater than 1 (since \(\left\lceil\dfrac{1}{x+2}\right\rceil\) is always greater than \(\left\lceil\dfrac{1}{x+2}\right\rceil - 1\)). This implies:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m   \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m   \frac{1}{x+2} > 1 \quad \Rightarrow \quad 1 > x+2 \quad \Rightarrow \quad x < -3
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m   \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m   Therefore, \(f(x) = \left\lceil\dfrac{1}{x+2}\right\rceil\) is defined for \(x > -2 \cup x < -3\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - For \(x < -2\), \(\frac{1}{x+2}\) must be less than -1 (since \(\left\lfloor\dfrac{1}{x+2}\right\rfloor\) is always less than \(\left\lfloor\dfrac{1}{x+2}\right\rfloor + 1\)). This implies:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m   \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m   x+2 < 0 \quad \Rightarrow \quad x < -2
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m   \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m   Therefore, \(f(x) = \left\lfloor\dfrac{1}{x+2}\right\rfloor\) is defined for \(-2 < x < -3\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m ### Step 2: Determine the Range of \(f(x)\)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m In the interval \(-2 < x < -3\), we need to find the values of \(\left\lceil\dfrac{1}{x+2}\right\rceil\) and \(\left\lfloor\dfrac{1}{x+2}\right\rfloor\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m #### For \(1.5 < x < 2\)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - \(\frac{1}{x+2}\) approaches 0 as \(x\) approaches 1.5 from the left.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - \(\frac{1}{x+2}\) approaches \(-\infty\) as \(x\) approaches 2 from the left.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Thus, \(\left\lceil\dfrac{1}{x+2}\right\rceil\) must be between 1 and 2, and \(\left\lfloor\dfrac{1}{x+2}\right\rfloor\) must be between 1 and 2.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m In this interval, the only integer that satisfies these constraints is \(x = 1.5\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m #### For \(-2 < x < -3\)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - \(\frac{1}{x+2}\) approaches \(-\infty\) as \(x\) approaches -3 from the left.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - \(\frac{1}{x+2}\) approaches 0 as \(x\) approaches -2 from the left.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Thus, \(\left\lceil\dfrac{1}{x+2}\right\rceil\) must be between 1 and 1 (the smallest integer greater than or equal to 1), and \(\left\lfloor\dfrac{1}{x+2}\right\rfloor\) must be between 1 and 1.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m In this interval, the only integer that satisfies these constraints is \(x = -2\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m ### Step 3: Identify the Integer Not in the Range of \(f(x)\)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m From the above analysis, we see that both integers 1.5 and -2 are not in the range of \(f(x)\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Thus, the integer that is not in the range of \(f(x)\) is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
