[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m However, we need to check if this value is possible. The maximum distance is actually the sum of the radius of the larger circle (which is 1) and the distance to the center of the base, which is \( \sqrt{3} \). So the maximum distance is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \sqrt{3} + \sqrt{3} = 2\sqrt{3}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m But we need to check if this is correct. The correct answer should be:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \sqrt{3} + \sqrt{3} = 2\sqrt{3}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Thus, the maximum distance is:
