[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To find the smallest prime divisor of \(5^{23} + 7^{17}\), we need to consider the expression modulo the smallest prime number, which is 2. Let's evaluate the expression \(5^{23} + 7^{17}\) modulo 2.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m First, observe that \(5 \equiv 1 \pmod{2}\) and \(7 \equiv 1 \pmod{2}\). Therefore,
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[5^{23} \equiv 1^{23} \equiv 1 \pmod{2}\]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[7^{17} \equiv 1^{17} \equiv 1 \pmod{2}\]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m So,
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[5^{23} + 7^{17} \equiv 1 + 1 \equiv 2 \equiv 0 \pmod{2}\]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m This tells us that \(5^{23} + 7^{17}\) is divisible by 2. The smallest prime divisor of \(5^{23} + 7^{17}\) is 2.
