[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Given that set $A$ is exactly equal to its double set $2A$, find the value of the real number $a$. We need to find the value of \(a\) such that the set \(A\) is exactly equal to its double set \(2A\). This implies that \(A = 2A\), which can be rewritten as \(A\) being a subset of itself. This means that all elements of \(A\) are also elements of \(2A\) and vice versa.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Let's write out the conditions:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. \(A \subseteq 2A\)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. \(A \subseteq 2A\) implies \(A = 2A\)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m For \(A \subseteq 2A\), any element in \(A\) must be in \(2A\). And for \(A \subseteq 2A\), any element in \(A\) must also be in \(A\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m We can see that \(A = 2A\) if and only if all elements of \(A\) are in \(A\), which means \(A\) must be the set of all elements that are in \(2A\). Since \(A\) must satisfy this condition for all \(x\) in \(A\) and \(x \in A\), the set \(A\) must be the set of all real numbers, \(\mathbb{R}\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Therefore, the value of \(a\) must be 0, because if \(a\) is any real number, the set \(A = \{a\}\) will be a subset of \(2A = \{2a\}\) and cannot be equal to \(2A\), which means there is no contradiction.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m So, the value of \(a\) is \(\boxed{0}\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To verify:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - If \(A = \{a\}\), then \(2A = \{2a\}\) and \(A \subseteq 2A\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - However, \(A = \{a\} \subseteq \{2a\} = \{2a\}\) does not satisfy \(A = 2A\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The correct answer is \(a = 0\).
