[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To find the greatest common factor (GCF) of 68 and 92, we can use the prime factorization method.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m First, let's find the prime factorization of each number:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - The prime factorization of 68:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m   - 68 is an even number, so it is divisible by 2.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m   \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m   68 = 2 \times 34
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m   \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m   - 34 is also an even number, so it is divisible by 2.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m   \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m   34 = 2 \times 17
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m   \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m   - Therefore, the prime factorization of 68 is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m   \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m   68 = 2^2 \times 17
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m   \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - The prime factorization of 92:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m   - 92 is an even number, so it is divisible by 2.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m   \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m   92 = 2 \times 46
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m   \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m   - 46 is an even number, so it is divisible by 2.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m   \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m   46 = 2 \times 23
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m   \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m   - Therefore, the prime factorization of 92 is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m   \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m   92 = 2^2 \times 23
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m   \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Next, we identify the common prime factors of 68 and 92.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - The prime factors of 68 are: 2 and 17.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - The prime factors of 92 are: 2 and 23.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The only common prime factor between 68 and 92 is 2.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Therefore, the greatest common factor of 68 and 92 is \boxed{2}.<|endoftext|>
