[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To expand the expression \(7(3y+2)\), we need to distribute the 7 across the terms inside the parentheses. This process is known as the distributive property of multiplication over addition. Here are the steps:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. Identify the term inside the parentheses, which is \(3y+2\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. Distribute the 7 to each term inside the parentheses:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - Distribute 7 to \(3y\): \(7 \cdot 3y = 21y\)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - Distribute 7 to 2: \(7 \cdot 2 = 14\)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3. Combine all the terms:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    7(3y+2) = 21y + 14
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m So, the expanded form of the expression \(7(3y+2)\) is \(\boxed{21y+14}\).<|endoftext|>
