[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To determine the residue of \(-811\) modulo 24, we need to find an equivalent positive integer that is less than 24. This can be done by finding the remainder when \(-811\) is divided by 24 and then adjusting it to be within the range of 0 to 23.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m First, we perform the division of \(-811\) by 24:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m -811 \div 24 = -33.875
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The integer part of \(-33.875\) is \(-34\). This tells us that \(-811\) is closer to \(-34\) than it is to \(-33\). Therefore, we add \(24\) to \(-811\) to get a number with more than 0 and more than 23 remaining.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m -34 + 24 = -10
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Since we need the residue in the range \(0, 1, 2,\) and \(3\), we convert \(-10\) to a positive equivalent by adding 24 to \(-10\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m -10 + 24 = 14
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Thus, the residue of \(-811 \pmod{24}\) is \(\boxed{14}\).<|endoftext|>
