[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To compute \(\tan 30^\circ\), we start by recalling the exact values for the tangent of \(30^\circ\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The tangent of \(30^\circ\) is a well-known trigonometric value, and it is given by:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \tan 30^\circ = \frac{1}{\sqrt{3}}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Next, we need to rationalize the denominator to express the result in the standard form of a fraction with a square root:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \tan 30^\circ = \frac{1}{\sqrt{3}} \times \frac{\sqrt{3}}{\sqrt{3}} = \frac{\sqrt{3}}{3}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Therefore, the value of \(\tan 30^\circ\) is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \boxed{\frac{\sqrt{3}}{3}}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m [Ground Truth]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \frac{\sqrt{3}}{3}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
