[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To find the area of the black region, we need to calculate the area of the larger square minus the area of the smaller square.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. **Calculate the area of the larger square:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - The side length of the larger square is 7 units.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - The area of a square is given by the formula: \(\text{Area} = \text{side length}^2\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - Therefore, the area of the larger square is \(7^2 = 49\) square units.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. **Calculate the area of the smaller square:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - The side length of the smaller square is 3 units.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - Using the same area formula, the area of the smaller square is \((3^2) = 9\) square units.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3. **Calculate the area of the black region:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - The black region is the area of the larger square minus the area of the smaller square.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - Therefore, the area of the black region is \(49 - 9 = 40\) square units.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Finally, we put the final answer in the box:
