[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Mr. Fat needs 20 minutes to eat a pound of cereal, while Mr. Thin needs 30 minutes. If they eat together, how long does it take for them to finish off three pounds of cereal? Express your answer in minutes.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To determine how long it will take Mr. Fat and Mr. Thin to finish off three pounds of cereal together, we need to calculate their combined rate of consumption. The rate of consumption is the amount of cereal divided by the time it takes to consume that amount.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m First, we calculate the rate of consumption for Mr. Fat:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - Mr. Fat eats 1 pound of cereal in 20 minutes, so his rate of consumption is \( \frac{1 \text{ pound}}{20 \text{ minutes}} \).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Next, we calculate the rate of consumption for Mr. Thin:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - Mr. Thin eats 1 pound of cereal in 30 minutes, so his rate of consumption is \( \frac{1 \text{ pound}}{30 \text{ minutes}} \).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To find the combined rate of consumption, we add the two rates together:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ \text{Combined rate} = \frac{1 \text{ pound}}{20 \text{ minutes}} + \frac{1 \text{ pound}}{30 \text{ minutes}} = \frac{1 \text{ pound}}{20 \text{ minutes}} + \frac{2 \text{ pounds}}{60 \text{ minutes}} = \frac{3 \text{ pounds}}{60 \text{ minutes}} = \frac{3}{60} \text{ pounds per minute} = \frac{1}{20} \text{ pounds per minute}. \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Now, we need to find out how long it takes for them to consume three pounds of cereal at this combined rate. If the combined rate is \( \frac{1}{20} \text{ pounds per minute} \), then the time required to consume three pounds is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ \text{Time} = \frac{3 \text{ pounds}}{\frac{1}{20} \text{ pounds per minute}} = 3 \text{ pounds} \times 20 \text{ minutes per pound} = 60 \text{ minutes}. \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Thus, the time it takes for both Mr. Fat and Mr. Thin to finish off three pounds of cereal is \(\boxed{60}\) minutes.<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
