[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m ### Step 2: Find the largest multiple of 7 less than 150
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m We continue checking the integer part up to just below 147 to see if it is a multiple of 7:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ 147 \div 7 = 21 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The integer part of the division is 21, so the largest integer less than 147 that is a multiple of 7 is also \( 7 \times 21 = 147 \).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m ### Step 3: Count the number of multiples of 7 between 147 and 149
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The multiples of 7 between 147 and 149 are:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ 147, 148 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To find the number of these multiples, we simply count them:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ 148 - 147 + 1 = 2 + 1 = 3 \]
