[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To solve the equation \(\log_2 2018 + \log_4 2018 + \log_8 2018 + \log_{64} 2018 = \log_x 2018\), we will use logarithmic properties and algebraic manipulation step by step.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m First, let's rewrite the given equation using the power rule of logarithms, \(\log_b (a^c) = c \log_b a\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \log_2 2018 + \log_4 2018 + \log_8 2018 + \log_{64} 2018 = \log_{2018} 2018
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Next, we combine the logarithms of the common base 2018:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \log_2 2018 + \log_4 2018 + \log_8 2018 + \log_{64} 2018 = \log_{2018} (2018)^{-1}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Now, simplify the logarithms using the power rule of logarithms again:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \log_2 2018 + \log_4 2018 + \log_8 2018 + \log_{64} 2018 = \log_{2018} 1
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Since \(\log_{2018} 1 = 0\), we have:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \log_2 2018 + \log_4 2018 + \log_8 2018 + \log_{64} 2018 = 0
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Combine the logarithms using the product rule of logarithms, which states that \(\log_b x + \log_b y + \log_b z = \log_b (xyz)\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m (\log_2 2018 \cdot \log_2 4) + (\log_4 2018 \cdot \log_4 8) + (\log_8 2018 \cdot \log_8 2018) = \log_{2018} (2018 \cdot 4 \cdot 8)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Simplify the product of the logarithms:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \log_2 2018 \cdot \log_2 4 = \log_2 (2018^{1/2}) = \frac{1}{2} \log_2 2018
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \log_4 2018 \cdot \log_4 8 = \log_4 (2018^{1/4}) = \frac{1}{4} \log_4 2018
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \log_8 2018 \cdot \log_8 2018 = \log_8 (2018^{1/3}) = \frac{1}{3} \log_8 2018
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
