[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m For a non-empty set $P$, we define $P(n)=\max \{n-m|m\in P\}$. For example, $P(3)=3-0=3$, $P(4)=4-0=4$, $P(5)=5-0=5$. If the set $S=\{1,2,3,4,5\}$, then the total number of non-empty subsets of $S$ that satisfy the condition $P({P(3)}+{P(4)})=10$ is ()
