[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m we start by expressing the projection formula. The projection of a vector \(\mathbf{v}\) onto a vector \(\mathbf{u}\) is given by:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \text{proj}_{\mathbf{u}} \mathbf{v} = \frac{\mathbf{u} \cdot \mathbf{v}}{\mathbf{u} \cdot \mathbf{u}} \mathbf{u} = \frac{\mathbf{v} \cdot \mathbf{u}}{\mathbf{u} \cdot \mathbf{u}} \mathbf{u}.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m First, consider the projection onto the vector \(\begin{pmatrix} 3 \\ 0 \end{pmatrix}\). This projection is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \operatorname{proj}_{\begin{pmatrix} 3 \\ 0 \end{pmatrix}} \mathbf{v} = \frac{\mathbf{v} \cdot \begin{pmatrix} 3 \\ 0 \end{pmatrix}}{\left\| \mathbf{v} \right\|^2} \begin{pmatrix} 3 \\ 0 \end{pmatrix}.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m We know this projection equals:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \begin{pmatrix} -5 \\ 0 \end{pmatrix}.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Thus, we have:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \frac{\mathbf{v} \cdot \begin{pmatrix} 3 \\ 0 \end{pmatrix}}{\left\| \mathbf{v} \right\|^2} \begin{pmatrix} 3 \\ 0 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} -5 \\ 0 \end{pmatrix}.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m This implies:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \frac{\left( \mathbf{v} \cdot \begin{pmatrix} 3 \\ 0 \end{pmatrix} \right) \cdot 3 + 0 \cdot 0}{\left\| \mathbf{v} \right\|^2} \begin{pmatrix} 3 \\ 0 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} -5 \\ 0 \end{pmatrix}.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Simplifying the dot product, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \frac{3 \left( \mathbf{v} \cdot \begin{pmatrix} 3 \end{pmatrix} \right)}{\left\| \mathbf{v} \right\|^2} \begin{pmatrix} 3 \\ 0 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} -5 \\ 0 \end{pmatrix}.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m This further simplifies to:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \frac{3 \left( \mathbf{v} \cdot \begin{pmatrix} 3 \end{pmatrix} \right)}{\left\| \mathbf{v} \right\|^2} \cdot 3 = \begin{pmatrix} -5 \\ 0 \end{pmatrix},
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \frac{3 \left( \mathbf{v} \cdot \begin{pmatrix} 3 \end{pmatrix} \right)}{\left\| \mathbf{v} \right\|^2} = \begin{pmatrix} -5 \\ 0 \end{pmatrix},
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \frac{\left( \mathbf{v} \cdot \begin{pmatrix} 3 \end{pmatrix} \right)}{\left\| \mathbf{v} \right\|^2} = \begin{pmatrix} -\frac{5}{3} \\ 0 \end{pmatrix}.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Thus, we have:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \frac{\left( \mathbf{v} \cdot \begin{pmatrix} 3 \end{pmatrix} \right)}{\left\| \mathbf{v} \right\|^2} = -\frac{5}{3}.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Next, consider the projection onto the vector \(\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ 3 \end{pmatrix}\). This projection is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \operatorname{proj}_{\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ 3 \end{pmatrix}} \mathbf{v} = \frac{\mathbf{v} \cdot \begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ 3 \end{pmatrix}}{\left\| \mathbf{v} \right\|^2} \begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ 3 \end{pmatrix}.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m We know this projection equals:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \begin{pmatrix} \frac{1}{10} \\ \frac{3}{10} \end{pmatrix}.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Thus, we have:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \frac{\mathbf{v} \cdot \begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ 3 \end{pmatrix}}{\left\| \mathbf{v} \right\|^2} \begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ 3 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} \frac{1}{10} \\ \frac{3}{10} \end{pmatrix}.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m This implies:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \frac{\left( \mathbf{v} \cdot \begin{pmatrix} 1 \end{pmatrix} \right) \cdot 1 + \left( \mathbf{v} \cdot \begin{pmatrix} 3 \end{pmatrix} \right) \cdot 3}{\left\| \mathbf{v} \right\|^2} \begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ 3 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} \frac{1}{10} \\ \frac{3}{10} \end{pmatrix},
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \frac{\left( \mathbf{v} \cdot \begin{pmatrix} 1 \end{pmatrix} \right) \cdot 1}{\left\| \mathbf{v} \right\|^2} + \frac{\left( \mathbf{v} \cdot \begin{pmatrix} 3 \end{pmatrix} \right) \cdot 3}{\left\| \mathbf{v} \right\|^2} = \frac{1}{10} + \frac{9}{10}.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m This simplifies to:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \frac{1 \left( \mathbf{v} \cdot \begin{pmatrix} 1 \end{pmatrix} \right)}{\left\| \mathbf{v} \right\|^2} + \frac{3 \left( \mathbf{v} \cdot \begin{pmatrix} 3 \end{pmatrix} \right)}{\left\| \mathbf{v} \right\|^2} = 0.5.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Since we know \( \frac{\left( \mathbf{v} \cdot \begin{pmatrix} 3 \end{pmatrix} \right)}{\left\| \mathbf{v} \right\|^2} = -\frac{5}{3} \), we substitute:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \frac{1}{\left\| \mathbf{v} \right\|^2} + \frac{3 \left( -\frac{5}{3} \right)}{\left\| \mathbf{v} \right\|^2} = 0.5,
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \frac{1}{\left\| \mathbf{v} \right\|^2} - \frac{5}{\left\| \mathbf{v} \right\|^2} = 0.5,
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - \frac{4}{\left\| \mathbf{v} \right\|^2} = 0.5,
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \left\| \mathbf{v} \right\|^2 = -1,
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m which is impossible. Therefore, we must re-evaluate our approach. Instead, consider the vectors \(\begin{pmatrix} 3 \\ 0 \end{pmatrix}\) and \(\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ 3 \end{pmatrix}\) are not necessarily orthogonal, but can still be part of a set of vectors that form a basis for the plane. The correct approach is to recognize that the projection must be the zero vector when the vector vector is a scalar multiple of the first vector. Thus, we know:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \mathbf{v} = k \begin{pmatrix} 3 \\ 0 \end{pmatrix},
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m for some scalar \(k\). From the third projection, we have:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \frac{k \mathbf{v} \cdot \begin{pmatrix} 3 \end{pmatrix}}{\mathbf{v} \cdot \begin{pmatrix} 3 \end{pmatrix}} = \begin{pmatrix} \frac{1}{10} \\ \frac{3}{10} \end{pmatrix},
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m k \frac{3 \left( \mathbf{v} \cdot \begin{pmatrix} 3 \end{pmatrix} \right)}{\left\| \mathbf{v} \right\|^2} = \begin{pmatrix} \frac{1}{10} \\ \frac{3}{10} \end{pmatrix},
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m k \frac{3 \left( \frac{1}{10} \right)}{\left\| \begin{pmatrix} 3 \\ 0 \end{pmatrix} \right\|^2} = \begin{pmatrix} \frac{1}{10} \\ \frac{3}{10} \end{pmatrix},
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m k \frac{\frac{3}{10}}{9} = \begin{pmatrix} \frac{1}{10} \\ \frac{3}{10} \end{pmatrix},
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m k \frac{1}{30} = \begin{pmatrix} \frac{1}{10} \\ \frac{3}{10} \end{pmatrix},
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m k = 3.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Thus, the vector \(\mathbf{v}\) is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \mathbf{v} = 3 \begin{pmatrix} 3 \\ 0 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 9 \\ 0 \end{pmatrix}.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
