[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To compute the matrix product \(\begin{pmatrix} 2 & 0 \\ 5 & -3 \end{pmatrix} \begin{pmatrix} 8 & -2 \\ 1 & 1 \end{pmatrix}\), we need to multiply each element of the first matrix by each element of the second matrix and then sum the results.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Let's denote the first matrix as \(A\) and the second matrix as \(B\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ A = \begin{pmatrix} 2 & 0 \\ 5 & -3 \end{pmatrix}, \quad B = \begin{pmatrix} 8 & -2 \\ 1 & 1 \end{pmatrix}. \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
