[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Amy takes a loan of $2000 from a bank, with an annual interest rate of 20%. If she successfully repays the loan, what will be her total repayment after 5 years? To solve this problem, we need to calculate the total repayment Amy will have after 5 years, given that she pays back the loan at an annual interest rate of 20%.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The formula to calculate the total repayment after \( t \) years is given by:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ \text{Total Repayment} = \text{Initial Loan} \times (1 + \text{Interest Rate})^t \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Here, the initial loan (\( \text{Initial Loan} \)) is \( \$2000 \), the annual interest rate (\( \text{Interest Rate} \)) is \( 0.20 \), and the number of years (\( t \)) is \( 5 \).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Let's plug in these values into the formula:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ \text{Total Repayment} = 2000 \times (1 + 0.20)^5 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ \text{Total Repayment} = 2000 \times (1.20)^5 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ \text{Total Repayment} = 2000 \times 2.48832 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ \text{Total Repayment} = 4976.64 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Therefore, Amy's total repayment after 5 years will be \(\$4976.64\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Here is the Python code to confirm this calculation:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m ```python
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m # Define the initial loan, interest rate, and number of years
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m initial_loan = 2000
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m interest_rate = 0.20
