[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To find the greatest multiple of 3 that is less than 500 and is also a multiple of 4, we need to find the greatest common multiple (GCM) of 3 and 4. This is because the only common multiple of 3 and 4 is 12, as 12 is the largest number that is a multiple of both 3 and 4.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Next, we need to determine the smallest multiple of 12 that is less than 500. We do this by dividing 500 by 12 and rounding down to the nearest whole number, and then multiply by 12:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \left\lfloor \frac{500}{12} \right\rfloor = \left\lfloor 41.67 \right\rfloor = 41
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m So, 41 is the smallest multiple of 12 that is less than 500. To confirm, we check the multiples of 12 that are less than 500 and divide by 12:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 12 \times 11 = 132, \quad 12 \times 12 = 144, \quad 12 \times 13 = 156, \quad 12 \times 14 = 168, \quad 12 \times 15 = 180, \quad 12 \times 16 = 192, \quad 12 \times 17 = 204, \quad 12 \times 18 = 216
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
