[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To solve the expression \(1273 + 120 \div 60 - 173\), we need to follow the order of operations, often remembered by the acronym PEMDAS (Parentheses, Exponents, Multiplication and Division (from left to right), Addition and Subtraction (from left to right)).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. **Division**: Perform the division \(120 \div 60\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    120 \div 60 = 2
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    So the expression now becomes:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    1273 + 2 - 173
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. **Addition and Subtraction**: Next, perform the addition and subtraction from left to right.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    1273 + 2 = 1275
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    1275 - 173 = 1102
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
