[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m ### Step 1: Calculate \(40^2\)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[40^2 = 40 \times 40 = 1600\]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Emily first calculates \(40^2\) and then adds \(164\) to get the result.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m ### Step 2: Identify the correct operation for \(38^2\)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Emily subtracts a number from \(40^2\) to calculate \(38^2\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m ### Step 3: Choose the correct correction for \(38^2\)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To give the correct result, Emily subtracts the number she needs to subtract. This number should be the difference between \(40^2\) and \(38^2\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
