[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To solve the equation \( |x-7| - 3 = -2 \), we need to isolate \( |x-7| \) and then consider the definition of the absolute value function.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. **Isolate the absolute value:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    |x-7| - 3 = -2
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    Add 3 to both sides of the equation to isolate the absolute value:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    |x-7| = -2 + 3
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    Simplifying the right side, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    |x-7| = 1
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. **Rewrite the absolute value equation:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    The equation \( |x-7| = 1 \) means that \( x \) could be 8 units away from 7 or 9 units away from 7. Therefore, we have two cases to consider:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    x-7 = 1
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    and
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    x-7 = -1
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3. **Solve the two cases:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - For \( x-7 = 1 \):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      x = 1 + 7
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      x = 8
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - For \( x-7 = -1 \):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      x = -1 + 7
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      \[
