[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To expand the product \((x+1)^2 \cdot x\), we need to multiply these two expressions together. We can do this by distributing each term in \((x+1)^2\) to each term in \(x\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m (x+1)^2 \cdot x = (x+1)^2 \cdot x = (x+1)(x+1)x = x(x^2 + x + x + x) = x(x^2 + 3x) = x^3 + 3x^2
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m So, the expanded form of \((x+1)^2 \cdot x\) is \(\boxed{x^3 + 3x^2}\).<|endoftext|>
