[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To determine the residue of \(-811 \pmod{24}\), we need to find an integer \(x\) such that:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ x \equiv -811 \pmod{24} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m First, we need to convert -811 into a positive number by adding 24:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ -811 + 24 = -787 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m So, we need to find the residue of \(-787\) modulo 24. To do this, we divide \(-787\) by 24 and find the remainder:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ -787 \div 24 = -32.7867 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The integer part of the quotient is \(-32\), and the integer part of the remainder is \(24\). We then lose this to the negative sign, so we get:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ -787 \equiv 27 \pmod{24} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m This is because the negative of the negative remainder (which is \(\pm 24\)), modulo 24, gives us the correct residue.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
