[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To solve the problem, we need to evaluate the function \( f(z) \) at several points, specifically \( f(i), f(1), f(-1), \) and \( f(-i) \). Let's start by understanding the function \( f(z) \).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The function is defined as:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m f(z) = \begin{cases} 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m z^2 & \text{if } z \text{ is not real,} \\
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m z + 2 & \text{if } z \text{ is real.}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \end{cases}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m First, let's determine the values for \( f(z) \) at specific points. We know that 1 is real, so we substitute \( z = 1 \) into the piecewise function.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. For \( f(1) \):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m f(1) = 1 + 2 = 3
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. For \( f(-1) \):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Since \(-1\) is not real, we use the second piece of the function:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m f(-1) = -1 + 2 = 1
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3. For \( f(-i) \):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Since \(-i\) is not real, we use the second piece of the function:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m f(-i) = -i + 2 = 2 - i
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Now, we need to find the sum \( f(i) + f(1) + f(-1) + f(-i) \).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - For \( f(i) \), we need to check if \( i \) is real:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m   Since \( i \) is not real, \( f(i) = 0 \).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - Therefore, the sum is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m f(i) + f(1) + f(-1) + f(-i) = 0 + 3 + 1 + (2 - i) = 3 + 1 + 2 - i = 6 - i
