[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Given $a \neq 0,$ solve for $x$ in
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[\begin{vmatrix} x + a & x  & x \\ x & x + a & x \\ x & x & x + a \end{vmatrix} = 0.\]Give your answer in terms of $a.$
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To solve the given determinant equation, we need to evaluate the determinant of the matrix:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \begin{vmatrix} x + a & x  & x \\ x & x + a & x \\ x & x & x + a \end{vmatrix} = 0.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m We will use the cofactor expansion along the first row to find the determinant.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The determinant of a 3x3 matrix \(\begin{vmatrix} a & b & c \\ d & e & f \\ g & h & i \end{vmatrix}\) can be computed as:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \text{det} = a \cdot \text{cofactor}(e, f, i) - b \cdot \text{cofactor}(d, e, i) + c \cdot \text{cofactor}(d, e, f).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m For our matrix, the cofactors are calculated as follows:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \text{cofactor}(e, f, i) = \begin{vmatrix} x + a & x \\ x & x + a \end{vmatrix},
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \text{cofactor}(d, e, i) = \begin{vmatrix} x & x \\ x & x + a \end{vmatrix} = x(x + a) - x \cdot x = a x + x^2 - x^2 = a x,
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \text{cofactor}(d, e, f) = \begin{vmatrix} x & x \\ x & x + a \end{vmatrix} = x(x + a) - x \cdot x = a x^2.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Given the matrix:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \begin{vmatrix} x + a & x  & x \\ x & x + a & x \\ x & x & x + a \end{vmatrix},
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m we evaluate the determinant as:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \text{det} = (x + a) \begin{vmatrix} x + a & x \\ x & x + a \end{vmatrix} - x \begin{vmatrix} x & x \\ x & x + a \end{vmatrix} + x \begin{vmatrix} x & x \\ x & x + a \end{vmatrix}.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Now we compute each of these determinants separately:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \begin{vmatrix} x + a & x \\ x & x + a \end{vmatrix} = (x + a)(x + a) - (x)(x) = x^2 + 2ax + a^2 - x^2 = 2ax + a^2.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \begin{vmatrix} x & x \\ x & x + a \end{vmatrix} = x(x + a) - x(x) = x^2 + ax - x^2 = ax.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \begin{vmatrix} x & x \\ x & x + a \end{vmatrix} = x(x + a) - x(x) = x^2 + ax - x^2 = ax.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Substituting these back into the determinant expression, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \text{det} = (x + a)(2ax + a^2) - x(ax) + x(ax).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Simplify each term:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m (x + a)(2ax + a^2) = 2ax^2 + ax^3 + 2a^3x + a^2a = 2ax^2 + ax^3 + 2a^3x + a^3,
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m -x(ax) = -ax^2,
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m x(ax) = ax^2.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Combine these terms:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \text{det} = (2ax^2 + ax^3 + 2a^3x + a^2a) - ax^2 + ax^2 = 2ax^2 + ax^3 + 2a^3x + a^2a - ax^2 + ax^2 = a^3x + 2a^3x + 2a^3x = 3a^3x.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Thus, the determinant is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \boxed{3a^3x}.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m [Ground Truth]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m -\frac{a}{3}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
