[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ 2x + \frac{1}{2}x + 2(1 + x) = 29 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m First, simplify the expression inside the parentheses:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ 2x + \frac{1}{2}x + 2 + 2x \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Combine like terms:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ 2x + \frac{1}{2}x + 2x + 2 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ 4x + \frac{1}{2}x + 2 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ \left(4 + \frac{1}{2}\right)x + 2 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ \frac{8}{2}x + \frac{1}{2}x + 2 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ \frac{9}{2}x + 2 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Now the equation becomes:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ \frac{9}{2}x + 2 = 29 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Next, isolate the term with \(x\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ \frac{9}{2}x = 29 - 2 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ \frac{9}{2}x = 27 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Convert the right side to a fraction with a common denominator:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ \frac{9}{2}x = \frac{54}{2} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Now solve for \(x\) by eliminating the fraction by multiplying both sides by the reciprocal of \(\frac{9}{2}\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ x = \frac{54}{2} \times \frac{2}{9} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ x = \frac{54 \times 2}{2 \times 9} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ x = \frac{108}{18} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ x = 6 \]
