[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To simplify the expression \(\sqrt[4]{2^7 \cdot 3^3}\), we will use the property of roots that \(\sqrt[n]{x \cdot y} = \sqrt[n]{x} \cdot \sqrt[n]{y}\). Here, \(n = 4\), \(x = 2^7 \cdot 3^3\), and \(y = 1\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m First, we distribute the fourth root to each factor in the expression:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \sqrt[4]{2^7 \cdot 3^3} = \sqrt[4]{2^7} \cdot \sqrt[4]{3^3}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Next, we simplify each fourth root individually. We know that \(\sqrt[4]{2^7} = 2^{7/4}\) because \(4\) is half of \(16\). Similarly, \(\sqrt[4]{3^3} = 3^{3/4}\). Therefore, we have:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \sqrt[4]{2^7 \cdot 3^3} = 2^{7/4} \cdot 3^{3/4}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Now, we observe that \(2^{7/4} = \sqrt[4]{2^7}\). We need to express \(3^{3/4}\) in a form that relates it to \(\sqrt[4]{2^7 \cdot 3^3}\). Notice that \(3^{3/4}\) can be written as \(\sqrt[4]{3^3}\). Thus, we can rewrite the expression as:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \sqrt[4]{2^7 \cdot 3^3} = \sqrt[4]{2^7} \cdot \sqrt[4]{3^3}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m This matches the form \(a \sqrt[4]{b}\) where \(a = \sqrt[4]{2^7}\) and \(b = 3^3\). However, we are asked to express the result in the form \(a \sqrt[4]{b}\), and since we have already simplified to:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2^{7/4} \cdot 3^{3/4} = \sqrt[4]{2^7 \cdot 3^3}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m It is clear that \(a = \sqrt[4]{2^7}\) and \(b = 3^3 = 27\). Therefore, \(a + b = \sqrt[4]{2^7} + 27 = 7 + 27 = 34\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Thus, the final answer is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
