[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The median of the set of numbers $\{$12, 38, 45, $x$, 14$\}$ is five less than the mean. If $x$ is a negative integer, what is the value of $x$?
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To solve the problem, we need to determine the value of \( x \) such that the median of the set \(\{12, 38, 45, x, 14\}\) is five less than the mean.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m ### Step 1: Calculate the Mean
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m First, recall the formula for the mean of a set of numbers:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \text{Mean} = \frac{\text{Sum of all elements}}{\text{Number of elements}}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Given the numbers:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 12, 38, 45, x, 14
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The number of elements is 5. Therefore, the mean is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \text{Mean} = \frac{12 + 38 + 45 + x + 14}{5}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m ### Step 2: Use the Median Formula
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The median of a set is the middle number when the numbers are arranged in increasing order. For a set with 5 elements:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \text{Median} = \begin{cases} 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \text{4th element} & \text{if } n \= \text{odd} \\
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m (\text{3rd element} + \text{4th element}) / 2 & \text{if } n \= \text{even} \\
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \end{cases}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
