[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Given that the gumball machine makes 15 lacers and each lacer corresponds to 0.01 liters of lemonade, we can calculate the total volume of lemonade as follows:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. Identify the number of lacers and the volume of each lacer.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. Multiply the number of lacers by the volume of each lacer to get the total volume.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3. Convert the volume from liters to milliliters (1 liter = 1000 milliliters).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
