[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Simplify the following: $(2y-1)\cdot(4y^{10}+2y^9+4y^8+2y^7).$  Express your answer as a polynomial with the degrees of the terms in decreasing order.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To simplify the expression \((2y-1)(4y^{10}+2y^9+4y^8+2y^7)\), we will use the distributive property (also known as the FOIL method for binomials) to multiply each term in the first polynomial by each term in the second polynomial. Here are the steps:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. Distribute \(2y\) to each term in the second polynomial.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. Distribute \(-1\) to each term in the second polynomial.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Let's do this step by step:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m (2y-1)(4y^{10}+2y^9+4y^8+2y^7) = 2y \cdot (4y^{10}+2y^9+4y^8+2y^7) - 1 \cdot (4y^{10}+2y^9+4y^8+2y^7)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m First, distribute \(2y\) inside the first polynomial:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2y \cdot (4y^{10}+2y^9+4y^8+2y^7) = 2y \cdot 4y^{10} + 2y \cdot 2y^9 + 2y \cdot 4y^8 + 2y \cdot 2y^7
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m = 8y^{11} + 4y^{10} + 8y^9 + 4y^{12}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Next, distribute \(-1\) outside the first polynomial:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m -1 \cdot (4y^{10}+2y^9+4y^8+2y^7) = -1 \cdot 4y^{10} - 1 \cdot 2y^9 - 1 \cdot 4y^8 - 1 \cdot 2y^7
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m = -4y^{10} - 2y^9 - 4y^8 - 2y^7
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Now, combine all the terms from the distributions:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 8y^{11} + 4y^{10} + 8y^9 + 4y^{12} - 4y^{10} - 2y^9 - 2y^7
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Combine like terms:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 8y^{12} + (4y^{10} - 4y^{10}) + (8y^9 - 2y^9) - 2y^7
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m = 8y^{12} + 6y^9 - 2y^7
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m So, the simplified polynomial is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \boxed{8y^{12}+6y^9-2y^7}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
