[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To convert the decimal number \(123_{10}\) to its base four equivalent, we need to repeatedly divide the number by 4 and keep track of the remainders. The remainders, read in reverse order, will give us the base four representation.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Here are the steps:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. Divide 123 by 4:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    123 \div 4 = 30 \text{ remainder } 3
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    So, the least significant digit (rightmost digit) is 3.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. Divide the quotient 30 by 4:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    30 \div 4 = 7 \text{ remainder } 2
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    So, the next digit is 2.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3. Divide the quotient 7 by 4:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    7 \div 4 = 1 \text{ remainder } 3
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    So, the next digit is 3.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 4. Divide the quotient 1 by 4:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    1 \div 4 = 0 \text{ remainder } 1
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    So, the most significant digit (leftmost digit) is 1.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Now, we collect all the remainders from the last division to the first:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \{1, 3, 2, 3\}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Thus, the base four equivalent of \(123_{10}\) is \(\boxed{1323_4}\).<|endoftext|>
