[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m First, we calculate the \( x \)-coordinate of the vertex:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ x = -\frac{b}{2a} = -\frac{12}{2 \cdot 1} = -\frac{12}{2} = -6 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Now that we have the \( x \)-coordinate, we can find the \( y \)-coordinate by substituting \( x = -6 \) back into the equation:
