[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To find the least positive integer that is divisible by three distinct prime numbers, we need to find the smallest integer that can be divided by 2, 3, and 5.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. Start with the smallest prime numbers available, which are 2, 3, and 5.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \begin{aligned}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    2 &= 2 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    3 &= 3 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    5 &= 5 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \end{aligned}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. Multiply these smallest prime numbers together to get:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    2 \times 3 \times 5
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3. Perform the multiplication:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    2 \times 3 = 6 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    6 \times 5 = 30
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 4. Therefore, the least positive integer that is divisible by three distinct prime numbers is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \boxed{30}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
