[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To find the sum of the first 10 odd positive integers, we can use the formula for the sum of the first \( n \) odd integers. The sum of the first \( n \) odd integers is given by:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ S_n = n^2 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Here, \( n = 10 \). Plugging in the value of \( n \), we get:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
