[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To find the largest perfect square factor of \(1512\), we need to follow these steps:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. **Find the prime factorization of \(1512\)**:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \(1512\) is an even number, so it is divisible by \(2\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    1512 \div 2 = 756
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \(756\) is also divisible by \(2\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    756 \div 2 = 378
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \(378\) is also divisible by \(2\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    378 \div 2 = 189
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \(189\) is divisible by \(3\) (since \(2 + 9 = 11\), and \(11\) is a prime number):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    189 \div 3 = 63
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \(63\) is also divisible by \(3\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    63 \div 3 = 21
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \(21\) is also divisible by \(3\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    21 \div 3 = 7
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \(7\) is also a prime number.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    Therefore, the prime factorization of \(1512\) is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    1512 = 2^3 \times 3^3 \times 7
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. **Identify the largest perfect square factor**:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    A perfect square has all prime factors with even exponents. From the factorization \(1512 = 2^3 \times 3^3 \times 7\), we can see that the exponent of \(3\) is already even (3 itself). Therefore, the largest perfect square factor is obtained by removing the exponent of \(3\) from the exponents of all other prime factors.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    Removing \(3\) from \(3^3\), the exponents become \(3 - 1 = 2\). The exponents of all other primes are \(0\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    Thus, the largest perfect square factor is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    2^0 \times 3^2 \times 7^0
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3. **Calculate the perfect square factor**:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    2^0 \times 3^2 \times 7^0 = 1 \times 9 \times 1 = 9
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Therefore, the largest perfect square factor of \(1512\) is \(\boxed{9}\).<|endoftext|>
