[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m In how many ways can I stack 5 different books on a shelf?
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To determine the number of ways to stack 5 different books on a shelf, we need to calculate the number of permutations of 5 distinct objects. The number of permutations of \( n \) distinct objects is given by \( n! \) (n factorial), which is the product of all positive integers up to \( n \).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m In this case, we have 5 different books, so \( n = 5 \). Therefore, we need to calculate \( 5! \):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 5! = 5 \times 4 \times 3 \times 2 \times 1
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Let's compute this step by step:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 5 \times 4 = 20
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 20 \times 3 = 60
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 60 \times 2 = 120
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 120 \times 1 = 120
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Thus, the number of ways to stack 5 different books on a shelf is \(\boxed{120}\).<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m [Ground Truth]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 120
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
