[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To find the area of the parallelogram generated by the vectors \(\mathbf{a} = \begin{pmatrix} 3 \\ 1 \\ -2 \end{pmatrix}\) and \(\mathbf{b} = \begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ -3 \\ 4 \end{pmatrix}\), we can use the determinant of the matrix formed by these vectors. The area of the parallelogram is given by the absolute value of the determinant of the matrix:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \text{Area} = \left| \det \begin{pmatrix} 3 & 1 \\ 1 & -3 \end{pmatrix} \right|
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m First, we calculate the determinant:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \det \begin{pmatrix} 3 & 1 \\ 1 & -3 \end{pmatrix} = (3)(-3) - (1)(1) = -9 - 1 = -10
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The absolute value of this determinant is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \left| \det \begin{pmatrix} 3 & 1 \\ 1 & -3 \end{pmatrix} \right| = |-10| = 10
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Therefore, the area of the parallelogram is \(\boxed{10}\).<|endoftext|>
