[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m This is true, so our assumption is consistent. Now, we need to solve for \( x \). From the first equation:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m d = \frac{\log_{12}{162}}{12}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Since \( \log_{12}{162} = \log_{12}{(2 \cdot 3^4)} = 2 \log_{12}{2} + \log_{12}{3^4} = 2 \log_{12}{2} + 8 \log_{12}{3} \), we get:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
