[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Using the property of logarithms that \( d = \frac{\log_{12}{x^{\log_{12}{x}}}}{\log_{12}{x}} = \log_{12}{x^{\log_{12}{x}}}/\log_{12}{x} = \log_{12}{x^{1/\log_{12}{x}}}/\log_{12}{x} = \log_{12}{x^{1/\log_{12}{x}} / \log_{12}{12}} = \log_{12}{(x^{1/\log_{12}{x}} / \log_{12}{12}} / \log_{12}{12}} = \log_{12}{x^{1/\log_{12}{x}} / \log_{12}{12}} = \log_{12}{x^{1/\log_{12}{x}} / \log_{12}{12}} = \log_{12}{x^{1/\log_{12}{x}} / \log_{12}{12}}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m So, the common difference is \( \log_{12}{x^{\log_{12}{x}}}/\log_{12}{12} = \log_{12}{x^{1/\log_{12}{x}} / \log_{12}{12}} \).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Now, we can find \( x \) by solving:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \log_{12}{x} = \log_{12}{162} + \log_{12}{x^{\log_{12}{x} - 1}} / \log_{12}{12} = \log_{12}{162} + \frac{\log_{12}{x^{\log_{12}{x} - 1}}}{\log_{12}{12}} = \log_{12}{162} + \frac{\log_{12}{(x-1)(ln{x})}}{\log_{12}{12}} = \log_{12}{162} + (x-1)(\log_{12}{x} - \log_{12}{12})
