[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. **Express the fractional part as a fraction:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - The decimal \(0.24\) can be written as \(\frac{24}{100}\) by moving the decimal point two places to the right.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - Simplify the fraction \(\frac{24}{100}\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3. **Simplify the fraction \(\frac{24}{100}\):**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - The greatest common divisor (GCD) of 24 and 100 is 4.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - Divide both the numerator and the denominator by their GCD:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      \[
