[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To solve the problem, we need to evaluate the expressions \(7@4\) and \(4@7\) using the given operation \(x@y = xy - 2x\). Then, we will subtract the result of \(4@7\) from \(7@4\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m First, let's evaluate \(7@4\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 7@4 = 7 \cdot 4 - 2 \cdot 7 = 28 - 14 = 14
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Next, let's evaluate \(4@7\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 4@7 = 4 \cdot 7 - 2 \cdot 4 = 28 - 8 = 20
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Now, we need to find the value of \((7@4) - (4@7)\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 7@4 - 4@7 = 14 - 20 = -6
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Therefore, the value of \((7@4) - (4@7)\) is \(\boxed{-6}\).<|endoftext|>
