[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To solve the system of equations, we will go through each equation step by step.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The equations are:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. \( c + o = u \)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. \( u + n = t \)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3. \( t + c = s \)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 4. \( o + n + s = 12 \)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m We can start by expressing \( u \), \( t \), \( s \), and \( n \) in terms of \( o \) and integers.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m First, from equation 1:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ t = c + o \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Next, from equation 3:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ s = o + n \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m We can substitute \( t \) from the first equation into the second and fourth equations:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ u = c + o \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ o + n + s = 12 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Substitute \( t \) and \( s \) from the first equation and the second equation above into the fourth equation:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ c + o + o + n + (o + n) = 12 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ c + 2o + 2n = 12 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ c + 2o + 2n = 12 \]  \quad \text{(Equation 5)}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Let's express \( n \) from Equation 1:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ n = u - o \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Now substitute \( n \) from Equation 1 into Equation 5:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ c + 2o + 2(u - o) = 12 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ c + 2o + 2u - 2o = 12 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ c + 2u = 12 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ c + 2u = 12 \]  \quad \text{(Equation 6)}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Now we know:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ t = c + o \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ s = o + n = o + (u - o) = u \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m We can use the third equation \( t + c = s \) to solve for \( t \):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ t + c = t \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ c = 0 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m From Equation 6:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ t = c + o = 0 + o = o \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m So, \( t = o \).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Now substitute \( s \) from Equation 5 and \( t = o \) back into the fourth equation:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ o + n + s = 12 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ o + (u - o) + u = 12 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ o + u - o + u = 12 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ 2u = 12 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ u = 6 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Since \( s = u \), we have:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ s = 6 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Now substitute \( u = 6 \), \( t = o \), and \( s = 6 \) back into the third equation:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ 0 + n + 6 = 12 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ n = 6 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m So, \( n = 6 \).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m We have:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ o = t = 0 \]
