[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m An isosceles right triangle is removed from each corner of a square piece of paper, as shown, to create a rectangle. If $AB = 12$ units, what is the combined area of the four removed triangles, in square units? [asy]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m unitsize(5mm);
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m defaultpen(linewidth(.7pt)+fontsize(8pt));
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m pair A=(1,4), Ap=(0,3), B=(3,0), Bp=(4,1);
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m draw((0,0)--(0,4)--(4,4)--(4,0)--cycle);
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m draw(A--Ap--B--Bp--cycle,linetype("4 3"));
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m label("$A$",A,N);
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m label("$B$",B,S);
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m [/asy]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To determine the combined area of the four removed triangles, we need to analyze the geometry of the problem. We start by identifying the side length of the original square and the side length of the removed triangles.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Given:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - \( AB = 12 \) units, which is the length of one side of the original square.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - The original square has all sides of length 12 units.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The isosceles right triangle that is removed from each corner consists of two right triangles on top and two right triangles at the bottom. Each right triangle has legs that are \(\frac{\sqrt{2}}{2}\) times the length of the square's side length. Therefore, the legs of each triangle are:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ \frac{\sqrt{2}}{2} \times 12 = 6\sqrt{2} \text{ units} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The area of one of the right triangles is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ \frac{1}{2} \times \left( \frac{\sqrt{2}}{2} \times 12 \right)^2 = \frac{1}{2} \times \left( \frac{12\sqrt{2}}{2} \right)^2 = \frac{1}{2} \times (6\sqrt{2})^2 = \frac{1}{2} \times 72 = 36 \text{ square units} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Since there are four such triangles, the total area of the four removed triangles is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ 4 \times 36 = 144 \text{ square units} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Thus, the combined area of the four removed triangles is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ \boxed{144} \]<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
