[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To find out how much Sarah spent on the sweatshirt, we first need to calculate the total cost of the t-shirts and then subtract that from the total amount spent. Here's the step-by-step reasoning:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. Calculate the cost of the two t-shirts:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \text{Cost of two t-shirts} = 2 \times 15.22 = 30.44 \text{ dollars}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. Subtract the cost of the t-shirts from the total amount spent to find the cost of the sweatshirt:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \text{Cost of sweatshirt} = 67.94 - 30.44 = 37.50 \text{ dollars}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Therefore, the cost of the sweatshirt is \(\boxed{37.50}\).<|endoftext|>
