[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m A circle is circumscribed around $ABCD$ as follows: [asy]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m pair pA, pB, pC, pD, pO;
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m pO = (0, 0);
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m pA = pO + dir(-40);
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m pB = pO + dir(40);
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m pC = pO + dir(130);
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m pD = pO + dir(190);
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m draw(pA--pB--pC--pA);
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m draw(pA--pD--pC--pA);
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m label("$A$", pA, SE);
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m label("$B$", pB, NE);
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m label("$C$", pC, NW);
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m label("$D$", pD, SW);
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m draw(circle(pO, 1));
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m label("$30^\circ$", pA + dir(150) * .45);
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m label("$40^\circ$", pC + dir(-20) * .35);
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m [/asy] How many degrees are in $\angle CAB + \angle ACD$?
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m A circle is circumscribed around the (unmodified) triangle \(ABCD\). The angles of the triangle at \(B\) and \(C\) are both \(40^\circ\), and the angle at \(A\) is \(30^\circ\). Thus, \(\angle BAD = 180^\circ - \angle ABD - \angle CAO\). Since \(\angle CAO = 40^\circ-\angle CAB\) and \(\angle CAO = 40^\circ - \angle ACD\), we have:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \angle BAD = 180^\circ - \angle ABD - (40^\circ - \angle ACD) = 140^\circ - \angle ABD - \angle ACD
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m We need to determine \(\angle CAB + \angle ACD\). 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m First, observe that:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \angle BAD = 140^\circ - (\angle ABD + \angle ACD)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Because \(ABCD\) lies inside the circle, we have:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \angle ABD + \angle ACD = 180^\circ - \angle B - \angle C
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m From the given angles:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \angle B = 180^\circ - \angle ABD - \angle CAO \implies \angle B = 180^\circ - \angle ABD - (40^\circ - \angle ACD) = \angle ACD + 140^\circ - \angle ABD
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Since \(\angle ABD + \angle ACD = 180^\circ - \angle B\):
