[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    1 = 1 + \text{height}^2
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \text{height}^2 = 0
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \text{height} = 0 \text{ meters}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    This indicates an error in interpretation. The height of the three shaded regions must be the hypotenuse of a right triangle with radius of the semicircle as one leg and the full radius as the other leg. So, the hypotenuse is 2 meters (1 + 1).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    Thus, we re-define the height calculation as:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    2^2 = 1^2 + \text{height}^2 \rightarrow 4 = 1 + \text{height}^2
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \text{height}^2 = 3 \rightarrow \text{height} = \sqrt{3} \approx 1.732 \text{ meters}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. **Calculate the area of the three congruent regions:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    The three congruent regions are right isosceles trapezions. Each trapezoid has an area equal to half of the area of the semicircle (since the area of each sector is \(\frac{1}{2} \times \text{area of semicircle} = \frac{1}{2} \times \pi \times 1^2 = \frac{\pi}{2}\)).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    Since there are three such regions (each with an area of \(\frac{\pi}{2}\)), the total area is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    3 \times \frac{\pi}{2} = \frac{3\pi}{2} \approx 4.712 \text{ square meters}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3. **Calculate the area of the entire trapezoid:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    The area of the entire trapezoid is the same as the sum of the areas of the three congruent trapezoids. Since each trapezoid has an area of \(\frac{\pi}{2}\), the total area of the trapezoid is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \frac{3\pi}{2} \approx 4.712
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The final answer is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \boxed{4.7}
