[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Given the matrix:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m A = \begin{pmatrix} \cos 1 & \cos 2 & \cos 3 \\ \cos 4 & \cos 5 & \cos 6 \\ \cos 7 & \cos 8 & \cos 9 \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The determinant of a 3x3 matrix can be computed as follows:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \text{det}(A) = a(ei− fh) − b(di− fg) + c(dh− eg)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Where:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - \(a = \cos 1\), \(b = \cos 2\), \(c = \cos 3\)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - \(d = \cos 4\), \(e = \cos 5\), \(f = \cos 6\)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - \(g = \cos 7\), \(h = \cos 8\), \(i = \cos 9\)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Applying this formula to our matrix:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \text{det}(A) = \cos 1 (\cos 5 \cdot \cos 9 - \cos 6 \cdot \cos 8) - \cos 2 (\cos 4 \cdot \cos 9 - \cos 6 \cdot \cos 7) + \cos 3 (\cos 4 \cdot \cos 8 - \cos 5 \cdot \cos 7)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Now let's compute the individual calculations step by step using Python to ensure accuracy.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m ```python
