[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m What is the ones digit of $7^{35}$ when written as an integer?
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To determine the ones digit of \(7^{35}\) when written as an integer, we need to find the value of \(7^{35} \mod 10\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m First, observe that \(7^1 = 7\) has a ones digit of 7.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[7^2 = 49 \equiv 9 \mod 10\]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[7^3 = 7 \times 9 = 63 \equiv 3 \mod 10\]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[7^4 = 7 \times 3 = 21 \equiv 1 \mod 10\]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[7^5 = 7 \times 1 = 7 \mod 10\]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m We observe that the powers of 7 repeat every 4 terms in modulo 10. To identify which term in the cycle corresponds to \(7^{35}\), we note that:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[35 \div 4 = 8 \text{ remainder } 3\]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[35 \equiv 3 \mod 4\]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m This means that \(7^{35}\) has the same ones digit as \(7^3\), which is 3.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Therefore, the ones digit of \(7^{35}\) is \(\boxed{3}\).<|endoftext|>
