[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To evaluate \(\left| (12 - 9i)(8 + 15i) \right| \), we will follow these steps:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. **Multiply the complex numbers:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    (12 - 9i)(8 + 15i)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    Use the distributive property (FOIL method):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    (12 \cdot 8) + (12 \cdot 15i) + (-9i \cdot 8) + (-9i \cdot 15i)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    Calculate each term:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    96 + 180i - 72i - 135i^2
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    Combine the real parts and the imaginary parts:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    (96 - 135) + (180 - 72)i
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    Simplify the real part:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    -39 + 108i
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. **Find the magnitude of the resulting complex number:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    The magnitude of a complex number \(a + bi\) is given by:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \left| a + bi \right| = \sqrt{a^2 + b^2}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    For our complex number \(-39 + 108i\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \left| -39 + 108i \right| = \sqrt{(-39)^2 + (108)^2}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    Calculate the squares:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    (-39)^2 = 1521
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    (108)^2 = 11664
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    Add the squares:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    1521 + 11664 = 13185
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    Take the square root:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \sqrt{13185}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    Simplify the square root:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \sqrt{13185} \approx 114.72
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Therefore, the magnitude of the complex number \((12 - 9i)(8 + 15i)\) is \(\boxed{114.72}\).<|endoftext|>
