[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m In triangle $BCD$, $\angle C = 90^\circ$, $CD = 3$, and $BD = \sqrt{13}$. What is $\tan B$?
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To find \(\tan B\), we start by noting that since \(\triangle BCD\) is a right triangle with \(\angle C = 90^\circ\) and \(\angle B = 90^\circ - \angle C\), \(\triangle BCD\) is a 45-45-90 triangle. In a right triangle with 45-degree angles, the legs are equal in length. Therefore, since \(CD = 3\), it follows that \(BD = CD = 3\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m We need to find \(\tan B\). Since \(BD = 3\) and \(CD = 3\), the ratio \(\frac{CD}{BD}\) is \(\frac{3}{3} = 1\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m In a right triangle, the tangent of an angle is the ratio of the length of the opposite side to the length of the adjacent side. For \(\triangle BCD\), the adjacent side is \(CD = 3\) and the opposite side is \(BD = 3\). Therefore, \(\tan B = \frac{\text{opposite}}{\text{adjacent}} = \frac{3}{3} = 1\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m So, the value of \(\tan B\) is \(\boxed{1}\).<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m [Ground Truth]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \frac{3}{2}
