[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Let
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[\bold{A} = \begin{pmatrix} 0 & 1 & 2 \\ 1 & 0 & 1 \\ 2 & 1 & 0 \end{pmatrix}.\]There exist constants $p$, $q$, and $r$ such that
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[\bold{A}^3 + p \bold{A}^2 + q \bold{A} + r \bold{I} = \bold{0},\]where $\bold{I}$ and $\bold{0}$ are the $3 \times 3$ identity matrix and zero matrix, respectively.  Enter the ordered triple $(p,q,r).$
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To determine the constants \( p \), \( q \), and \( r \) in the equation \(\mathbf{A}^3 + p \mathbf{A}^2 + q \mathbf{A} + r \mathbf{I} = \mathbf{0}\), we start by finding the characteristic polynomial of the matrix \(\mathbf{A}\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The characteristic polynomial \(\det(\mathbf{A} - \lambda \mathbf{I}) = 0\) is given by:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \det\begin{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m p & q & r \\ 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m q & p & r \\ 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m r & q & p 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \end{pmatrix}.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Expanding this determinant, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m p\begin{vmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m p & r \\ 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m r & p 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \end{vmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - q \begin{vmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m q & r \\ 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m r & p 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \end{vmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m + r \begin{vmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m q & p \\ 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m r & q 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \end{vmatrix}.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Calculating the 2x2 determinants, we have:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m p(p^2 - r^2), \quad -q(q^2 - r^2), \quad qr(p - q).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m This simplifies to:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m p(p^2 - r^2) - q(q^2 - r^2) - qr(p - q) = p(p^2 - r^2) - q(p^2 - r^2) - qr(p - q).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Factoring out \((p^2 - r^2)\), we get:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m (p^2 - r^2)(p - q - q) = (p^2 - r^2)(p - 2q).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Thus, the characteristic polynomial is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \det(\mathbf{A} - \lambda \mathbf{I}) = (p^2 - r^2)(p - 2q).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Setting this equal to the zero polynomial, we have:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m (p^2 - r^2)(p - 2q) = 0.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m This gives us two separate equations:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m p^2 - r^2 = 0 \quad \text{and} \quad p - 2q = 0.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m From \(p^2 - r^2 = 0\), we get:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m (p - r)(p + r) = 0.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Thus, \(p = r\) or \(p = -r\). From \(p - 2q = 0\), we get:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m p = 2q.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m If \(p = r = 0\), then \(\mathbf{A} = \begin{pmatrix} 0 & 1 & 2 \\ 1 & 0 & 1 \\ 2 & 1 & 0 \end{pmatrix}\) and:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \mathbf{A}^2 = \begin{pmatrix} 0 & 1 & 2 \\ 1 & 0 & 1 \\ 2 & 1 & 0 \end{pmatrix} \begin{pmatrix} 0 & 1 & 2 \\ 1 & 0 & 1 \\ 2 & 1 & 0 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 5 & 3 & 0 \\ 3 & 5 & 0 \\ 0 & 0 & 1 \end{pmatrix},
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m p \mathbf{A} = [0][0] + [0][0] + [0][0] = \begin{pmatrix} 0 \\ 0 \\ 0 \end{pmatrix},
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m q \mathbf{A} = [0][0] + [1][0] + [0][0] = \begin{pmatrix} 0 \\ 0 \\ 0 \end{pmatrix},
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m r \mathbf{I} = [0][0] + [0][0] + [0][0] = \begin{pmatrix} 0 \\ 0 \\ 0 \end{pmatrix}.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Thus, the equation becomes:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \begin{pmatrix} 5 & 3 & 0 \\ 3 & 5 & 0 \\ 0 & 0 & 1 \end{pmatrix} + [0] + [0] + [0] + [0] = \begin{pmatrix} 5 & 3 & 0 \\ 3 & 5 & 0 \\ 0 & 0 & 1 \end{pmatrix}.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m This is satisfied, so \(p = 0\), \(q = 0\), and \(r = 0\) is a solution. If \(p = r = 2q\), then:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \mathbf{A}^2 = \begin{pmatrix} 3^2 & 0 & 2 \cdot 2 \cdot 2 \\ 0 & 2 \cdot 3 & 2 \cdot 2 \\ 2 \cdot 2 & 2 \cdot 3 & 0 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 9 & 0 & 8 \\ 0 & 6 & 4 \\ 4 & 6 & 0 \end{pmatrix},
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m p \mathbf{A} = [2][0] + [2][0] + [2][0] = \begin{pmatrix} 0 \\ 0 \\ 0 \end{pmatrix},
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m q \mathbf{A} = [2][0] + [2][0] + [2][0] = \begin{pmatrix} 0 \\ 0 \\ 0 \end{pmatrix},
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m r \mathbf{I} = [2][0] + [2][0] + [2][0] = \begin{pmatrix} 0 \\ 0 \\ 0 \end{pmatrix}.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Thus, the equation becomes:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \begin{pmatrix} 3^2 & 0 & 8 \\ 0 & 6 & 4 \\ 4 & 6 & 0 \end{pmatrix} + [0] + [0] + [0] + [0] = \begin{pmatrix} 3^2 & 0 & 8 \\ 0 & 6 & 4 \\ 4 & 6 & 0 \end{pmatrix}.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m This is satisfied, so \(p = 2q, q = 2r, r = 0\) is another solution. The solution set of the homogeneous system is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \boxed{(0, 0, 0), (2, 0, 0), (0, 2, 0)},
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m where \((p, q, r) = (0, 0, 0), (2, 0, 0), (0, 2, 0)\).<|endoftext|>
