[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To find the magnitude (or modulus) of the complex number \((3 + \sqrt{7}i)^3\), we can use the property of the magnitude of a complex number raised to a power. The magnitude of a complex number \(a + bi\) is given by \(\sqrt{a^2 + b^2}\). Therefore, the magnitude of \((3 + \sqrt{7}i)^3\) is \(3^3 + (\sqrt{7}i)^3\), where \((\sqrt{7}i)^3\) is the product of three \(\sqrt{7}i\) terms. Let's break this down step by step.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. Calculate \(3^3\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3^3 = 27
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. Calculate \((\sqrt{7}i)^3\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m (\sqrt{7}i)^3 = (\sqrt{7}i)^2 \cdot \sqrt{7}i = (\sqrt{7})^2 \cdot i^2 \cdot \sqrt{7}i = 7 \cdot (-1) \cdot i^2 \cdot \sqrt{7}i = 7 \cdot (-1) \cdot -1 \cdot \sqrt{7} \cdot i^2 = 7 \cdot \sqrt{7} \cdot (-1) = 7 \cdot (-\sqrt{7}) = (-7\sqrt{7})
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3. Add \(27\) and \(-7\sqrt{7}\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 27 + (-7\sqrt{7}) = 27 - 7\sqrt{7}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m So, the magnitude of \((3 + \sqrt{7}i)^3\) is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \boxed{27 - 7\sqrt{7}}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m [Ground Truth]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 64
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m [Is Boxed Matched]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m True
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m [Extracted Answer]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 27-7\sqrt{7}
