[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m A regular hexagon of side length 1 is placed vertically along one of its edges on a flat surface.  A particle is fired from the surface and passes through four of the vertices of the hexagon, as shown below, tracing the arc of a parabola.  If the particle starts at $A$ and ends at $B,$ then find the length $AB.$
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m [asy]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m unitsize(1.5 cm);
