[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To find the magnitude (absolute value) of \[\left|\left(1 + \sqrt{3}i\right)^4\right|\], we can use the property of magnitudes and angles in a complex number. The magnitude of a complex number \( z = a + bi \) is given by \( |z| = \sqrt{a^2 + b^2} \).
