[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To find the remainder when \(2000 + 2001 + 2002 + 2003 + 2004 + 2005 + 2006\) is divided by \(7\), we can simplify the calculation by first finding the sum of the digits and then using that to find the remainder of each individual digit when divided by \(7\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m First, let's find the sum of the digits of each number:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2000 = 20 \times 100
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2001 = 20 \times 100 + 10
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2002 = 20 \times 100 + 2
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2003 = 20 \times 100 + 3
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2004 = 20 \times 100 + 4
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2005 = 20 \times 100 + 5
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2006 = 20 \times 100 + 6
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Now, let's add these sums together:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2000 + 2001 + 2002 + 2003 + 2004 + 2005 + 2006
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m = 20 \times 100 + (100 + 10 + 2 + 3 + 4 + 5 + 6)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m = 20 \times 100 + (10 + 10 + 2 + 3 + 4 + 5 + 6)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m = 20 \times 100 + 1 + (1 + 2 + 3 + 4 + 5 + 6)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m = 20 \times 100 + 1 + 9
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m = 20 \times 100 + 10
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m = 2000 + 10
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m = 2010
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Now, we need to find the remainder when \(2010\) is divided by \(7\). We can do this by dividing \(2010\) by \(7\) and finding the remainder:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2010 \div 7 = 288 \text{ remainder } 6
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Thus, the remainder when \(2000 + 2001 + 2002 + 2003 + 2004 + 2005 + 2006\) is divided by \(7\) is \(\boxed{6}\).<|endoftext|>
