[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m A magician designed an unfair coin so that the probability of getting a Head on a flip is $60\%$. If he flips the coin three times, what is the probability that he flips more Heads than Tails? Express your answer as a common fraction.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To determine the probability that a magician flipping a coin three times will flip more heads than tails, we first need to understand the probability distribution of the number of heads. Given that the probability of getting a Head on a flip is \(60\%\), the probability of getting a Tail is \(20\%\). We can identify these probabilities and calculate the probabilities of getting exactly \(0\) heads, exactly \(1\) head, and exactly \(2\) heads.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. **Calculate the probability of getting exactly 0 heads:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    P(0 \text{ Heads}) = \left(\frac{60}{100}\right) \left(\frac{20}{100}\right) \left(\frac{60}{100}\right) = \left(\frac{1}{10}\right)^2 \left(\frac{2}{5}\right) = \frac{1 \cdot 2}{10 \cdot 5} = \frac{2}{50} = \frac{1}{25}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. **Calculate the probability of getting exactly 1 head:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    P(1 \text{ Head}) = \left(\frac{60}{100}\right) \left(\frac{20}{100}\right) \left(\frac{40}{100}\right) + \left(\frac{60}{100}\right) \left(\frac{40}{100}\right) \left(\frac{20}{100}\right) + \left(\frac{20}{100}\right) \left(\frac{40}{100}\right) \left(\frac{20}{100}\right) + \left(\frac{60}{100}\right) \left(\frac{40}{100}\right) \left(\frac{30}{100}\right)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    = \left(\frac{3}{5}\right) \left(\frac{2}{5}\right) + \left(\frac{3}{5}\right) \left(\frac{2}{5}\right) + \left(\frac{1}{5}\right) \left(\frac{2}{5}\right) + \left(\frac{3}{5}\right) \left(\frac{3}{5}\right)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    = \frac{6}{25} + \frac{6}{25} + \frac{2}{25} + \frac{9}{25} = \frac{27}{25}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3. **Calculate the probability of getting exactly 2 heads:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    P(2 \text{ Heads}) = \left(\frac{60}{100}\right)^2 \left(\frac{20}{100}\right) + \left(\frac{60}{100}\right)^2 \left(\frac{40}{100}\right) + \left(\frac{60}{100}\right)^2 \left(\frac{40}{100}\right)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    = \left(\frac{3}{5}\right)^2 + \left(\frac{3}{5}\right)^2 + \left(\frac{3}{5}\right)^2 = 3 \cdot \left(\frac{9}{25}\right) = \frac{27}{25}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Now, to find the probability of getting more heads than tails, we sum the probabilities of getting 1 head:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m P(\text{More than 1 heads}) = P(1 \text{ Head}) + P(2 \text{ Heads}) = \frac{6}{25} + \frac{27}{25} = \frac{33}{25}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Thus, the probability that the magician flips more heads than tails is \(\boxed{\frac{33}{25}}\).<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m [Ground Truth]
