[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To determine the number of terms in the list \( 2.5, 5.5, 8.5, 11.5, \ldots, 80.5, 83.5 \), we can use the formula for the \( n \)-th term of an arithmetic sequence. The general form of the \( n \)-th term of an arithmetic sequence is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m a_n = a_1 + (n-1)d
