[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To determine the remainder when the sum \(1 + 12 + 123 + 1234 + 12345 + 123456 + 1234567 + 12345678\) is divided by 5, we will first find the sum of the numbers and then determine the remainder of that sum when divided by 5.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m First, let's group the numbers into blocks of three digits:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[1234 + 12345 + 12346 + 12347 + 12348\]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Next, we sum each block:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[1234 + 12345 + 12346 + 12347 + 12348 = 1234 + 12345 + 12346 + 12347 + 12348 = 6862\]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Now, we need to find the remainder when 6862 is divided by 5. We do this by performing the division:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[6862 \div 5 = 1372 \text{ R } 2\]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m This means that 6862 is 5 more than a multiple of 5, so the remainder is 2.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Therefore, the remainder when \(1 + 12 + 123 + 1234 + 12345 + 12346 + 12347 + 12348\) is divided by 5 is \(\boxed{2}\).<|endoftext|>
