[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Mark used 0.5 gallon of milk to make 2.5 liters of yoghurt. In order to make richer yoghurt, he doubles the milk he uses. How many liters of milk will Mark need to make 14 liters of richer yoghurt?
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To determine how many liters of milk Mark will need to make 14 liters of richer yoghurt, we first need to understand the conversion rates for milk and yoghurt.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. **Conversion from Liquid Yoghurt to Dry Yogurt:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - Mark starts using 0.5 gallons of milk to make 2.5 liters of yoghurt.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. **Conversion from Dry Yogurt to Richer Yogurt:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - To make richer yoghurt, Mark doubles the amount of milk he uses.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - Therefore, if 0.5 gallons of milk make 2.5 liters of yoghurt, then 1 gallon of milk will make 5 liters of richer yoghurt.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - Since Mark doubles the milk he uses, to make 14 liters of richer yoghurt, he will use twice the amount of milk. 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3. **Calculate the Amount of Milk Needed:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - If 0.5 gallons of milk originally make 2.5 liters of yoghurt, to make 14 liters of yoghurt, the amount of milk required is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      2.5 \text{ liters} \times 2 = 5 \text{ liters}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Thus, Mark will need \boxed{5} liters of milk to make 14 liters of richer yoghurt.<|endoftext|>
