[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To find \( f(g(-5)) \), we need to evaluate the functions step by step.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m First, let's determine \( g(-5) \). The function \( g(x) \) is given by:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ g(x) = 5x + 2x^2 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Substituting \( x = -5 \) into the function \( g(x) \):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ g(-5) = 5(-5) + 2(-5)^2 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ g(-5) = -25 + 2 \cdot 25 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ g(-5) = -25 + 50 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ g(-5) = 25 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Now that we have \( g(-5) = 25 \), we need to evaluate \( f(25) \). The function \( f(x) \) is given by:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ f(x) = 3 - \sqrt{x} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Substituting \( x = 25 \) into the function \( f(x) \):
