[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The partial fraction decomposition of
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[\frac{x^2 - 19}{x^3 - 2x^2 - 5x + 6}\]is
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[\frac{A}{x - 1} + \frac{B}{x + 2} + \frac{C}{x - 3}.\]Find the product $ABC.$
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To find the partial fraction decomposition of \(\frac{x^2 - 19}{x^3 - 2x^2 - 5x + 6}\), we start by setting up the equation:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \frac{x^2 - 19}{x^3 - 2x^2 - 5x + 6} = \frac{A}{x - 1} + \frac{B}{x + 2} + \frac{C}{x - 3}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m First, we combine the right-hand side over a common denominator:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \frac{A}{x - 1} + \frac{B}{x + 2} + \frac{C}{x - 3} = \frac{A(x + 2)(x - 3) + B(x - 1)(x - 3) + C(x - 1)(x + 2)}{(x - 1)(x + 2)(x - 3)}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Since the denominators are the same, we equate the numerators:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m x^2 - 19 = A(x + 2)(x - 3) + B(x - 1)(x - 3) + C(x - 1)(x + 2)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Next, we expand the right-hand side:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m A(x + 2)(x - 3) = A(x^2 - 3x + 2x - 6) = A(x - 3) - 6A = Ax - 3A - 6A = Ax - 9A
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m B(x - 1)(x - 3) = B(x^2 - 3x - x + 3) = B(x^2 - 4x + 3) = Bx^2 - 4Bx + 3B
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m C(x - 1)(x + 2) = C(x^2 - x + 2x - 2) = C(x^2 + x - 2) = Cx^2 + Cx - 2C
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Adding these together, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Ax - 9A + Bx^2 - 4Bx + 3B + Cx^2 + Cx - 2C = (Ax + Cx^2) + (-9A + Bx^2 - 4Bx + Cx - 2C)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Separating the rational and irrational parts, we have:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Ax + Cx^2 + (-9A + B + C)x + (-4B + C - 2C) = Ax + Cx^2 - (9A + B)x + (-4B - C)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Since the left-hand side must simplify to \(x^2 - 19\), we compare coefficients of corresponding terms:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Ax + Cx^2 - (9A + B)x + (-4B - C) = x^2 - 19
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m This gives us the following system of equations:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. \(A = 1\)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. \(C = 0\)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3. \(-9A - B = 0\) (from the coefficient of \(-x\))
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 4. \(-4B - C = -19\) (from the constant term)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m From equation 1, \(A = 1\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m From equation 3:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m -9(1) - B = 0 \implies -9 - B = 0 \implies B = -9
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m From equation 4:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m -4(-9) - C = -19 \implies 36 - C = -19 \implies C = 36 + 19 = 55
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Thus, the partial fraction decomposition is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \frac{x^2 - 19}{x^3 - 2x^2 - 5x + 6} = \frac{1}{x - 1} + \frac{-9}{x + 2} + \frac{55}{x - 3}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The product of the constants \(A\), \(B\), and \(C\) is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m A \cdot B \cdot C = 1 \cdot (-9) \cdot 55 = -495
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Therefore, the answer is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \boxed{-495}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
