[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Let $f(x) = 2x^4-17x^3+26x^2-24x-60$. Find $f(7)$.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To find \( f(7) \) for the polynomial \( f(x) = 2x^4 - 17x^3 + 26x^2 - 24x - 60 \), we need to substitute \( x = 7 \) into the polynomial and then compute the result.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Here are the steps:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. Substitute \( x = 7 \) into the polynomial: \( f(7) = 2(7)^4 - 17(7)^3 + 26(7)^2 - 24(7) - 60 \).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. Calculate each term separately:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - \( 7^4 = 2401 \), so \( 2(7)^4 = 2 \times 2401 = 4802 \).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - \( 7^3 = 343 \), so \( 17(7)^3 = 17 \times 343 = 5831 \).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - \( 26(7)^2 = 26 \times 49 = 1274 \), so \( 26(7)^2 = 26 \times 127 = 3182 \).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - \( -24(7) = -168 \), so \( -24(7) = -168 \).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - The constant term is \( -60 \).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3. Put it all together: \( f(7) = 4802 - 5831 + 3182 - 168 - 60 \).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 4. Perform the addition and subtraction step by step:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - \( 4802 - 5831 = -1029 \).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - \( -1029 + 3182 = 2153 \).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - \( 2153 - 168 = 2085 \).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - \( 2085 - 60 = 2025 \).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m So, the value of \( f(7) \) is \(\boxed{2025}\).<|endoftext|>
