[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To solve this problem, we can set up a system of equations based on the information given. Let's denote the two numbers as \( x \) and \( y \). According to the problem, we have two equations:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. The sum of the two numbers is 22:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    x + y = 22
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. The difference between the two numbers is 4:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    x - y = 4
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To find the values of \( x \) and \( y \), we can add these two equations together. This will eliminate \( y \) and give us a system of linear equations in \( x \) and \( y \):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m (x + y) + (x - y) = 22 + 4
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2x = 26
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m x = 13
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Now that we have the value of \( x \), we can substitute it back into one of the original equations to solve for \( y \). Let's use the first equation:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m x + y = 22
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 13 + y = 22
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m y = 22 - 13
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m y = 9
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m So, the two numbers are \( x = 13 \) and \( y = 9 \). The greater of the two numbers is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \boxed{13}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
