[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m In any isosceles triangle $ABC$ with $AB=AC$, the altitude $AD$ bisects the base $BC$ so that $BD=DC$.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m As shown in $\triangle ABC$, $AB=AC=25$ and $BC=14$.  Determine the length of the altitude $AD$.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m [asy]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m draw((0,0)--(14,0)--(7,24)--cycle,black+linewidth(1));
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m draw((7,24)--(7,0),black+linewidth(1)+dashed);
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m draw((7,0)--(7,1)--(6,1)--(6,0)--cycle,black+linewidth(1));
