[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To find the value of \(\frac{109^2 - 100^2}{9}\), we can use the difference of squares formula. The difference of squares formula states that \(a^2 - b^2 = (a - b)(a + b)\). In this case, \(a = 109\) and \(b = 100\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m So, we can rewrite the expression as:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \frac{109^2 - 100^2}{9} = \frac{(109 - 100)(109 + 100)}{9}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Simplifying the numerator, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m (109 - 100) \cdot (109 + 100) = 9 \cdot 209
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Now we can substitute the simplified numerator back into the expression:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \frac{9 \cdot 209}{9} = 209
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Thus, the value of \(\frac{109^2 - 100^2}{9}\) is \(\boxed{209}\).<|endoftext|>
