[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. **Identify the relation between cat and panda coolness:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - We know that 2 cats are equivalent to 5 alpacas. This can be expressed as:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      \text{If } 2 \text{ cats are A){}, \text{ then } 5 \text{ alpacas are C}{}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      This means:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      \text{If } x = 2, \text{ then } 5x = 5
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - Similarly, we know that 5 alpacas are equivalent to 7 pandas. This can be expressed as:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      \text{If } 5 \text{ alpacas are A}{}, \text{ then } 7 \text{ pandas are B}{}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      This means:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      \text{If } y = 5, \text{ then } 7y = 70
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. **Determine the value of \(x\):**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - From the first condition, we found that if \(2\) cats are as cool as \(5\) alpacas, then:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      \[
