[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - So, \(x = 1\). This means that 2 cats are as cool as 1 alpaca.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3. **Determine the value of \(y\):**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - From the second condition, we found that if \(5\) alpacas are as cool as \(7\) pandas, then:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      7y = 70 \implies y = 10
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - So, \(y = 10\). This means that \(7\) pandas are as cool as \(10\) alpacas.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Therefore, the number of pandas that are as cool as \(70\) alpacas is \(\boxed{10}\).<|endoftext|>
