[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To compute \(\arcsin \left( -\frac{\sqrt{3}}{2} \right)\), we need to determine the angle whose sine is \(-\frac{\sqrt{3}}{2}\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The sine function \(\sin \theta\) is negative in the third and fourth quadrants. The reference angle for \(\sin \theta = \frac{\sqrt{3}}{2}\) is \(\frac{\pi}{3}\) (or 60 degrees).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m However, since the sine function is negative, \(\theta\) must be in the third or fourth quadrant. In the third quadrant, the angle is \(-\frac{\pi}{3}\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m So, \(\theta = -\frac{\pi}{3}\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The value of \(\arcsin \left( -\frac{\sqrt{3}}{2} \right)\) in radians is \(-\frac{\pi}{3}\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Therefore, the final answer is \(\boxed{-\frac{\pi}{3}}\).<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m [Ground Truth]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m -\frac{\pi}{3}
