[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. **Identify the possible side lengths of an isosceles triangle:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - The three side lengths of the triangle are equal.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - Let the length of each of these sides be \( x \).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - The perimeter of the triangle is given by \( 2x \).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. **Set up the equation for the perimeter:**
