[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To find \(\cot 90^\circ\), we need to evaluate the cotangent function with the angle \(90^\circ\). The cotangent of an angle is the reciprocal of the tangent of that angle, i.e., \(\cot \theta = \frac{1}{\tan \theta}\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m First, we note that \(90^\circ\) is an angle in the unit circle where the tangent is undefined. The tangent of \(90^\circ\) is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \tan 90^\circ = \frac{\text{opposite}}{\text{adjacent}} = \frac{0}{1} = 0
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Since \(\cot \theta = \frac{1}{\tan \theta}\), we have:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \cot 90^\circ = \frac{1}{\tan 90^\circ} = \frac{1}{0}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m This expression is undefined, which means that \(\cot 90^\circ\) does not exist.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Thus, the final answer is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \boxed{\text{undefined}}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
