[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \left( r + \frac{1}{r} \right)^3 = r^3 + \frac{1}{r^3} + 3 + 3 \cdot 1
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m This simplifies to:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \left( r + \frac{1}{r} \right)^3 = r^3 + \frac{1}{r^3} + 6
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Since we know from the given equation:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m r^2 + \frac{1}{r^2} = 1
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m We can square both sides to find \( r^3 + \frac{1}{r^3} \):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
