[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Given:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. The point \( A \) has coordinates \( \overrightarrow{A} = (A_x, A_y) \).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. The point \( B \) has coordinates \( \overrightarrow{B} = (B_x, B_y) \).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3. The point \( P \) has coordinates \( \overrightarrow{P} = (P_x, P_y) \).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 4. The ratio \( AP:PB = 10:3 \).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Since \( AP:PB = 10:3 \), point \( P \) divides the line segment \( AB \) in the ratio \( 10:3 \). The coordinates of the point \( P \) can be expressed as:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
