[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m P_y = \frac{10A_y + 3B_y}{10+3} = \frac{10A_y + 3B_y}{13}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m We are also given:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \overrightarrow{P} = t \overrightarrow{A} + u \overrightarrow{B}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Substituting the expressions for \( P_x \) and \( P_y \) into the equation, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m P_x = t A_x + u B_x
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
