[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Equating the two expressions for \( P_x \):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \frac{10A_x + 3B_x}{13} = t A_x + u B_x
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Equating the two expressions for \( P_y \):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \frac{10A_y + 3B_y}{13} = t A_y + u B_y
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m We now have a system of linear equations in \( t \) and \( u \):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. \( \frac{10A_x + 3B_x}{13} = t A_x + u B_x \)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. \( \frac{10A_y + 3B_y}{13} = t A_y + u B_y \)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To eliminate \( t \) and \( u \), we can subtract the second equation from the first equation:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \frac{10A_x + 3B_x}{13} - \frac{10A_y + 3B_y}{13} = (t A_x + u B_x) - (t A_y + u B_y)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \frac{10(A_x - A_y) + 3(B_x - B_y)}{13} = (t A_x - t A_y) + (u B_x - u B_y)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \frac{10(A_x - A_y) + 3(B_x - B_y)}{13} = t (A_x - A_y) + (u (B_x - B_y))
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m For this equation to hold for all values of \( A_x \) and \( A_y \), the coefficients of \( (A_x - A_y) \) and \( (B_x - B_y) \) must each be zero:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 10 = t \quad \text{(coefficient of } (A_x - A_y) \text{)}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3 = u \quad \text{(coefficient of } (B_x - B_y) \text{)}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Substituting \( t = 10 \) and \( u = 3 \) into one of the original equations:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \frac{10 A_x + 3 B_x}{13} = 10 A_x + 3 B_x
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \frac{10 A_x + 3 B_x}{13} = 10 A_x + 3 B_x
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Subtracting \(\frac{10 A_x + 3 B_x}{13}\) from both sides:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 0 = 0
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m This confirms our values of \( t \) and \( u \). Therefore, the ordered pair \((t, u)\) is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \boxed{(10, 3)}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
