[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To find the range of the function \( k(x) = \frac{2x + 7}{x - 3} \), we need to determine all possible values that \( k(x) \) can take as \( x \) varies over all real numbers except where the function is undefined, i.e., at \( x = 3 \) and \( x = -\frac{7}{2} \).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m ### Step 1: Analyze the function at the points where it is undefined
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The function \( k(x) = \frac{2x + 7}{x - 3} \) is undefined at \( x = 3 \) and \( x = -\frac{7}{2} \). These points divide the real number line into three intervals: \( (-\infty, -\frac{7}{2}) \), \( (-\frac{7}{2}, 3) \), and \( (3, \infty) \).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m ### Step 2: Express \( k(x) \) in different forms
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m We can rewrite \( k(x) \) using partial fractions:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ k(x) = 2 + \frac{20}{x - 3}. \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m This form shows that \( k(x) \) is an even function, meaning \( k(x) = k(-x) \).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m ### Step 3: Determine the range using the steps above
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Given the above expression, we can analyze the behavior of \( k(x) \) as \( x \) approaches the vertical asymptotes \( x = 3 \) and \( x = -\frac{7}{2} \):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - As \( x \) approaches 3 from the left, \( k(x) \) approaches \( +\infty \).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - As \( x \) approaches 3 from the right, \( k(x) \) approaches \( -\infty \).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - As \( x \) approaches \( -\frac{7}{2} \) from the left, \( k(x) \) approaches \( +\infty \).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - As \( x \) approaches \( -\frac{7}{2} \) from the right, \( k(x) \) approaches \( -\infty \).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Since \( k(x) \) is even, the range of \( k(x) \) will be between the values it takes at the boundary points \( +\infty \) and \( -\infty \). Therefore, the range of \( k(x) \) is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ (-\infty, +\infty). \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m ### Conclusion
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The range of the function \( k(x) = \frac{2x + 7}{x - 3} \) is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \boxed{(-\infty, +\infty)}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
