[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. Write the number as a fraction: \(0.35 = \frac{35}{100}\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3. Simplify the fraction by finding the greatest common divisor (GCD) of 35 and 100. The GCD of 35 and 100 is 5.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 4. Divide both the numerator and the denominator by their GCD: \(\frac{35 \div 5}{100 \div 5} = \frac{7}{20}\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
