[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m On a number line, we place the decimal point at 0.35 and mark it on the line. We then continue adding 0.35 to get 0.70, 0.95, 0.10, 0.45, etc., until we reach a point where the division by 10 makes the decimal smaller or cannot be represented as a fraction of whole numbers on a number line. Once we reach 0.35, the point we end up at is 0.35.
