[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Tom can type 90 words a minute.  A page is 450 words.  How long would it take him to type out 10 pages? To determine how long it will take Tom to type out 10 pages, we need to follow these steps:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. **Calculate the total number of words in 10 pages:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    A page contains 450 words. Therefore, 10 pages will contain:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    10 \text{ pages} \times 450 \text{ words/page} = 4500 \text{ words}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. **Determine Tom's typing speed in words per minute:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    Tom can type 90 words per minute.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3. **Calculate the time required to type 4500 words:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    Time is calculated by dividing the total number of words by Tom's typing speed:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \text{Time} = \frac{4500 \text{ words}}{90 \text{ words/minute}}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    Simplify the division:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \frac{4500}{90} = 50 \text{ minutes}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Thus, it would take Tom 50 minutes to type out 10 pages. The final answer is:
