[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To find the area of the polygon, we need to determine the side length first. From the given information, each side is perpendicular to the adjacent sides and all sides are congruent. This means the polygon is an equilateral triangle.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The perimeter of the triangle is given as 56 units. Since an equilateral triangle has all sides of equal length, we can find the side length \( s \) by dividing the perimeter by the number of sides. There are 28 sides in total, so the side length is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m s = \frac{56}{28} = 2 \text{ units}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
