[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 7. **Divide the leading term of the new dividend by the leading term of the divisor:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \frac{x^4}{x^2} = x^2
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    So, the next term of the quotient is \(x^2\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 8. **Multiply the entire divisor by this term and subtract from the new dividend:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    (x - 2)^2 = x^2 - 4x + 4
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    x^4 - 4x^2 + 16x - 14 - (x^2 - 4x + 4) = x^4 - 4x^2 + 16x - 14 - x^2 + 4x - 4 = x^4 - 5x^2 + 20x - 18
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    So, the dividend is \(x^4 - 5x^2 + 20x - 18\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 9. **Repeat the process one last time:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \frac{x^4}{x^2} = x^2
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
