[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To find \(\cot 45^\circ\), we need to know the definition of the cotangent function. The cotangent of an angle \(\theta\) is defined as the ratio of the cosine of the angle to the sine of the angle:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \cot \theta = \frac{\cos \theta}{\sin \theta}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m For \(\theta = 45^\circ\), we know from trigonometry that \(\cos 45^\circ = \sin 45^\circ = \frac{\sqrt{2}}{2}\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Substituting these values into the cotangent formula, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \cot 45^\circ = \frac{\cos 45^\circ}{\sin 45^\circ} = \frac{\frac{\sqrt{2}}{2}}{\frac{\sqrt{2}}{2}} = 1
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Therefore, the value of \(\cot 45^\circ\) is \(\boxed{1}\).<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
