[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To determine how many cookies Annie can make with \(\frac{3}{2}\) pounds of cookie dough, we need to divide the total amount of cookie dough by the amount needed to make one cookie. The calculation is as follows:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \frac{3}{2} \div \frac{1}{16}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Dividing by a fraction is equivalent to multiplying by its reciprocal. The reciprocal of \(\frac{1}{16}\) is 16. So, we can rewrite the division as multiplication:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \frac{3}{2} \times \frac{16}{1}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Next, we multiply the numerators together and the denominators together:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \frac{3 \times 16}{2 \times 1} = \frac{48}{2}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Now, we perform the division:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \frac{48}{2} = 24
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Therefore, Annie can make \(\boxed{24}\) cookies.<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
