[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Find $\tan \frac{9 \pi}{4}.$
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m We need to find $\tan \frac{9\pi}{4}$.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Recall the periodicity of the tangent function: $\tan(x) = \tan(x + 2\pi)$. Therefore, $\tan \frac{9\pi}{4} = \tan \left( \frac{9\pi}{4} - 2\pi \right) = \tan \left( \frac{\pi}{4} - 2\pi \right)$.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Using the identity $\tan(x - 2\pi) = \tan x$, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \tan \left( \frac{\pi}{4} - 2\pi \right) = \tan \left( \frac{\pi}{4} \right) = \frac{1}{\tan \left( \frac{\pi}{4} \right)}.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m We know that $\tan \left( \frac{\pi}{4} \right) = 1$. Therefore:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \tan \left( \frac{\pi}{4} \right) = 1 \implies \sec \left( \frac{\pi}{4} \right) = 1 \implies \sin \left( \frac{\pi}{4} \right) = \cos \left( \frac{\pi}{4} \right) = \frac{1}{\sqrt{2}} = \frac{\sqrt{2}}{2}.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Thus, the tangent is $\frac{1}{\sqrt{2}} = \frac{\sqrt{2}}{2}$.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m So, $\boxed{\frac{\sqrt{2}}{2}}$.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
