[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To find the value of \(2 \times x - 3 \times y\) given \(x = 2\) and \(y = 1\), we will follow these steps:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. Substitute the given values of \(x\) and \(y\) into the expression \(2 \times x - 3 \times y\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. Perform the multiplication for each term.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Let's start with the substitution:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[2 \times x = 2 \times 2 = 4\]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[3 \times y = 3 \times 1 = 3\]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m So, the expression becomes:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[2 \times x - 3 \times y = 4 - 3\]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Next, perform the subtraction:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[4 - 3 = 1\]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Therefore, the value of \(2 \times x - 3 \times y\) is \(\boxed{1}\).<|endoftext|>
