[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m First, we substitute the expression for \( f(x) \) into the given equation:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m (x^3 - 2x - 2) + g(x) = -2 + x
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Next, we isolate \( g(x) \) by moving all terms involving \( g(x) \) to one side of the equation:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m g(x) = (-2 + x) - (x^3 - 2x - 2)
