[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To convert a base-$n$ number to base $B$, we can use the following series:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m $$
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \begin{array}{rcl}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m &\text{Base}\ (&n, 10)=(\left (\sum x_k \cdot \frac{10}{n}\right) + \sum y_k \cdot \frac{10^{-1}}{10}) & \text{Base}\ (&n, B)\\
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m &\ \equiv & \left \{ \sum x_k \cdot \frac{B^{k-1}}{n} \right \} + \sum y_k \cdot \frac{B^{-k}}{n-B^{-1}}.& \text{Base}\ (&n, B)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \end{array}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m $$
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m For $n = 64$, let's convert $100_{64}$ to base $62$.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m We have $100_{64} = 1\cdot62+0\cdot64+0\cdot6+0\cdot2+0\cdot2+0\cdot2+0\cdot2+1\cdot35+2\cdot35+0\cdot15+0\cdot5+0\cdot5+0\cdot5+0\cdot5 +0\cdot5+0\cdot5+0\cdot5+0\cdot5+ \mathbf{0}$.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m This simplifies to $1\cdot62 + 0\cdot64 + 0\cdot6 + 0\cdot2 + 0\cdot2 + 0\cdot2 + 0\cdot2 + 1\cdot35 + 2\cdot 35 + \mathbf{0} = 62 + 0 = 62$ and the suffix isn't significant since it's renamed to zero.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The series is 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m $$
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \begin{align}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m &16\cdot6^0 = 16 + \mathbf{0},\\\\
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m &17\cdot6^1 + 35\cdot6^0 = 112 + 35 = 147,\\\\
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m &16\cdot6^2 + 25\cdot6^1 + 44\cdot6^0 = 360 + 150 + 10 - 20 + 1 = 339,
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \end{align}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m $$
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m now combine the two series:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m $$
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \begin{array}{rcl}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m &\text{Base}\ (&62, 10)=0+0+0+0+0+1+2 + 3+5 +6 - \mathbf{0}+4 + 10\\\\
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m &\equiv & 0 + 147 + 339 + 360 + 6 - 20 + 2 + 1 + \mathbf{0} = \mathbf{177} 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \end{array}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m $$
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Therefore, $100_{64} = 1\cdot 62^{10} + 0\cdot 62^9 + 0\cdot 62^8 + 1\cdot 62^7 + 2\cdot 62^6 + 3\cdot 62^5 + 5\cdot 62^4 + 16\cdot 62^3 + 35\cdot 62^2 + 57\cdot 62 + 112$.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Conversely, by substituting $100 = R_{31} \equiv (2^5 + 13) \cdot 9 + 34 = 18\cdot 9 + 34 \equiv 951$, we get $2^{19} + 73 \equiv 951 \equiv 25 \pmod{62}$, which can be approached using Euler $\phi(n)$. By iterating:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m $$
