[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To find the units digit of the sum of the first \(21\) positive perfect cubes, we need to determine the units digit of each cube and then sum these units digits. The units digit of a cube can be found by considering the units digits of the numbers \(1^3, 2^3, 3^3, \ldots, 21^3\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m First, let's identify the units digits of the cubes of the numbers from 1 to 21:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
