[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    Now, subtract the original \(x\) from this equation:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    10000x - x = 3283.283283283\ldots - 3.283283283\ldots
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    This simplifies to:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    9999x = 3280
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    Solving for \(x\), we get:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    x = \frac{3280}{9999}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3. **Simplify the fraction:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    To simplify \(\frac{3280}{9999}\), we need to find the greatest common divisor (GCD) of 3280 and 9999. We can use the Euclidean algorithm to find the GCD.
