[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To compute \(\begin{pmatrix} -3 \\ 5 \end{pmatrix} \cdot \begin{pmatrix} -2 \\ 1 \end{pmatrix}\), we will use the definition of the dot product for matrices. The dot product of two matrices is defined by their entries as follows:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m (A \cdot B)_ij = (A_{ij})_i (B_{ji})_j
