[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Here, \(A = \begin{pmatrix} -3 & 5 \end{pmatrix}\) and \(B = \begin{pmatrix} -2 & 1 \end{pmatrix}\). We need to calculate each entry of the resulting matrix:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. For the first element \((A \cdot B)_11\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m (A \cdot B)_11 = (-3) \cdot (-2) + 5 \cdot 1 = 6 + 5 = 11
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. For the second element \((A \cdot B)_21\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m (A \cdot B)_21 = (-3) \cdot 1 + 5 \cdot (-2) = -3 - 10 = -13
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3. For the first element \((A \cdot B)_12\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m (A \cdot B)_12 = (-3) \cdot (-2) + 5 \cdot 1 = 6 + 5 = 11
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 4. For the second element \((A \cdot B)_22\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m (A \cdot B)_22 = (-3) \cdot 1 + 5 \cdot (-2) = -3 - 10 = -13
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Putting these together, the resulting matrix is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \begin{pmatrix} 11 & 11 \\ -13 & -13 \end{pmatrix}
