[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ g(x) = x - 1 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ g(1) = 1 - 1 = 0 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Now that we have \( g(1) = 0 \), we need to evaluate \( f(0) \):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ f(x) = x^3 + 2x + 1 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ f(0) = 0^3 + 2 \cdot 0 + 1 = 0 + 0 + 1 = 1 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Therefore, the value of \( f(g(1)) \) is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ \boxed{1} \]<|endoftext|>
