[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To solve for \(x^2 - y^2\), we start with the given equations:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ x + y = 10 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ 2x + y = 13 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m We observe that the second equation can be derived from the first equation by multiplying the first equation by 2:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ 2(x + y) = 2 \cdot 10 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ 2x + 2y = 20 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m We now have the system of linear equations:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. \( x + y = 10 \)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. \( 2x + y = 13 \)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To eliminate \(y\), we subtract the first equation from the second:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ (2x + y) - (x + y) = 13 - 10 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ 2x + y - x - y = 3 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ x = 3 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Now that we have \(x = 3\), we substitute this value back into the first equation to solve for \(y\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ 3 + y = 10 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ y = 10 - 3 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ y = 7 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Next, we need to find \(x^2 - y^2\). We use the difference of squares formula:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ x^2 - y^2 = (x + y)(x - y) \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m We already know:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ x + y = 10 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ x - y = -3 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Substituting these values into the difference of squares formula:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ x^2 - y^2 = 10(-3) \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ x^2 - y^2 = -30 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Thus, the value of \(x^2 - y^2\) is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \boxed{-30}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
