[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To find the coefficient of \(x\) in the expression \((1+2x)-(2+2x+3x^2)+3(1+2x+3x^2+4x^3)-(4+4x+5x^2+6x^3+7x^4)\), we will first simplify each term and then identify the coefficient of \(x\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The expression is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m (1+2x)-(2+2x+3x^2)+3(1+2x+3x^2+4x^3)-(4+4x+5x^2+6x^3+7x^4)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Let's simplify each term step by step:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. Simplify \((1+2x)-(2+2x+3x^2)\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1+2x - (2+2x+3x^2) = 1+2x - 2 - 2x - 3x^2 = 1 - 2 - 3x^2 = -1 - 3x^2
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. Simplify \(3(1+2x+3x^2+4x^3)\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3(1+2x+3x^2+4x^3) = 3 + 6x + 9x^2 + 12x^3
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3. Simplify \(-(4+4x+5x^2+6x^3+7x^4)\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m -(4+4x+5x^2+6x^3+7x^4) = -4 - 4x - 5x^2 - 6x^3 - 7x^4
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Now, substitute these simplified terms back into the expression:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m -1 - 3x^2 - 4 - 4x - 5x^2 - 6x^3 - 7x^4
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Combine all the like terms:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m -1 - 4 - 5x^2 - 6x^3 - 7x^4 - 3x^2 = -5 - 11x^2 - 6x^3 - 7x^4
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The coefficient of \(x\) in the expression is \(-11x^2\).
