[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Simplify $\cos 10^\circ \cos 30^\circ \cos 50^\circ \cos 70^\circ.$
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To simplify \(\cos 10^\circ \cos 30^\circ \cos 50^\circ \cos 70^\circ\), we will use trigonometric identities to find a simpler form of the expression.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m First, recall the double-angle identity for cosine:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \cos 2\theta = 2 \cos^2 \theta - 1
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m We will apply this identity twice to the given expression:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. For \(\cos 2 \cdot 10^\circ\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \cos 2 \cdot 10^\circ = 2 \cos 20^\circ
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. Now, compute \(\cos 2 \cdot 2 \cdot 10^\circ = \cos 40^\circ\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Next, use the triple-angle identity for cosine:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \cos 3\theta = 4 \cos^3 \theta - 3 \cos \theta
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m We will apply this identity three times to \(\cos 40^\circ\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3. First, compute \(\cos 40^\circ\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \cos 40^\circ = \cos (40^\circ \mod 180^\circ)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Since \(40^\circ \mod 180^\circ = 100^\circ\), we have:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \cos 40^\circ = \cos 100^\circ
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 4. Now, compute \(\cos 100^\circ\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \cos 100^\circ = \cos (180^\circ - 80^\circ) = -\cos 80^\circ
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m We know that:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \cos 80^\circ = \sin 10^\circ
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Thus,
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \cos 100^\circ = -\sin 10^\circ
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Putting it all together:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \cos 40^\circ = -\sin 10^\circ
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Therefore, the original expression becomes:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \cos 10^\circ \cos 30^\circ \cos 50^\circ \cos 70^\circ = \cos 100^\circ \cdot \cos 40^\circ \cdot \cos 100^\circ
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Substituting the known values:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \cos 100^\circ \cdot \cos 40^\circ \cdot \cos 100^\circ = -\sin 10^\circ \cdot (-\sin 10^\circ) \cdot \cos 100^\circ = \sin^2 10^\circ \cdot \cos 100^\circ
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Since \(\cos 100^\circ = -\sin 10^\circ\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \sin^2 10^\circ \cdot (-\sin 10^\circ) = -\sin^3 10^\circ
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Thus, the simplified form of the given expression is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \boxed{-\sin^3 10^\circ}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
