[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To find the value of \(a\) for which the line \(ax + (a+1)y = a+2\) passes through the point \((4, -8)\), we can substitute the coordinates of the point into the equation and solve for \(a\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The equation of the line is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ ax + (a+1)y = a+2 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Substitute \(x = 4\) and \(y = -8\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ a(4) + (a+1)(-8) = a+2 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Simplify the left side of the equation:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ 4a - 8(a+1) = a+2 \]
