[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Find the area of the triangle with vertices $(0,7,10),$ $(-1,6,6),$ and $(-4,9,6).$
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To find the area of the triangle with vertices \((0,7,10)\), \((-1,6,6)\), and \((-4,9,6)\), we can use the formula for the area of a triangle given its vertices \((x_1, y_1, z_1)\), \((x_2, y_2, z_2)\), and \((x_3, y_3, z_3)\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \text{Area} = \frac{1}{2} \left\| \vec{AB} \times \vec{AC} \right\|
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m where \(\vec{AB} = (x_2 - x_1, y_2 - y_1, z_2 - z_1)\) and \(\vec{AC} = (x_3 - x_1, y_3 - y_1, z_3 - z_1)\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m First, we calculate the vectors \(\vec{AB}\) and \(\vec{AC}\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \vec{AB} = (-1 - 0, 6 - 7, 6 - 10) = (-1, -1, -4)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \vec{AC} = (-4 - 0, 9 - 7, 6 - 10) = (-4, 2, -4)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Next, we find the cross product \(\vec{AB} \times \vec{AC}\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \vec{AB} \times \vec{AC} = \begin{vmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \mathbf{i} & \mathbf{j} & \mathbf{k} \\
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m -1 & -1 & -4 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m -4 & 2 & -4
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \end{vmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Expanding the determinant, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \vec{AB} \times \vec{AC} = \mathbf{i}((-1)(-4) - (-4)(2)) - \mathbf{j}((-1)(-4) - (-4)(-4)) + \mathbf{k}((-1)(2) - (-1)(-4))
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m = \mathbf{i}(4 + 8) - \mathbf{j}(4 - 16) + \mathbf{k}(-2 - 4)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m = 12\mathbf{i} + 12\mathbf{j} - 6\mathbf{k}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m = (12, 12, -6)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The magnitude of \(\vec{AB} \times \vec{AC}\) is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \left\| (12, 12, -6) \right\| = \sqrt{12^2 + 12^2 + (-6)^2} = \sqrt{144 + 144 + 36} = \sqrt{324} = 18
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Therefore, the area of the triangle is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \text{Area} = \frac{1}{2} \times 18 = 9
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Thus, the area of the triangle is \(\boxed{9}\).<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
