[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. Calculate the value of \(\frac{1}{2^{10}}\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. Extract the decimal part of the result.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3. Determine the number of digits to the right of the decimal point.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m **Step 1: Calculate \(\frac{1}{2^{10}}\)**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m First, compute \(2^{10}\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2^{10} = 1024
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Now, divide 1 by 1024:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
