[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m **Step 2: Extract the decimal part**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To find the decimal part, we need to subtract the integer part from \(\frac{1}{1024}\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1024 - 1 = 1023
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m So, \(\frac{1}{1024} = 0.00098790625\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m **Step 3: Determine the number of digits to the right of the decimal point**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
