[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To solve for \( a \) given that the system of equations has a solution \((x, y)\) when \( x = 2 \), we will substitute \( x = 2 \) into the system of equations and solve for \( y \).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The given system of equations is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3x + y = a \quad \text{(1)}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2x + 5y = 2a \quad \text{(2)}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m First, substitute \( x = 2 \) into both equations.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Substitute into equation (1):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3(2) + y = a
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 6 + y = a
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m y = a - 6 \quad \text{(3)}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Substitute into equation (2):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2(2) + 5y = 2a
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 4 + 5y = 2a
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 5y = 2a - 4
