[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To express the repeating decimal \(0.6\overline{333}\) as a common fraction, we can follow these steps:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. **Let \( x = 0.6\overline{333} \)**.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. **Express the repeating part in terms of a simpler repeating decimal**:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - The digit 333 repeats, so we can write \(333\) as \(3 + 0.333\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - We can now express \(0.6\overline{333}\) as:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      x = 0.6 + 0.333\overline{333}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      1000x = 633.33333\overline{333}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      \]
