[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Calculate the following:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m (1) $\frac{\sqrt{24}}{\sqrt{3}}$
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m (2) $-10\sqrt{\frac{1}{10}}$
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m (3) $\sqrt{\frac{9}{4}}$ To solve the given problems, we will use the properties of square roots and fractions. Here are the step-by-step solutions for each part of the problem:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. \(\frac{\sqrt{24}}{\sqrt{3}}\)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    To simplify this, we can multiply the square roots by the conjugate:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \frac{\sqrt{24}}{\sqrt{3}} = \sqrt{\frac{24}{3}} = \sqrt{8} = \sqrt{4 \cdot 2} = \sqrt{4} \cdot \sqrt{2} = 2\sqrt{2}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    So, the answer is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \boxed{2\sqrt{2}}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. \(-10\sqrt{\frac{1}{10}}\)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    To simplify this, we can separate the cube root into two parts:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    -10\sqrt{\frac{1}{10}} = -10 \cdot \frac{\sqrt{1}}{\sqrt{10}} = -10 \cdot \frac{1}{\sqrt{10}} = -\frac{10}{\sqrt{10}}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    To rationalize the denominator, we multiply the numerator and the denominator by \(\sqrt{10}\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    -\frac{10}{\sqrt{10}} = -\frac{10 \sqrt{10}}{10} = -\sqrt{10}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    So, the answer is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \boxed{-\sqrt{10}}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3. \(\sqrt{\frac{9}{4}}\)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    To simplify this, we can separate the numerator into a fraction:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \sqrt{\frac{9}{4}} = \frac{\sqrt{9}}{\sqrt{4}} = \frac{3}{2}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    So, the answer is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \boxed{\frac{3}{2}}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
