[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Since \( PA \) and \( PB \) are perpendicular, triangle \( PAC \) is a right triangle with \( PA \) and \( PB \) as the legs and \( PC \) as the hypotenuse. We can use the Pythagorean theorem to find the length of \( PC \):
