[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To compute the expression \(\frac{1}{\cos 80^\circ} - \frac{\sqrt{3}}{\sin 80^\circ}\), we'll start by rewriting it in a simplified form:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \frac{1}{\cos 80^\circ} - \frac{\sqrt{3}}{\sin 80^\circ} = \frac{\sin 80^\circ - \sqrt{3} \cos 80^\circ}{\sin 80^\circ \cos 80^\circ}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Next, we'll simplify the numerator \(\sin 80^\circ - \sqrt{3} \cos 80^\circ\). To do this, we can use the angle addition formula for sine:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \sin A \cos B - \cos A \sin B = \sin (A - B)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m In our case, \(A = 80^\circ\) and \(B = 80^\circ\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \sin 80^\circ - \sqrt{3} \cos 80^\circ = \sin 80^\circ - \sqrt{3} \cos 80^\circ
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m So the expression becomes:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \frac{\sin 80^\circ - \sqrt{3} \cos 80^\circ}{\sin 80^\circ \cos 80^\circ}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Notice that \(\sin 80^\circ \cos 80^\circ\) is the double-angle identity for sine:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \sin 80^\circ \cos 80^\circ = \frac{1}{2} \sin 160^\circ
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Since \(\sin 160^\circ = \sin (180^\circ - 20^\circ) = \sin 20^\circ\), we have:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \sin 80^\circ \cos 80^\circ = \frac{1}{2} \sin 20^\circ
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Substituting this back into our expression, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \frac{\sin 80^\circ - \sqrt{3} \cos 80^\circ}{\sin 80^\circ \cos 80^\circ} = \frac{\sin 80^\circ - \sqrt{3} \cos 80^\circ}{\frac{1}{2} \sin 20^\circ} = \frac{2 (\sin 80^\circ - \sqrt{3} \cos 80^\circ)}{\sin 20^\circ} = \frac{2 \sin 80^\circ}{\sin 20^\circ} - \frac{2 \sqrt{3} \cos 80^\circ}{\sin 20^\circ}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Recognize that \(\frac{2 \sin 80^\circ}{\sin 20^\circ} = 2 \sin 80^\circ / 2 \sin 10^\circ\) and \(\frac{2 \sqrt{3} \cos 80^\circ}{\sin 20^\circ} = 2 \sqrt{3} \cos 80^\circ / \sin 20^\circ\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2 \sin 80^\circ / 2 \sin 10^\circ - 2 \sqrt{3} \cos 80^\circ / \sin 20^\circ
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Using the double-angle identity for cosine, \(\sin 80^\circ = 2 \sin 40^\circ \cos 40^\circ\), and \(\cos 40^\circ = \sqrt{1 - \sin^2 40^\circ}\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \sin 80^\circ = 2 \cdot 2 \sin 40^\circ \cdot \frac{\sqrt{1 - \left(\frac{\sqrt{3}}{2}\right)^2}}{2} \cos 40^\circ = \sqrt{1 - \frac{3}{4}} \cdot \sqrt{1 - \left(\frac{\sqrt{3}}{2}\right)^2} \cos 40^\circ = \frac{1}{2} \cdot \frac{1}{2} \cos 40^\circ = \frac{\cos 40^\circ}{4}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m We know that \(\cos 40^\circ = \sqrt{1 - \sin^2 40^\circ}\) and \(\sin 80^\circ = 2 \sin 40^\circ \cdot \frac{\sqrt{1 - \left(\frac{\sqrt{3}}{2}\right)^2}}{2} \cos 40^\circ = \frac{\sqrt{3}}{2} \cos 40^\circ\), but we can simplify directly 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \frac{\cos 40^\circ}{4} - \sqrt{3} \cos 80^\circ = \frac{1}{4} \cos 40^\circ - \sqrt{3} \cos 80^\circ
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Recognize that \(\frac{1}{4} = \frac{\sin^2 20^\circ}{20}\) and \(\sqrt{3} \cos 80^\circ = 2 \cos 20^\circ \cos 60^\circ = 2 \cos 20^\circ\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 20 \frac{\sin^2 20^\circ}{20} - 2 \sqrt{3} \cdot 2 \cos 20^\circ = \sin 20^\circ - 2 \sqrt{3} \cos 20^\circ
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m So the final simplified answer is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \boxed{-1}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
