[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To find the area of triangle \( \triangle ABC \), we can use the formula for the area of a right triangle, since \( \angle A = 90^\circ \). The formula for the area of a right triangle is given by:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \text{Area} = \frac{1}{2} \times \text{base} \times \text{height}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m In this problem, the base of the triangle is \( AB \) and the height is \( AC \). We are given that \( AB = 25 \) cm and \( AC = 20 \) cm. Substituting these values into the formula, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \text{Area} = \frac{1}{2} \times 25 \times 20
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m First, we calculate the product of the base and the height:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 25 \times 20 = 500
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Then, we multiply by \(\frac{1}{2}\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \text{Area} = \frac{1}{2} \times 500 = 250
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Therefore, the area of triangle \( \triangle ABC \) is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
