[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m What is the coefficient of $x^3$ when $$x^4-3x^3 + 5x^2-6x + 1$$is multiplied by $$2x^3 - 3x^2 + 4x + 7$$and the like terms are combined?
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To determine the coefficient of \(x^3\) in the product of the polynomials \(x^4 - 3x^3 + 5x^2 - 6x + 1\) and \(2x^3 - 3x^2 + 4x + 7\), we need to consider all the terms that will contribute to \(x^3\) when these polynomials are multiplied. The only terms that will contribute are the \(x^3\) term from each polynomial because the other terms are 0 (since multiplication has properties like \(x^3 \cdot (-3x^3) = -3x^6\), and also the other terms are 1/2, 4/2, and -6/2, which still contribute 0 to the \(x^3\) term).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The first polynomial is \(x^4 - 3x^3 + 5x^2 - 6x + 1\), which contributes \(x^3\). The second polynomial is \(2x^3 - 3x^2 + 4x + 7\), which also contributes \(x^3\). Therefore, the total coefficient of \(x^3\) in the product is the sum of the coefficients from each polynomial:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1 \cdot 2 + 0 \cdot (-3) + 0 \cdot 4 + 0 \cdot 7 = 2 + 0 + 0 + 0 = 2
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Thus, the coefficient of \(x^3\) is \(\boxed{2}\).<|endoftext|>
