[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Let \[f(x) = \left\{
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \begin{array}{cl}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m x^2+1 &\text{ if }x>5, \\
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2x-3 &\text{ if } -5 \le x \le 5, \\
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3 &\text{ if } x <-5.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \end{array}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \right.\]Find $f(-7)+f(0)+f(7)$.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To find \( f(-7) + f(0) + f(7) \), we need to evaluate the piecewise function \( f(x) \) at \( x = -7 \), \( x = 0 \), and \( x = 7 \) separately. The function \( f(x) \) is defined as follows:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m f(x) = \begin{cases} 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m x^2 + 1 & \text{if } x > 5, \\
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2x - 3 & \text{if } -5 \le x \le 5, \\
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3 & \text{if } x < -5.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \end{cases}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m ### Step 1: Evaluate \( f(-7) \)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Since \( -7 < -5 \), we use the third case of the piecewise function:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m f(-7) = 3.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m ### Step 2: Evaluate \( f(7) \)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Since \( 7 > 5 \), we use the first case of the piecewise function:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m f(7) = 7^2 + 1 = 49 + 1 = 50.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m ### Step 3: Evaluate \( f(0) \)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Since \( 0 \le 5 \), we use the second case of the piecewise function:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m f(0) = 2(0) - 3 = 0 - 3 = -3.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m ### Step 4: Sum the results
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Now we add the values of \( f(-7) \), \( f(0) \), and \( f(7) \):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m f(-7) + f(0) + f(7) = 3 + (-3) + 50 = 50.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Thus, the final answer is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \boxed{50}
