[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Points $A$, $B$, $C$, $D$, and $E$ are located in 3-dimensional space with $AB= BC= CD= DE= EA= 2$ and $\angle ABC = \angle CDE = \angle
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m DEA = 90^\circ$.  The plane of triangle $ABC$ is parallel to $\overline{DE}$. What is the area of triangle $BDE$?
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
