[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Let
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[f(a,b) = \left\{
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \renewcommand{\arraystretch}{3}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \begin{array}{cl}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \dfrac{ab - a + 2}{2a} & \text{if $a + b \le 3$}, \\
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \dfrac{ab - b - 2}{-2b} & \text{if $a + b > 3$}.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \end{array}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \renewcommand{\arraystretch}{1}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \right.\]Find $f(2,1) + f(2,4).$
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To solve the problem, we need to evaluate the function \( f(a, b) \) at the points \( (2, 1) \) and \( (2, 4) \) and then sum the results.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The function \( f(a, b) \) is defined piecewise as follows:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m f(a, b) = \left\{
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \begin{array}{cl}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \dfrac{ab - a + 2}{2a} & \text{if } a + b \le 3, \\
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \dfrac{ab - b - 2}{-2b} & \text{if } a + b > 3.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \end{array}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \right.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m First, let's evaluate \( f(2, 1) \):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2 + 1 = 3
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Since \( 2 + 1 \le 3 \), we use the first piece of the function:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m f(2, 1) = \dfrac{2 \cdot 1 - 2 + 2}{2 \cdot 2} = \dfrac{2 - 2 + 2}{4} = \dfrac{2}{4} = \dfrac{1}{2}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Next, let's evaluate \( f(2, 4) \):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2 + 4 = 6
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Since \( 6 > 3 \), we use the second piece of the function:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m f(2, 4) = \dfrac{2 \cdot 4 - 4 - 2}{-2 \cdot 4} = \dfrac{8 - 4 - 2}{-8} = \dfrac{2}{-8} = -\dfrac{1}{4}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Now, we sum the results of the two evaluations:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m f(2, 1) + f(2, 4) = \dfrac{1}{2} + \left(-\dfrac{1}{4}\right) = \dfrac{1}{2} - \dfrac{1}{4}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To add these fractions, we need a common denominator:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \dfrac{1}{2} - \dfrac{1}{4} = \dfrac{2}{4} - \dfrac{1}{4} = \dfrac{1}{4}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Therefore, the final answer is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \boxed{\dfrac{1}{4}}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m [Ground Truth]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \frac{1}{4}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m [Is Boxed Matched]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m True
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
