[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m At the Gooddog Obedience School, dogs can learn to do three tricks: sit, stay, and roll over. Of the dogs at the school: \begin{tabular}{l@{\qquad}l}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 50 dogs can sit & 17 dogs can sit and stay \\
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 29 dogs can stay & 12 dogs can stay and roll over \\
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 34 dogs can roll over & 18 dogs can sit and roll over \\
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 9 dogs can do all three & 9 dogs can do none
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \end{tabular} How many dogs are in the school?
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To find the total number of dogs at the Gooddog Obedience School, we need to consider the dogs that can perform each trick individually and who can perform them all (i.e., dogs who can do none of them).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Here's a step-by-step breakdown:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. Calculate the number of dogs that can only perform one trick:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - Dogs that can only sit: \( 50 - 9 = 41 \)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - Dogs that can only sit and stay: \( 17 - 9 = 8 \)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - Dogs that can only stay: \( 29 \)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - Dogs that can only stay and roll over: \( 12 \)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - Dogs that can only roll over: \( 34 \)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - Dogs that can only sit and roll over: \( 18 \)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. Calculate the number of dogs that can only perform none of these tricks:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - Dogs that can only do all three tricks: \( 9 \)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3. Calculate the number of dogs that can only do one trick (i.e., dogs that can only do none of the other tricks):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - Dogs that can only sit and stay and roll over: \( 41 + 18 + 18 = 67 \)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - Dogs that can only do sit, stay, and roll over but not both sit and roll over: \( 8 + 12 + 18 = 38 \)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - Dogs that can only do sit and stay but not roll over or stay: \( 17 + 29 + 18 = 54 \)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - Dogs that can only do sit and stay but not of the above choices: \( 17 + 29 = 46 \)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - Dogs that can only do sit and stay but not of the above choices and also either of the sit and stay or roll over: \( 17 + 29 = 46 \)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - Dogs that can only do sit and stay but not of the above choices and also both stay and roll over: \( 17 + 12 = 29 \)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - Dogs that can only do sit and stay but not of the above choices and also both stay and rolling over and also sitting or standing: \( 17 + 12 = 29 \)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - Dogs that can only do sit and stay but not of the above choices and also both sitting and standing or rolling over but also either always sit or always stand: \( 17 + 9 = 26 \)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - Dogs that can only do sit and stay but not of the above choices and also both sitting and standing or rolling over but also either always sit or always stand: \( 17 + 9 = 26 \)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - Dogs that can only do sit and stay and cannot both sit and roll over or both stay and roll over: \( 29 + 9 = 38 \)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - Dogs that can only do sit and stay but cannot both sit and rolling over or both stay and sitting: \( 29 + 9 = 38 \)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 4. Sum up all the dogs that can only do one trick plus those that can only perform none of the tricks:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    67 + (46 + 54 + 46 + 46 + 29 + 26) + 38 = 67 + 228 + 38 = 333
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Therefore, the total number of dogs at the Gooddog Obedience School is \(\boxed{333}\).<|endoftext|>
