[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - The leading digit of \(8! = 40320\) is 0.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - The leading digit of \(9! = 362880\) is 0.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - The leading digit of \(10! = 3628800\) is 0.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - The leading digit of \(11! = 39916800\) is 0.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - The leading digit of \(12! = 479001600\) is 0.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - The leading digit of \(13! = 6227020800\) is 0.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - The leading digit of \(14! = 87178291200\) is 1.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - The leading digit of \(15! = 1307674368000\) is 2.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - The leading digit of \(16! = 20922789888000\) is 4.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - The leading digit of \(17! = 35568742808000\) is 6.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - The leading digit of \(18! = 5109094217172800\) is 8.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - The leading digit of \(19! = 121645100408832000\) is 10.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - The leading digit of \(20! = 3628800000000000000\) is 12.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - The leading digit of \(21! = 560758969760160000000\) is 14.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - The leading digit of \(22! = 906089695201600000000\) is 16.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - The leading digit of \(23! = 141425903687123372000000\) is 18.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - The leading digit of \(24! = 2799326184467844160000000000000\) is 19.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m We observe that the leading digit of \(20! \times (21-1)!\) is \(0 \times 44 = 0\), and the leading digit of \(21! \times (22-1)!\) is \(1 \times 43 = 43\). This means the numbers 20! and 21! have leading digits that either end in zero (leading digit 0) or a leading digit of 43. We need to find out how many numbers between 7! and 2006! end in a leading digit of 43.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
