[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. **Area of the White Triangle:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - The white triangle is similar to the gray rectangle. The ratio of the areas of two similar triangles is the square of the ratio of their corresponding sides.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - The hypotenuse of the white triangle (which is twice the leg length) is 10 units.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - The leg of the white triangle is half the hypotenuse of the gray rectangle, which is \( \frac{10}{2} = 5 \) units.
