[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m How many of the following 10 numbers are multiples of 6:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 20, 30, 40, 50, 60, 70, 80, 90, 100, 110
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m $\textbf{(A) }1\qquad\textbf{(B) }2\qquad\textbf{(C) }3\qquad\textbf{(D) }4\qquad\textbf{(E) }5$
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To solve this problem, we need to determine which of the given numbers are multiples of 6. A number is a multiple of 6 if it can be expressed as \(6k\) or \(6k+6\), where \(k\) is an integer.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Let's examine each number in the list:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 20: \(20 \div 6 = 3\) remainder 2 (so 20 is not a multiple of 6)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 30: \(30 \div 6 = 5\) remainder 0 (so 30 is not a multiple of 6)
