[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To find the slope of the line given by the equation \(2y = -3x + 6\), we need to rewrite the equation in the slope-intercept form, which is \(y = mx + b\), where \(m\) is the slope and \(b\) is the y-intercept.
