[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The distance from the origin to the focus \(F\) is 1, so the radius of the circle is \(\sqrt{2}\). Therefore, the coordinates of \(P\) must be \((p,0)\), and we need to find \(p\) such that the conditions are satisfied. By solving the equations, we find that the coordinates of \(P\) are \((\sqrt{2}, 0)\) or \((- \sqrt{2}, 0)\).
