[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To solve this problem, we need to determine the common difference \(d\) of the arithmetic sequence. The \(n\)-th term of an arithmetic sequence can be found using the formula:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ a_n = a_1 + (n-1)d \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m where \(a_n\) is the \(n\)-th term, \(a_1\) is the first term, \(d\) is the common difference, and \(n\) is the term number.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Given:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - The fifth term (\(a_5\)) is 5.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - The sixth term (\(a_6\)) is 9.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - The seventh term (\(a_7\)) is 13.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m We can set up the following equations based on the formula:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m For the fifth term (\(a_5\)):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ a_5 = a_1 + 4d = 5 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m For the sixth term (\(a_6\)):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ a_6 = a_1 + 5d = 9 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m And for the seventh term (\(a_7\)):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ a_7 = a_1 + 6d = 13 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m We now have a system of three linear equations:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. \(a_1 + 4d = 5\)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. \(a_1 + 5d = 9\)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3. \(a_1 + 6d = 13\)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To solve this system, we can subtract the first equation from the second and the second from the third to eliminate \(a_1\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Subtracting the first equation from the second:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ (a_1 + 5d) - (a_1 + 4d) = 9 - 5 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ d = 4 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Subtracting the second equation from the third:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ (a_1 + 6d) - (a_1 + 5d) = 13 - 9 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ d = 4 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Both equations are consistent with \(d = 4\), so we can verify our solution:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m For \(a_1 + 4d = 5\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ a_1 + 4(4) = 5 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ a_1 + 16 = 5 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ a_1 = 5 - 16 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ a_1 = -11 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m For \(a_1 + 5d = 9\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ -11 + 5(4) = 9 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ -11 + 20 = 9 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ 9 = 9 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m For \(a_1 + 6d = 13\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ -11 + 6(4) = 13 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ -11 + 24 = 13 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ 13 = 13 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m So, the sequence is \(a_1 = -11\), \(d = 4\). The first four terms of the sequence are:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ -11, -7, -3, -1 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The sum of the first four terms is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ \boxed{-11 - 7 - 3 - 1} = \boxed{-22} \]<|endoftext|>
