[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Sandy plans to paint one wall in her bedroom. The wall is 9 feet high and 12 feet long. There is a 2-foot by 4-foot area on that wall that she will not have to paint due to the window. How many square feet will she need to paint?
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To find out how many square feet Sandy needs to paint, we'll follow these steps:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. Calculate the total area of the wall.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. Subtract the area of the window.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3. Subtract the area of the unassigned area.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 4. The remaining area is the one that needs to be painted.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Let's do this step by step.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. Calculate the total area of the wall:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ \text{Total area of the wall} = 9 \, \text{feet-height} \times 12 \, \text{feet-long} = 108 \, \text{square feet} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. Calculate the area of the window:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ \text{Area of the window} = 2 \, \text{feet-high} \times 4 \, \text{feet-long} = 8 \, \text{square feet} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3. Calculate the area of the unassigned area:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ \text{Area of the unassigned area} = 12 \, \text{feet-long} \times 9 \, \text{feet-high} = 108 \, \text{square feet} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 4. Calculate the area that needs to be painted:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ \text{Area of the wall} - \text{Area of the window} - \text{Area of the unassigned area} = 108 \, \text{square feet} - 8 \, \text{square feet} - 108 \, \text{square feet} = -8 \, \text{square feet} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Since the result is negative, it means Sandy does not need to paint the window because it is overlapping with the wall and is outside the area that needs to be painted. The total area that is being emptied by the window should be accounted for separately.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To calculate this individually:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ \text{Area cleaned by window} = 12 \, \text{feet-long} \times 9 \, \text{feet-high} = 108 \, \text{square feet} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m And subsequently:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ \text{Area that needs to be painted} = 9 \, \text{feet-high} \times 12 \, \text{feet-long} - 12 \, \text{feet-long} \times 9 \, \text{feet-high} = 108 \, \text{square feet} - 108 \, \text{square feet} = 0 \, \text{square feet} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Therefore, Sandy does not need to paint the wall due to the window. The final answer is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ \boxed{0} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
