[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To find the determinant of the product \(\mathbf{A} \mathbf{B}\), we use the property of determinants that states the determinant of the product of two matrices is the product of their determinants. Mathematically, this is expressed as:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \det(\mathbf{A} \mathbf{B}) = \det(\mathbf{A}) \cdot \det(\mathbf{B})
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Given:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \det(\mathbf{A}) = 4 \quad \text{and} \quad \det(\mathbf{B}) = -5
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Substitute these values into the formula:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \det(\mathbf{A} \mathbf{B}) = 4 \cdot (-5)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Now, perform the multiplication:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 4 \cdot (-5) = -20
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Therefore, the determinant of \(\mathbf{A} \mathbf{B}\) is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \boxed{-20}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
