[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Robert likes chocolate milk, so he decides to visit the milk bottling plant every day for a week to get the free samples. Unfortunately for him, the bottling plant sometimes bottles regular milk instead of chocolate milk, so each day the plant has a 2/3 chance of bottling chocolate milk. What is the probability that the bottling plant bottles chocolate milk exactly 4 of the 5 days he visits?
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To determine the probability that the bottling plant bottles chocolate milk exactly 4 out of 5 days, we can use the binomial probability formula. The binomial probability formula is given by:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ P(X = k) = \binom{n}{k} p^k (1-p)^{n-k} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m where:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - \( n \) is the number of trials (days),
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - \( k \) is the number of成功(成功 == 瓶奶瓶装的产品) successes,
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - \( p \) is the probability of success on an individual trial,
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - \( \binom{n}{k} \) is the binomial coefficient, calculated as \( \binom{n}{k} = \frac{n!}{k!(n-k)!} \).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m In this problem, \( n = 5 \), \( k = 4 \), and \( p = \frac{2}{3} \).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m First, we calculate the binomial coefficient:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ \binom{5}{4} = \frac{5!}{4!(5-4)!} = \frac{5!}{4!1!} = \frac{5 \times 4!}{4! \times 1} = 5 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Next, we calculate the probability:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ P(X = 4) = \binom{5}{4} \left( \frac{2}{3} \right)^4 \left( \frac{1}{3} \right)^{5-4} = 5 \left( \frac{2}{3} \right)^4 \left( \frac{1}{3} \right) = 5 \cdot \frac{2^4}{3^4} \cdot \frac{1}{3} = 5 \cdot \frac{16}{81} \cdot \frac{1}{3} = 5 \cdot \frac{16}{243} = \frac{80}{243} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Therefore, the probability that the bottling plant bottles chocolate milk exactly 4 of the 5 days he visits is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ \boxed{\frac{80}{243}} \]<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m [Ground Truth]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \frac{80}{243}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m [Is Boxed Matched]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m True
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m [Extracted Answer]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \frac{80}{243}
