[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To solve the expression \((x+3)(2x-4)(x-6)\), we can follow these steps:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. First, expand \((x+3)(2x-4)\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m (x+3)(2x-4) = x(2x) + x(-4) + 3(2x) + 3(-4) = 2x^2 - 4x + 6x - 12 = 2x^2 + 2x - 12
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. Next, multiply the result by \((x-6)\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
