[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Now, we substitute \(a + b + c = \frac{1}{2}\) and \(ab + bc + ca = -4\) into the identity for \(a^2 + b^2 + c^2\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m a^2 + b^2 + c^2 = (a+b+c)^2 - 2(ab + bc + ca)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m a^2 + b^2 + c^2 = \left(\frac{1}{2}\right)^2 - 2(-4)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
