[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \right)$. To multiply a scalar by a matrix, you multiply each element of the matrix by the scalar. Here, we need to multiply the scalar \(\frac{5}{2}\) by each element of the matrix \(\left(
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \begin{array}{ccc}
