[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To solve the expression \(9^3 + 3(9^2) + 3(9) + 1\), we will break it down step by step.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m First, we calculate each term separately:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. Calculate \(9^3\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 9^3 = 9 \times 9 \times 9 = 81 \times 9 = 729
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. Calculate \(3 \cdot 9^2\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 9^2 = 729
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3 \cdot 729 = 3 \times 729 = 2187
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3. Calculate \(3 \cdot 9\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3 \cdot 9 = 27
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Now, substitute these values back into the original expression:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 9^3 + 3(9^2) + 3(9) + 1 = 729 + 2187 + 27 + 1
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Next, we add these values together:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 729 + 2187 = 2916
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2916 + 27 = 2943
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2943 + 1 = 2944
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Therefore, the value of the expression \(9^3 + 3(9^2) + 3(9) + 1\) is \(\boxed{2944}\).<|endoftext|>
