[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To evaluate \(\left\lceil\sqrt{2}\,\right\rceil + \left\lceil\sqrt{22}\,\right\rceil + \left\lceil\sqrt{222}\,\right\rceil\), we need to compute each ceiling value separately and then sum them up. Let's start with each step.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. Compute \(\left\lceil\sqrt{2}\,\right\rceil\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - We need to find the integer part of \(\sqrt{2}\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - \(\sqrt{2} \approx 1.414\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - The integer part is 1, so \(\left\lceil\sqrt{2}\,\right\rceil = 1\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. Compute \(\left\lceil\sqrt{22}\,\right\rceil\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - We need to find the integer part of \(\sqrt{22}\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - \(\sqrt{22} \approx 4.695\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - The integer part is 4, so \(\left\lceil\sqrt{22}\,\right\rceil = 4\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3. Compute \(\left\lceil\sqrt{222}\,\right\rceil\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - We need to find the integer part of \(\sqrt{222}\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - \(\sqrt{222} \approx 14.87\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - The integer part is 14, so \(\left\lceil\sqrt{222}\,\right\rceil = 14\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Now, we sum these ceiling values:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \left\lceil\sqrt{2}\,\right\rceil + \left\lceil\sqrt{22}\,\right\rceil + \left\lceil\sqrt{222}\,\right\rceil = 1 + 4 + 14 = 19
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Therefore, the final answer is \(\boxed{19}\).<|endoftext|>
