[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To solve the functional equation \( xf(y) - yf(x) = f \left( \frac{x}{y} \right) \) for all positive real numbers \( x \) and \( y \), we will follow these steps:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. **Substitute \( x = y \):**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    xf(y) - yf(x) = f \left( \frac{x}{y} \right)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    Let \( f(x) = k \), where \( k \) is a constant. Then:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    xk - kyk = kf \left( \frac{x}{y} \right)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    Simplify the right-hand side:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    xk - kyk = k \left( x \cdot \frac{y}{k} - 1 \right)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    xk - kyk = k \left( x - 1 \right)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    Since \( xk - kyk = 0 \), we have:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    0 = k \left( x - 1 \right)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    This implies:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    x - 1 = 0
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    Hence, \( x = 1 \).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. **Substitute \( y = 1 \):**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    xf(1) - 1f(x) = f \left( \frac{x}{1} \right)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    Simplify the right-hand side:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    xf(1) - f(x) = f(x)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    Add \( f(x) \) to both sides:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    xf(1) = 2f(x)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    Since this must hold for all \( x \), we conclude:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    f(1) = 2f(x)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3. **Substitute \( x = 1 \) into the original functional equation:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    f(y) - yf(1) = f \left( \frac{1}{y} \right)
