[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m This equation can be rewritten as:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ x^2 - 16 = 0 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To find the values of \( x \), we can factor the left side of the equation:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ (x - 4)(x + 4) = 0 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m This gives us two possible solutions for \( x \):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ x - 4 = 0 \quad \text{or} \quad x + 4 = 0 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Solving these equations, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ x = 4 \quad \text{or} \quad x = -4 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The sum of all possible values of \( x \) is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ 4 + (-4) = 0 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Therefore, the sum of all possible values of \( x \) is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \boxed{0}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
