[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m A railroad trestle spans a gorge 80 feet wide and connects two cliffs at heights of 112 and 172 feet above the bottom of the gorge. A train is crossing this gorge from the higher cliff to the lower. When the front of the train has traveled $\frac{3}{4}$ of the trestle's length, how many feet is it above the bottom of the gorge?
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To determine how many feet above the bottom of the gorge the train is at the time the front of the train has traveled \(\frac{3}{4}\) of the trestle's length, we can follow these steps:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. **Identify the total length of the trestle:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \text{Total length of trestle} = 80 \text{ feet}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. **Determine the length of the first half of the trestle:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \text{Length of first half} = \frac{80}{2} = 40 \text{ feet}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3. **Find the position of the front of the train:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    The train is traveling \(\frac{3}{4}\) of the trestle's length. Therefore, the distance traveled by the front of the train \(d\) (in feet) at this point is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    d = \frac{3}{4} \times 40 = 30 \text{ feet}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 4. **Calculate how many feet above the bottom of the gorge the train is:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    The train starts at a height of 172 feet above the bottom of the gorge when it starts crossing the gorge. The top of the train will be 112 feet above this starting point. Therefore, the height the train is above the bottom of the gorge when it reaches the halfway point is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    172 - 112 = 60 \text{ feet}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Thus, the train is \(\boxed{60}\) feet above the bottom of the gorge when the front of the train has traveled \(\frac{3}{4}\) of the trestle's length.<|endoftext|>
