[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To simplify the given expression \(\cos^2 x + \cos^2 \left( \frac{\pi}{3} + x \right) + \cos^2 \left( \frac{\pi}{3} - x \right)\), we will use some trigonometric identities and properties of trigonometric functions.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m First, recall the trigonometric identity for the cosine of a sum and difference:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \cos(\alpha + \beta) = \cos \alpha \cos \beta - \sin \alpha \sin \beta \quad \text{and} \quad \cos(\alpha - \beta) = \cos \alpha \cos \beta + \sin \alpha \sin \beta
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Specifically, we use the identity:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \cos\left( \frac{\pi}{3} + x \right) = \cos \frac{\pi}{3} \cos x - \sin \frac{\pi}{3} \sin x = \frac{1}{2} \cos x - \frac{\sqrt{3}}{2} \sin x
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \cos\left( \frac{\pi}{3} - x \right) = \cos \frac{\pi}{3} \cos x + \sin \frac{\pi}{3} \sin x = \frac{1}{2} \cos x + \frac{\sqrt{3}}{2} \sin x
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Now, substitute these into the original expression:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \cos^2 x + \left( \frac{1}{2} \cos x - \frac{\sqrt{3}}{2} \sin x \right) + \left( \frac{1}{2} \cos x + \frac{\sqrt{3}}{2} \sin x \right)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Combine the like terms:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \cos^2 x + \frac{1}{2} \cos x + \frac{1}{2} \cos x - \frac{\sqrt{3}}{2} \sin x + \frac{\sqrt{3}}{2} \sin x
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m = \cos^2 x + \cos x
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m = \cos^2 x + \cos x + \cos x + \cos x
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m = \cos^2 x + \cos x + \cos x
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m = \cos^2 x + \cos x + \cos x
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m = \cos^2 x + \cos x + \cos x + \cos x
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m = \cos^2 x + \cos x
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Thus, the simplified form of the given expression is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \boxed{\cos^2 x + \cos x}
