[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To determine the number of integers within the range \((3\sqrt{5}, 5\sqrt{3})\), we need to first find the approximate values of these two expressions.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. Calculate \(3\sqrt{5}\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    3\sqrt{5} \approx 3 \times 2.236 = 6.708
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    The smallest integer greater than 6.708 is 7.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. Calculate \(5\sqrt{3}\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    5\sqrt{3} \approx 5 \times 1.732 = 8.66
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    The smallest integer greater than 8.66 is 9.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Now, we need to find the integers within the range of 7 to 9. The integers in this range are:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 7, 8, 9
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
