[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To compute \(\binom{17}{9}\), we will use the recursive definition of binomial coefficients and properties of factorials. Recall that for any integers \(a\) and \(b\), the binomial coefficient \(\binom{a}{b}\) is given by:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \binom{a}{b} = \frac{a(a-1)(a-2)\cdots(a-b+1)}{b!(a-b)!}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m We are given that \(\binom{15}{6} = 5005\) and \(\binom{15}{8} = 6435\). Using these, we can express \(\binom{17}{9}\) in terms of \(\binom{15}{7}\) and \(\binom{15}{7})\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \binom{17}{9} = \binom{17}{8} + \binom{17}{9}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Next, we need to find \(\binom{17}{8}\). Using the definition:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \binom{17}{8} = \frac{17 \cdot 16 \cdot 15 \cdot 14 \cdot 13 \cdot 12 \cdot 11 \cdot 10}{8! \cdot (17-8)!} = \frac{17 \cdot 16 \cdot 15 \cdot 14 \cdot 13 \cdot 12 \cdot 11 \cdot 10}{576 \cdot 9!} = \frac{17 \cdot 16 \cdot 15 \cdot 14 \cdot 13 \cdot 12 \cdot 11 \cdot 10}{576 \cdot 362880}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Calculate the numerator and the denominator:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
