[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m This graph shows the linear relationship between the time in seconds, $x$, for Caroline's walk and the distance in meters, $y$, Caroline is from her starting point. The graph passes through the point $(20,30)$. According to the graph, how many meters will Caroline walk in exactly one hour? [asy]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m pair A,B,C,D,E,F,G;
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m A=(-20,0);
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m B=(120,0);
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m C=(0,-20);
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m D=(0,120);
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m E=(-6.2,-8);
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m F=(60,90);
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m G=(70,105);
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
