[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Find the dot product of $\begin{pmatrix} 3 \\ -4 \\ -3 \end{pmatrix}$ and $\begin{pmatrix} -5 \\ 2 \\ 1 \end{pmatrix}.$
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To find the dot product of two vectors \(\mathbf{a} = \begin{pmatrix} 3 \\ -4 \\ -3 \end{pmatrix}\) and \(\mathbf{b} = \begin{pmatrix} -5 \\ 2 \\ 1 \end{pmatrix}\), we use the formula for the dot product of two vectors in \(\mathbb{R}^3\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \mathbf{a} \cdot \mathbf{b} = a_1 b_1 + a_2 b_2 + a_3 b_3
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Here, the components of \(\mathbf{a}\) are \(a_1 = 3\), \(a_2 = -4\), and \(a_3 = -3\), and the components of \(\mathbf{b}\) are \(b_1 = -5\), \(b_2 = 2\), and \(b_3 = 1\). Substituting these values into the dot product formula, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \mathbf{a} \cdot \mathbf{b} = (3)(-5) + (-4)(2) + (-3)(1)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Now, we perform the multiplications:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m (3)(-5) = -15
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m (-4)(2) = -8
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m (-3)(1) = -3
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Adding these results together gives:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m -15 + (-8) + (-3) = -15 - 8 - 3 = -26
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Therefore, the dot product of the vectors is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \boxed{-26}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
