[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To make pizza dough, Luca mixes 50 mL of milk for every 250 mL of flour. How many mL of milk does he mix with 750 mL of flour?
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Luca mixes 50 mL of milk for every 250 mL of flour. To find out how much milk he mixes with 750 mL of flour, we can set up a proportion.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \frac{50 \text{ mL}}{250 \text{ mL}} = \frac{x \text{ mL}}{750 \text{ mL}}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Here, \(x\) is the amount of milk he mixes with 750 mL of flour.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m First, solve for \(x\) by cross-multiplying:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 50 \text{ mL} \times 750 \text{ mL} = 250 \text{ mL} \times x \text{ mL}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 37500 \text{ mL}^2 = 250 \text{ mL} \times x
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Next, divide both sides by 250:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
