[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To determine the number of digits in the number \(2^3 \cdot 3^1 \cdot 4^3 \cdot 5^8\), we will first simplify the expression and then count the number of digits.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m First, simplify the expression step by step:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[2^3 = 8\]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[3^1 = 3\]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[4^3 = 64\]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[5^8 = 390625\]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m So, the expression becomes:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[2^3 \cdot 3^1 \cdot 4^3 \cdot 5^8 = 8 \cdot 3 \cdot 64 \cdot 390625\]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Next, calculate the value of this expression:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[8 \cdot 3 = 24\]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[24 \cdot 64 = 1536\]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[1536 \cdot 390625 = 604890000\]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Now, we need to count the number of digits in the number 604890000. We do this by finding the number of digits in the integer part of the number, which is 604890000 itself.
