[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Sandy plans to paint one wall in her bedroom. The wall is 9 feet high and 12 feet long. There is a 2-foot by 4-foot area on that wall that she will not have to paint due to the window. How many square feet will she need to paint?
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To determine how many square feet Sandy will need to paint, we need to follow these steps:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. **Calculate the area of the wall:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    The wall is 9 feet high and 12 feet long. The area \( A_{\text{wall}} \) of a rectangle is given by:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    A_{\text{wall}} = \text{height} \times \text{length} = 9 \, \text{feet} \times 12 \, \text{feet}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    A_{\text{wall}} = 108 \, \text{square feet}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. **Determine the area that does not need to be painted:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    The area that needs to be painted is the part of the wall that is not covered by the window. There is a 2-foot by 4-foot area except for the window. Therefore, the area of the area that does not need to be painted is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    A_{\text{not painted}} = \text{width} \times \text{length} = 2 \, \text{feet} \times 4 \, \text{feet}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    A_{\text{not painted}} = 8 \, \text{square feet}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3. **Calculate the area that needs to be painted:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    The area that needs to be painted is the total area of the wall minus the area that does not need to be painted:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    A_{\text{painted}} = A_{\text{wall}} - A_{\text{not painted}}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    A_{\text{painted}} = 108 \, \text{square feet} - 8 \, \text{square feet}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    A_{\text{painted}} = 100 \, \text{square feet}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Thus, the area Sandy will need to paint is \(\boxed{100}\) square feet.<|endoftext|>
