[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To find the measure of \(\angle CED\), we need to understand the geometric properties and angles involved in the given figure.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. **Identify Key Angles:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - \(AB\) is a diameter of the circle centered at \(O\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - \(E\) is a point on the circle such that \(AE\) is tangent to the circle at \(A\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - The tangent at \(B\) intersects the tangent at \(E\) and \(AE\) at \(C\) and \(D\), respectively.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - \(\angle BAE = 43^\circ\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. **Label the Angles:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - \(\angle BAE = 43^\circ\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - Since \(AE\) is tangent to the circle at \(A\), \(\angle AEB\) is a right angle (90°).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - \(\angle BEA\) is half of \(\angle BAE\) because angle \(EBA\) subtends the same arc as \(\angle BAE\) at the center.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3. **Calculate \(\angle BEA\):**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - \(\angle BEA = \frac{1}{2} \times 43^\circ = 21.5^\circ\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 4. **Determine \(\angle OBE\):**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - Since \(O\) is the center of the circle and \(AB\) is a diameter, \(\angle OBE\) is a right angle (90°).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 5. **Determine \(\angle AEB\):**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - \(\angle AEB = 43^\circ\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - Since \(\angle OBE\) is a right angle and \(\angle BEA\) is half of \(\angle BAE\), \(\angle AEB = 21.5^\circ\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 6. **Determine \(\angle AEC\):**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - \(\angle AOE = 90^\circ\) (because \(E\) is the tangent point and forms a right angle with the radius at \(E\)).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - \(\angle AEC = \angle AOE - \angle AEB = 90^\circ - 21.5^\circ = 68.5^\circ\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 7. **Determine \(\angle CED\):**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - \(\angle CED = \angle OBD - \angle CDE\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - Since \(D\) is a point directly opposite \(E\) on the circle, \(\angle OBD = 180^\circ - \angle OBE\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - \(\angle CDE = \angle OEB - \angle ODB\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - \(\angle ODB = 90^\circ - \angle AEB = 90^\circ - 21.5^\circ = 68.5^\circ\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - \(\angle CDE = 180^\circ - 68.5^\circ - 21.5^\circ = 88^\circ\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - \(\angle CED = 180^\circ - \angle CDE - \angle ODB = 180^\circ - 88^\circ - 68.5^\circ = 33.5^\circ\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Thus, the measure of \(\angle CED\) is \(\boxed{33.5}\).<|endoftext|>
