[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To determine how many natural numbers from 1 to 600 (inclusive) contain the digit 5 at least once, we can approach this problem by counting the total number of natural numbers from 1 to 600 and then subtracting the number of natural numbers that do not contain the digit 5 at all. There are 600 natural numbers in this range, so the number of natural numbers that do not contain the digit 5 at all is \(600 - 99 = 501\). Therefore, the number of natural numbers that contain the digit 5 at least once is \(600 - 501 = 99\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Here is the complete reasoning step-by-step:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. Calculate the total number of natural numbers from 1 to 600:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    600 - 1 = 599
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. Calculate the number of natural numbers from 1 to 600 that do not contain the digit 5 at all:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - This is equivalent to counting all natural numbers from 1 to 600 minus the 99 numbers that do not contain the digit 5.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    600 - 99 = 501
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3. The number of natural numbers from 1 to 600 that contain the digit 5 at least once is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    600 - 501 = 99
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Therefore, the final answer is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \boxed{99}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
