[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m In the triangular pyramid $P-ABC$, the side faces angle $PAB$ and $PBC$ are both equal to $60^{\circ}$. point $P$ lies on the surface of the right circular cone cut by water from a cup, and $PA$ and $PC$ are⊥the side faces $ABC$ and $PBC$ respectively. This water cone height $PA = PC = 2\sqrt{3}$ and $AB =$ $PC $-$ AC $=$ $2\sqrt{3}$. What is the maximum volume of the water cone?
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The problem can be approached by analyzing the geometry of the right circular cone and the triangular pyramid. The key points to consider are:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
