[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. **Proposition ②:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - We are given \(a = i\), \(b = -i\), and \(c = 1 - ai\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - The imaginary part of \(c = 1 - ai\) is \(0\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - This means \(b\) is purely imaginary, so \(b = 0\), and thus \(c\) is a real number.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - Therefore, \(c\) is not an imaginary number.
