[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - This means \(q\) is true when both parts of \(q\) are true. Therefore, \(q\) is false when both parts are false, which means \(p\) is false.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 4. **Proposition ④:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - The equation \(mx + 4y - 3m = 0\) can be rewritten as \(y = -\frac{m}{4}(x - 3)\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - The two-dimensional coordinate plane is bisectors of the angles formed by the lines \(y = -1\) and \(x = 0\).
