[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Find the value of $x$ for which the matrix
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[\begin{pmatrix} 1 + x & 7 \\ 3 - x & 8 \end{pmatrix}\]is not invertible.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To determine the value of \( x \) for which the matrix 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m A = \begin{pmatrix} 1 + x & 7 \\ 3 - x & 8 \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m is not invertible, we need to find when the determinant of \( A \) iszero. A matrix is not invertible if and only if its determinant is zero.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The determinant of a 2x2 matrix 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \begin{pmatrix} a & b \\ c & d \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m is given by \( ad - bc \). Applying this formula to our matrix \( A \), we have:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \det(A) = (1 + x)(8) - (7)(3 - x).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Simplifying the expression inside the determinant, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \det(A) = 8(1 + x) - 7(3 - x).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Expanding and simplifying further, we have:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \det(A) = 8 + 8x - 21 + 7x = 15x - 13.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Since the determinant is zero, the matrix \( A \) is not invertible when 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 15x - 13 = 0.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Solving for \( x \), we get:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 15x = 13 \implies x = \frac{13}{15}.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Therefore, the value of \( x \) for which the matrix is not invertible is
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \boxed{\frac{13}{15}}.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
