[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To calculate the sum \(1 + 3 + 5 + \cdots + 15 + 17\), we need to recognize that this is an arithmetic series. An arithmetic series is a sequence of numbers such that the difference of any two successive members is a constant.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m In this series:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - The first term \(a\) is \(1\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - The common difference \(d\) is \(2\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - The last term \(l\) is \(17\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The formula to find the sum \(S_n\) of the first \(n\) terms of an arithmetic series is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m S_n = \frac{n}{2} (a + l)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Here, \(n = 8\) (since the sequence has 8 terms), \(a = 1\), and \(l = 17\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Substituting these values into the formula, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m S_8 = \frac{8}{2} (1 + 17) = 4 \times 18 = 72
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Therefore, the sum \(1 + 3 + 5 + \cdots + 15 + 17\) is \(\boxed{72}\).<|endoftext|>
