[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To solve the given expression, we start with the definition of the tangent of an angle. Recall that the tangent of an angle in a right triangle is the ratio of the opposite side to the adjacent side. Specifically, for an angle \(\theta\),
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \tan \theta = \frac{\text{opposite}}{\text{adjacent}}.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m In this problem, \(\theta = 20^\circ\), so the sides of the right triangle are the sides it depicts. The sides are the opposite and adjacent to the 20-degree angle in an isosceles right triangle, where the opposite side is the hypotenuse and both adjacent sides are equal to the opposite side. This symmetry implies that the ratio of the sides \(2 \tan 20^\circ\) is always 1, regardless of the specific length of the opposite side. Therefore, we can write:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \tan^2 20^\circ = 1,
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \sin^2 20^\circ = 1.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Substituting these into the given expression, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \frac{\tan^2 20^\circ - \sin^2 20^\circ}{\tan^2 20^\circ \sin^2 20^\circ} = \frac{1 - 1}{1 \cdot 1} = \frac{0}{1} = 0.
