[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Three positive integers $a$, $b,$ and $x$ form an O'Hara triple $(a,b,x)$ if $\sqrt{a}+\sqrt{b}=x.$ For example, $(1,4,3)$ is an O'Hara triple because $\sqrt{1}+\sqrt{4}=3.$
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m If $(a,9,5)$ is an O'Hara triple, determine the value of $a.$
