[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To evaluate \(\left|\dfrac{2-4i}{2+i}\right|\), we can use the property of the modulus of a complex number. The modulus of a complex number \(\dfrac{a+bi}{c+di}\) is given by \(\dfrac{\sqrt{a^2 + b^2}}{\sqrt{c^2 + d^2}}\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Here, \(a = 2\), \(b = -4\), \(c = 2\), and \(d = 1\). So, the modulus is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \left|\dfrac{2-4i}{2+i}\right| = \dfrac{\sqrt{2^2 + (-4)^2}}{\sqrt{2^2 + 1^2}} = \dfrac{\sqrt{4 + 16}}{\sqrt{4 + 1}} = \dfrac{\sqrt{20}}{\sqrt{5}} = \dfrac{2\sqrt{5}}{\sqrt{5}} = 2
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Thus, the answer is \(\boxed{2}\).<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
