[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - The hundredths place is the next digit to the left of the decimal point. In 36.89753, it is the digit 9.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. **Determine whether to round up or down:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - According to rounding rules, if the digit in the hundredths place is 5 or greater, we round up the digit in the tenths place.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - If the digit in the hundredths place is less than 5, we leave the digit in the tenths place as it is.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3. **Apply the rounding rule:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - The digit in the tenths place is 8, which is greater than 5.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - Therefore, we round the digit in the tenths place up by 1, which means we round 8 to 9.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 4. **Replace all digits after the tenths place with zeros:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - After rounding, the number 36.89753 becomes 36.90.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m So, the number 36.89753 rounded to the nearest tenth is \boxed{36.9}.<|endoftext|>
