[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Find $A+B$ (in base 10), given the following addition problem  \[ \begin{array}{c@{}c@{\;}c@{}c@{}c@{}c}& & & 4 & A & B_{6}\\ &+& & & 4 & 1_{6}\\ \cline{2-6}& & & 5 & 3 & A_{6}\\ \end{array} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To find \( A + B \) where \( 4A + B_{6} = (4 \times 10 + 1) + (4 \times 1 + 1) \) and \( A \) and \( B \) are digits in base 6, we need to follow these steps:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. **Evaluate the right-hand side of the equation in base 10:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    (4 \times 10 + 1) + (4 \times 1 + 1) = 40 + 1 + 4 + 1 = 45
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    So, in base 10, we have:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    4A + B_{6} = 45
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. **Convert the number \( 45 \) from base 10 to base 6:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    To convert \( 45 \) to base 6, we repeatedly divide the number by 6 and keep track of the remainders:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \begin{aligned}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    45 \div 6 &= 7 \text{ remainder } 3 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    7 \div 6 &= 1 \text{ remainder } 1 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    1 \div 6 &= 0 \text{ remainder } 1 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \end{aligned}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    Reading the remainders from bottom to top, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    45_{10} = 113_6
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    So, \( A = 1 \) and \( B = 3 \).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3. **Calculate \( A + B \):**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    A + B = 1 + 3 = 4
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Therefore, the final answer is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \boxed{4}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
