[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To determine the number of ways to arrange the letters of the word "TOOT," we will use the formula for permutations of a multiset. The word "TOOT" contains the following letters: T, O, O, T.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The formula for the number of permutations of a multiset is given by:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \frac{n!}{n_1! \cdot n_2! \cdot \ldots \cdot n_k!}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m where \( n \) is the total number of items to arrange, and \( n_1, n_2, \ldots, n_k \) are the frequencies of the distinct items.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m For the word "TOOT":
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - \( n = 4 \) (total number of letters)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - \( n_1 = 2 \) (the letter O appears twice)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - \( n_2 = 1 \) (the letter T appears once)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Plugging these values into the formula, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \frac{4!}{2! \cdot 1!}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m First, calculate the factorial of 4 (the total number of letters):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 4! = 4 \times 3 \times 2 \times 1 = 24
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Next, calculate the factorials of the occurrences of each distinct item:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2! = 2 \times 1 = 2
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1! = 1
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Now, substitute these values back into the formula:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \frac{24}{2 \times 1} = \frac{24}{2} = 12
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Therefore, the number of ways to arrange the letters of the word "TOOT" is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \boxed{12}
