[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    The normal vector \(\bold{n}\) to the plane containing \(\bold{v}\) and \(\bold{w}\) can be found by taking the cross product of \(\bold{v}\) and \(\bold{w}\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \bold{n} = \bold{v} \times \bold{w}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    Calculating the cross product:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \bold{n} = \begin{vmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \mathbf{i} & \mathbf{j} & \mathbf{k} \\
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    2 & 3 & -1 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    2 & -1 & 0
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \end{vmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    Expanding the determinant:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \bold{n} = \mathbf{i} \left(3 \cdot 0 - (-1) \cdot (-1)\right) - \mathbf{j} \left(2 \cdot 0 - (-1) \cdot 2\right) + \mathbf{k} \left(2 \cdot (-1) - 3 \cdot 2\right)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \bold{n} = \mathbf{i} (0 - 1) - \mathbf{j} (0 + 2) + \mathbf{k} (-2 - 6)
