[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To find the inverse of the matrix \(\begin{pmatrix} 2 & 3 \\ -1 & 7 \end{pmatrix}\), we will use the formula for the inverse of a 2x2 matrix. For a matrix \(\begin{pmatrix} a & b \\ c & d \end{pmatrix}\), the inverse is given by:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \boxed{\frac{1}{ad - bc} \begin{pmatrix} d & -b \\ -c & a \end{pmatrix}}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Providing \(a = 2\), \(b = 3\), \(c = -1\), and \(d = 7\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \text{Ad - bc} = 2 \cdot 7 - 3 \cdot (-1) = 14 + 3 = 17
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m So the inverse matrix is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
