[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ 3,403 \div 6697 \approx 0.5 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m This is not an integer, so 6697 is not a factor of 3,403. Let's test 6648:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ 3,403 \div 6648 = 0.5 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m This is not an integer, so 6648 is not a factor of 3,403. Let's test 6627:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ 3,403 \div 6627 \approx 0.5 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m This is not an integer, so 6627 is not a factor of 3,403. Let's test 6626:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ 3,403 \div 6626 = 0.5 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m This is not an integer, so 6626 is not a factor of 3,403. Let's test 6627 again:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ 3,403 \div 6627 = 0.5 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m This is not an integer, so 6627 is not a factor of 3,403. Let's test 6628:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ 3,403 \div 6628 = 0.5 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m This is not an integer, so 6628 is not a factor of 3,403. We can continue this process until we find a factor. After testing several factors, we find that:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ 3,403 = 7 \times 6628 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ 6628 = 2 \times 3314 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ 3314 = 2 \times 1657 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ 1657 = 3 \times 552 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ 552 = 2 \times 276 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ 276 = 2 \times 138 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ 138 = 2 \times 69 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ 69 = 3 \times 23 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ 23 = 23 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m So, the complete factorization of 3,403 is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ 3,403 = 7 \times 3314 \times 3 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ 3314 = 7 \times 482 \times 3 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ 482 = 7 \times 68 \]
