[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \right.\] What is $f(f(f(17)))$?
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To solve \( f(f(f(17))) \), we need to evaluate the function \( f \) step by step. The function \( f \) is defined piecewise as follows:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m f(x) = \begin{cases} 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m x^2 - 4 & \text{if } x < 7, \\
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m x - 13 & \text{if } x \geq 7.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \end{cases}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m First, we need to find \( f(17) \). Since \( 17 \geq 7 \), we use the second part of the piecewise function:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m f(17) = 17 - 13 = 4.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Next, we need to find \( f(f(17)) = f(4) \). Since \( 4 < 7 \), we use the first part of the piecewise function:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m f(4) = 4^2 - 4 = 16 - 4 = 12.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Finally, we need to find \( f(f(f(17))) = f(f(4)) = f(12) \). Since \( 12 \geq 7 \), we use the second part of the piecewise function:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m f(12) = 12 - 13 = -1.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Thus, the value of \( f(f(f(17))) \) is \(\boxed{-1}\).<|endoftext|>
