[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    Simplify this congruence:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    4k + 1 \equiv 2 \pmod{5}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    Subtract 1 from both sides:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    4k \equiv 1 \pmod{5}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    To solve for \( k \), we need the multiplicative inverse of 4 modulo 5. The inverse of 4 modulo 5 is a number \( m \) such that:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    4m \equiv 1 \pmod{5}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    By testing values, we find that \( m = 4 \) because:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    4 \cdot 4 = 16 \equiv 1 \pmod{5}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    Therefore:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    k \equiv 4 \pmod{5}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    This means that \( k \) can be written in the form:
