[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    Simplify this congruence:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    4k + 1 \equiv 3 \pmod{7}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    Subtract 1 from both sides:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    4k \equiv 2 \pmod{7}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    To solve for \( k \), we need the multiplicative inverse of 4 modulo 7. The inverse of 4 modulo 7 is a number \( n \) such that:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    4n \equiv 1 \pmod{7}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    By testing values, we find that \( n = 2 \) because:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    4 \cdot 2 = 8 \equiv 1 \pmod{7}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    Therefore:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    k \equiv 2 \pmod{7}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    This means that \( k \) can be written in the form:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
