[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m We can use the identity \(\cos A \cos B = \frac{1}{2} [\cos (A+B) + \cos (A-B)]\) and \(\sin A \sin B = \frac{1}{2} [\cos (A-B) - \cos (A+B)]\) to simplify the expressions. However, a simpler approach is to recognize that the expression can be simplified by recognizing a trigonometric identity or by using known values of trigonometric functions.
