[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \text{Area of } e = 4 \times 4 = 16 \text{ square inches}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 4. **Determine the area of the square \(ABCD\):**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    The area of the square \(ABCD\) is given as 16 square inches. Therefore, the area of the square \(ABCD\) is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \text{Area of } ABCD = 16 \text{ square inches}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 5. **Calculate the area of the gray piece:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    The gray piece is the area of the square \(e\) minus the area of the square \(ABCD\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
