[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To find the new class mean, we need to calculate the average of the means of the two rounds of tests. The mean score of the first group of 30 students is given as 72%, and the mean score of the second group of 6 students is given as 78%.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The new class mean can be calculated as follows:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \text{New Class Mean} = \frac{72\% + 78\%}{6}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Let's calculate this step by step using Python.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m ```python
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m # Given scores
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m mean_1 = 72
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m count_1 = 30
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m mean_2 = 78
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m count_2 = 6
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m # Calculate the new mean
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m new_class_mean = (mean_1 + mean_2) / count_2
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m print(new_class_mean)
