[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m When 700 students from Genius M.S. played SCOOZ, 90$\%$ of them scored ''proficient or above.'' What number of students at Genius M.S. did not score ''proficient or above?''
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To find the number of students who did not score proficient or above, we need to first determine the number of students who scored proficient or above, then subtract that number from the total number of students.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. Calculate the number of students who scored proficient or above:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \text{Number of students who scored proficient or above} = 0.90 \times 700
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    0.90 \times 700 = 630
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    So, 630 students scored proficient or above.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. Subtract the number of students who scored proficient or above from the total number of students to find the number of students who did not score proficient or above:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \text{Number of students who did not score proficient or above} = 700 - 630
