[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To find the integer \( n \) such that \( -90 < n < 90 \) and \( \tan n^\circ = \tan 312^\circ \), we start by using the property of the tangent function, which states that \( \tan (180^\circ + \theta) = \tan \theta \). Therefore, we can write:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
