[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m However, the negative value does not affect our periodicity or the range of \( n \). So, the range of \( n \) is \( 0^\circ \leq n < 360^\circ \). But since we are given \( -90 < n < 90 \), we need to find the equivalent angle within the range \( 0^\circ \leq n < 60^\circ \) because \( 360^\circ - 90^\circ = 270^\circ \) is within our range.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Thus, \( n = 0^\circ \) or \( n = 60^\circ \). However, \( 60^\circ \) is not within the range \( -90 < n < 90 \). So, we need to re-evaluate the problem. The correct approach is to recognize that the tangent function has periods of \( 180^\circ \), but we need to find \( n \) within the given range.
