[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To determine the greatest number of police officers needed in Math City, we need to understand that each police officer at an intersection is limited to visiting two intersection streets. Therefore, the maximum number of police officers needed is limited by how many streets (or intersections) each street can be visited. 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Let's analyze the city's eight streets:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. Mathematics Street (MS)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. History Street (HS)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3. Science Street (SS)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 4. Art History Street (ASH)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 5. History of Science Street (HOS)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 6. Science of Mathematics Street (SOM)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 7. Mathematics of Science Street (MSO)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 8. History of Art Street (HAT)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The maximum number of police officers is achieved when each street can be visited once. So, in theory, each street can be visited by one police officer.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Therefore, the greatest number of police officers needed is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
