[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To determine the height of the enlarged logo, we need to use the principle of proportionality. The width of the logo remains the same, so we can set up a proportion to find the height.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. **Identify the given dimensions:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - Width of the logo: \(2 \text{ inches}\)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - Height of the logo: \(1.5 \text{ inches}\)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. **Set up the proportion:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    We know that the ratio of the width of the logo to the total width of the picture (2 inches for notebooks with a net width of 8 inches tall) should be equal to the ratio of the height of the logo to the total height of the picture (1.5 inches for notebooks with a net height of 1 inch). This can be written as:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \frac{2 \text{ inches}}{8 \text{ inches}} = \frac{1.5 \text{ inches}}{x}
