[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m If $\tan \alpha = 8$ and $\tan \beta = 7,$ then find $\tan (\alpha - \beta).$
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To find \(\tan(\alpha - \beta)\) given \(\tan \alpha = 8\) and \(\tan \beta = 7\), we can use the tangent subtraction formula:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \tan(\alpha - \beta) = \frac{\tan \alpha - \tan \beta}{1 + \tan \alpha \tan \beta}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Substitute the given values \(\tan \alpha = 8\) and \(\tan \beta = 7\) into the formula:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \tan(\alpha - \beta) = \frac{8 - 7}{1 + 8 \cdot 7}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Simplify the numerator:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \tan(\alpha - \beta) = \frac{1}{1 + 56} = \frac{1}{57}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Therefore, the value of \(\tan(\alpha - \beta)\) is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \boxed{\frac{1}{57}}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
