[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The first round of the 2010 FIFA World Cup consisted of several groups of four teams each. Within each group, each of the four teams played each other once. How many matches were there in each group?
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To determine the number of matches in each group of four teams, we start by noting that there are four teams in each group. The number of matches in a round-robin tournament where each team plays every other team exactly once is given by the combination formula \( \binom{n}{2} \), where \( n \) is the number of teams. Here, \( n = 4 \).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The formula for the combination of 4 items taken 2 at a time is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \binom{4}{2} = \frac{4!}{2!(4-2)!} = \frac{4!}{2!2!} = \frac{4 \times 3 \times 2 \times 1}{2 \times 1 \times 2 \times 1} = \frac{24}{4} = 6
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m So, the number of matches in each group is 6. Therefore, the final answer is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \boxed{6}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m [Ground Truth]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 6
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
