[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To determine how many more digits the base-3 representation of \(987_{10}\) has than the base-8 representation of \(987_{10}\), we will follow these steps:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. **Convert \(987_{10}\) to its base-3 representation.**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. **Convert \(987_{10}\) to its base-8 representation.**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3. **Compare the lengths of the two representations to find the difference in the number of digits.**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m ### Step 1: Convert \(987_{10}\) to its base-3 representation
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To convert \(987_{10}\) to base-3, we repeatedly divide the number by 3 and keep track of the remainders:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 987 \div 3 = 329 \quad \text{remainder} \quad 0
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 329 \div 3 = 109 \quad \text{remainder} \quad 2
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 109 \div 3 = 36 \quad \text{remainder} \quad 1
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 36 \div 3 = 12 \quad \text{remainder} \quad 0
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 12 \div 3 = 4 \quad \text{remainder} \quad 0
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 4 \div 3 = 1 \quad \text{remainder} \quad 1
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1 \div 3 = 0 \quad \text{remainder} \quad 1
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Reading the remainders from bottom to top, we get \(987_{10} = 1100021_3\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m ### Step 2: Convert \(987_{10}\) to its base-8 representation
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To convert \(987_{10}\) to base-8, we repeatedly divide the number by 8 and keep track of the remainders:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 987 \div 8 = 123 \quad \text{remainder} \quad 3
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 123 \div 8 = 15 \quad \text{remainder} \quad 3
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 15 \div 8 = 1 \quad \text{remainder} \quad 7
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1 \div 8 = 0 \quad \text{remainder} \quad 1
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Reading the remainders from bottom to top, we get \(987_{10} = 1733_8\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m ### Step 3: Compare the lengths of the two representations
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - The length of \(1100021_3\) is 7 (the number of digits).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - The length of \(1733_8\) is 4 (the number of digits).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The difference in the number of digits is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 7 - 4 = 3
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Thus, the base-3 representation of \(987_{10}\) has 3 more digits than the base-8 representation of \(987_{10}\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
