[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To determine the value of \( a \) that makes the system of equations have infinitely many solutions, we need to analyze both equations and find a common solution. The system of equations is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2x + 5y &= -8 \quad \text{(1)} \\
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 6x &= 16 + a - 15y \quad \text{(2)}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m First, we can solve equation (1) for \( x \):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2x + 5y = -8
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2x = -8 - 5y
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m x = -4 - \frac{5y}{2} \quad \text{(3)}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Now, substitute \( x = -4 - \frac{5y}{2} \) into equation (2):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 6\left(-4 - \frac{5y}{2}\right) = 16 + a - 15y
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m -24 - 15y = 16 + a - 15y
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Subtract \( -15y \) from both sides:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m -24 = 16 + a
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Subtract 16 from both sides:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m -40 = a
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Thus, the value of \( a \) that makes the system of equations have infinitely many solutions is:
