[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To find the projection of the vector \(\begin{pmatrix} 3 \\ 0 \end{pmatrix}\) onto the vector \(\begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ -3 \end{pmatrix}\), we can use the formula for the projection of one vector onto another:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \text{proj}_{\mathbf{a}} \mathbf{b} = \frac{\mathbf{a} \cdot \mathbf{b}}{\mathbf{a} \cdot \mathbf{a}} \mathbf{a}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Here, \(\mathbf{a} = \begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ -3 \end{pmatrix}\) and \(\mathbf{b} = \begin{pmatrix} 3 \\ 0 \end{pmatrix}\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m First, we need to compute the dot product \(\mathbf{a} \cdot \mathbf{b}\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \mathbf{a} \cdot \mathbf{b} = 2 \cdot 3 + (-3) \cdot 0 = 6 + 0 = 6
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Next, we need to compute the dot product \(\mathbf{a} \cdot \mathbf{a}\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \mathbf{a} \cdot \mathbf{a} = 2 \cdot 2 + (-3) \cdot (-3) = 4 + 9 = 13
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Now, we can substitute these values into the projection formula:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
