[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To determine the average disk space usage per hour of music in the library, we need to follow these steps:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. **Find the total disk space used by the library:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \text{Total disk space} = 16,000 \text{ megabytes}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. **Determine the number of days of music in the library:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \text{Number of days of music} = 12
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3. **Calculate the average disk space usage per hour by dividing the total disk space by the number of days of music:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \text{Average disk space per hour} = \frac{\text{Total disk space}}{\text{Number of days of music}} = \frac{16,000 \text{ megabytes}}{12} = \frac{16,000}{12} \approx 1,333.33 \text{ megabytes}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 4. **Round the result to the nearest whole number:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \boxed{1333}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Thus, the average disk space used by one hour of music in this library is \(\boxed{1333}\) megabytes.<|endoftext|>
