[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To determine the value of \( x \) in the UPC code equation where the sum of the digits in the odd positions \( n \), when multiplied by 3, is added to the sum of the digits in the even positions, and then the identity element for modular arithmetic (which is 10 modulo 10) is applied, the following steps will be taken:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. Identify the positions of the odd and even digits.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. Calculate the sum of these digits.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3. Multiply this sum by 3.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 4. Add the sum from step 3 to the sum of the digits in the even positions.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 5. Find the value of \( n \) such that \( n \) is divisible by 10 when considering the final result modulo 10.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Let's perform each step in detail:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. **Identify the positions of the odd and even digits:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - The odd positions are the first, third, fifth, etc.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - The even positions are the second, fourth, sixth, etc.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. **Calculate the sum of these digits:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    S = 1 \times \text{odd} + 2 \times \text{odd} + 3 \times \text{odd} + 4 \times \text{odd} + 5 \times \text{odd} + 6 \times \text{odd} + 7 \times \text{odd} + 8 \times \text{odd} = 45
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3. **Multiply this sum by 3:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    1 \times 3 + 2 \times 3 + 3 \times 3 + 4 \times 3 + 5 \times 3 + 6 \times 3 + 7 \times 3 + 8 \times 3 = 1 + 6 + 9 + 12 + 15 + 18 + 21 + 24 = 105
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 4. **Add the sum from step 3 to the sum of the digits in the even positions:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    1 + 3 + 7 + 0 + 9 = 20
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 5. **Find the value of \( n \) such that \( n \) is divisible by 10 when modulo 10:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - A number \( n \) is divisible by 10 if its last digit is 0.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - We need to check the values of \( n \) calculated here to see which one is divisible by 10.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - Here, \( n = 20 \). Check if 20 is divisible by 10:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      20 \div 10 = 2 \quad \text{(which is an integer)}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - Therefore, \( n = 20 \) is divisible by 10.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Since \( n = 20 \) is the only value that meets the criteria, the value of \( x \) is:
