[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To find the perimeter of the sector of the circle with radius 12 and a central angle of \(60^\circ\), we need to calculate the lengths of the two radii and the two segments of the arc that make up the sector. The arc length \(L\) of a sector with a central angle \(\theta\) in degrees is given by:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ L = \frac{\theta}{360^\circ} \times 2\pi r \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m where \(r\) is the radius of the circle. Here, the radius \(r = 12\) and the central angle \(\theta = 60^\circ\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m First, calculate the arc length of the sector:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ L = \frac{60^\circ}{360^\circ} \times 2\pi \times 12 = \frac{1}{6} \times 24\pi = 4\pi \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The two radii of the sector together add up to the circumference of the circle. The circumference \(C\) of the circle is given by:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ C = 2\pi r = 2\pi \times 12 = 24\pi \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m So, the perimeter of the sector is the sum of the arc length and the two radii:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ 4\pi + 24\pi = 28\pi \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Therefore, the perimeter of the sector of the circle with radius 12 is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ \boxed{28\pi} \]<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
