[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. Determine which container is selected.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. Calculate the probability of selecting a ball from each container that is green.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3. Sum the probabilities of selecting a green ball from each container.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m **Step 1: Determine the container selected.**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Container A holds 4 red balls and 6 green balls, so the probability of selecting a green ball from Container A is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \frac{6}{10} = \frac{3}{5}
