[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m A TV screen measures 24 by 16 inches. If each dimension is increased by 20$\%$, by what percent is the area increased?
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To determine by what percent the area of the TV screen is increased when each dimension is increased by 20%, we can follow these steps:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. **Calculate the new dimensions after the 20% increase in length and width:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - Original length: \(24\) inches
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - Increase in length: \(20\%\)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - Increase in width: \(20\%\)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \text{Increased length} = 24 + (0.20 \times 24) = 24 + 4.8 = 28.8 \text{ inches}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \text{Increased width} = 16 + (0.20 \times 16) = 16 + 3.2 = 19.2 \text{ inches}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. **Calculate the new area of the TV screen:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \text{New area} = \text{Increased length} \times \text{Increased width} = 28.8 \times 19.2
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    Performing the multiplication:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    28.8 \times 19.2 = 553.36
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3. **Calculate the original area of the TV screen:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \text{Original area} = 24 \times 16 = 384 \text{ square inches}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 4. **Determine the percent increase in area:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \text{Percent increase} = \left( \frac{\text{New area} - \text{Original area}}{\text{Original area}} \right) \times 100\%
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    Plugging in the values:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \text{Percent increase} = \left( \frac{553.36 - 384}{384} \right) \times 100\%
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \text{Percent increase} = \left( \frac{169.36}{384} \right) \times 100\%
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \text{Percent increase} = 0.435 \times 100\%
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \text{Percent increase} = 43.5\%
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Therefore, the area is increased by \boxed{43.5\%}.<|endoftext|>
