[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To find the polynomial \( p(x) \) that satisfies the equation \((x^2 - 3x + 5)p(x) = x^4 - 3x^3 + 15x - 25\), we start by expressing the polynomial \( p(x) \) in its factored form. Let \( x = y - 3 \). Substituting \( x = y - 3 \) into the equation, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m (x^2 - 3x + 5)(y - 3) = y^4 - 3y^3 + 15y - 25.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Next, we simplify the left-hand side of the equation:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m x^2 - 3x + 5 = (y - 3)^2 - 3(y - 3) + 5 = y^2 - 6y + 9 - 3y + 9 + 5 = y^2 - 9y + 23.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m So the equation becomes:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m (y^2 - 9y + 23)(y - 3) = y^4 - 3y^3 + 15y - 25.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m We expand the left-hand side:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m (y^2 - 9y + 23)(y - 3) = y^3 - 3y^2 + 23y - 9y^2 + 27y - 69 = y^3 - 12y^2 + 50y - 69.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m So the equation is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m y^3 - 12y^2 + 50y - 69 = y^4 - 3y^3 + 15y - 25.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m We rearrange all terms to one side of the equation:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m y^4 - 4y^3 + (50 + 3)y - (69 + 25) = 0,
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m which simplifies to:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m y^4 - 4y^3 + 53y - 94 = 0.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m This is a polynomial of degree 4. Therefore, the polynomial \( p(x) \) is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m p(x) = y^4 - 4y^3 + 53y - 94.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m However, \( y = 3 \) is the root of the polynomial \( p(x) \), which is consistent with the form of the polynomial being a degree 4 polynomial with a double root at \( x = 3 \) and a leading coefficient. Therefore, the polynomial \( p(x) \) is:
