[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m In right $\triangle ABC$, shown here, $AB = 15 \text{ units}$, $AC = 24 \text{ units}$ and points $D,$ $E,$ and $F$ are the midpoints of $\overline{AC}, \overline{AB}$ and $\overline{BC}$, respectively. In square units, what is the area of $\triangle DEF$?
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m [asy]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m size(150);
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m import olympiad;
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m pair A,B,C,D,E,F;
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m A = (0,0); B = (15, 0); C = (0, 24);
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m E = midpoint(A--B); D = midpoint(A--C); F = midpoint(B--C);
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m draw(A--B); draw(B--C); draw(C--A);
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m draw(D--F); draw(F--E); draw(E--D);
