[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To find the ordered pair \((r, k)\) that parameterizes the line \(y = 3x - 11\), we start with the given parametric form:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \begin{pmatrix} x \\ y \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} r \\ 1 \end{pmatrix} + t \begin{pmatrix} 4 \\ k \end{pmatrix}.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m This means that the coordinates \(x\) and \(y\) can be written as:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m x = r + 4t \quad \text{and} \quad y = 1 + kt.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
