[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Now, we substitute \(r = 4\) back into the equation for \(y\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m y = 1 + kt = 1 + 4k.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m We also know from the standard form of the line \(y = 3x - 11\), which is \(y = 3x - 11\), that the \(x\)-component of the first and second coordinates must be equal:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
