[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m What is the greatest common divisor of $1729$ and $1768$?
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To find the greatest common divisor (GCD) of \(1729\) and \(1768\), we can use the Euclidean algorithm. The Euclidean algorithm involves repeated division and taking remainders until we reach a remainder of \(0\). The last non-zero remainder is the GCD.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Here are the steps:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. Divide \(1768\) by \(1729\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    1768 = 1729 \cdot 1 + 39
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    The remainder is \(39\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. Now, replace \(1768\) with \(1729\) and \(1729\) with \(39\), and divide \(1729\) by \(39\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    1729 = 39 \cdot 44 + 17
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    The remainder is \(17\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3. Replace \(1729\) with \(39\) and \(39\) with \(17\), and divide \(39\) by \(17\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    39 = 17 \cdot 2 + 11
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    The remainder is \(11\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 4. Replace \(39\) with \(17\) and \(17\) with \(11\), and divide \(17\) by \(11\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    17 = 11 \cdot 1 + 6
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    The remainder is \(6\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 5. Replace \(17\) with \(11\) and \(11\) with \(6\), and divide \(11\) by \(6\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    11 = 6 \cdot 1 + 5
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    The remainder is \(5\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 6. Replace \(11\) with \(6\) and \(6\) with \(5\), and divide \(6\) by \(5\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    6 = 5 \cdot 1 + 1
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    The remainder is \(1\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 7. Replace \(6\) with \(5\) and \(5\) with \(1\), and divide \(5\) by \(1\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    5 = 1 \cdot 5 + 0
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    The remainder is \(0\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Since the last non-zero remainder is \(1\), the GCD of \(1729\) and \(1768\) is \(\boxed{1}\).<|endoftext|>
