[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To solve this problem, we need to find the number of real numbers \(x, y, z\) that satisfy the given system of equations. The system is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m x &= 2018 - 2019 \operatorname{sign}(y + z), \\
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m y &= 2018 - 2019 \operatorname{sign}(x + z), \\
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m z &= 2018 - 2019 \operatorname{sign}(x + y).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The sign function \(\operatorname{sign}(a)\) can be defined as follows:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \operatorname{sign}(a) =
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \begin{cases}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1 & \text{if $a > 0$}, \\
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 0 & \text{if $a = 0$}, \\
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m -1 & \text{if $a < 0$}.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \end{cases}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Let's express \(y\) and \(z\) in terms of the sign of \(x\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m y = 2018 - 2019 \operatorname{sign}(x + z),
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m z = 2018 - 2019 \operatorname{sign}(x + y).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m For each \(x\), both \(y\) and \(z\) are expressions involving the sign of \(x + z\) and \(x + y\), which is simply \(2018 - 2019 \operatorname{sign}(x + y)\). Therefore, \(y = 2018 - 2019 \operatorname{sign}(x + z)\) and \(z = 2018 - 2019 \operatorname{sign}(x + y)\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Given the complexity of the expressions, we will write a Python code to check all possible values of \(x\). However, directly handling the expression of \(\operatorname{sign}\) function for a large number of terms and solving the system separately could be computationally intensive. Instead, we will utilize a reasoning approach to find the solution.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m First, let's observe that for \(x \neq 0\), the expression \(2018 - 2019 \operatorname{sign}(x + y)\) will be non-zero only if \(\operatorname{sign}(x + y)\) is not equal to -1 when \(y = z\) and \(|y| > |z|\). This condition will ensure that \(y\) and \(z\) are distinct positive values.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Thus, we focus on \(x = 0\) and \(x \neq 0\). Let's break it down for \(x = 0\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
