[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Find the projection of the vector $\begin{pmatrix} 3 \\ 0 \end{pmatrix}$ onto the vector $\begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ -3 \end{pmatrix}.$
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To find the projection of the vector \(\mathbf{a} = \begin{pmatrix} 3 \\ 0 \end{pmatrix}\) onto the vector \(\mathbf{b} = \begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ -3 \end{pmatrix}\), we use the formula for the projection of \(\mathbf{a}\) onto \(\mathbf{b}\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \text{proj}_{\mathbf{b}} \mathbf{a} = \frac{\mathbf{a} \cdot \mathbf{b}}{\mathbf{b} \cdot \mathbf{b}} \mathbf{b}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m First, we calculate thedot product \(\mathbf{a} \cdot \mathbf{b}\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \mathbf{a} \cdot \mathbf{b} = \begin{pmatrix} 3 \\ 0 \end{pmatrix} \cdot \begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ -3 \end{pmatrix} = 3 \cdot 2 + 0 \cdot (-3) = 6
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Next, we calculate thedot product \(\mathbf{b} \cdot \mathbf{b}\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \mathbf{b} \cdot \mathbf{b} = \begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ -3 \end{pmatrix} \cdot \begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ -3 \end{pmatrix} = 2 \cdot 2 + (-3) \cdot (-3) = 4 + 9 = 13
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Now, we substitute these values into the projection formula:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \text{proj}_{\mathbf{b}} \mathbf{a} = \frac{6}{13} \begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ -3 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} \frac{6 \cdot 2}{13} \\ \frac{6 \cdot (-3)}{13} \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} \frac{12}{13} \\ -\frac{18}{13} \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Therefore, the projection of \(\begin{pmatrix} 3 \\ 0 \end{pmatrix}\) onto \(\begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ -3 \end{pmatrix}\) is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \boxed{\begin{pmatrix} \frac{12}{13} \\ -\frac{18}{13} \end{pmatrix}}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m [Ground Truth]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \begin{pmatrix} 12/13 \\ -18/13 \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m [Is Boxed Matched]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m True
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m [Extracted Answer]
