[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To solve the problem \(x = \left|2x - |60 - 2x|\right|\), we need to consider different cases based on the value of \(60 - 2x\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m First, let's simplify the expression inside the absolute value:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[60 - 2x \geq 0 \implies x \leq 30.\]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m So, for \(x \leq 30\), the expression inside the absolute value is non-negative, and we can drop the absolute value.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[x - |60 - 2x| \geq 0 \implies x - (60 - 2x) \geq 0 \implies x - 60 + 2x \geq 0 \implies 3x - 60 \geq 0 \implies x \geq 20.\]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Since \(x \leq 30\), this condition is always satisfied.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Now, let's analyze the expression \(2x - |60 - 2x|\) for different \(x\) in the interval \([20, 30]\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. When \(20 \leq x \leq 25\), \(|60 - 2x| = 2x - 60\), so the expression becomes:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[x - (2x - 60) = x - 2x + 60 = -x + 60.\]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. When \(25 < x \leq 30\), \(|60 - 2x| = 2x - 60\), so the expression becomes:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[x - (2x - 60) = x - 2x + 60 = -x + 60.\]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3. When \(x > 30\), \(|60 - 2x| = 2x - 60\), so the expression becomes:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[x - (2x - 60) = x - 2x + 60 = -x + 60.\]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m From these cases, we can see that the expression simplifies to:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[-x + 60\]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m for \(20 \leq x \leq 30\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Therefore, the solution to the equation \(x = \left|2x - |60 - 2x|\right|\) within the interval \([20, 30]\) is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[-20 + 60 = 40\]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m and
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[30 - 60 = -30.\]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The sum of all the solutions is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[40 - 30 = 10.\]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Thus, the sum of all the solutions is \(\boxed{10}\).<|endoftext|>
