[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m We want to find the sum of the series $S = 1 \cdot 2^2 + 2 \cdot 3^2 + 3 \cdot 4^2 + \cdots + 19 \cdot 20^2$.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To do this, we can use the formula for the sum of the squares of the first $n$ natural numbers:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m $$S = \frac{n(n+1)(2n+1)}{6}.$$
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m In this case, $n = 19$, so we have
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m $$S = \frac{19(19+1)(2 \cdot 19 + 1)}{6} = \frac{19 \cdot 20 \cdot 39}{6} = \boxed{11700}.$$
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m ####
