[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m A math textbook with a double-digit number of pages is split into sections. Each section is exactly $12$ pages long, with the exception of the epilogue, which is $11$ pages long. Every page belongs to a section. Furthermore, on the bottom of each $5$th page, a trivia fact is presented on the bottom of the page, starting from the fifth page. If a trivia fact appears on the bottom of the second-to-last page, then how many pages does the textbook have?
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To determine the total number of pages in the textbook, we need to analyze the structure of the text. The textbook has a double-digit number of pages, and it is structured as follows:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - Beginning of each section: 12 pages
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - Epilogue: 11 pages
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - Beginning of the second-to-last page: 5th page
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Let's denote the total number of pages in the textbook by \( N \).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m First, let's identify the position of the first question mark (the first page where a trivia fact appears on the bottom of the second-to-last page) and how that affects our calculation of \( N \).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Since the trivia fact appears on the bottom of the second-to-last page, we need to account for this fact in our calculation. Specifically, the first page where a trivia fact appears (i.e., the first page in the 12th section) can be classified as part of a section of 12 pages (since it's the first 12 pages of the part of the section that includes the trivia fact below it). This means the page immediately after it is part of this section. So, let's say the trivia fact appears immediately after the first page in the 12th section, which means the trivia fact is on page 14 (the 12th page of the 13th section).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m This leaves us with 8 pages to fill from the 13th (inclusive) to the 24th (inclusive) because the 15th page (the 13th last page) is not part of the trivia fact. This means the first 12 - 8 + 1 = 5 pages are occupied by the trivia fact, and we need to determine how many pages are left for the remaining 7 sections.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The remaining 7 - 5 = 2 pages are split between the first three sections. Each section has 12 pages, so the first section has \( 12 + 12 + 2 - (1 - 2) = 52 \) pages, the second section has \( 12 + 12 - 1 = 13 \) pages, and the third section has \( 12 + 1 + 2 = 15 \) pages.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Therefore, the total number of pages in the textbook is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ N = 11 \times 52 + 11 \times 13 + 11 \times 15 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ N = 572 + 143 + 165 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ N = 880 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m So, the total number of pages in the textbook is \(\boxed{880}\).<|endoftext|>
