[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m x = \frac{3 - 9}{2} = -3
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Since \( x \) is a positive integer, we have:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m x = 6
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Now, substitute \( x = 6 \) back into the equation \( y = x - 3 \):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m y = 6 - 3 = 3
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To verify, we check the product \( xy = 6 \times 3 = 18 \), which satisfies the condition.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Finally, the sum of the two integers is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m x + y = 6 + 3 = 9
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Thus, the sum of the two integers is:
