[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To find the units digit of the product of all odd integers between 0 and 12, we will follow these steps:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. Determine which numbers between 0 and 12 are odd.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. Compute the product of these odd numbers.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3. Identify the units digit of the resulting product.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m First, let's identify the odd numbers between 0 and 12. They are: 1, 3, 5, 7, 9, and 11. 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Next, we compute the product of these numbers:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1 \times 3 \times 5 \times 7 \times 9 \times 11
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m We can simplify this step-by-step:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1 \times 3 = 3
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3 \times 5 = 15
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 15 \times 7 = 105
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 105 \times 9 = 945
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 945 \times 11 = 10395
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m So, the product of all odd numbers from 0 to 12 is 10395.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Now, we need to find the units digit of 10395. The units digit of 10395 is 5.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Therefore, the units digit of the product of all odd integers between 0 and 12 is \(\boxed{5}\).<|endoftext|>
