[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m When the polynomial $p(x)$ is divided by $x - 1,$ the remainder is 3.  When the polynomial $p(x)$ is divided by $x - 3,$ the remainder is 5.  What is the remainder when the polynomial $p(x)$ is divided by $(x - 1)(x - 3)$?
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To find the remainder when the polynomial \( p(x) \) is divided by \((x - 1)(x - 3)\), we can use polynomial long division. The divisor is the product of two linear factors, and the remainder will be a linear polynomial of the form \( ax + b \).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Given:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m p(x) = q(x) \cdot (x - 1)(x - 3) + r(x)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m where \( r(x) \) is the remainder when \( p(x) \) is divided by \((x - 1)(x - 3)\), we need to determine the coefficients \( a \) and \( b \).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m From the problem, we know:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. When \( p(x) \) is divided by \( x - 1 \), the remainder is 3. Therefore, \( p(1) = 3 \).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. When \( p(x) \) is divided by \( x - 3 \), the remainder is 5. Therefore, \( p(3) = 5 \).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Since \( r(x) \) is a linear polynomial of the form \( ax + b \), we have:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m p(1) = a \cdot 1 + b = a + b = 3
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m p(3) = a \cdot 3 + b = 3a + b = 5
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m We now have a system of linear equations:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \begin{cases}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m a + b = 3 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3a + b = 5
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \end{cases}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To solve for \( a \) and \( b \), we can subtract the first equation from the second:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m (3a + b) - (a + b) = 5 - 3
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2a = 2
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m a = 1
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Substituting \( a = 1 \) back into the first equation:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1 + b = 3
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m b = 2
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Thus, the remainder \( r(x) \) when \( p(x) \) is divided by \((x - 1)(x - 3)\) is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m r(x) = x + 2
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Therefore, the remainder when \( p(x) \) is divided by \((x - 1)(x - 3)\) is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \boxed{x + 2}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m [Ground Truth]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m x + 2
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m [Is Boxed Matched]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m True
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m [Extracted Answer]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m x+2
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
