[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m How many feet long is the shadow of a 15-foot flagpole if a 5-foot woman standing at the base of the flagpole has a shadow that is six feet long?
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To determine the length of the shadow of a 15-foot flagpole when a 5-foot woman standing at the base of the flagpole has a shadow that is six feet long, we can use the concept of similar triangles. The proportion of the height of the flagpole to the length of its shadow will be the same for both the woman and the flagpole.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Let's denote the length of the shadow of the flagpole as \( s \) feet. According to the problem, the woman is 5 feet tall and her shadow is 6 feet long. The height of the flagpole is 15 feet. We can set up the following proportion:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \frac{\text{height of the flagpole}}{\text{length of the flagpole's shadow}} = \frac{\text{height of the woman}}{\text{length of the woman's shadow}}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Substituting the known values into the proportion, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \frac{15}{s} = \frac{5}{6}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To solve for \( s \), we can cross-multiply:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 15 \times 6 = 5 \times s
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 90 = 5s
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Next, we divide both sides by 5:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m s = \frac{90}{5} = 18
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Therefore, the length of the shadow of the flagpole is \(\boxed{18}\) feet.<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
