[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m If $n$ is an integer, what is the remainder when the sum of $7 - n$ and $n + 3$ is divided by $7$?
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To find the remainder when the sum of \(7 - n\) and \(n + 3\) is divided by 7, we can follow these steps:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. First, find the sum of the expressions \(7 - n\) and \(n + 3\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    (7 - n) + (n + 3) = 7 - n + n + 3 = 10
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    So, we have \(10\) to work with.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. Next, find the remainder when 10 is divided by 7. We can do this by performing the division:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    10 \div 7 = 1 \text{ remainder } 3
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    This means that \(10 = 7 \cdot 1 + 3\), so the remainder is 3.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Therefore, the remainder when the sum of \(7 - n\) and \(n + 3\) is divided by 7 is \(\boxed{3}\).<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
