[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - \( P \) is the set of boxes containing pencils.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - \( B \) is the set of boxes containing pens.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - \( B \cap P \) is the set of boxes containing both pens and pencils.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m From the problem, we know:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - The total number of boxes \( |P \cup B| = 10 \).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - The number of boxes containing pencils \( |P| = 6 \).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - The number of boxes containing pens \( |B| = 3 \).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - The number of boxes containing both pens and pencils \( |P \cap B| = 2 \).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Using the principle of inclusion and exclusion, we have:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ |P \cup B| = |P| + |B| - |P \cap B| \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
