[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To solve for \( p(7) \) given the polynomial \( p(x) = x^6 + ax^5 + bx^4 + cx^3 + dx^2 + ex + f \) and the values of the polynomial at specific points, we start by setting up the following system of equations based on the given values:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \begin{cases}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m p(1) = 1 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m p(2) = 2 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m p(3) = 3 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m p(4) = 4 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m p(5) = 5 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m p(6) = 6 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \end{cases}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Substitute \( x = 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6 \) into \( p(x) \):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \begin{cases}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1^6 + a \cdot 1^5 + b \cdot 1^4 + c \cdot 1^3 + d \cdot 1^2 + e \cdot 1 + f = 1 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2^6 + a \cdot 2^5 + b \cdot 2^4 + c \cdot 2^3 + d \cdot 2^2 + e \cdot 2 + f = 2 \\
