[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m If a school bus leaves school with 48 students on board, and one-half of the students get off the bus at each of the first three stops, how many students remain on the bus after the third stop?
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To solve this problem, we need to determine how many students remain on the bus after all three stops due to the first stop of half the students getting off. Then, we apply this calculation to the third stop.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. **Initial number of students on the bus:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    N_{\text{initial}} = 48
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. **First stop:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    N_{\text{students get off at the first stop}} = \frac{48}{2} = 24
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    N_{\text{remaining after the first stop}} = 48 - 24 = 24
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3. **Second stop:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    N_{\text{students get off at the second stop}} = \frac{24}{2} = 12
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    N_{\text{remaining after the second stop}} = 24 - 12 = 12
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 4. **Third stop:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    N_{\text{students get off at the third stop}} = \frac{12}{2} = 6
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    N_{\text{remaining after the third stop}} = 12 - 6 = 6
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Thus, the number of students remaining on the bus after the third stop is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \boxed{6}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
