[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m When Carlos divides his marbles into groups of six, seven, or eight, he has one marble left over. Assuming Carlos has more than one marble, what is the smallest possible number of marbles in Carlos's collection?
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Carlos has more than one marble, so let's denote the number of marbles Carlos has as \( N \). According to the problem, when Carlos divides his marbles into groups of 6, 7, or 8, he has one marble left over. This means that \( N \) satisfies the following congruence:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ N \equiv 1 \pmod{6} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ N \equiv 1 \pmod{7} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ N \equiv 1 \pmod{8} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m This means that \( N - 1 \) is a common multiple of 6, 7, and 8. The least common multiple (LCM) of 6, 7, and 8 is the smallest number that is a multiple of all three. To find the LCM, we note that the prime factorizations are:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ 6 = 2 \times 3 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ 7 = 7 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ 8 = 2^3 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The LCM is found by taking the highest power of each prime that appears in the factorizations:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ \text{LCM}(6, 7, 8) = 2^3 \times 3 \times 7 = 504 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Thus, \( N - 1 = 504k \) for some integer \( k \), so the smallest positive \( N \) is when \( k = 1 \):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ N = 504 + 1 = 505 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Therefore, the smallest possible number of marbles in Carlos's collection is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \boxed{505}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m [Ground Truth]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 169
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
