[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To find the least possible value of the expression \( |x - 1| + |x - 1.5| + |x - 2| \), we need to analyze the behavior of the absolute value function. The absolute value function changes its behavior at the points \( x = 1 \), \( x = 1.5 \), and \( x = 2 \). We will evaluate the expression for these points and test its validity to ensure it has no lower value.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. **Evaluate at \( x = 1 \):**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    |1 - 1| + |1 - 1.5| + |1 - 2| = 0 + 0.5 + 1 = 1.5
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. **Evaluate at \( x = 1.5 \):**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
