[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3. **Evaluate at \( x = 2 \):**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    |2 - 1| + |2 - 1.5| + |2 - 2| = 1 + 0.5 + 0 = 1.5
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Next, we will consider the value of the expression as \( x \) moves from 1 to 2. Since the absolute value function is non-negative and achieves its minimum value on any interval where it is defined, the minimum value of the expression occurs when \( x = 2 \).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Therefore, the least possible value of the expression \( |x - 1| + |x - 1.5| + |x - 2| \) is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \boxed{1.5}
