[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To find \(\cot \frac{3\pi}{2}\), first, we need to know the exact value of \(\cot \frac{3\pi}{2}\). The cotangent function, \(\cot x\), is the reciprocal of the tangent function, \(\tan x\). Therefore, we have:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \cot \frac{3\pi}{2} = \frac{1}{\tan \frac{3\pi}{2}}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m But we can also express \(\tan \frac{3\pi}{2}\) in terms of the unit circle. When \(x = \frac{3\pi}{2}\), the point on the unit circle corresponds to the negative x-axis. In the second quadrant, the tangent of an angle is negative. We know that:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \tan \frac{3\pi}{2} = -\tan \frac{\pi}{2} = 0
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Thus:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \tan \frac{3\pi}{2} = 0
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m So:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \cot \frac{3\pi}{2} = \frac{1}{0}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m This is undefined because division by zero is not allowed in mathematics. Therefore, the cotangent of \(\frac{3\pi}{2}\) is undefined. Hence, the final answer is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \boxed{\text{undefined}}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
