[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m So, the second inequality simplifies to:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ x < 4 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Combining the results from both inequalities, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ 9 < x < 4 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The integer values of \( x \) that satisfy this inequality are \( 10, 11, 12, \) and \( 13 \). To find the sum of these values, we add them together:
