[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To find the scalars \( p \) and \( q \) such that \(\mathbf{M}^2 = p \mathbf{M} + q \mathbf{I}\), we need to follow these steps:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. Compute \(\mathbf{M}^2\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. Compare it with the form \(p \mathbf{M} + q \mathbf{I}\) to identify \(p\) and \(q\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m First, we calculate \(\mathbf{M}^2\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \mathbf{M}^2 = \mathbf{M} \cdot \mathbf{M}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Given:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \mathbf{M} = \begin{pmatrix} 0 & -5 \\ -2 & 4 \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To compute \(\mathbf{M}^2\), we multiply \(\mathbf{M}\) by itself:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \mathbf{M}^2 = \begin{pmatrix} 0 & -5 \\ -2 & 4 \end{pmatrix} \cdot \begin{pmatrix} 0 & -5 \\ -2 & 4 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 0 \cdot 0 + (-5) \cdot (-2) & 0 \cdot (-5) + (-5) \cdot 4 \\ -2 \cdot 0 + 4 \cdot (-2) & -2 \cdot (-5) + 4 \cdot 4 \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \mathbf{M}^2 = \begin{pmatrix} 10 & -20 \\ -8 & 22 \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Next, we need to compare \(\mathbf{M}^2\) with the form \(p \mathbf{M} + q \mathbf{I}\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \mathbf{M}^2 = p \mathbf{M} + q \mathbf{I}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m We now equate this with:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \mathbf{M}^2 = p \mathbf{M} + q \mathbf{I}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \begin{pmatrix} 10 & -20 \\ -8 & 22 \end{pmatrix} = p \begin{pmatrix} 0 & -5 \\ -2 & 4 \end{pmatrix} + q \begin{pmatrix} 1 & 0 \\ 0 & 1 \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m This gives us two equations for each element of the matrix:
