[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To find the area of the circle circumscribed around an equilateral triangle with side lengths of 9 units each, we can follow these steps:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. **Determine the radius of the inscribed circle (inradius):**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    The radius \( r \) of the circumscribed circle (circumradius) of an equilateral triangle with side length \( s \) is given by:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    r = \frac{s \sqrt{3}}{6}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    Here, \( s = 9 \) units. Plugging in the value, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    r = \frac{9 \sqrt{3}}{6} = \frac{3 \sqrt{3}}{2} \text{ units}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. **Calculate the area of the triangle:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    The area \( A \) of an equilateral triangle with side length \( s \) is given by:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    A = \frac{s^2 \sqrt{3}}{4}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    For \( s = 9 \) units:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    A = \frac{9^2 \sqrt{3}}{4} = \frac{81 \sqrt{3}}{4} \text{ square units}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3. **Calculate the area of the circle:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    The area \( A_{\text{circle}} \) of a circle with radius \( r \) is given by:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    A_{\text{circle}} = \pi r^2
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    Substituting the value of \( r \):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    A_{\text{circle}} = \pi \left( \frac{3 \sqrt{3}}{2} \right)^2 = \pi \left( \frac{9 \cdot 3}{4} \right) = \pi \left( \frac{27}{4} \right) = \frac{27 \pi}{4} \text{ square units}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Therefore, the area of the circle is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \boxed{\frac{27 \pi}{4}}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m [Ground Truth]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 27\pi
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m [Is Boxed Matched]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m True
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m [Extracted Answer]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \frac{27\pi}{4}
