[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m What integer $n$ satisfies $0\le n<{101}$ and $$123456\equiv n\pmod {101}~?$$
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To solve the problem, we need to determine the integer \( n \) such that \( 0 \le n < 101 \) and \( 123456 \equiv n \pmod{101} \). This means that \( 123456 - n \) is divisible by 101.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m First, we find the remainder when 123456 is divided by 101. We can do this by performing the division:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ 123456 \div 101 = 1225 \text{ remainder } 1 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m This means that \( 123456 = 101 \cdot 1225 + 1 \), so
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ 123456 \equiv 1 \pmod{101} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Thus, \( n = 1 \).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Therefore, the integer \( n \) that satisfies the given conditions is
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \boxed{1}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
