[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To evaluate \(\lfloor 17.2 \rfloor + \lfloor -17.2 \rfloor\), we need to understand what the floor function \(\lfloor x \rfloor\) returns for a real number \(x\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. **Floor Function Definition**:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \(\lfloor x \rfloor\) is the greatest integer less than or equal to \(x\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. **Apply the Floor Function to Each Term**:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - For \(17.2\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      \lfloor 17.2 \rfloor = 17
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - For \(-17.2\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      \lfloor -17.2 \rfloor = -18
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3. **Sum the Values**:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \lfloor 17.2 \rfloor + \lfloor -17.2 \rfloor = 17 + (-18) = 17 - 18 = -1
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Therefore, the final answer is:
