[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To determine whether the curves \(C_1\) and \(C_2\) are independent for a vector-valued function, we need to check if the vector fields \(\vec{R}_1\) and \(\vec{R}_2\) are parallel. Two vector fields are parallel if their partial derivatives are proportional.
