[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The components of \(\vec{R}_2(t)\) relative to \(C_1\) are still \(\langle 4\cos t, \cos^2 t, 5\sin t, 6\cos^2 t \rangle\). Since \(\vec{R}^1(t_0) = \alpha \vec{R}_1(t_0)\), the curve \(C_1\) is independent of the curve \(C_2\) for all \(t \leq L\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m For \(t > L\), the components of \(\vec{R}^1(t_0)\) still satisfy the same system of equations, so \(\vec{R}^1(t_0)\) is independent of \(\vec{R}_2(t)\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
