[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m If $a @ b$ is defined as $a @ b$ = $3a - 3b$, what is the value of $3 @ 5$?
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To solve the problem, we need to determine the value of \(3 @ 5\) using the given definition \(a @ b = 3a - 3b\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m First, we substitute \(a = 3\) and \(b = 5\) into the expression \(3a - 3b\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3 @ 5 = 3(3) - 3(5)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Next, we perform the multiplications:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3(3) = 9 \quad \text{and} \quad 3(5) = 15
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m So, the expression becomes:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3 @ 5 = 9 - 15
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Finally, we perform the subtraction:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 9 - 15 = -6
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Therefore, the value of \(3 @ 5\) is \(\boxed{-6}\).<|endoftext|>
