[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m New York and Denver are in different time zones.  When it is noon in New York, it is 10 a.m. in Denver.  A train leaves New York at 2 p.m. (New York time) and arrives in Denver 45 hours later.  What time is it in Denver when the train arrives?
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To determine the time at which the train arrives in Denver, we need to follow these steps:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. **Calculate the train's travel time:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - The train leaves New York at 2 p.m. (noon in New York time).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - It arrives in Denver 45 hours later.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - Therefore, the train arrives at \( 2 \text{ p.m.} + 45 \text{ hours} = 6 \text{ p.m.} \).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. **Determine the train's arrival time in Denver:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - Since New York is 45 hours ahead of Denver, we need to subtract 45 hours from the arrival time in New York to find Denver's time.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - 6 p.m. in New York is equivalent to \( 6 \text{ p.m.} - 45 \text{ hours} = 6 \text{ p.m.} - 45 \text{ hours} = 7 \text{ p.m.} \).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m So, the time at which the train arrives in Denver is \(\boxed{7 \text{ p.m.}}\).<|endoftext|>
