[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To determine the number of distinct arrangements of the letters in the word "monkey," we need to calculate the number of permutations of the letters. The word "monkey" consists of 6 distinct letters: M, O, K, E, N, Y.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The formula to calculate the number of distinct permutations of a word with unique letters is given by:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ \text{Number of permutations} = \frac{6!}{n_1! \times n_2! \times \cdots \times n_k!} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m where \( n_1, n_2, \ldots, n_k \) are the counts of each distinct letter in the word.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m For "monkey":
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - The total number of letters is 6.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - The letter M appears 1 times.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - The letter O appears 1 time.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - The letter K appears 1 time.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - The letter E appears 1 time.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - The letter N appears 1 time.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - The letter Y appears 1 time.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Using the formula, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ \text{Number of permutations} = \frac{6!}{1! \times 1! \times 1! \times 1! \times 1! \times 1!} = \frac{720}{6} = 120 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Thus, the number of distinct arrangements of the letters in the word "monkey" is \(\boxed{120}\).<|endoftext|>
