[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To find the product of the greatest common divisor (GCD) and the least common multiple (LCM) of \(18\) and \(42\), we will follow these steps:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. **Calculate the GCD of \(18\) and \(42\):**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    The prime factorizations of \(18\) and \(42\) are:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    18 = 2 \times 3^2
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    42 = 2 \times 3 \times 7
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    The GCD is the product of the lowest power of all prime factors present in both numbers:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \text{GCD}(18, 42) = 2 \times 3 = 6
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. **Calculate the LCM of \(18\) and \(42\):**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    The prime factorizations of \(18\) and \(42\) are the same as above:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    18 = 2 \times 3^2
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    42 = 2 \times 3 \times 7
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    The LCM is the product of the highest power of all prime factors present in either number:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \text{LCM}(18, 42) = 2 \times 3^2 \times 7 = 2 \times 9 \times 7 = 126
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3. **Calculate the product of the GCD and the LCM:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \text{GCD}(18, 42) \times \text{LCM}(18, 42) = 6 \times 126
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    To find \(6 \times 126\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    6 \times 126 = 6 \times (120 + 6) = 6 \times 120 + 6 \times 6 = 720 + 36 = 756
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Therefore, the product of the GCD and the LCM of \(18\) and \(42\) is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \boxed{756}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
