[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Find the greatest common divisor of $2863$ and $1344$.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To find the greatest common divisor (GCD) of \( 2863 \) and \( 1344 \), we can use the Euclidean algorithm. The Euclidean algorithm involves repeated division until the remainder is zero. The divisor at that step will be the GCD.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Here are the steps:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. Divide \( 2863 \) by \( 1344 \) and find the remainder.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    2863 \div 1344 = 2 \quad \text{with a remainder of} \quad 2863 - 2 \cdot 1344 = 2863 - 2688 = 175
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    So, the remainder is \( 175 \).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. Now, we replace \( 2863 \) with \( 1344 \) and \( 1344 \) with \( 175 \), and repeat the process.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    1344 \div 175 = 7 \quad \text{with a remainder of} \quad 1344 - 7 \cdot 175 = 1344 - 1225 = 119
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    So, the remainder is \( 119 \).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3. Next, we replace \( 1344 \) with \( 175 \) and \( 175 \) with \( 119 \), and repeat the process.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    175 \div 119 = 1 \quad \text{with a remainder of} \quad 175 - 1 \cdot 119 = 175 - 119 = 56
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    So, the remainder is \( 56 \).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 4. Now, we replace \( 175 \) with \( 119 \) and \( 119 \) with \( 56 \), and repeat the process.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    119 \div 56 = 2 \quad \text{with a remainder of} \quad 119 - 2 \cdot 56 = 119 - 112 = 7
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    So, the remainder is \( 7 \).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 5. Now, we replace \( 119 \) with \( 56 \) and \( 56 \) with \( 7 \), and repeat the process.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    56 \div 7 = 8 \quad \text{with a remainder of} \quad 56 - 8 \cdot 7 = 56 - 56 = 0
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    So, the remainder is \( 0 \).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Since the remainder is now \( 0 \), the GCD is the last non-zero remainder, which is \( 7 \).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Therefore, the greatest common divisor of \( 2863 \) and \( 1344 \) is \(\boxed{7}\).<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
