[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m First, we calculate the length of side \(PQ\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m PQ = \sqrt{(28 - 0)^2 + (0 - 0)^2} = \sqrt{28^2} = 28
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Next, we calculate the length of side \(QR\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m QR = \sqrt{(8 - 28)^2 + (15 - 0)^2} = \sqrt{(-20)^2 + 15^2} = \sqrt{400 + 225} = \sqrt{625} = 25
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Finally, we calculate the length of side \(PR\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m PR = \sqrt{(8 - 0)^2 + (15 - 0)^2} = \sqrt{8^2 + 15^2} = \sqrt{64 + 225} = \sqrt{289} = 17
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The perimeter of \(\triangle PQR\) is the sum of the lengths of its sides:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m PQ + QR + PR = 28 + 25 + 17 = 60
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Thus, the perimeter of \(\triangle PQR\) is \(\boxed{60}\).<|endoftext|>
