[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To find the sum of the given matrices \(\begin{pmatrix} 1 & 5 \\ -2 & 4 \end{pmatrix}\) and \(\begin{pmatrix} 0 & -3 \\ 8 & -5 \end{pmatrix}\), we need to add the corresponding elements from each matrix.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Let's denote the first matrix as:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m A = \begin{pmatrix} 1 & 5 \\ -2 & 4 \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m and the second matrix as:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m B = \begin{pmatrix} 0 & -3 \\ 8 & -5 \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m We add the corresponding elements:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m A + B = \begin{pmatrix} 1 & 5 \\ -2 & 4 \end{pmatrix} + \begin{pmatrix} 0 & -3 \\ 8 & -5 \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Adding the elements one by one:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \begin{pmatrix} 1 & 5 \\ -2 & 4 \end{pmatrix} + \begin{pmatrix} 0 & -3 \\ 8 & -5 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 1 + 0 & 5 + (-3) \\ -2 + 8 & 4 + (-5) \end{pmatrix}
