[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m A rectangular room measures 12-feet by 6-feet. How many square yards of carpet are needed to cover the floor of the room?
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To determine the amount of carpet needed to cover the floor of the room, we can follow these steps:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. **Calculate the area of the room in square feet:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    The room measures 12 feet by 6 feet.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \text{Area} = \text{length} \times \text{width} = 12 \text{ feet} \times 6 \text{ feet} = 72 \text{ square feet}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. **Convert square feet to square yards:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    Since 1 yard is equivalent to 3 feet, 1 square yard is equivalent to \(3 \text{ feet} \times 3 \text{ feet} = 9 \text{ square feet}\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    To convert 1 square foot to square yards, we divide by 9:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \text{Area in square yards} = \frac{72 \text{ square feet}}{9 \text{ square feet per square yard}} = 8 \text{ square yards}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Therefore, the number of square yards of carpet needed to cover the floor of the room is \(\boxed{8}\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
