[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To solve the problem of finding the value of \(25_{10} + 36_{10}\) in base 3, we can follow these steps:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. **Add the binary numbers \(25_{10} + 36_{10}\):**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    25_{10} + 36_{10} = 61_{10}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    This is because when we add 25 and 36, we get 61.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. **Convert the resultant binary number \(61_{10}\) to base 3:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    To convert \(61_{10}\) to base 3, we need to divide 61 by 3 and keep track of the remainders.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - Divide 61 by 3: 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      61 \div 3 = 20 \quad \text{remainder} \quad 1
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - Divide 20 by 3:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      20 \div 3 = 6 \quad \text{remainder} \quad 2
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - Divide 6 by 3:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      6 \div 3 = 2 \quad \text{remainder} \quad 0
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - Finally, divide 2 by 3:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      2 \div 3 = 0 \quad \text{remainder} \quad 2
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    Reading the remainders from bottom to top, we get \(61_{10} = 2021_3\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Therefore, the value of \(25_{10} + 36_{10}\) in base 3 is \(\boxed{2021_3}\).<|endoftext|>
