[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To determine how many hours it takes for Stephan to write all possible rearrangements of his name, we first need to find the total number of possible rearrangements of his name, which is 26 letters. This can be calculated using the formula for permutations of a multiset:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \text{Number of rearrangements} = \frac{26!}{n! \times 2!}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m where \( n \) is the number of letters in the name. Here, \( n = 26 \), so we have:
