[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To determine the time in Denver when the train arrives, we need to follow these steps:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. **Convert the time in New York to Denver time:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - The train leaves New York at 2 p.m. (noon) and arrives at Denver 45 hours later.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - First, convert 45 hours to hours since midnight:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      45 \text{ hours} = 45 \times 60 = 2700 \text{ minutes}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - Since noon in New York is 12:00 p.m., which is 12:00 hours since midnight in Denver (reversing the clock):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      2700 \text{ minutes} = 2700 \div 60 = 450 \text{ minutes}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - Adding 2700 minutes to 2 p.m. (noon) in Denver:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      2:00 \text{ p.m.} + 450 \text{ minutes} = 2:00 \text{ p.m.} + 450 \text{ minutes} - 450 \text{ minutes} = 2:00 \text{ p.m.} + 450 \text{ minutes} = 2:45 \text{ p.m.}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - So, the train arrives at 2:45 p.m. in Denver.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. **Consider the time difference in Denver:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - Denver is 45 hours later than New York.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - If it's 2:45 p.m. in Denver, that's 0:45 p.m. in New York.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - Therefore, Denver is 45 hours later than New York.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Given this, the time in Denver when the train arrives is (00:45 p.m.).
