[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Recall that if $b$ is a residue $\pmod{m}$, then the modular inverse of $b$ is the residue $c$ for which $bc \equiv 1\pmod{m}$. The table below shows the inverses of the first 9 positive residues modulo 47.  \begin{tabular}{c|ccccccccc}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m $b$ & 1 & 2 & 3 & 4 & 5 & 6 & 7 & 8 & 9 \\ \hline
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m inverse of $\,b$ & 1 & 24 & 16 & 12 & 19 & 8 & 27 & 6 & 21
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \end{tabular}Find the modular inverse of $35\pmod{47}$.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Express your answer as an integer from $0$ to $46$, inclusive.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To find the modular inverse of \(35 \pmod{47}\), we need to find an integer \(x\) such that:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[35x \equiv 1 \pmod{47}\]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m This is equivalent to finding \(x\) such that:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[35x = 1 + 47k\]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m for some integer \(k\). This is a typical case of solving the linear Diophantine equation. We can use the Extended Euclidean Algorithm to find a solution.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m First, we apply the Euclidean algorithm to find the greatest common divisor (gcd) of 35 and 47:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[47 = 1 \cdot 35 + 22\]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[35 = 1 \cdot 22 + 13\]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[22 = 1 \cdot 13 + 9\]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[13 = 1 \cdot 9 + 4\]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[9 = 2 \cdot 4 + 1\]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[4 = 4 \cdot 1 + 0\]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The gcd is 1, and we can work backwards to express 1 as a combination of 35 and 47. Performing the reverse steps:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[1 = 9 - 2 \cdot 4\]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[4 = 13 - 1 \cdot 9\]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[13 = 22 - 1 \cdot 13\]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[22 = 35 - 1 \cdot 22\]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[35 = 47 - 1 \cdot 35\]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Substituting back:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[1 = 9 - 2 \cdot (13 - 1 \cdot 9) = 9 - 2 \cdot 13 + 2 \cdot 9 = 3 \cdot 9 - 2 \cdot 13\]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[1 = 3 \cdot (22 - 1 \cdot 13) - 2 \cdot 13 = 3 \cdot 22 - 15 \cdot 13\]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[1 = 3 \cdot 22 - 15 \cdot (4 - 1 \cdot 22) = 18 \cdot 22 - 15 \cdot 4\]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[1 = 18 \cdot (47 - 1 \cdot 35) - 15 \cdot 4 = 18 \cdot 47 - 18 \cdot 35 - 15 \cdot 4 = 18 \cdot 47 - 53 \cdot 4\]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Thus, we have:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[1 = 18 \cdot 47 - 53 \cdot 4\]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m This equation has been written as:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[1 = -53 \cdot 4 + 18 \cdot 47\]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m So, \(x = -53\) and \(18x \equiv 1 \pmod{47}\). Since we want a positive residue, we add 47 to \(-53\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[-53 + 47 = -6\]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Thus, the modular inverse of 35 modulo 47 is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[\boxed{-6}\]<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m [Ground Truth]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 43
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m [Is Boxed Matched]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m True
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m [Extracted Answer]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m -6
