[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To determine the value of \(x\) for which the expression \(\frac{x-3}{4x}\) is equal to zero, we need to find the values of \(x\) that make the numerator zero (provided the denominator is not zero).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. Set the numerator equal to zero:
