[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 240 = 5.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m This implies that the left-hand side is less than 5 when \(x\) is a root of the equation. To determine the nature of the roots, we need to find the values of \(x\) for which the equation holds true. We can use numerical methods or trial and error to find the roots. Let's test some values of \(x\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
