[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To find the vector on the line at \( t = 3 \), we need to determine the parametric form of the line and then use the given points to find the coordinates of the vector at \( t = 3 \).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The parametric form of a line passing through two points \(\mathbf{P}_1\) and \(\mathbf{P}_2\) with direction vector \(\mathbf{d}\) is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \mathbf{r}(t) = \mathbf{P}_1 + t \mathbf{d}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m where \(\mathbf{P}_1 = \begin{pmatrix} x_1 \\ y_1 \\ z_1 \end{pmatrix}\) and \(\mathbf{P}_2 = \begin{pmatrix} x_2 \\ y_2 \\ z_2 \end{pmatrix}\), and \(\mathbf{d} = \begin{pmatrix} d_1 \\ d_2 \\ d_3 \end{pmatrix}\).
