[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    0.\overline{15}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    The repeating part is "15".
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 4. **Identify the given position:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    We need to find the 92nd digit in the decimal part. Since the repeating part is "15", we can break it down into its first three digits:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    15 \overset{92}{\text{th frst digit}}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 5. **Count the total length of one repeating block:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    The repeating block "15" has a total length of:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    1 \text{ year} + 5 \text{ months} = 6 \text{ blocks}
