[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Testing \( x = -4 \):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m (-4)^3 + 5(-4)^2 - 12(-4) - 16 = -64 + 80 + 48 - 16 = 36 \neq 0
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Testing \( x = -2 \):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m (-2)^3 + 5(-2)^2 - 12(-2) - 16 = -8 + 20 + 24 - 16 = 20 \neq 0
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m We need to factor the polynomial further. By trying synthetic division or other methods, we find that \( x = -2 \) is a root. We can use polynomial division to factor out \( (x + 2) \).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Perform polynomial division of \( x^3 + 5x^2 - 12x - 16 \) by \( x + 2 \):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \begin{array}{r|rrrr}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m -2 & 1 & 5 & -12 & -16 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    &   & -2 & -8 & 16 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \hline
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    & 1 & 3 & -20 & 8 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \end{array}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The quotient is \( x^2 + 3x - 8 \), so we have:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m x^3 + 5x^2 - 12x - 16 = (x + 2)(x^2 + 3x - 8)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To find the roots of \( x^2 + 3x - 8 \), we solve:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m x^2 + 3x - 8 = 0
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Using the quadratic formula \( x = \frac{-b \pm \sqrt{b^2 - 4ac}}{2a} \):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m x = \frac{-3 \pm \sqrt{3^2 - 4(1)(-8)}}{2(1)} = \frac{-3 \pm \sqrt{9 + 32}}{2} = \frac{-3 \pm \sqrt{41}}{2}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m So the solutions to \( x^2 + 3x - 8 = 0 \) are \( x = \frac{-3 + \sqrt{41}}{2} \) and \( x = \frac{-3 - \sqrt{41}}{2} \).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Since \( p > q \), and we have the roots \( x = -2 \), \( x = \frac{-3 + \sqrt{41}}{2} \), and \( x = \frac{-3 - \sqrt{41}}{2} \), the value of \( p - q \) is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m p - q = \frac{-3 + \sqrt{41}}{2} - \left( -2 \right) - \frac{-3 - \sqrt{41}}{2} = \frac{-3 + \sqrt{41}}{2} + 2 + \frac{3 + \sqrt{41}}{2} = \frac{-3 + \sqrt{41} + 4 + 3 + \sqrt{41}}{2} = \sqrt{41}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Thus, the value of \( p - q \) is:
