[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To evaluate \(\sqrt{5 \cdot 10 \cdot 14 \cdot 21 \cdot 15 \cdot 20}\), we first simplify the expression inside the square root by expressing each number in terms of its prime factors:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[5 \cdot 10 = 5 \cdot 2 \cdot 5 \cdot 2 = 2 \cdot 5^2\]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[14 \cdot 21 \cdot 15 \cdot 20 = 7 \cdot 2 \cdot 3 \cdot 7 \cdot 5 \cdot 2 \cdot 5 \cdot 3 \cdot 5 = 2^3 \cdot 3^3 \cdot 5^3 \cdot 7^2\]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Now, we substitute these factorizations into the original expression:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[\sqrt{5 \cdot 10 \cdot 14 \cdot 21 \cdot 15 \cdot 20} = \sqrt{2 \cdot 5^2 \cdot 7 \cdot 5^3 \cdot 3^3 \cdot 5^3 \cdot 7^2} = \sqrt{(2 \cdot 7^2) \cdot (5^2 \cdot 3^3) \cdot (5^2 \cdot 7^2)} = \sqrt{2^1 \cdot 7^2 \cdot 5^4 \cdot 3^3 \cdot 7^2 \cdot 5^2 \cdot 7^2} = \sqrt{2^1 \cdot 7^{2+2} \cdot 5^{4+2} \cdot 3^3 \cdot 7^2 \cdot 5^2 \cdot 7^2} = \sqrt{2^4 \cdot 5^6 \cdot 7^5} = 2^2 \cdot 5^3 \cdot 7^2 \cdot \sqrt{5 \cdot 7} = 4 \cdot 5^3 \cdot 7^2 \cdot 7 \cdot \sqrt{35} = 4 \cdot 5^3 \cdot 7^3 \cdot \sqrt{35}.\]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Thus, the final answer is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[\boxed{4 \cdot 5^3 \cdot 7^3 \cdot \sqrt{35}}.\]<|endoftext|>
