[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m ```
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The roots of the polynomial equation \( t^3 - t^2 - 9t + 7 = 0 \) are:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ t = -1 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ t = 2 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ t = 3 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m These values of \( t \) correspond to crossing points of the curve. We need to find the corresponding \( x \)-coordinates for these points.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m For \( t = -1 \):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ x = (-1)^2 - 2 = 1 - 2 = -1 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ y = (-1)^3 - 9(-1) + 5 = -1 + 9 + 5 = 13 \]
