[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To solve the equation \(3^{x^2 + 4x + 4} = 9^{x + 2}\), we start by expressing both sides with the same base. Note that \(9 = 3^2\) and \(8 = 2^3\), so we can rewrite the right side of the equation:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[9^{x+2} = (3^2)^{x+2} = 3^{2(x+2)} = 3^{2x+4}\]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Now the equation becomes:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[3^{x^2 + 4x + 4} = 3^{2x + 4}\]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Since the bases are the same, we can set the exponents equal to each other:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[x^2 + 4x + 4 = 2x + 4\]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Next, we simplify this equation by subtracting \(2x + 4\) from both sides:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[x^2 + 4x + 4 - 2x - 4 = 0\]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[x^2 + 2x = 0\]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m We can factor out \(x\) from the left side:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[x(x + 2) = 0\]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m This gives us two solutions:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[x = 0 \quad \text{or} \quad x = -2\]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To find the sum of all possible values of \(x\), we add these solutions together:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[\boxed{0 + (-2)} = \boxed{-2}\]<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m [Ground Truth]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m -2
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m [Is Boxed Matched]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m True
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
