[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To find \( f(f(f(2))) \), we need to evaluate the function \( f \) three times starting from \( n = 2 \). Let's go through each step in detail.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m First, we need to evaluate \( f(2) \).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Since \( 2 < 4 \), we use the first case of the function definition:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
