[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To compute the product of the two matrices, we will multiply each element of the first matrix by the corresponding element of the second matrix, summing the results for each position. Let's denote the matrices as follows:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \mathbf{A} = \begin{pmatrix} 3a^2 - 3 & 3a \\ 2a^2 - a - 2 & 2a - 1 \end{pmatrix}, \quad
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \mathbf{B} = \begin{pmatrix} -1 & -3a - 2 \\ a & 3a^2 + 2a - 3 \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The product \(\mathbf{A} \mathbf{B}\) is given by the sum of the elements in the same positions of \(\mathbf{A}\) and \(\mathbf{B}\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \begin{pmatrix} 3a^2 - 3 & 3a \\ 2a^2 - a - 2 & 2a - 1 \end{pmatrix} \begin{pmatrix} -1 & -3a - 2 \\ a & 3a^2 + 2a - 3 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 3a^2 - 3(-1) + 3a(a) + (3a)^2 - 2(a^2) - 2(a) - 2 & 3a(-3a - 2) + 3a(a) + ((3a)(3a^2) + (3a^2)(2a) - 3(3a^2) - 3(2a) + 3(-2) + 1) \\ (2a^2 - a - 2)(-1) + (2a - 1)(a) + (2a^2 - (a) - 2)^2 & (2a^2 - a - 2)(-3a - 2) + (2a - 1)(a) + (2a^2 - a - 2)^2 \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Now, let's simplify each element step by step:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. The element in the first row, first column:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m (3a^2 - 3)(-1) + (3a)(a) + (3a)^2 - 2(a^2) - 2(a) - 2 = -3a^2 + 3 + 3a^2 + 9a - 2a^2 - 2a - 2 = -5a^2 + 7a + 1
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. The element in the first row, second column:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3a(-3a - 2) + 3a(a) + ((3a)(3a^2) + (3a^2)(2a) - 3(3a^2) - 3(2a) + 3(-2) + 1) = -9a^2 - 6a + 3a^2 + 9a^3 + 6a^2 - 9a^3 - 6a - 6 + 3(-2) + 1 = -6a^3 - 9a + 5
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3. The element in the second row, first column:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m (2a^2 - a - 2)(-1) + (2a - 1)(a) + (2a^2 - (a) - 2)^2 = -2a^2 + a + 2 + 2a^2 - a + 2 = 2
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 4. The element in the second row, second column:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m (2a^2 - a - 2)(-3a - 2) + (2a - 1)(a) + (2a^2 - a - 2)^2 = -6a^3 - 4a^2 + 3a^2 - a + 6 + 2a - a + 2 + 4a^2 - 2a - 2 + 4a^3 - 9a^2 - 4a + 4 + 8a^2 - 2a - 4
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m = 4a^3 - 10a^2 + 2a + 12
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m So, the product \(\mathbf{A} \mathbf{B}\) is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \begin{pmatrix} -5a^2 + 7a + 1 & 2 \\ 2 & 4a^3 - 10a^2 + 2a + 12 \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The final answer is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \boxed{\begin{pmatrix} -5a^2 + 7a + 1 & 2 \\ 2 & 4a^3 - 10a^2 + 2a + 12 \end{pmatrix}}
