[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To find the value of \(\frac{14!}{5!9!}\), we need to recognize that \(\frac{14!}{5!9!}\) can be simplifies as follows:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \frac{14!}{5!9!} = \frac{14 \times 13 \times 12 \times 11 \times 10 \times 9!}{5! \times 9!}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Notice that \(9!\) in the numerator and the denominator cancel each other out, leaving us with:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \frac{14 \times 13 \times 12 \times 11 \times 10}{5!}
