[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m So, the expression becomes:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \frac{14 \times 13 \times 12 \times 11 \times 10}{120}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Now, let's break this down step by step:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. Calculate the numerator:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 14 \times 13 \times 12 \times 11 \times 10
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. Calculate the denominator:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 120
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To simplify the calculation of the product of the numerator and the denominator, we can break it down further. Consider the prime factorization of each number:
