[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To find the greatest integer less than \(10.3^3\) without using a calculator, we will compute \(10.3^3\) step by step.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m First, let's calculate \(10.3^2\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 10.3^2 = 10.3 \times 10.3 = 106.09
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Next, let's calculate \(10.3^3\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 10.3^3 = 10.3 \times 106.09
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To make the multiplication easier, we can express 10.3 as \(1 + 0.3\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 10.3 = 10 + 0.3
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m So,
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 10.3^3 = (10 + 0.3)^3 = 10^3 + 3 \times 10^2 \times 0.3 + 3 \times 10 \times 0.3^2 + 0.3^3
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Now, compute each term:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 10^3 = 1000
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3 \times 10^2 \times 0.3 = 3 \times 100 \times 0.3 = 90
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3 \times 10 \times 0.3^2 = 3 \times 10 \times 0.09 = 2.7
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 0.3^3 = 0.3 \times 0.3 \times 0.3 = 0.027
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Add these terms together:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1000 + 90 + 2.7 + 0.027 = 1097.727
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m So, \(10.3^3 = 1097.727\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Now, we need to find the greatest integer less than \(10.3^3 = 1097.727\). Since \(1097.727\) is just slightly less than \(1098\), the greatest integer less than \(10.3^3\) is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \boxed{1097}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
