[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m How many miles can a car travel in 20 minutes if it travels $ \, \frac{3}{4} \, $ as fast as a train going 80 miles per hour?
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To determine how many miles a car can travel in 20 minutes when it travels at \(\frac{3}{4}\) of the speed of a train going 80 miles per hour, we can follow these steps:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. **Calculate the speed of the train:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    The train is going 80 miles per hour. Therefore, the speed of the train is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    80 \text{ miles per hour}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. **Calculate the speed of the car:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    The car travels at \(\frac{3}{4}\) of the speed of the train. So, the speed of the car is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \frac{3}{4} \times 80 \text{ miles per hour} = 60 \text{ miles per hour}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3. **Calculate the distance traveled by the car in 20 minutes:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    One minute is equal to \(\frac{1}{60}\) of an hour. Therefore, 20 minutes is equivalent to:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    20 \text{ minutes} \times \frac{1}{60} \text{ hours per minute} = \frac{20}{60} \text{ hours} = \frac{1}{3} \text{ hours}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 4. **Calculate the distance traveled by the car in \(\frac{1}{3}\) hours:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    Distance is calculated using the formula:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \text{Distance} = \text{Speed} \times \text{Time}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    Substituting the known values:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \text{Distance} = 60 \text{ miles per hour} \times \frac{1}{3} \text{ hours} = 20 \text{ miles}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Therefore, the car can travel \(\boxed{20}\) miles in 20 minutes.<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m [Ground Truth]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 20\text{ miles}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
