[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To find the value of \(x\) at the point of intersection of the lines \(y = 4x - 19\) and \(2x + y = 95\), we can follow these steps:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. **Solve the system of equations:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    y = 4x - 19
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    2x + y = 95
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. **Substitute the expression for \(y\) from the first equation into the second equation:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    2x + (4x - 19) = 95
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3. **Simplify and solve for \(x\):**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    2x + 4x - 19 = 95
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    6x - 19 = 95
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    6x = 95 + 19
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    6x = 114
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    x = \frac{114}{6}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    x = 19
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m So, the value of \(x\) at the point of intersection is \(\boxed{19}\).<|endoftext|>
