[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To find the sum of the coordinates of point \( B \), we start by using the midpoint formula. The midpoint \( M \) of a line segment with endpoints \( A(x_1, y_1) \) and \( B(x_2, y_2) \) is given by:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
