[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - The midpoint \( M \) is \( (1, -6) \).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - The coordinates of the endpoint \( A \) are \( (-2, 1) \).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Let the coordinates of point \( B \) be \( (x, y) \). Using the midpoint formula, we can set up the following equations based on the coordinates of \( A \) and \( M \):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
