[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1 = \frac{-2 + x}{2}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Multiply both sides by 2:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2 = -2 + x
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Add 2 to both sides:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m x = 4
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Next, solve for \( y \) from the second equation:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m -6 = \frac{1 + y}{2}
