[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m How many paths are there from $A$ to $C$, if every step must be up or to the right?[asy]size(4cm,4cm);int w=6;int h=5;int i;pen p=fontsize(9);for (i=0; i<h; ++i){draw((0,i) -- (w-1,i));}for (i=0; i<w; ++i){draw((i, 0)--(i,h-1));}label("A", (0,0), SW, p);label("C", (1,2), NE, p);label("B", (w-1,h-1), NE, p);[/asy]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To determine the number of paths from \( A \) to \( C \) using only moves to the right and up, we can think of this as a combinatorial problem. Specifically, we need to find the number of ways to arrange 3 right moves (\( R \)) and 3 up moves (\( U \)) in a sequence of 6 moves.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m This is a classic "stars and bars" problem in combinatorics. The number of ways to arrange \( k \) \( R \)'s and \( k \) \( U \)'s in a sequence of \( 2k \) moves is given by the binomial coefficient:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \binom{2k}{k}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m For our problem, \( k = 3 \) (since we need to make 3 moves to the right and 3 moves up), so we use the formula:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \binom{6}{3}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m We compute this as follows:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \binom{6}{3} = \frac{6!}{3!(6-3)!} = \frac{6!}{3!3!} = \frac{6 \times 5 \times 4 \times 3!}{3! \times 3 \times 2 \times 1} = \frac{6 \times 5 \times 4}{3 \times 2 \times 1} = \frac{120}{6} = 20
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Therefore, the number of paths from \( A \) to \( C \) using only moves to the right and to the right is \(\boxed{20}\).<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
