[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m How many miles can a car travel in 20 minutes if it travels $ \, \frac{3}{4} \, $ as fast as a train going 80 miles per hour?
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To determine how many miles a car can travel in 20 minutes if it travels \(\frac{3}{4}\) as fast as a train going 80 miles per hour, we need to follow these steps:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. **Calculate the speed of the train in miles per minute:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    The train is going 80 miles per hour. To find the speed in miles per minute, we divide the speed by 60 (since there are 60 minutes in an hour):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \text{Speed of the train} = \frac{80 \text{ miles per hour}}{60 \text{ minutes per hour}} = \frac{4}{3} \text{ miles per minute}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. **Determine the speed of the car:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    The car is traveling \(\frac{3}{4}\) as fast as the train. Therefore, the speed of the car is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \text{Speed of the car} = \frac{3}{4} \times \frac{4}{3} = 1 \text{ mile per minute}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3. **Calculate the distance the car can travel in 20 minutes:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    Distance is calculated by multiplying the speed by the time. The time in minutes is 20 minutes, so:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \text{Distance} = \text{Speed of the car} \times \text{Time} = 1 \text{ mile per minute} \times 20 \text{ minutes} = 20 \text{ miles}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Thus, the car can travel \(\boxed{20}\) miles in 20 minutes.<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m [Ground Truth]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 20\text{ miles}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
