[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ r \equiv (k^2) \mod 55025. \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m We need to find a value \( k \) such that \( k^2 \leq 20000 \). This means \( k \) must be an integer from 1 to 49 because \( 49^2 = 2401 \) and \( 50^2 = 2500 \). Therefore, \( r \) will fall into the range from 1 to 2401 when \( k = 1, 2, \ldots, 49 \). This implies that there are 49 possible values of \( r \) that satisfy the condition.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To find the remainder of \( r \) when divided by 55025, we need to find a perfect square \( r \) such that when divided by 55025, the remainder is one of the values from 0 to 5492, because \( 55025 = (55025 / n)^2 \) for some \( n \), and \( r \) must be less than 20000.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The possible values of \( r \) modulo 55025 are \( 0, 1, 2, \ldots, 5492 \). To find the remainder when \( r \) is divided by 55025, we need to find \( r \mod 55025 \). This can be done by taking the floor of \( r \mod 55025 \) because the remainder will be within the required range.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The value \( r \mod 55025 \) can be found by computing \( r \mod 55025 \) for \( r = k^2 \) where \( k = 1, 2, \ldots, 49 \). This is straightforward because \( k^2 \mod 55025 \) will be the remainder when \( 1^2, 2^2, \ldots, 49^2 \) is divided by 55025.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
