[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To find the surface area of the cylinder formed by rotating the curve \(y = r^2(x)\) about the \(y\)-axis, we need to use the formula for the surface area of a cylinder. The formula for the surface area of a cylinder is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ S = 2\pi \int_{a}^{b} r(x) h(x) \, dx \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m where \(r(x)\) is the radius of the cylinder and \(h(x)\) is the height of the cylinder, which in this case is \(y = r^2(x)\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Here, the radius \(r(x)\) is constant because the curve is a function only in the \(x\)-direction. Since \(r(x)\) is a constant, we can factor it out of the integral:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ S = 2\pi h(x) \int_{a}^{b} r(x) \, dx = 2\pi r(x) \int_{a}^{b} y \, \frac{dy}{dx} \, dx = 2\pi r(x) \int_{a}^{b} y^{2} \, dx \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Given the curve \(y = r^2(x)\), the height of the cylinder is \(r^2(b) - r^2(a) = r^2(b) - r^2(a)\). Therefore:
