[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ S = 2\pi r(x) r^2(b) \int_{a}^{b} dy \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Since \(r(x)\) is constant in \(x\), the integral \( \int_{a}^{b} dy = 0 \), so the surface area simplifies to:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ S = 2\pi r(x) r^2(b) \cdot 0 = 0 \]
