[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To determine how many kilograms of veal Alice should buy, we need to convert the number of pounds she wants to buy from kilograms to kilograms. We know that 1 kilogram is equal to 2.20 pounds. Therefore, to convert pounds to kilograms, we use the conversion factor 2.20.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Alice wants to buy 3 pounds of veal. We can calculate the weight in kilograms by multiplying the number of pounds by the conversion factor:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3 \text{ pounds} \times 2.20 \text{ pounds per kilogram} = 6.60 \text{ kilograms}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m So, Alice should buy \(\boxed{6.60}\) kilograms of veal.<|endoftext|>
