[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To simplify \((1 + \tan 20^\circ)(1 + \tan 25^\circ)\), we will use a trigonometric identity and some properties of symmetric angles. First, recall that for angles \(20^\circ\) and \(25^\circ\), the sum of these angles is \(45^\circ\). This means that \(\tan 20^\circ + \tan 25^\circ = \cot 45^\circ = 1\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m We can use the identity for the tangent of a sum:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \tan(A + B) = \frac{\tan A + \tan B}{1 - \tan A \tan B}.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m If \(A = 20^\circ\) and \(B = 25^\circ\), then
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \tan(20^\circ + 25^\circ) = \tan 45^\circ = 1.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Thus,
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1 = \frac{\tan 20^\circ + \tan 25^\circ}{1 - \tan 20^\circ \tan 25^\circ}.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m We can rearrange this equation to solve for \(\tan 20^\circ + \tan 25^\circ\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1 - \tan 20^\circ \tan 25^\circ = \tan 20^\circ + \tan 25^\circ.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To isolate \(\tan 20^\circ + \tan 25^\circ\), we can add \(1 - \tan 20^\circ \tan 25^\circ\) to both sides of the equation:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2 = \tan 20^\circ + \tan 25^\circ.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Therefore, the sum of \(\tan 20^\circ\) and \(\tan 25^\circ\) is 2. So, the expression \((1 + \tan 20^\circ)(1 + \tan 25^\circ)\) simplifies to:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m (1 + \tan 20^\circ)(1 + \tan 25^\circ) = 2 \cdot 1 = 2.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Thus, the simplified value is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \boxed{2}.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
