[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3. **Using Commutativity:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    We know that matrix multiplication is commutative, i.e., \(\mathbf{A}^2 = \mathbf{A} \mathbf{A}\). Therefore, we can express the trace of the square of the matrix as:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \operatorname{Tr}(\mathbf{A}^2) = \operatorname{Tr}((\mathbf{A} \mathbf{A})) = \operatorname{Tr}(\mathbf{A})(\mathbf{A}^2)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    Since \(\operatorname{Tr}(\mathbf{A})(\mathbf{A}^2) = \operatorname{Tr}(\mathbf{A})^2\) (because matrix multiplication and the trace operation are associative and commute), we have:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \operatorname{Tr}(\mathbf{A}^2) = (\operatorname{Tr}(\mathbf{A}))^2 = 2^2 = 4
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 4. **Setting Up the Equation:**
