[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The Senate has 100 members, 55 Republicans and 45 Democrats.  In how many ways can I choose a 5-person committee consisting of 3 Republicans and 2 Democrats?
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Certainly! To solve the problem of choosing a 5-person committee consisting of 3 Republicans and 2 Democrats from a group of 55 Republicans and 45 Democrats, we can use the concept of combinations. The number of ways to choose 3 Republicans from 55 and 2 Democrats from 45 is given by the combination formula:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \binom{n}{r} = \frac{n!}{r!(n-r)!}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m where \( n \) is the total number of items to choose from, \( r \) is the number of items to choose, and \( ! \) denotes factorial, which is the product of all positive integers up to that number.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m In this case, \( n = 55 \) and \( r = 3 \) (the number of Republicans to choose). So, we have:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \binom{55}{3} = \frac{55!}{3!(55-3)!} = \frac{55!}{3! \cdot 52!}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m We can simplify this by canceling out the \( 52! \) in the numerator and the denominator:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \binom{55}{3} = \frac{55 \times 54 \times 53 \times 52!}{3! \times 52!} = \frac{55 \times 54 \times 53}{3!}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Next, we calculate \( 3! \):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3! = 3 \times 2 \times 1 = 6
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m So, we have:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \binom{55}{3} = \frac{55 \times 54 \times 53}{6}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Now, we perform the multiplication and division:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 55 \times 54 = 2970
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2970 \times 53 = 167010
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \frac{167010}{6} = 27835
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Therefore, the number of ways to choose a 5-person committee consisting of 3 Republicans and 2 Democrats is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \boxed{27835}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m [Ground Truth]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 25,\!972,\!650
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
