[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Next, we need to factor the cubic polynomial \(-32x^3 + 17x^2 + 7x + 1\). We will use the Rational Root Theorem again. The possible rational roots are the factors of the constant term (1) divided by the factors of the leading coefficient (-32). Therefore, the possible rational roots are \(\pm 1, \pm \frac{1}{2}, \pm \frac{1}{4}, \pm \frac{1}{8}, \pm \frac{1}{16}, \pm \frac{1}{32}\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
