[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To solve for \( y \) in the equation \( x^3y - 2x^2y + xy = 101000 \) given that \( x = 101 \), we will follow a step-by-step approach.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m First, substitute \( x = 101 \) into the equation:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 101^3 y - 2 \cdot 101^2 y + 101 y = 101000
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Next, calculate \( 101^3 \) and \( 101^2 \):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 101^3 = 101 \cdot 101 \cdot 101
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 101^2 = 101 \cdot 101
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Now, calculate \( 2 \cdot 101^2 \):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2 \cdot 101^2 = 2 \cdot 101 \cdot 101 = 2 \cdot 101^2
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m So the equation becomes:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 101^3 y - 2 \cdot 101^2 y + 101 y = 101000
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Factor out \( y \) from the first three terms:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m y (101^3 - 2 \cdot 101^2 + 101) = 101000
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m This can be rewritten as:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m y (101^3 - 2 \cdot 101^2 + 101) = 101 \cdot 101000
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Since \( 101000 = 1010 \times 101 = 101 \times 101 \times 101 \), we can rewrite the equation as:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m y (101^3 - 2 \cdot 101^2 + 101) = 101 \times 101 \times 101
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To isolate \( y \), divide both sides by \( 101 \times 101 \):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m y = \frac{101 \times 101 \times 101}{101^3 - 2 \cdot 101^2 + 101}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Simplify the numerator and the denominator:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m y = \frac{101 \times 101 \times 101}{101 \left( 101^2 - 2 \cdot 101 + 1 \right)}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Factor out \( 101 \) from the denominator:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m y = \frac{101 \times 101 \times 101}{101} = 101 \times 101
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Thus, we have:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m y = 101^2
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Therefore, the value of \( y \) is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \boxed{10201}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
