[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m First, we find the greatest common divisor (gcd) of \(555\) and \(1\). Since \(555 = 3 \times 5 \times 41\) and neither \(3\), \(5\), nor \(41\) can divide \(1\), the gcd of \(555\) and \(1\) is \(1\). Therefore, there are no common multiples of \(1\) and \(5\) within \(555\).
