[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To determine the value of \( f(600) \), we start by using the given functional equation \( f(xy) = \frac{f(x)}{y} \) for all positive real numbers \( x \) and \( y \). Specifically, we will use the fact that \( f(500) = 3 \) to simplify our calculations.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m First, let's substitute \( x = 500 \) and \( y = 1 \) into the functional equation:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
