[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m However, this result doesn't make logical sense in the context of the problem because it would imply the tank is empty, which contradicts the given information that the water is currently 1/5 full. Let's re-evaluate the equation carefully.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The correct interpretation should be that when the tank is \(\frac{1}{5}\) full, 3 liters is added to the tank, so the new level is \(\frac{1 - 3}{4} = \frac{1}{4}\) full. Therefore, the capacity of the tank \( V \) can be rearranged to:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \frac{1}{4}V = \frac{1 - 3}{4} = \frac{-2}{4} = -\frac{1}{2}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
