[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To determine the most number of trading cards Jasmine can purchase, we need to divide her total amount of money by the cost of each card. Here are the steps:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. Identify the total amount of money Jasmine has: \$7.50.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. Identify the cost of each card: \$0.85.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3. Divide the total amount of money by the cost of each card to find out how many cards she can buy:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \frac{7.50}{0.85}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To make the division easier, we can multiply both the numerator and the denominator by 100 to eliminate the decimal:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \frac{750}{85} = \frac{750 \times 100}{85 \times 100} = \frac{75000}{8500}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Now, we perform the division:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 75000 \div 8500 = 9
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m So, Jasmine can buy \boxed{9} sets of trading cards.<|endoftext|>
