[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To find the value of \(5 \ast 2\) given the operation \(a \ast b = 3a + 4b - ab\), we will substitute \(a = 5\) and \(b = 2\) into the expression.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m First, we write down the expression we need to evaluate:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[5 \ast 2 = 3(5) + 4(2) - (5)(2)\]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Next, we perform the multiplications:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[3(5) = 15\]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[4(2) = 8\]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[(5)(2) = 10\]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Now, we substitute these values back into the expression:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[5 \ast 2 = 15 + 8 - 10\]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Finally, we perform the addition and subtraction from left to right:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[15 + 8 = 23\]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[23 - 10 = 13\]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Thus, the value of \(5 \ast 2\) is \(\boxed{13}\).<|endoftext|>
