[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m $P(x)$ is a polynomial such that when $P(x)$ is divided by $x-13$ the remainder is $19$, and when $P(x)$ is divided by $x+17$ the remainder is $-11$. What is the remainder when $P(x)$ is divided by $(x-13)(x+17)$?
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To determine the remainder when \( P(x) \) is divided by \((x-13)(x+17)\), we can use the properties of polynomials and the method of polynomial long division. The remainder theorem states that the remainder of the division of a polynomial \( P(x) \) by \((x-a)\) is \( P(a) \). Here, \( a = 13 \) and the remainder is 19 when \( P(x) \) is divided by \( x-13 \). So, \( P(13) = 19 \).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m When \( P(x) \) is divided by \( x+17 \), the remainder is \(-11\) when \( P(x) \) is divided by \( x+17 \). Therefore, the remainder when \( P(x) \) is divided by \((x-13)(x+17)\) is the same as the remainder when \( P(x) \) is divided by \((x-13)\) and by \((x+17)\), which is 19 and \(-11\), respectively. So, the remainder is \(19 - 11 = 8\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Thus, the remainder when \( P(x) \) is divided by \((x-13)(x+17)\) is \(\boxed{8}\).<|endoftext|>
