[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To find the possible values of the expression \(\frac{a}{|a|} + \frac{b}{|b|} + \frac{c}{|c|} + \frac{abc}{|abc|}\), we need to analyze each term separately and how they behave within the absolute value signs.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. \(\frac{a}{|a|}\)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - If \(a > 0\), then \(|a| = a\), so \(\frac{a}{|a|} = a\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - If \(a < 0\), then \(|a| = -a\), so \(\frac{a}{|a|} = -a\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - If \(a = 0\), then \(|a| = 0\), so \(\frac{a}{|a|} = \frac{0}{0}\), which is undefined.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. \(\frac{b}{|b|}\)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - If \(b > 0\), then \(|b| = b\), so \(\frac{b}{|b|} = b\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - If \(b < 0\), then \(|b| = -b\), so \(\frac{b}{|b|} = -b\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - If \(b = 0\), then \(|b| = 0\), so \(\frac{b}{|b|} = \frac{0}{0}\), which is undefined.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3. \(\frac{c}{|c|}\)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - If \(c > 0\), then \(|c| = c\), so \(\frac{c}{|c|} = c\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - If \(c < 0\), then \(|c| = -c\), so \(\frac{c}{|c|} = -c\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - If \(c = 0\), then \(|c| = 0\), so \(\frac{c}{|c|} = \frac{0}{0}\), which is undefined.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 4. \(\frac{abc}{|abc|}\)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - If \(a, b, c > 0\), then \(|abc| = abc\), so \(\frac{abc}{|abc|} = \frac{abc}{abc} = 1\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - If \(a, b, c < 0\), then \(|abc| = abc\), so \(\frac{abc}{|abc|} = \frac{abc}{abc} = 1\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - If \(a, b, c = 0\), then \(|abc| = 0\), so \(\frac{abc}{|abc|} = \frac{0}{0}\), which is undefined.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m From the above analysis, we see that the expression \(\frac{a}{|a|} + \frac{b}{|b|} + \frac{c}{|c|} + \frac{abc}{|abc|}\) simplifies to 3 when \(a, b, c > 0\), and it is undefined when \(a, b, c \leq 0\). Therefore, the expression can only take on the values \(\pm 3\) when \(a, b, c > 0\), which can be either \(\frac{3}{1}\) or \(-\frac{3}{1}\) or \(\frac{3}{-1}\) or \(-\frac{3}{-1}\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m However, since \(a, b, c\) are nonzero and cannot both be zero, the expression can only take on these values when one of them is positive and the others are negative, but the absolute value conditions make it undefined if all three positive are zero. Therefore, the expression can only take on the value \(\pm 3\).
