[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To find the value of the expression \(x^2 + 5x - 6\) when \(x = -1\), we will substitute \(x = -1\) into the expression and then simplify step by step.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. Start with the expression:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    x^2 + 5x - 6
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. Substitute \(x = -1\) into the expression:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    (-1)^2 + 5(-1) - 6
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3. Calculate \((-1)^2\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
