[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To find the quotient when \(x^5 + 7\) is divided by \(x + 1\), we can use polynomial long division or synthetic division. Here, I will use synthetic division for clarity.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Here are the steps for synthetic division:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. Write down the coefficients of the polynomial \(x^5 + 0x^4 + 0x^3 + 0x^2 + 0x + 7\). These are ±1, ±2, ±3, ±7.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. Write the root of the divisor \(x + 1\), which is \(-1\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3. Perform the synthetic division by \(x + 1\):
