[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m A squirrel travels at a constant 4 miles per hour. How long does it take for this squirrel to travel 1 mile? Express your answer in minutes.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To determine how long it takes for the squirrel to travel 1 mile, we start by using the formula for time, which is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ \text{Time} = \frac{\text{Distance}}{\text{Speed}} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Here, the distance the squirrel travels is 1 mile, and the speed is 4 miles per hour. Substituting these values into the formula, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ \text{Time} = \frac{1 \text{ mile}}{4 \text{ miles per hour}} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Performing the division, we find:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ \text{Time} = 0.25 \text{ hours} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To convert this time into minutes, we use the fact that there are 60 minutes in an hour. Therefore, we multiply the time in hours by 60:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ 0.25 \text{ hours} \times 60 \text{ minutes per hour} = 15 \text{ minutes} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Thus, the time it takes for the squirrel to travel 1 mile is \(\boxed{15}\) minutes.<|endoftext|>
