[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Evaluate $\lfloor6.7\rfloor+\lfloor-6.7\rfloor$.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To evaluate the expression \(\lfloor6.7\rfloor + \lfloor-6.7\rfloor\), we need to understand the behavior of the floor function. The floor function, denoted by \(\lfloor x \rfloor\), returns the greatest integer less than or equal to \(x\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m First, we find the integer part of 6.7:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \lfloor 6.7 \rfloor = 6
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m This is because 6 is the greatest integer that is less than or equal to 6.7.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Next, we find the integer part of -6.7:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \lfloor -6.7 \rfloor = -7
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m This is because -7 is the greatest integer that is less than or equal to -6.7.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Now, we add the integer parts together:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \lfloor 6.7 \rfloor + \lfloor -6.7 \rfloor = 6 + (-7) = 6 - 7 = -1
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Therefore, the final answer is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \boxed{-1}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
