[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      y = 1 \sin \theta + 1 \cos \theta
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 5. **Determine the angle \(\theta\):**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - Since the darker point is at \((1, 1)\), we need to find the angle \(\theta\) that, when rotated 90 degrees counterclockwise, maps the point to the darker half of the mirror.
