[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 6. **Calculate the angle:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - Rotating the point \((1, 1)\) 90 degrees counterclockwise around the origin brings it to the point \((1, -1)\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - So, we need to find the angle \(\theta\) such that:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      1 \sin \theta - 1 \cos \theta = 1
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      \]
