[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To calculate the sum \(1 \cdot 1 + 2 \cdot 2 + 3 \cdot 3 + \ldots + 100 \cdot 100\), we start by considering the pattern in the sequence. The \(n\)-th term of the sequence is \(n \cdot n\), which means the \(n\)-th term is simply \(n^2\). Therefore, the sum becomes:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1^2 + 2^2 + 3^2 + \ldots + 100^2
