[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The sum of the squares of the first \(n\) natural numbers is given by the formula:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \sum_{k=1}^n k^2 = \frac{n(n+1)(2n+1)}{6}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m In our case, \(n = 100\), so we substitute \(n\) into the formula:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \sum_{k=1}^{100} k^2 = \frac{100 \cdot 101 \cdot 201}{6}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Next, we calculate the product of the numbers:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 100 \cdot 101 = 10100
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 10100 \cdot 201 = 2020100
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Now, we divide by 6:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \frac{2020100}{6} = 336683.3333
