[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Given that the function $f(x) = \log_a(bx-c)$ ($a>0$ and $a\neq1$) is an odd function defined on $\mathbb{R}$, and is increasing on $(0, +\infty)$, with the smallest positive period of $f(x) - 2$ being 4:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. Find the values of $a$, $b$, and $c$;
