[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - \(\angle ABC = 71^\circ\)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - \(H\) is the orthocenter (the intersection point of the altitudes) of \(\triangle ABC\)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m First, we need to determine \(\angle ABC\). Since the sum of the angles in a triangle is \(180^\circ\),
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
