[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m How many miles can a car travel in 20 minutes if it travels $ \, \frac{3}{4} \, $ as fast as a train going 80 miles per hour?
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To determine how far a car can travel in 20 minutes when it travels at one-fourth the speed of a train that travels 80 miles per hour, we need to follow these steps:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. **Find the speed of the train:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    The train travels at 80 miles per hour.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. **Calculate the speed of the car:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    The car travels at one-fourth the speed of the train.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \text{Speed of the car} = \frac{80}{4} = 20 \text{ miles per hour}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3. **Determine the distance traveled by the car in 20 minutes:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    One hour is 60 minutes, so 20 minutes is \(\frac{20}{60}\) hours.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \text{Distance} = \text{Speed of the car} \times \text{Time} = 20 \text{ miles per hour} \times \frac{20}{60} \text{ hours}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    Simplify the fraction:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \frac{20}{60} = \frac{1}{3}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    Therefore:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \text{Distance} = 20 \times \frac{1}{3} = \frac{20}{3} \text{ miles}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 4. **Convert the distance to a decimal to match the format of the final answer:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \frac{20}{3} \approx 6.67 \text{ miles}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Thus, the car can travel approximately \(\boxed{\frac{20}{3}}\) miles in 20 minutes.<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m [Ground Truth]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 20\text{ miles}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m [Is Boxed Matched]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m True
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
