[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To convert the point \((-2, -2\sqrt{3}, -1)\) from rectangular coordinates to cylindrical coordinates, we need to use the following formulas:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. \( r = \sqrt{x^2 + y^2} \)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. \( \theta = \tan^{-1}\left(\frac{y}{x}\right) \)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3. \( z = z \)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Given the point \((-2, -2\sqrt{3}, -1)\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. Calculate \( r \):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m r = \sqrt{(-2)^2 + (-2\sqrt{3})^2} = \sqrt{4 + 12} = \sqrt{16} = 4
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. Calculate \( \theta \):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \theta = \tan^{-1}\left(\frac{-2\sqrt{3}}{-2}\right) = \tan^{-1}(\sqrt{3}) = \frac{\pi}{3}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3. The \( z \)-coordinate remains the same:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m z = -1
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m So, the cylindrical coordinates are:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m (r, \theta, z) = (4, \frac{\pi}{3}, -1)
