[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m What is $\dbinom{n}{1}$ for any positive integer $n$?
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To determine the value of \(\dbinom{n}{1}\) for any positive integer \(n\), we need to understand the definition of the binomial coefficient. The binomial coefficient \(\dbinom{n}{k}\) represents the number of ways to choose \(k\) elements from a set of \(n\) elements without regard to the order of selection. The formula for \(\dbinom{n}{k}\) is given by:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \dbinom{n}{k} = \frac{n!}{k!(n-k)!}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m In this problem, we need to find \(\dbinom{n}{1}\), which means we are choosing 1 element from a set of \(n\) elements. According to the formula for the binomial coefficient, \(\dbinom{n}{1} = \frac{n!}{1!(n-1)!} = \frac{n!}{1 \cdot (n-1)!} = \frac{n \cdot (n-1)!}{1 \cdot (n-1)!} = n\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Therefore, the value of \(\dbinom{n}{1}\) is \(n\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m So, the final answer is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \boxed{n}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m [Ground Truth]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m n
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m [Is Boxed Matched]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m True
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m [Extracted Answer]
