[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Let $a_1,a_2,\ldots$ be a sequence determined by the rule $a_n= \frac{a_{n-1}}{2}$ if $a_{n-1}$ is even and $a_n=3a_{n-1}+1$ if $a_{n-1}$ is odd. For how many positive integers $a_1 \le 2008$ is it true that $a_1$ is less than each of $a_2$, $a_3$, and $a_4$?
