[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To solve the equation \(\frac{9-4x}{x+6}=7\) for \(x\), we will follow these steps:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. **Eliminate the denominator**: To do this, we multiply both sides of the equation by \(x+6\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    9 - 4x = 7(x + 6)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. **Distribute the 7 on the right-hand side**: Expand the right-hand side.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    9 - 4x = 7x + 42
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3. **Move all terms involving \(x\) to one side**: To isolate \(x\), we move all terms involving \(x\) to one side of the equation. Subtract \(7x\) from both sides.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    9 - 4x - 7x = 42
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    Simplify the left-hand side.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    9 - 11x = 42
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 4. **Isolate the term with \(x\)**: Subtract 9 from both sides.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    -11x = 42 - 9
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    Simplify the right-hand side.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    -11x = 33
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 5. **Solve for \(x\)**: Divide both sides by \(-11\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    x = \frac{33}{-11}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    Simplify the fraction.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    x = -3
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Thus, the solution to the equation is \(\boxed{-3}\).<|endoftext|>
