[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To find the sum of the complex numbers \(1 + 3i\) and \(2 - 4i\), we need to add the real parts together and the imaginary parts together separately.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. Identify the real parts: \(1\) and \(2\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. Identify the imaginary parts: \(3i\) and \(-4i\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Now, we add the real parts:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[1 + 2 = 3\]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Next, we add the imaginary parts:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[3i + (-4i) = 3i - 4i = -i\]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Combining these results, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[3i + (-4i) = -i\]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Therefore, the sum of the complex numbers \(1 + 3i\) and \(2 - 4i\) is \(\boxed{-i}\).<|endoftext|>
