[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To determine when the ball hits the ground, we need to find the time \( t \) when the height \( y \) is zero. The given equation is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ y = -6t^2 - 10t + 56 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Setting \( y = 0 \):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ 0 = -6t^2 - 10t + 56 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m This is a quadratic equation in the standard form \( at^2 + bt + c = 0 \), where \( a = -6 \), \( b = -10 \), and \( c = 56 \). We can solve this quadratic equation using the quadratic formula:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ t = \frac{-b \pm \sqrt{b^2 - 4ac}}{2a} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m First, we calculate the discriminant \( \Delta \):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ \Delta = b^2 - 4ac \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ \Delta = (-10)^2 - 4(-6)(56) \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ \Delta = 100 + 1344 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ \Delta = 1444 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Next, we find the roots of the quadratic equation:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ t = \frac{-(-10) \pm \sqrt{1444}}{2(-6)} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ t = \frac{10 \pm \sqrt{1444}}{-12} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m We simplify \( \sqrt{1444} \):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ \sqrt{1444} = 2\sqrt{361} = 2 \times 19 = 38 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m So the roots are:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ t = \frac{10 \pm 38}{-12} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m This gives us two solutions:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ t = \frac{10 + 38}{-12} = \frac{48}{-12} = -4 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ t = \frac{10 - 38}{-12} = \frac{-28}{-12} = \frac{7}{3} \approx 2.33 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Since time cannot be negative, we discard the negative solution. Therefore, the ball hits the ground in the first 2.33 seconds.
