[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Calculate the determinant of the following matrix:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \left[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \begin{array}{ccc}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m -\frac{8}{5} & -\frac{19}{5} & -\frac{16}{5} \\
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \frac{23}{5} & 4 & -\frac{19}{5} \\
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \frac{17}{5} & \frac{12}{5} & 5 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \end{array}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \right]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To calculate the determinant of the given \(3 \times 3\) matrix, we will use the cofactor expansion along the first row. The matrix is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m A = \left[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \begin{array}{ccc}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m -\frac{8}{5} & -\frac{19}{5} & -\frac{16}{5} \\
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \frac{23}{5} & 4 & -\frac{19}{5} \\
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \frac{17}{5} & \frac{12}{5} & 5 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \end{array}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \right]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The determinant of \(A\) is given by:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \det(A) = -\frac{8}{5} \det\left[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \begin{array}{cc}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 4 & -\frac{19}{5} \\
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \frac{12}{5} & 5 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \end{array}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \right]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - \left(-\frac{19}{5}\right) \det\left[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \begin{array}{cc}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \frac{23}{5} & -\frac{19}{5} \\
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \frac{17}{5} & 5 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \end{array}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \right]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - \left(-\frac{16}{5}\right) \det\left[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \begin{array}{cc}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \frac{23}{5} & 4 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \frac{17}{5} & \frac{12}{5} \\
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \end{array}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \right]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m We need to calculate the determinants of the \(2 \times 2\) matrices:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \det\left[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \begin{array}{cc}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 4 & -\frac{19}{5} \\
