[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m An angle measures $\frac{9 \pi }{20}$ radians. Find the values of the trigonometric functions for this angle.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To find the values of the trigonometric functions for the angle \(\frac{9\pi}{20}\) radians, we will follow these steps:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. **Determine the reference angle:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    The reference angle is the positive angle that the terminal side of the given angle makes with the x-axis. Since \(\frac{9\pi}{20}\) is in the first quadrant, the reference angle is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \left| \frac{9\pi}{20} - \pi \right| = \left| \frac{9\pi}{20} - \frac{20\pi}{20} \right| = \left| -\frac{11\pi}{20} \right| = \frac{11\pi}{20}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    The reference angle \(\alpha\) is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \alpha = \pi - \frac{9\pi}{20} = \frac{20\pi}{20} - \frac{9\pi}{20} = \frac{11\pi}{20}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. **Use the known values:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    The sine and cosine functions for the reference angle \(\alpha = \frac{11\pi}{20}\) are:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \sin \left( \frac{11\pi}{20} \right) = \sin \left( \pi - \frac{\pi}{20} \right) = \sin \left( \frac{\pi}{20} \right)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \cos \left( \frac{11\pi}{20} \right) = \cos \left( \pi - \frac{\pi}{20} \right) = -\cos \left( \frac{\pi}{20} \right)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3. **Calculate the trigonometric functions:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    Using approximations and the known values:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \sin \left( \frac{9\pi}{20} \right) \approx 0.9511
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \cos \left( \frac{9\pi}{20} \right) \approx 0.4848
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \sin \left( \frac{\pi}{20} \right) \approx 0.1564
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \cos \left( \frac{\pi}{20} \right) \approx 0.9848
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 4. **Summarize the results:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    The values of the trigonometric functions for the angle \(\frac{9\pi}{20}\) are:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \sin \left( \frac{9\pi}{20} \right) \approx 0.9511
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \cos \left( \frac{9\pi}{20} \right) \approx 0.4848
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \sin \left( \frac{\pi}{20} \right) \approx 0.1564
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Thus, the final answer is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \boxed{\sin \left( \frac{9\pi}{20} \right) \approx 0.9511, \quad \cos \left( \frac{9\pi}{20} \right) \approx 0.4848, \quad \sin \left( \frac{\pi}{20} \right) \approx 0.1564}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
