[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To simplify the expression \(i^0 + i^1 + i^2 + i^3 + \cdots + i^{2009}\), we need to understand the pattern of the powers of the imaginary unit \(i\). The powers of \(i\) repeat every four terms:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \begin{aligned}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m i^0 &= 1, \\
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m i^1 &= i, \\
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m i^2 &= -1, \\
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m i^3 &= -i, \\
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m i^4 &= 1, \\
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m i^5 &= i, \\
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m i^6 &= -1, \\
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m i^7 &= -i, \\
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m i^8 &= 1, \\
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m &\vdots
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \end{aligned}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m This means that the sequence \(i^0, i^1, i^2, i^3, \ldots, i^{2009}\) is periodic with a period of 4, and the terms repeat every four terms. We can group these terms into four complete cycles: \(i^0, i^1, i^2, -i^1, i^3, -i^2, i^4, -i^3, i^5, \ldots\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The sum of one complete cycle \(i^0 + i^1 + i^2 + i^3\) is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1 + i - 1 - i = 0
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Since there are 4 complete cycles in 2009 terms, the sum of these four cycles is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 4 \times 0 = 0
