[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m From the same diagram, we know that the sum of the interior angles of a triangle is always \(180^\circ\). Therefore, we can write the equation:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ A + B + C = 180^\circ \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Substituting the given relationship \(C = 2B\) into the equation, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ A + B + 2B = 180^\circ \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ A + 3B = 180^\circ \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m We are asked to find the measure of angle \(A\). To do this, we solve for \(A\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
