[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 4. \( \triangleADB \)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Each of these triangles will then contribute to the area of the four quadrilaterals that can be formed by extending the diagonals of the origin through these vertices. Specifically, the area of each quadrilateral can be calculated by subtracting from the four-dimensional opposite face of the tetrahedron the volume of the tetrahedron formed by the points.
