[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m A committee of three students met with the principal today and agreed that Rachel will report to the principal every $9$ days, Jessica every $12$ days, and Richard every $15$ days. What is the least number of days before all three will again report to the principal on the same day?
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To determine the least number of days before all three students will report to the principal on the same day, we need to find the least common multiple (LCM) of the three reporting intervals: 9 days, 12 days, and 15 days.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The LCM of a set of integers is the smallest positive integer that is divisible by each of the integers in the set. We can find the LCM by first finding the prime factorization of each integer:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - The prime factorization of 9 is \(9 = 3 \times 3\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - The prime factorization of 12 is \(12 = 2^2 \times 3\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - The prime factorization of 15 is \(15 = 3 \times 5\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The LCM is found by taking the highest power of each prime that appears in the factorizations:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - The highest power of 2 is \(2^2\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - The highest power of 3 is \(3^2\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - The highest power of 5 is \(5\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Therefore, the LCM is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m LCM = 2^2 \times 3^2 \times 5 = 4 \times 9 \times 5 = 180
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m So, the least number of days before all three students will report to the principal on the same day is \(\boxed{180}\).<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m [Ground Truth]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 180
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m [Is Boxed Matched]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m True
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m [Extracted Answer]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 180
