[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m First, we start with the given equations:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \frac{m}{n} = 15
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \frac{p}{n} = 3
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \frac{p}{q} = \frac{1}{10}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m From the first equation, we can express \( m \) in terms of \( n \):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m m = 15n
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m From the second equation, we can express \( p \) in terms of \( n \):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m p = 3n
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Now, we substitute these expressions for \( m \) and \( p \) into the third equation:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \frac{p}{q} = \frac{1}{10}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \frac{3n}{q} = \frac{1}{10}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To isolate \( \frac{3n}{q} \), we solve for \( n \) by multiplying both sides by \( q \):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3n = \frac{1}{10}q
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Next, we solve for \( n \) by dividing both sides by 3:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m n = \frac{1}{30}q
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Now, substitute \( n = \frac{1}{30}q \) back into the expression for \( p \):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m p = 3n = 3 \left( \frac{1}{30}q \right) = \frac{3}{30}q = \frac{1}{10}q
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m We already know that \( p = 3n \), so:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \frac{1}{10}q = 3 \left( \frac{1}{30}q \right) = \frac{3}{30}q = \frac{1}{10}q
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m This confirms that our expressions for \( m \) and \( p \) are consistent. Now, we need to find \( \frac{m}{q} \):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \frac{m}{q} = \frac{15n}{q}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Substitute \( n = \frac{1}{30}q \) into the expression for \( \frac{m}{q} \):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \frac{m}{q} = \frac{15 \left( \frac{1}{30}q \right)}{q} = \frac{15 \cdot \frac{1}{30}q}{q} = \frac{15}{30} = \frac{1}{2}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Therefore, the value of \( \frac{m}{q} \) is:
