[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To determine how many daps are equivalent to 42 dips, we need to find out the relationship between dops and daps. We are given the following relationships:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. 4 daps = 3 dops
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. 2 dops = 7 dips
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m First, we need to find out how many dops are equivalent to 7 dips. According to the information given, 2 dops = 7 dips. Therefore, 1 dip = \(\frac{7}{2}\) dops. So, 1 dip = \(\frac{14}{2}\) dops = 7 dops. Now, we can find out how many dops are equivalent to 42 dips by multiplying the number of dips by the number of dops needed for one dip:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ 42 \text{ dips} \times 7 \text{ dops/dip} = 294 \text{ dops} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Now, we need to find out how many daps are equivalent to 294 dops. According to the given relationship, 4 daps = 3 dops. Therefore, 4 daps = \(\frac{3}{4}\) dops. So, 1 dap = \(\frac{4}{3}\) dops. Therefore, 1 dap = \(\frac{4}{3} \times 294\) dops. Calculating this, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ \frac{4}{3} \times 294 = 328 \text{ daps} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Thus, the number of daps equivalent to 42 dips is \(\boxed{328}\).<|endoftext|>
