[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To solve for the ordered pair \((a, b)\) that satisfies the given linear equation, we need to compute the cross product of the two given vectors. The cross product of two vectors \(\mathbf{u} = \begin{pmatrix} u_1 \\ u_2 \\ u_3 \end{pmatrix}\) and \(\mathbf{v} = \begin{pmatrix} v_1 \\ v_2 \\ v_3 \end{pmatrix}\) is given by:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \mathbf{u} \times \mathbf{v} = \begin{vmatrix} \mathbf{i} & \mathbf{j} & \mathbf{k} \\ u_1 & u_2 & u_3 \\ v_1 & v_2 & v_3 \end{vmatrix} = \left( u_2 v_3 - u_3 v_2 \right) \mathbf{i} - \left( u_1 v_3 - u_3 v_1 \right) \mathbf{j} + \left( u_1 v_2 - u_2 v_1 \right) \mathbf{k}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Given the vectors:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ a \\ -7 \end{pmatrix} \quad \text{and} \quad \begin{pmatrix} 5 \\ 4 \\ b \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m We can write the cross product as:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ a \\ -7 \end{pmatrix} \times \begin{pmatrix} 5 \\ 4 \\ b \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} (a \cdot b) - (-7) \cdot 4 \\ (-7 \cdot 5 - 2b) \\ (2 \cdot 4 - a \cdot 5) \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Simplify each component:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \begin{pmatrix} a \cdot b + 28 \\ -35 - 2b \\ 8 - 5a \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m We are given that this cross product is the zero vector. Therefore, each component must be zero:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m a \cdot b + 28 = 0
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m -35 - 2b = 0
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 8 - 5a = 0
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Solve each equation for \(a\) and \(b\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. From \(a \cdot b + 28 = 0\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m a \cdot b = -28
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. From \(-35 - 2b = 0\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m -2b = 35 \implies b = -\frac{35}{2}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3. From \(8 - 5a = 0\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 5a = 8 \implies a = \frac{8}{5}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Substitute \(a = \frac{8}{5}\) and \(b = -\frac{35}{2}\) back into one of the previous equations to verify. Using \(-35 - 2b = 0\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
