[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The projection of $\begin{pmatrix} 0 \\ 3 \end{pmatrix}$ onto a certain vector $\mathbf{w}$ is $\begin{pmatrix} -9/10 \\ 3/10 \end{pmatrix}.$  Find the projection of $\begin{pmatrix} 4 \\ 1 \end{pmatrix}$ onto $\mathbf{w}.$
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To find the projection of the vector \(\mathbf{a} = \begin{pmatrix} 4 \\ 1 \end{pmatrix}\) onto the vector \(\mathbf{w}\), we use the formula for the projection of \(\mathbf{a}\) onto \(\mathbf{w}\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \text{proj}_{\mathbf{w}} \mathbf{a} = \frac{\mathbf{a} \cdot \mathbf{w}}{\mathbf{w} \cdot \mathbf{w}} \mathbf{w}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m We know that:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \text{proj}_{\mathbf{w}} \mathbf{a} = \frac{\begin{pmatrix} 4 \\ 1 \end{pmatrix} \cdot \begin{pmatrix} -9/10 \\ 3/10 \end{pmatrix}}{\begin{pmatrix} -9/10 \\ 3/10 \end{pmatrix} \cdot \begin{pmatrix} -9/10 \\ 3/10 \end{pmatrix}} \begin{pmatrix} -9/10 \\ 3/10 \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m First, we calculate the dot products:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \mathbf{a} \cdot \mathbf{w} = 4 \left(-\frac{9}{10}\right) + 1 \left(\frac{3}{10}\right) = -\frac{36}{10} + \frac{3}{10} = -\frac{33}{10}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \mathbf{w} \cdot \mathbf{w} = \left(-\frac{9}{10}\right)^2 + \left(\frac{3}{10}\right)^2 = \frac{81}{100} + \frac{9}{100} = \frac{90}{100} = \frac{9}{10}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Now, we substitute these values into the projection formula:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \text{proj}_{\mathbf{w}} \mathbf{a} = \frac{-\frac{33}{10}}{\frac{9}{10}} \begin{pmatrix} -9/10 \\ 3/10 \end{pmatrix} = -\frac{33}{9} \begin{pmatrix} -9/10 \\ 3/10 \end{pmatrix} = -\frac{11}{3} \begin{pmatrix} -9/10 \\ 3/10 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} \frac{99}{10} \\ -11 \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Thus, the projection of \(\begin{pmatrix} 4 \\ 1 \end{pmatrix}\) onto \(\mathbf{w}\) is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \boxed{\begin{pmatrix} 33 \\ -33 \end{pmatrix}}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
