[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To find the arithmetic mean of all positive two-digit multiples of 7, we first need to identify all such numbers and then calculate the average.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. Identify the smallest two-digit multiple of 7:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[7 \times 1 = 7\]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    The smallest two-digit multiple of 7 is 7.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. Identify the largest two-digit multiple of 7:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[7 \times 9 = 63\]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    The largest two-digit multiple of 7 is 63.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3. List all the multiples of 7 within the range of two-digit numbers:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[7, 14, 21, 28, 35, 42, 49, 56, 63\]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 4. Count the multiples:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    There are 9 multiples of 7 within the range of two-digit numbers.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[63 - 7 + 1 = 67\]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 5. Calculate the arithmetic mean:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    The arithmetic mean is the sum of the multiples divided by the number of multiples.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[\text{Mean} = \frac{67}{9}\]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 6. Simplify the fraction:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[\frac{67}{9} = 7.4444 \approx 7.4444\]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    However, we typically use decimal approximations unless specified otherwise. But typically, we round to the nearest practical value.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[\text{Mean} \approx 7.4\]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Thus, the arithmetic mean of all positive two-digit multiples of 7 is \(\boxed{7.4}\).<|endoftext|>
