[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3. **Calculate the probability:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    The probability is the number of favorable outcomes divided by the total number of possible outcomes:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \frac{36}{36} = 1
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Therefore, the probability that the sum of the two numbers showing is less than 11 is \(\boxed{1}\).<|endoftext|>
