[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m ### Step 2: Consider the derivative for convexity
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To ensure the minimum value is found, we will analyze the function \( f(x) \) for \( -1 \le x \le 1 \).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The function \( f(x) \) is nonlinear and convex on the interval \([-1, 1]\). To confirm this, we can use the fact that the function is of the form \( g(x) = \sqrt{A - Bx} + \sqrt{C - Dx} \) where \( A, B, C, D \) are constants.
