[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. **Substitute \( x = -2 \) into the function:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    y = 8 - 5(-2) + 4(-2)^2
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. **Calculate each term separately:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - For the constant term:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      8 - 5(-2) = 8 + 10 = 18
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - For the coefficient of \( x \):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      \[
