[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - For the squared term, since \((-2)^2 = 4\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      4(-2)^2 = 4 \cdot 4 = 16
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3. **Combine all the terms:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    y = 18 + 10 + 16
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 4. **Add the results:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    y = 18 + 10 + 16 = 44
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Therefore, the value of \( y \) when \( x = -2 \) is \(\boxed{44}\).<|endoftext|>
