[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To find the remainder when the sum \(1 + 7 + 13 + 19 + \cdots + 253 + 259\) is divided by 6, we can use the property that the sum of an arithmetic series can be simplified. The series \(1 + 7 + 13 + 19 + \cdots + 253 + 259\) is an arithmetic series where the first term \(a = 1\) and the common difference \(d = 6\). The last term \(l = 259\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The number of terms \(n\) in the series can be found using the formula for the \(n\)-th term of an arithmetic series:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m l = a + (n-1)d
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Plugging in the values, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 259 = 1 + (n-1) \cdot 6
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Solving for \(n\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 259 = 1 + 6(n-1) \implies 258 = 6(n-1) \implies n-1 = 43 \implies n = 44
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m So, there are 44 terms in the series.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The sum \(S_n\) of the first \(n\) terms of an arithmetic series can be found using the formula:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m S_n = \frac{n}{2} (a + l)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Plugging in the values, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m S_{44} = \frac{44}{2} (1 + 259) = 22 \cdot 260 = 5720
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Now, we need to find the remainder when 5720 is divided by 6. We do this by calculating:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 5720 \div 6 = 953 \text{ remainder } 2
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m So, the remainder when 5720 is divided by 6 is 2.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Therefore, the remainder when the sum \(1 + 7 + 13 + 19 + \cdots + 253 + 259\) is divided by 6 is \(\boxed{2}\).<|endoftext|>
