[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To convert the decimal number \(115_{10}\) to base 11, we need to repeatedly divide the number by 11 and keep track of the remainders. Here are the steps:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. **Divide 115 by 11:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    115 \div 11 = 10 \text{ remainder } 5
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    So, the quotient is 10 and the remainder is 5.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. **Divide the quotient (10) by 11:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    10 \div 11 = 0 \text{ remainder } 10
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    So, the quotient is 0 and the remainder is 10.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Since the quotient is now 0, we stop the division process. The remainders, read from bottom to top, give us the number in base 11. Therefore, the base 11 representation of \(115_{10}\) is \(105_{11}\).
