[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The patron has visited every 4th book store starting from his old favorite, which was the one located at 75th Street and Broadway. If this patron also refuses to read the store that he bought his book for, in what year does he visit based on his new bookchain that starts at the second store and increases by the same interval each year? To solve this problem, we need to determine the patron's bookchain year based on his new layout after visiting every 4th store, starting at a specific store (75th Street and Broadway) and increasing by 1 store each year.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Let's denote the year/year 4th stop as \(n\). Given that the patron starts on the 75th store and visits every 4th store, the pattern can be described as follows:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. Start at the 75th store.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. Visit the 5th store.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3. Visit the 10th store.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 4. Visit the 15th store.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 5. Visit the 20th store.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 6. Visit the 25th store.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 7. Visit the next store, which is the 30th store.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 8. Visit the 35th store.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 9. Visit the 40th store.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 10. Visit the 45th store.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m This means that the patron visits the store at \(4k + 75\) (where \(k\) is the year) years after the starting store. We need to find the year such that the store visited is different from the starting store. The starting store is at the 75th store.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Let's list out the stores visited by calculating the modulus value:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \begin{aligned}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m &\text{Up until the 5th store,}\quad 0 \mod 75 = 0 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m &\text{From the 5th store to the 10th store,}\quad (10 - 5) \mod 75 = 5 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m &\text{From the 10th store to the 15th store,}\quad (15 - 10) \mod 75 = 5 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m &\text{From the 15th store to the 20th store,}\quad (20 - 15) \mod 75 = 5 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m &\text{From the 20th store to the 25th store,}\quad (25 - 20) \mod 75 = 5 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m &\text{From the 25th store to the 40th store,}\quad (40 - 25) \mod 75 = 25 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m &\text{From the 40th store to the 45th store,}\quad (45 - 40) \mod 75 = 5 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \end{aligned}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m From the calculations, the store visited is the 40th store, which is different from the starting store. So the patron visits the 40th store year after the starting store. 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Therefore, the year he visits is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m n = 40
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The final answer is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \boxed{40}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
