[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To find the sum of the odd integers from 11 through 39 inclusive, we can use the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series. The general form of the sum of the first \( n \) odd numbers is given by:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m S_n = n^2
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m where \( S_n \) is the sum of the first \( n \) odd numbers. Here, \( n = 39 - 11 + 1 = 29 \) because we count from 11 to 39 (5 ones plus 29 twos), and since the number of odd numbers between 11 and 39 is 39, we have 29 terms in total.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m So, we can substitute \( n = 29 \) into the formula:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
