[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Find an ordered pair $(u,v)$ that solves the system: \begin{align*} 5u &= -7 - 2v,\\ 3u &= 4v - 25 \end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To solve the system of equations:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 5u &= -7 - 2v, \\
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3u &= 4v - 25,
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m we can use the method of substitution or elimination. Here, we will use the substitution method.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m First, solve the first equation for \(u\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 5u = -7 - 2v \implies u = \frac{-7 - 2v}{5}.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Now substitute this expression for \(u\) into the second equation:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3u = 4v - 25 \implies 3\left(\frac{-7 - 2v}{5}\right) = 4v - 25.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Simplify the left side:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \frac{3(-7 - 2v)}{5} = \frac{-21 - 6v}{5} = 4v - 25.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Now, we can solve for \(v\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 4v - 25 = \frac{-21 - 6v}{5} \implies 4v - 25 = -\frac{21}{5} - \frac{6v}{5} \implies 4v - 25 = -\frac{21}{5} - \frac{6v}{5}.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To eliminate the fractions, multiply every term by 5:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 5(4v - 25) = 5\left(-\frac{21}{5} - \frac{6v}{5}\right) \implies 20v - 125 = -21 - 6v \implies 26v = 104 \implies v = \frac{104}{26} = \frac{52}{13}.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Now that we have \(v\), substitute it back into the expression for \(u\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m u = \frac{-7 - 2\left(\frac{52}{13}\right)}{5} = \frac{-7 - \frac{104}{13}}{5} = \frac{-\frac{91}{13} - \frac{104}{13}}{5} = \frac{-195}{13 \cdot 5} = \frac{-39}{13}.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Thus, the ordered pair \((u, v)\) that solves the system is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \boxed{\left( \frac{-39}{13}, \frac{52}{13} \right)}.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
