[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To find the sum of the roots of the equation \(\tan^2 x - 9 \tan x + 1 = 0\) that are between \(x = 0\) and \(x = 2\pi\) radians, we start by letting \(y = \tan x\). The equation then becomes a quadratic equation in terms of \(y\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[y^2 - 9y + 1 = 0.\]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m We solve this quadratic equation using the quadratic formula \(y = \frac{-b \pm \sqrt{b^2 - 4ac}}{2a}\), where \(a = 1\), \(b = -9\), and \(c = 1\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[y = \frac{9 \pm \sqrt{81 - 4}}{2} = \frac{9 \pm \sqrt{77}}{2}.\]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m So, the solutions for \(y\) are:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[y = \frac{9 + \sqrt{77}}{2} \quad \text{and} \quad y = \frac{9 - \sqrt{77}}{2}.\]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Recall that \(y = \tan x\), so we have:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[\tan x = \frac{9 + \sqrt{77}}{2} \quad \text{and} \quad \tan x = \frac{9 - \sqrt{77}}{2}.\]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The roots of the original equation \(\tan^2 x - 9 \tan x + 1 = 0\) are the values of \(x\) that satisfy these equations. These roots are the same as the values of \(x\) that satisfy the original equation. Therefore, the roots of the equation are:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[\tan x = \frac{9 + \sqrt{77}}{2} \quad \text{and} \quad \tan x = \frac{9 - \sqrt{77}}{2}.\]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The sum of the roots of the equation \(\tan^2 x - 9 \tan x + 1 = 0\) is the sum of these two roots:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[\left(\frac{9 + \sqrt{77}}{2}\right) + \left(\frac{9 - \sqrt{77}}{2}\right) = \frac{9 + \sqrt{77} + 9 - \sqrt{77}}{2} = \frac{18}{2} = 9.\]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Thus, the sum of the roots of the equation is \(\boxed{9}\).<|endoftext|>
