[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The length of \(AD\) is the length of the hyperbolic segment from \(B\) to \(C\). This segment is the remaining segment on the x-axis after subtracting \(BD\) from a right triangle with hypotenuse 15 units, and since the right triangle is \(BAD\), the candidate length for \(AD\) is 12 units. Let the coordinates of \(A\) be \((x_1, y_1)\). Then \(A\) can be found by solving the system:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m x_1^2 + y_1^2 = 225
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m x_1^2 + (x_1 - 12)^2 = 144
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Expanding the second equation:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
