[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m This gives us \(x_1 = 0\) or \(x_1 = 12\). Since \(x_1 = 0\) would place \(A\) at the origin, which is not on the left side of \(BD\), we have \(x_1 = 12\). Substituting \(x_1 = 12\) into the first equation:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 12^2 + y_1^2 = 225
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 144 + y_1^2 = 225
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
