[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Thus, the coordinates of \(A\) are \((12, 9)\) or \((12, -9)\). For the sake of a single calculation, we will use \((12, 9)\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Now, we need to find the lengths of the sides of quadrilateral \(ABCD\). The lengths of the sides are the same as the lengths of the sides of triangle \(BAD\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m For \(ABCD\), the lengths of the sides are:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
