[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The area of triangle \(BAD\) can be calculated using Heron's formula. First, calculate the semi-perimeter \(s\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m s = \frac{12 + 17 + 15}{2} = 20.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The area \(K\) of triangle \(BAD\) is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m K = \sqrt{s(s-a)(s-b)(s-c)} = \sqrt{20(20-12)(20-15)(20-17)} = \sqrt{20 \cdot 8 \cdot 5 \cdot 3} = \sqrt{1200} = 20\sqrt{3}.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Since \(ABCD\) is a rectangle along the x-axis, the perimeter is also the sum of all sides:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
