[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. Isolate the variable \(y\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3. Solve for \(y\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Let's start with the left side of the equation:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[3y + 7y = 10y.\]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m So the equation becomes:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[10y = 282 - 8(y - 3).\]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Next, let's simplify the right side of the equation:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[282 - 8(y - 3) = 282 - 8y + 24 = 306 - 8y.\]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m So the equation now is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[10y = 306 - 8y.\]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To isolate \(y\), we need to get all the \(y\)-terms on one side of the equation. We do this by adding \(8y\) to both sides:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[10y + 8y = 306 - 8y + 8y,\]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m which simplifies to:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[18y = 306.\]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Now, we solve for \(y\) by dividing both sides by 18:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[y = \frac{306}{18}.\]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m This simplifies to:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[y = 17.\]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
