[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m How many feet long is the shadow of a 20-foot flagpole if a 6-foot woman standing at the base of the flagpole has a shadow that is nine feet long?
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To determine the length of the shadow of a 20-foot flagpole when a 6-foot woman standing at the base of the flagpole has a shadow that is 9 feet long, we can use similar triangles. The triangle formed by the woman, her shadow, and the flagpole is similar to the triangle formed by the ground and the shadow of the flagpole.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Let's denote the length of the shadow of the flagpole by \( S \) feet.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The ratio of the height of the woman to the length of her shadow is equal to the ratio of the height of the flagpole to the length of its shadow. Therefore, we can set up the following proportion:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \frac{\text{height of woman}}{\text{length of shadow of woman}} = \frac{\text{height of flagpole}}{\text{length of shadow of flagpole}}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Substituting the known values into the proportion, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \frac{6}{9} = \frac{20}{S}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To solve for \( S \), we can cross-multiply:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 6S = 9 \times 20
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 6S = 180
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Next, we divide both sides of the equation by 6:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m S = \frac{180}{6}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m S = 30
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Thus, the length of the shadow of the flagpole is \(\boxed{30}\) feet.<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
