[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To solve this problem, we can use the concept of similar triangles. The flagpole and the woman form two corresponding triangles that are similar because they are both symmetric. The ratio of the heights of the flagpole and the woman will be equal to the ratio of the distances from the woman to the base of the flagpole and the base of the man-made object (the shadow).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Let's denote:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - \( h \) as the height of the flagpole (20 feet).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - \( s \) as the distance from the woman to the base of the flagpole (9 feet).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - \( h_{\text{shadow}} \) as the height of the woman (6 feet).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Using the property of similar triangles, we know:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \frac{h}{h_{\text{shadow}}} = \frac{h_{\text{woman}}}{s_{\text{woman}}}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Substituting the known values into the equation:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \frac{20}{h_{\text{woman}}} = \frac{6}{9}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Simplify the right-hand side:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \frac{20}{h_{\text{woman}}} = \frac{2}{3}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Cross-multiply to solve for \( h_{\text{woman}} \):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 20 \cdot 3 = 2 \cdot h_{\text{woman}}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 60 = 2 \cdot h_{\text{woman}}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m h_{\text{woman}} = \frac{60}{2}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m h_{\text{woman}} = 30
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Therefore, the length of the shadow of the flagpole is 30 feet.<|endoftext|>
