[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Suppose the area under a curve defined by $$\frac{1}{x^2-x} = \lim_{c \rightarrow 0^+} \int_{a-c}^{a+c} \frac{dx}{x^2-x}$$ has a definite integral $C$. Does the value of the definite integral $$\int_{1}^{\infty} \frac{dx}{x^2-x} = \int_{1}^{\infty} \frac{dx}{x(x-1)} = -C$$ yield a surprising result? To determine whether the value of the definite integral \(\int_{1}^{\infty} \frac{dx}{x(x-1)}\) yields a surprising result, let's first simplify the integrand \(\frac{1}{x(x-1)}\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m We can use partial fraction decomposition to simplify \(\frac{1}{x(x-1)}\). We want to express it as:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \frac{1}{x(x-1)} = \frac{A}{x} + \frac{B}{x-1}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Multiplying both sides by \(x(x-1)\) gives:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1 = A(x-1) + Bx
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To find \(A\) and \(B\), we set up the system of equations by equating the coefficients of like terms:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1 = Ax - A + Bx = (A + B)x - A
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m This gives us two equations:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m A + B = 0 \quad \text{and} \quad -A = 1
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m From the second equation, we find \(A = -1\). Substituting \(A = -1\) into the first equation gives:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m -1 + B = 0 \implies B = 1
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m So, we have:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \frac{1}{x(x-1)} = \frac{-1}{x} + \frac{1}{x-1}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m This can be rewritten as:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \frac{1}{x(x-1)} = \frac{1}{x-1} - \frac{1}{x}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Now we can split the integral:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \int_{1}^{\infty} \frac{dx}{x(x-1)} = \int_{1}^{\infty} \left( \frac{1}{x-1} - \frac{1}{x} \right) dx
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m We can split this integral into two separate integrals:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \int_{1}^{\infty} \frac{1}{x-1} dx - \int_{1}^{\infty} \frac{1}{x} dx
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The first integral is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \int_{1}^{\infty} \frac{1}{x-1} dx = \lim_{t \to \infty} \int_{1}^{t} \frac{1}{x-1} dx = \lim_{t \to \infty} \left[ \ln|x-1| \right]_{1}^{t} = \lim_{t \to \infty} \left( \ln(t-1) - \ln(0) \right)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Since \(\ln(0)\) is undefined, we interpret this as the limit approaching \(-\infty\). However, for the purpose of this problem, we can see that \(\int_{1}^{\infty} \frac{1}{x-1} dx\) diverges, so it does not contribute to the value of the integral.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The second integral is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \int_{1}^{\infty} \frac{1}{x} dx = \lim_{t \to \infty} \int_{1}^{t} \frac{1}{x} dx = \lim_{t \to \infty} \left[ \ln|x| \right]_{1}^{t} = \lim_{t \to \infty} \left( \ln t - \ln(1) \right) = \lim_{t \to \infty} \ln t
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Since \(\ln t\) diverges to \(-\infty\), the value of the integral is \(-\infty\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Therefore, the integral \(\int_{1}^{\infty} \frac{dx}{x(x-1)}\) does not yield a surprising result, but rather results in \(-\infty\). So the answer is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \boxed{-\infty}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
