[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Compute $\dbinom{16}{4}-\dbinom{16}{12}$.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To compute \(\binom{16}{4} - \binom{16}{12}\), we will first find the values of the binomial coefficients \(\binom{16}{4}\) and \(\binom{16}{12}\), and then subtract them.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. Calculate \(\binom{16}{4}\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \binom{16}{4} = \frac{16!}{4!(16-4)!} = \frac{16!}{4! \cdot 12!}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m We can reduce the factorials by canceling out terms:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 16! = 16 \times 15 \times 14 \times 13 \times 12!
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m So,
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \binom{16}{4} = \frac{16 \times 15 \times 14 \times 13}{4 \times 3 \times 2 \times 1} = \frac{16 \times 15 \times 14 \times 13}{24}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Now, compute the numerator and the denominator:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 16 \times 15 = 240
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 240 \times 14 = 3360
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3360 \times 13 = 43680
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m So,
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \binom{16}{4} = \frac{43680}{24} = 1820
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. Calculate \(\binom{16}{12}\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \binom{16}{12} = \frac{16!}{12!(16-12)!} = \frac{16!}{12! \cdot 4!}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m We can reduce the factorials by canceling out terms:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 16! = 16 \times 15 \times 14 \times 13 \times 12!
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m So,
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \binom{16}{12} = \frac{16 \times 15 \times 14 \times 13 \times 12!}{12! \times 4!} = \frac{16 \times 15 \times 14 \times 13}{4 \times 3 \times 2 \times 1} = \frac{16 \times 15 \times 14 \times 13}{24}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Now, compute the numerator and the denominator:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 16 \times 15 = 240
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 240 \times 14 = 3360
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3360 \times 13 = 43680
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m So,
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \binom{16}{12} = \frac{43680}{24} = 1820
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3. Subtract \(\binom{16}{12}\) from \(\binom{16}{4}\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \binom{16}{4} - \binom{16}{12} = 1820 - 1820 = 0
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Therefore, the final answer is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \boxed{0}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
