[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To compute \(\binom{16}{15}\), we can use the property of binomial coefficients that \(\binom{n}{k} = \binom{n}{n-k}\). This property tells us that \(\binom{16}{15} = \binom{16}{1}\). Since the binomial coefficient is symmetric, we know that \(\binom{16}{1} = \binom{16}{16-1} = \binom{16}{15}\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Let's use Python and the `sympy` library to confirm this calculation.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m ```python
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m import sympy as sp
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m # Define the variables
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m n = 16
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m k = 15
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m # Calculate the binomial coefficient using sympy's binomial function
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m binom_16_15 = sp.binomial(n, k)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m # Print the result
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m print(binom_16_15)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m ```
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m ```output
