[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m We are given that the hypotenuse has a length of 8. We need to find the length of the side opposite the \( 30^\circ \) angle, which we will call \( x \).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m We can use trigonometric functions for this:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. In the right triangle, the side opposite the \( 30^\circ \) angle is \( x \), and the hypotenuse is 8.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. The adjacent side to the \( 30^\circ \) angle is 1.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
