[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To solve for \( XY \) in the given trapezoid \( WXYZ \), we start by noting the provided information:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - \( WXYZ \) is a trapezoid.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - \( \overline{WX} \parallel \overline{ZY} \).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - \( \overline{WY} \perp \overline{ZY} \).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - \( YZ = 12 \).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - \( \tan Z = 1.5 \).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - \( \tan X = 2 \).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m First, we use the given tangent values to find the lengths of the opposite sides. We know:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ \tan Z = \frac{\text{opposite}}{\text{adjacent}} = 1.5 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ \sqrt{1 + \tan^2 Z} = \sqrt{1 + 1.5^2} = \sqrt{1 + 2.25} = \sqrt{3.25} = \frac{\sqrt{13}}{2} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ \tan Z = \frac{XY}{WZ} = \frac{XY}{12} = \frac{\sqrt{13}}{2} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m So, \( XY = 12 \cdot \frac{\sqrt{13}}{2} = 6\sqrt{13} \).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Next, to find \( WZ \), we use the right triangle formed by dropping a perpendicular from \( Z \) to \( \overline{WY} \). Let \( M \) be the foot of this perpendicular. Since \( \tan X = 2 \), we can use the trigonometric identity:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ \tan X = \frac{\text{opposite}}{\text{adjacent}} = \frac{XY}{WZ} = 2 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ XY = 6\sqrt{13} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ WZ = \frac{XY}{\tan X} = \frac{6\sqrt{13}}{2} = 3\sqrt{13} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The length \( WZ \) is the same as the other corresponding length in the isosceles trapezoid, which is \( WZ = 3\sqrt{13} \). Thus, the complete length \( WXYZ \) is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ XY + WZ = 6\sqrt{13} + 3\sqrt{13} = 9\sqrt{13} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Therefore, the length of \( XY \) is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ \boxed{6\sqrt{13}} \]<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m [Ground Truth]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 9\sqrt{5}
