[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To evaluate the determinant of the given \(3 \times 3\) matrix, we will use the formula for the determinant of a \(3 \times 3\) matrix. The determinant of a matrix 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \begin{vmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m a & b & c \\
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m d & e & f \\
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m g & h & i
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \end{vmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m is given by
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m a(ei - fh) - b(di - fg) + c(dh - eg).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m For the matrix 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \begin{vmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1 & x & y \\
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1 & x + y & y \\
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1 & x & x + y
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \end{vmatrix},
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m we can identify the elements as follows:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - \(a = 1\),
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - \(b = x\),
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - \(c = y\),
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - \(d = 1\),
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - \(e = x + y\),
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - \(f = y\),
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - \(g = 1\),
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - \(h = x\),
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - \(i = x + y\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Substituting these values into the determinant formula, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1 \cdot ((x + y)(x + y) - y \cdot x) - x \cdot (1(x + y) - y \cdot 1) + y \cdot (1 \cdot x - x \cdot (x + y)).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Now, let's simplify each term step by step.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. Simplify the first term:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m (x + y)(x + y) - y \cdot x = (x + y)^2 - xy = x^2 + 2xy + y^2 - xy = x^2 + xy + y^2.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. Simplify the second term:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1(x + y) - y \cdot 1 = x + y - y = x.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3. Simplify the third term:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1 \cdot x - x \cdot (x + y) = x - x(x + y) = x - x^2 - xy = -x^2 - xy.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Putting it all together, the determinant is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1 \cdot (x^2 + xy + y^2) - x \cdot x - y \cdot (-x^2 - xy) + y \cdot x = x^2 + xy + y^2 - x^2 - xy - 2xy + xy = xy.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Therefore, the determinant of the matrix is
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \boxed{xy}.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
