[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Compute: $6\div6-6+6\times6$.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To compute the expression \(6 \div 6 - 6 + 6 \times 6\), we will follow the order of operations, often remembered by the acronym PEMDAS (Parentheses, Exponents, Multiplication and Division (from left to right), Addition and Subtraction (from left to right)).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m First, we perform the division and multiplication:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[6 \div 6 = 1\]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[6 \times 6 = 36\]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Now, substitute these values back into the expression:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[6 \div 6 - 6 + 6 \times 6 = 1 - 6 + 36\]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Next, we perform the addition and subtraction from left to right:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[1 - 6 = -5\]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[-5 + 36 = 31\]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Therefore, the final answer is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[\boxed{31}\]<|endoftext|>
