[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To find the area of the region enclosed by the graph of \( |x-60| + |y| = \left| \frac{x}{4} \right| \), we need to analyze the equation and understand its geometric interpretation.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The equation \( |x-60| + |y| = \left| \frac{x}{4} \right| \) will be broken down into different cases based on the value of \( x \):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. \( x \geq 60 \) and \( y \geq 0 \)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. \( x \geq 60 \) and \( y \leq 0 \)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3. \( x \leq 60 \) and \( y \geq 0 \)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 4. \( x \leq 60 \) and \( y \leq 0 \)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Let's analyze each case:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m ### Case 1: \( x \geq 60 \) and \( y \geq 0 \)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The equation becomes:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m x - 60 + y = \left| \frac{x}{4} \right|
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Since \( y \geq 0 \), we have:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m x - 60 + y = \frac{x}{4}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Rearranging gives:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m x - 60 = \frac{x}{4} - y
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m x = \frac{5}{4}x - 60 - y
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \frac{1}{4}x = 60 + y
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m x = 240 + 4y
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m ### Case 2: \( x \geq 60 \) and \( y \leq 0 \)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The equation becomes:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m x - 60 - y = \left| \frac{x}{4} \right|
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Since \( y \leq 0 \), we have:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m x - 60 - y = -\frac{x}{4}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Rearranging gives:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m x = 60 + \frac{x}{4} + y
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
