[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Let $\mathbf{A} = \begin{pmatrix} 1 & 2 \\ 3 & 4 \end{pmatrix}$ and $\mathbf{B} = \begin{pmatrix} a & b \\ c & d \end{pmatrix}$ be two matrices such that $\mathbf{A} \mathbf{B} = \mathbf{B} \mathbf{A}.$  Assuming $3b \neq c,$ find $\frac{a - d}{c - 3b}.$
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To solve the problem, we start by using the given condition \(\mathbf{A} \mathbf{B} = \mathbf{B} \mathbf{A}\). This equation represents the equality of the product of the matrices \(\mathbf{A}\) and \(\mathbf{B}\) to the product of the matrices \(\mathbf{B}\) and \(\mathbf{A}\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m First, let's write down the given matrices:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \mathbf{A} = \begin{pmatrix} 1 & 2 \\ 3 & 4 \end{pmatrix}, \quad \mathbf{B} = \begin{pmatrix} a & b \\ c & d \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The product \(\mathbf{A} \mathbf{B}\) is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \mathbf{A} \mathbf{B} = \begin{pmatrix} 1 & 2 \\ 3 & 4 \end{pmatrix} \begin{pmatrix} a & b \\ c & d \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 1 \cdot a + 2 \cdot c & 1 \cdot b + 2 \cdot d \\ 3 \cdot a + 4 \cdot c & 3 \cdot b + 4 \cdot d \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} a + 2c & b + 2d \\ 3a + 4c & 3b + 4d \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The product \(\mathbf{B} \mathbf{A}\) is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \mathbf{B} \mathbf{A} = \begin{pmatrix} a & b \\ c & d \end{pmatrix} \begin{pmatrix} 1 & 2 \\ 3 & 4 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} a \cdot 1 + b \cdot 3 & a \cdot 2 + b \cdot 4 \\ c \cdot 1 + d \cdot 3 & c \cdot 2 + d \cdot 4 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} a + 3b & 2a + 4b \\ c + 3d & 2c + 4d \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Since \(\mathbf{A} \mathbf{B} = \mathbf{B} \mathbf{A}\), we equate the corresponding elements of the two matrices:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \begin{cases}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m a + 2c = a + 3b \\
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m b + 2d = 2a + 4b \\
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3a + 4c = c + 3d \\
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3b + 4d = 2c + 4d
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \end{cases}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m From the first and third equations, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2c = 3b \quad \text{and} \quad 3a + 4c = c + 3d
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m From the second and fourth equations, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m b + 2d = 2a + 4b \quad \text{and} \quad 3b + 4d = 2c + 4d
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m We can simplify these equations. First, subtract the second equation from the first:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m (3a + 4c) - (b + 2d) = (c + 3d) - (2a + 4b) \\
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3a + 4c - b - 2d = c + 3d - 2a - 4b
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3a + 4c - b - 2d = c + 3d - 2a - 4b \\
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 5a + 7c - 5d = 5b
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Next, subtract the first equation from the third:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m (3b + 4d) - (a + 2c) = (c + 3d) - (a + 2c) \\
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3b + 4d - a - 2c = c + 3d - a - 2c \\
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3b + 4d - a - 2c = 3d \\
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3b + 4d - 3a = 5c
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m We now have the system of equations:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 5a + 7c - 5d = 5b \\
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3b + 4d - 3a = 5c
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m From \(5a + 7c - 5d = 5b\), we can express \(b\) in terms of \(a\) and \(c\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 5a + 7c - 5d = 5b \implies 5a + 7c - 5d = 5b \implies b = 5a + jc + 5d
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Substitute \(b\) into the third equation:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3j + 4d - 3a = 5c \implies 3j + 4d - 3a = 5c \implies j = j - 5d
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Since \(b = 5a + jc + 5d\), and substituting \(b\) back into the equation for the determinant, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \frac{a - d}{c - 3b} = \frac{a - d}{c - 3(5a + jc + 5d)} = \frac{a - d}{c - 15a - 3jc - 15d}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Simplifying the denominator:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \frac{a - d}{c - 15a - 3jc - 15d} = \frac{a - d}{c - 15a - 3jc - 15d} = \frac{a - d}{c - 15a - 3jc - 15d}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Thus, the final answer is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \boxed{2}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
