[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To find the sum of the digits of the base-8 expression for \(8888_{10}\), we need to follow these steps:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. Convert the decimal number \(8888_{10}\) to its base-8 (octal) equivalent.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. Convert the resulting base-8 number to its decimal (base-10) equivalent.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3. Sum the digits of the base-10 number.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m **Step 1: Convert \(8888_{10}\) to base-8.**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m We divide \(8888_{10}\) by 8 and keep track of the remainders:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 8888 \div 8 = 1110 \quad \text{(remainder is } 0\text{)}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1110 \div 8 = 131 \quad \text{(remainder is } 6\text{)}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 131 \div 8 = 16 \quad \text{(remainder is } 5\text{)}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 16 \div 8 = 2 \quad \text{(remainder is } 0\text{)}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2 \div 8 = 0 \quad \text{(remainder is } 2\text{)}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Reading the remainders from bottom to top, we get \(8888_{10} = 20650_8\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m **Step 2: Convert \(20650_8\) to base-10.**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The base-8 number \(20650_8\) can be expanded as:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 20650_8 = 2 \cdot 8^4 + 0 \cdot 8^3 + 6 \cdot 8^2 + 5 \cdot 8^1 + 0 \cdot 8^0
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Calculating each term:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2 \cdot 8^4 = 2 \cdot 4096 = 8192
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 0 \cdot 8^3 = 0 \cdot 512 = 0
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 6 \cdot 8^2 = 6 \cdot 64 = 384
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 5 \cdot 8^1 = 5 \cdot 8 = 40
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 0 \cdot 8^0 = 0
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Adding these values together:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 8192 + 0 + 384 + 40 + 0 = 8616
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m So, the base-10 equivalent of \(20650_8\) is \(8616\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m **Step 3: Sum the digits of \(8616_{10}\).**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The digits of \(8616\) are \(8\), \(6\), \(1\), and \(6\). Adding these together:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 8 + 6 + 1 + 6 = 21
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Therefore, the sum of the digits of the base-8 expression for \(8888_{10}\) is \(\boxed{21}\).<|endoftext|>
