[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To determine the ordered pair \((a, b)\) for which the system of equations has infinite solutions, we need to analyze the given system of equations:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3ax + 3y &= 5b, \\
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2x + y &= 5.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m First, let's rewrite the second equation for clarity:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2x + y = 5.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m This equation can be rearranged to:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m y = 5 - 2x.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m We can substitute this expression for \(y\) into the first equation:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3ax + 3(5 - 2x) = 5b.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Simplify the left-hand side:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3ax + 15 - 6x = 5b.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Rearrange the equation to isolate the terms involving \(a\) and \(b\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3ax - 6x + 15 = 5b.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Factor out the common term \(3x\) on the left-hand side:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3x(a - 2) + 15 = 5b.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m For the system to have infinitely many solutions, the coefficient of \(x\) must be zero (otherwise, the lines would not intersect). Therefore, we set \(a - 2 = 0\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m a - 2 = 0 \implies a = 2.
