[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m y = 5 - 2x.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Since the system has infinitely many solutions, we need to choose \(b\) such that the line \(3x(y - 5) + 15 = 5b\) passes through infinitely many points. This occurs when \(y = 0\) and \(x = 1\), because the term \(15\) becomes zero when \(y = 0\) and \(x = 1\). This gives us the point \((1, 0)\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
