[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To simplify and write the result as a common fraction, we need to first simplify the innermost cube root, then the next, and so on, until we are left with a single cube root.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Given:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \sqrt{\sqrt[3]{\sqrt{\frac{1}{4096}}}}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. Start by simplifying the innermost expression:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \sqrt{\frac{1}{4096}}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Since \(\frac{1}{4096}\) can be written as \(2^{-10}\), we have:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \sqrt{2^{-10}} = 2^{-5}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. Now, take the cube root of \(2^{-5}\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
