[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To compute the product \(\prod_{n = 1}^{20} \frac{n + 3}{n}\), let's break it down step-by-step.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m First, we write the product explicitly:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \prod_{n = 1}^{20} \frac{n + 3}{n}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m This can be written as:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \frac{4}{1} \cdot \frac{5}{2} \cdot \frac{6}{3} \cdot \frac{7}{4} \cdot \ldots \cdot \frac{23}{19}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Notice that this can be written in a more compact form:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \frac{4 \cdot 5 \cdot 6 \cdot \ldots \cdot 23}{1 \cdot 2 \cdot 3 \cdot \ldots \cdot 19}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m We can rewrite \(1 \cdot 2 \cdot 3 \cdot \ldots \cdot 19\) as \(20!\) because \(19!\) includes all numbers from 1 to 19, and thus we can pair each number with its complement, which is \(19 - n\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1 \cdot 2 \cdot 3 \cdot \ldots \cdot 19 = \frac{20!}{1 \cdot 10!} = \frac{20!}{10! \cdot 10!} = \frac{20!}{10! \cdot 10!}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m So the product becomes:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \frac{4 \cdot 5 \cdot 6 \cdot \ldots \cdot 23}{\frac{20!}{10! \cdot 10!}} = \frac{4 \cdot 5 \cdot 6 \cdot \ldots \cdot 23 \cdot 10! \cdot 10!}{20!}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m This is equivalent to:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \frac{4 \cdot 5 \cdot 6 \cdot \ldots \cdot 23}{20 \cdot 19 \cdot 18 \cdot \ldots \cdot 9} = \frac{9}{10}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Thus, the value of the product is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \boxed{\frac{9}{10}}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
