[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m We are given that the area of square \(A_1\) is 25 square centimeters, and the area of square \(A_2\) is 49 square centimeters. These areas correspond to the side lengths of rectangles \(A_3\). Therefore, we have:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ x^2 = 25 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ y^2 = 49 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m We can solve these equations for \(x\) and \(y\). Taking the square roots of both sides of each equation, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ x = 5 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ y = 7 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Now we can calculate the area of rectangle \(A_3\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
