[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To determine the value of \( a \) for which the lines \( 2y - 2a = 6x \) and \( y + 1 = (a + 6)x \) are parallel, we need to compare their slopes. Two lines are parallel if and only if their slopes are equal.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m First, let's rewrite each line in slope-intercept form, \( y = mx + b \), where \( m \) is the slope.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. Rewriting the first line \( 2y - 2a = 6x \):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    2y = 6x + 2a
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    y = 3x + a
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    So, the slope \( m_1 \) of the first line is \( 3 \).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. Rewriting the second line \( y + 1 = (a + 6)x \):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    y = (a + 6)x - 1
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    So, the slope \( m_2 \) of the second line is \( a + 6 \).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Since the lines are parallel, their slopes must be equal:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3 = a + 6
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Now, solve for \( a \):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m a + 6 = 3
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m a = 3 - 6
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m a = -3
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Thus, the value of \( a \) is \(\boxed{-3}\).<|endoftext|>
