[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    Take the square root:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    |z| = \sqrt{164425} = 407
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. **Calculate the argument (argument of the complex number)**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    The argument \(\arg(z)\) of a complex number \( z = a + bi \) is given by:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \arg(z) = \tan^{-1}\left(\frac{b}{a}\right)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    Here, \( a = -324 \) and \( b = 243 \).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \arg(z) = \tan^{-1}\left(\frac{243}{-324}\right)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
