[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m m \leq -4\sqrt{7} \quad \text{or} \quad m \geq 4\sqrt{7}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Since \( m \) is a positive integer, the possible values for \( m \) are \( 1, 2, 3, \ldots \). Therefore, the possible values for \( m \) are \( 1, 2, 3, \ldots, 14 \). This means there are 14 possible values for \( m \).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
