[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Let $A, B, C$ be vertices of an icosidodecahedron in space, all in spherical coordinates where $\rho=1$ (even regular polytope). Use spherical coordinates to compute $\mathrm{dist}(A, B)$ without using the cosine rule. To compute the distance between two vertices \(A\) and \(B\) of an icosidodecahedron in spherical coordinates, we can use the spherical distance formula. The spherical distance \(d_A(B)\) between two points in a spherical coordinate system is given by:
