[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To find the remainder when \(x^3 - 3x^2 - 9x + 30\) is divided by \(x - 3\), we can use polynomial long division. Here are the steps:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. **Set up the division**: We divide \(x^3 - 3x^2 - 9x + 30\) by \(x - 3\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. **First step**: Divide the leading term of the dividend \(x^3\) by the leading term of the divisor \(x\), which gives \(x^2\). Write \(x^2\) above the division bar.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \begin{array}{r|rrrr}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      x - 3 & x^3 & -3x^2 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m            & x^3 &       & \\
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \end{array}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    This gives us \(x^2\) as the first term of the quotient.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3. **Multiply and subtract**: Multiply \(x^2\) by \(x - 3\) to get \(x^3 - 3x^2\). Subtract this from the original polynomial.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \begin{array}{r|rrrr}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      x - 3 & x^3 & -3x^2 \\
