[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To solve the expression \(\left \lceil \frac{\left \lfloor 52/3 \right\rfloor}{5/23} \right \rceil\), we will break it down step by step.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m First, we need to evaluate the floor function \(\left \lfloor 52/3 \right\rfloor\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 52 \div 3 = 17.3333\ldots
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The greatest integer less than or equal to 17.3333 is 17. Therefore,
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \left \lfloor 52/3 \right\rfloor = 17
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Next, we substitute this back into the expression:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \frac{17}{5/23} = 17 \times \frac{23}{5} = \frac{391}{5} = 78.2
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Now, we need to divide this result by \(\frac{5}{23}\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \frac{78.2}{\frac{5}{23}} = 78.2 \times \frac{23}{5} = \frac{1823.6}{5} = 364.72
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Finally, we apply the ceiling function to this result:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \left \lceil 364.72 \right \rceil = 365
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Thus, the final answer is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \boxed{365}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
