[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To determine how many numbers less than 25 are abundant numbers, we need to check each number from 1 up to 24 and see if the sum of its proper factors is greater than the number itself.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The proper factors of a number \( n \) are all the factors of \( n \) excluding \( n \) itself. We can list the proper factors of numbers from 1 to 24 as follows:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \begin{aligned}
