[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m A freight train travels 1 mile in 1 minute 30 seconds. At this rate, how many miles will the train travel in 1 hour?
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To determine how many miles the train will travel in 1 hour, we need to follow these steps:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. **Convert the train's speed from minutes and seconds to seconds:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - The train travels 1 mile in 1 minute 30 seconds. First, convert this time into seconds.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      - 1 minute = 60 seconds
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      - 30 seconds = 30 seconds
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      - Therefore, \(\text{train's speed in seconds} = 1 \times 60 + 30 = 70\) seconds
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - Convert the train's speed into miles per hour.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      - 1 mile = 1609.344 meters
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      - 1 meter = \(\frac{1}{1000}\) meters
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      - 1 hour = 3600 seconds
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      - Therefore, \(\text{progress per second} = \frac{1609.344}{1000} \times \frac{1}{3600}\)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      - \(\text{progress per second} = \frac{1609.344}{3600000} \approx 0.000442036667\) miles per hour
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      - The total progress in meters per hour:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m        \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m        \text{Total progress} = 70 \times 0.000442036667 \approx 0.03054266699 \text{ miles per hour}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m        \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. **Convert the total distance traveled in 1 hour to miles:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - 1 hour = 3600 seconds
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - Total distance = 0.03054266699 miles per hour
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - Total distance in 1 hour = \(3600 \times 0.03054266699 \approx 110.376 \text{ miles}\)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Therefore, the train will travel \(\boxed{110.38}\) miles in 1 hour.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
