[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To determine how many 270-page books Robert can read in six hours, we need to follow these steps:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. **Calculate Robert's reading speed:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    Robert reads 90 pages per hour.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. **Determine the total number of pages of a single book:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    Each book contains 270 pages.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3. **Calculate the time required to read one book completely:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    We divide the total number of pages by the number of pages per hour.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \text{Time to read one book} = \frac{270 \text{ pages}}{90 \text{ pages per hour}} = 3 \text{ hours}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 4. **Calculate the total number of books Robert can read in six hours:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    We multiply the reading time by the number of hours.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
