[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To express 20 as a sum of distinct powers of 2, we would write $20 = 2^4 + 2^2$. The sum of the exponents of these powers is $4 + 2 = 6$. If 1562 were expressed as a sum of distinct powers of 2, what would be the least possible sum of the exponents of these powers?
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To express 1562 as a sum of distinct powers of 2, we need to find the largest power of 2 that does not exceed 1562. We do this by repeatedly dividing 1562 by 2 and recording the integer parts of the results.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Starting with 1562:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ 1562 \div 2 = 781 \text{ remainder } 0 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ 781 \div 2 = 390 \text{ remainder } 1 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ 390 \div 2 = 195 \text{ remainder } 0 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ 195 \div 2 = 97 \text{ remainder } 1 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ 97 \div 2 = 48 \text{ remainder } 1 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ 48 \div 2 = 24 \text{ remainder } 0 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ 24 \div 2 = 12 \text{ remainder } 0 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ 12 \div 2 = 6 \text{ remainder } 0 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ 6 \div 2 = 3 \text{ remainder } 0 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ 3 \div 2 = 1 \text{ remainder } 1 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ 1 \div 2 = 0 \text{ remainder } 1 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m So, the powers of 2 that sum up to 1562 are:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ 2^9 = 512, \quad 2^{10} = 1024 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m This corresponds to the sum:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ 512 + 1024 = 1568 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Thus, the least possible sum of the exponents is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ 9 + 10 = 19 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Therefore, the answer is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \boxed{19}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
