[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m It took $4$ days for $75$ workers, all working together at the same rate, to build an embankment. If only $50$ workers had been available, how many total days would it have taken to build the embankment?
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To determine the number of days it would take for 50 workers to build the embankment, we need to first find the combined work rate of the workers. We know that 75 workers can build the embankment in 4 days. Therefore, the combined work rate of 75 workers is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[75 \text{ workers} \times 4 \text{ days} = 300 \text{ workers-days}\]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m This means that 300 worker-days are required to build the embankment. Now, we need to find out how many days it would take for 50 workers to complete this same work. Let \(D\) be the number of days required for 50 workers to build the embankment. The combined work rate of 50 workers is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[50 \text{ workers} \times D \text{ days} = 300 \text{ worker-days}\]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m From this equation, we can solve for \(D\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[50D = 300\]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[D = \frac{300}{50} = 6\]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Therefore, it would take 50 workers 6 days to build the embankment. The final answer is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[\boxed{6}\]<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m [Ground Truth]
