[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To solve the problem, we need to use the property of similar triangles. Since triangles \(DEF\) and \(ABC\) are similar, the ratios of their corresponding sides are equal. Let's denote the length of segment \(AB\) as \(x\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Given:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - \(DE = 6\)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - \(EF = 12\)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - \(BC = 18\) units
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m We can set up the following proportion based on the similarity of triangles:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \frac{DE}{EF} = \frac{BC}{AB}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Substitute the given values into the proportion:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \frac{6}{12} = \frac{18}{x}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Simplify the fraction \(\frac{6}{12}\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \frac{1}{2} = \frac{18}{x}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To solve for \(x\), cross-multiply:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1 \cdot x = 2 \cdot 18
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m x = 36
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Thus, the length of segment \(AB\) is \(\boxed{36}\).<|endoftext|>
