[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To find the value of \( f(11) \) for the function \( f(n) = n^2 + n + 17 \), we need to substitute \( n = 11 \) into the function and perform the arithmetic operation step by step.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. Start with the function:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    f(n) = n^2 + n + 17
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. Substitute \( n = 11 \) into the function:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    f(11) = 11^2 + 11 + 17
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3. Calculate \( 11^2 \):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    11^2 = 121
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 4. Now add 11 to 121:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    11^2 + 11 = 121 + 11 = 132
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 5. Add 17 to 132:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    132 + 17 = 149
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Therefore, the value of \( f(11) \) is \(\boxed{149}\).<|endoftext|>
