[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m In triangle $ABC$, $AB = BC$, and $\overline{BD}$ is an altitude. Point $E$ is on the extension of $\overline{AC}$ such that $BE =
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 10$.  The values of $\tan \angle CBE$, $\tan \angle DBE$, and $\tan \angle ABE$ form a geometric progression, and the values of $\cot \angle DBE$, $\cot \angle CBE$, $\cot \angle DBC$ form an arithmetic progression.  What is the area of triangle $ABC$?
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m [asy]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m pair A,B,C,D,E;
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m A=(0,0);
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m B=(4,8);
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m C=(8,0);
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m E=(10,0);
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m D=(4,0);
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m draw(A--B--E--cycle,linewidth(0.7));
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m draw(C--B--D,linewidth(0.7));
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m label("$B$",B,N);
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m label("$A$",A,S);
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m label("$D$",D,S);
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m label("$C$",C,S);
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m label("$E$",E,S);
