[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Amy works for 36 hours per week for 10 weeks during the summer, making $\$3000$. If she works for 30 weeks during the school year at the same rate of pay and needs to make another $\$3000$, how many hours per week must she work?
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To determine how many hours per week Amy must work during the school year to earn another \$3000, we can follow these steps:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. Calculate her hourly wage during the summer.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. Determine her hourly wage during the school year.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3. Calculate the total number of hours she needs to work during the school year to earn another \$3000.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m **Step 1: Calculate her hourly wage during the summer.**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Amy works 36 hours per week for 10 weeks during the summer, making a total of:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ 36 \text{ hours/week} \times 10 \text{ weeks} = 360 \text{ hours} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Her hourly wage during the summer is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ \frac{3000 \text{ dollars}}{360 \text{ hours}} = \frac{3000}{360} \approx 8.33 \text{ dollars/hour} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m **Step 2: Determine her hourly wage during the school year.**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m In the school year, she works 30 weeks, so her hourly wage is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ \frac{3000 \text{ dollars}}{30 \text{ weeks}} = 100 \text{ dollars/hour} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m **Step 3: Calculate the total number of hours she needs to work during the school year to earn another \$3000.**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To earn another \$3000 over 30 weeks, she needs to work:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ \frac{3000 \text{ dollars}}{100 \text{ dollars/hour}} = 30 \text{ hours/week} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Therefore, Amy must work \(\boxed{30}\) hours per week during the school year.<|endoftext|>
