[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To find the maximum value of the expression \(\sqrt{3x + 1} + \sqrt{3y + 3} + \sqrt{3z + 5}\) given the constraints \(x + y + z = 1\) and \(x \ge -\frac{1}{3}\), \(y \ge -1\), and \(z \ge -\frac{5}{3}\), we will evaluate the expression at the boundary points of these constraints.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m First, consider the point \((x, y, z) = (1, 0, 0)\). The expression becomes:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \sqrt{3 \cdot 1 + 1} + \sqrt{3 \cdot 0 + 3} + \sqrt{3 \cdot 0 + 5} = \sqrt{4} + \sqrt{3} + \sqrt{5} = 2 + \sqrt{3} + \sqrt{5}.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Next, consider the point \((x, y, z) = (0, 1, 0)\). The expression becomes:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \sqrt{3 \cdot 0 + 1} + \sqrt{3 \cdot 1 + 3} + \sqrt{3 \cdot 0 + 5} = \sqrt{1} + \sqrt{6} + \sqrt{5} = 1 + \sqrt{6} + \sqrt{5}.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Now, consider the point \((x, y, z) = \left(-\frac{1}{3}, -1, -\frac{5}{3}\right)\). The expression becomes:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \sqrt{3 \cdot -\frac{1}{3} + 1} + \sqrt{3 \cdot -1 + 3} + \sqrt{3 \cdot -\frac{5}{3} + 5} = \sqrt{-1 + 1} + \sqrt{-3 + 3} + \sqrt{-5 + 5} = \sqrt{0} + \sqrt{0} + \sqrt{0} = 0.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
