[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m A church rings its bells every 15 minutes, the school rings its bells every 20 minutes and the day care center rings its bells every 25 minutes. If they all ring their bells at noon on the same day, at what time will they next all ring their bells together?  (Answer in the form AB:CD without am or pm, such as 08:00)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To determine when the church, school, and day care center will next ring their bells together, we need to find the least common multiples (LCM) of the intervals at which they ring their bells. The intervals are 15 minutes for the church, 20 minutes for the school, and 25 minutes for the day care center. We need to find the LCM of these numbers.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m First, we find the prime factorizations of the numbers:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - \(15 = 3 \times 5\)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - \(20 = 2^2 \times 5\)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - \(25 = 5^2\)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The LCM is found by taking the highest power of each prime that appears in these factorizations:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - The highest power of 2 is \(2^2\)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - The highest power of 3 is \(3^1\)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - The highest power of 5 is \(5^2\)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Therefore, the LCM is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2^2 \times 3^1 \times 5^2 = 4 \times 3 \times 25 = 300
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m So, the LCM of 15, 20, and 25 is 300. This means that the bells will all ring together every 300 minutes.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To find out what time they will next ring together, we need to add 300 minutes to the current time. If we start from noon, the time will be:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
