[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Sure, let's break down the problem step-by-step.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. **Understanding the Diagram and Perimeter**:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - Rectangle \(PQRS\) is divided into three identical squares, so each square has side length \(x\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - The perimeter of the entire rectangle is 120 cm. Since a rectangle has four sides, the perimeter can be expressed as \(2 \times (\text{length} + \text{width})\). In this case, the two longer sides can be thought of as horizontal sides of length \(3x\) (since the rectangle is divided into three squares, the length of each side of the longer squares is half the length of the shorter squares, which is \(x\)).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. **Setting Up the Equation**:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - The perimeter of the rectangle is given by the equation:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      2(3x + \text{height}) = 120
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - Simplifying the equation:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      6x + \text{height} = 60
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      Since the height of each square is \(x\) and the rectangle has a total height of 1 cm (the original length of \(P\) at the top minus the height of the bottom \( -x \)), the height of the rectangle is \(1 - x\). So, the equation becomes:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      6x + 1 - x = 60
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      Simplifying further:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      5x + 1 = 60
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      Subtracting 1 from both sides:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      5x = 59
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      Dividing by 5:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      x = 11
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3. **Calculating the Area**:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - The area of the rectangle \(PQRS\) is the product of its length and width:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      \text{Area} = 3x \times 11 = 33x
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - Substituting \(x = 11\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      \text{Area} = 33 \times 11 = 363
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m So, the area of the rectangle is \(\boxed{363}\) square centimeters.<|endoftext|>
