[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To find the least positive multiple of 21 that is greater than 380, we start by determining the smallest multiple of 21 that is greater than 380. We do this by dividing 380 by 21 and then rounding up to the next whole number.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m First, we perform the division:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ 380 \div 21 \approx 17.647 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Since we need a whole number, we round 17.647 up to 18. This means the smallest integer greater than 17.647 is 18. Therefore, we multiply 21 by 18 to find the least positive multiple of 21 that is greater than 380.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ 21 \times 18 = 378 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
