[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To determine the number of ways to arrange the letters of the word "TOOT", we need to calculate the number of permutations of 4 distinct items. The formula for the number of permutations of \( n \) distinct items is given by \( n! \) (n factorial), which is the product of all positive integers up to \( n \).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Here, we have 4 distinct letters: T, O, O, T. So, we need to calculate \( 4! \).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 4! = 4 \times 3 \times 2 \times 1 = 24
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Therefore, the number of ways to arrange the letters of the word "TOOT" is \(\boxed{24}\).<|endoftext|>
