[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m $ f(x)=x [\sin [ \pi x] + \sin^2 [ \pi x]] $ for $x\in (0,0.5) $, where $x$ is in units of the time $\,dt\,$ . Let $t=dt$ and define $F(t)= \frac{\partial^2f(x)}{\partial t^2}$ .
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The function $F(t)$  is also known as the error function and is closely related to the probability distribution function $ .$ 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Suppose $ t\geq 1 $ and $ F(t) $ obeys the transformation $ \displaystyle \frac{\partial f}{\partial t} |_{t=1}= 1$ ,$ \ \ \frac{\partial^2 f}{\partial t^2} |_{t=1} =  0 $ and in the fast region,the magnitude is obtained by $oreg$ 
