[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    This equation does not hold true. Therefore, there are no values of \( x \) that satisfy \( f(x) = 2 \).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The correct interpretation is that the function does not cross the horizontal asymptote at \( x = 2 \). The correct answer is that there is no \( x \)-value that satisfies the function equaling the horizontal asymptote.
