[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ 3f(1) = 2f(1) \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m This is consistent, but doesn't give us new information. Let's find \( f(5) \) directly. Set \( x = 4 \) and \( y = 1 \):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ f(4 + 1) = f(4) + f(1) \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ f(5) = 5 + f(1) \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Since we know \( f(4) = 5 \), we can substitute this value in:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ f(5) = 5 + f(1) \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To find \( f(1) \), we use the functional equation again. Set \( x = 1 \) and \( y = 1 \):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ f(1 + 1) = f(1) + f(1) \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ f(2) = 2f(1) \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ 5 = 2f(1) \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ f(1) = \frac{5}{2} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Now substitute \( f(1) = \frac{5}{2} \) back into the equation for \( f(5) \):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ f(5) = 5 + \frac{5}{2} = \frac{10}{2} + \frac{5}{2} = \frac{15}{2} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Therefore, the value of \( f(5) \) is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ \boxed{\frac{15}{2}} \]<|endoftext|>
