[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m A math textbook with a double-digit number of pages is split into sections. Each section is exactly $12$ pages long, with the exception of the epilogue, which is $11$ pages long. Every page belongs to a section. Furthermore, on the bottom of each $5$th page, a trivia fact is presented on the bottom of the page, starting from the fifth page. If a trivia fact appears on the bottom of the second-to-last page, then how many pages does the textbook have?
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To determine the total number of pages in the textbook, we need to break down the problem into smaller parts and calculate step by step.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. **Identify the number of pages in each section:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - Each section is exactly \(12\) pages long.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - The text has an epilogue, which is \(11\) pages long, on the bottom.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - On the bottom of each \(5\)th page, there is a trivia fact.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. **Determine the number of sections:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - We know that every page belongs to a section.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - The text is placed \(0\) pages long (since the epilogue has not yet appeared and trivia facts are not additional lengths more than the epilogue).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3. **Calculate the number of textbooks:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - Since each page is one page long, the text will have \(0\) textbooks.
