[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - The hundredths place is the next digit to the right of the decimal point. In \(3.45\), the hundredths place is \(5\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. ** Look at the digit in the thousandths place to determine whether to round up or keep the digit in the tenths place:**
