[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To find the largest integer less than 80 that leaves a remainder of 3 when divided by 5, we can follow these steps:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. Identify the general form of the integer. A number \( n \) that leaves a remainder of 3 when divided by 5 can be written as:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    n = 5k + 3
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    where \( k \) is an integer.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. We need \( n \) to be less than 80. So, we set up the inequality:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    5k + 3 < 80
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3. Solve the inequality for \( k \):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    5k < 80 - 3
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    5k < 77
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    k < \frac{77}{5}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    k < 15.4
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 4. Since \( k \) must be an integer, the largest possible value for \( k \) is 15.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 5. Substitute \( k = 15 \) back into the expression for \( n \):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    n = 5 \cdot 15 + 3
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    n = 75 + 3
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    n = 78
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 6. Verify that 78 is indeed less than 80 and leaves a remainder of 3 when divided by 5:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    78 \div 5 = 15 \text{ remainder } 3
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Therefore, the largest integer less than 80 that leaves a remainder of 3 when divided by 5 is:
