[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Is the function $f(x) = 5^x - 5^{-x}$ even, odd, or neither?
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Enter "odd", "even", or "neither".
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To determine whether the function \( f(x) = 5^x - 5^{-x} \) is even, odd, or neither, we need to analyze its behavior under the transformation \( x \to -x \).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m ### Step 1: Effect of the Transformation
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Consider \( f(-x) \):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m f(-x) = 5^{-x} - 5^x
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m ### Step 2: Evaluate \( f(-x) \)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Now, substitute \( -x \) into the function:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m f(-x) = 5^{-x} - 5^x
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m ### Step 3: Compare \( f(-x) \) with \( f(x) \) and \( -f(x) \)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m We need to compare \( f(-x) \) with \( f(x) \) and \( -f(x) \):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m f(x) = 5^x - 5^{-x}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m -f(x) = -(5^x - 5^{-x}) = -5^x + 5^{-x}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m ### Step 4: Check for Even or Odd Properties
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m A function \( g(x) \) is even if \( g(-x) = g(x) \) for all \( x \) in its domain, and it is odd if \( g(-x) = -g(x) \) for all \( x \) in its domain.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m f(-x) = 5^{-x} - 5^x
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m f(x) = 5^x - 5^{-x}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Clearly, \( f(-x) = -f(x) \), so \( f(x) \) is odd.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m ### Conclusion
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The function \( f(x) = 5^x - 5^{-x} \) is \(\boxed{\text{odd}}\).<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m [Ground Truth]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \text{odd}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
