[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Sure! Let's break this down step by step.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. **Dana's Meals Calculation:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - Dana divides his 9 peaches evenly into 0.36 peaches per meal.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - To find out how many meals Dana can make, we divide the total number of peaches he has by the number of peaches per meal:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      \frac{9 \text{ peaches}}{0.36 \text{ peaches/meal}} = \frac{9}{0.36} = 25 \text{ meals}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. **Anna's Meals Calculation:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - Anna divides her 7 peaches into 20 meals of equal size.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - To find out how many meals Anna can make, we divide the total number of peaches she has by the number of peaches per meal:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      \frac{7 \text{ peaches}}{20 \text{ peaches/meal}} = \frac{7}{20} = 0.35 \text{ meals}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
