[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To find the least positive three-digit multiple of 7, we need to determine the smallest number that is a multiple of 7 and less than or equal to 999. We can do this by dividing 999 by 7 and rounding up to the nearest whole number. The number result of this division, minus 1 (since we need a multiple of 7), will give us the smallest three-digit multiple of 7.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
