[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Let $\mathbf{a} = \begin{pmatrix} 4 \\ \sqrt{\pi} \\ -14 \end{pmatrix}$ and $\mathbf{b} = \begin{pmatrix} -1 \\ 3 \\ 10 \end{pmatrix}.$  Compute $\mathbf{a} \cdot (\mathbf{a} \times \mathbf{b}).$
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To solve the problem of finding \(\mathbf{a} \cdot (\mathbf{a} \times \mathbf{b})\), we will use the property of the dot product and the cross product of vectors. Let's proceed step by step.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. **Compute the cross product \(\mathbf{a} \times \mathbf{b}\):**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    The cross product \(\mathbf{a} \times \mathbf{b}\) is given by the determinant of the following matrix:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \mathbf{a} \times \mathbf{b} = \begin{vmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \mathbf{i} & \mathbf{j} & \mathbf{k} \\
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    4 & \sqrt{\pi} & -14 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    -1 & 3 & 10
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \end{vmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    Expanding this determinant, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \mathbf{a} \times \mathbf{b} = \mathbf{i} \left( \sqrt{\pi} \cdot 10 - (-14) \cdot 3 \right) - \mathbf{j} \left( 4 \cdot 10 - (-14) \cdot (-1) \right) + \mathbf{k} \left( 4 \cdot 3 - \sqrt{\pi} \cdot (-1) \right)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    = \mathbf{i} \left( 10\sqrt{\pi} + 42 \right) - \mathbf{j} \left( 40 - 14 \right) + \mathbf{k} \left( 12 + \sqrt{\pi} \right)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    = \mathbf{i} \left( 10\sqrt{\pi} + 42 \right) - \mathbf{j} \left( 26 \right) + \mathbf{k} \left( 12 + \sqrt{\pi} \right)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    = \begin{pmatrix} 10\sqrt{\pi} + 42 \\ -26 \\ 12 + \sqrt{\pi} \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. **Compute the dot product \(\mathbf{a} \cdot (\mathbf{a} \times \mathbf{b})\):**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    The dot product of \(\mathbf{a} = \begin{pmatrix} 4 \\ \sqrt{\pi} \\ -14 \end{pmatrix}\) and \(\mathbf{a} \times \mathbf{b}\) is given by the dot product of the two vectors:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \mathbf{a} \cdot (\mathbf{a} \times \mathbf{b}) = 4 \cdot (10\sqrt{\pi} + 42) + \sqrt{\pi} \cdot (-26) + (-14) \cdot (12 + \sqrt{\pi})
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    = 4 \left( 10\sqrt{\pi} + 42 \right) - 26\sqrt{\pi} - 168 - 14\sqrt{\pi}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    = 40\sqrt{\pi} + 168 - 26\sqrt{\pi} - 168 - 14\sqrt{\pi}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    = (40\sqrt{\pi} - 26\sqrt{\pi} - 14\sqrt{\pi}) + (168 - 168)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    = 24\sqrt{\pi}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Therefore, the final answer is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \boxed{24\sqrt{\pi}}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
