[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Let $a,$ $b,$ $c$ be positive real numbers.  Find the minimum value of
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[\frac{(a + b)(a + c)(b + c)}{abc}.\]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To find the minimum value of the expression \(\frac{(a + b)(a + c)(b + c)}{abc}\), we can use the AM-GM (Arithmetic Mean-Geometric Mean) inequality. The AM-GM inequality states that for any non-negative real numbers \(x_1, x_2, \ldots, x_n\),
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \frac{x_1 + x_2 + \cdots + x_n}{n} \geq \sqrt[n]{x_1 x_2 \cdots x_n},
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m with equality if and only if \(x_1 = x_2 = \cdots = x_n\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m We apply the AM-GM inequality to the terms \(a + b\), \(a + c\), and \(b + c\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \frac{(a + b) + (a + c) + (b + c)}{3} \geq \sqrt[3]{(a + b)(a + c)(b + c)}.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m This simplifies to
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \frac{2(a + b + c)}{3} \geq \sqrt[3]{(a + b)(a + c)(b + c)}.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Next, we need to maximize \((a + b)(a + c)(b + c)\). Consider the expression \(a + b + c\). By the AM-GM inequality,
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \frac{a + b + c}{3} \geq \sqrt[3]{abc},
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m which implies
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m a + b + c \geq 3\sqrt[3]{abc}.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The equality holds if and only if \(a = b = c\). So, if \(a = b = c\), then
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m a + b + c = 3a \geq 3\sqrt[3]{3a^3} = 3\sqrt[3]{9a^3} = 3\sqrt[3]{9}a = 3\sqrt[3]{9}a,
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m and
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m a + b + c = 3c \geq 3\sqrt[3]{3c^3} = 3\sqrt[3]{9c^3} = 3\sqrt[3]{9}c.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Thus, \(\sqrt[3]{(a + b)(a + c)(b + c)} = \sqrt[3]{(3\sqrt[3]{9}a)(3\sqrt[3]{9}c)(3\sqrt[3]{9}a)} = \sqrt[3]{(3\sqrt[3]{9})^3(a + b + c)} = \sqrt[3]{9a + c + 3ca} = \sqrt[3]{9} = \sqrt[3]{9} = \sqrt[3]{9} = 3\sqrt[3]{9}.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Therefore, we have
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \frac{(a + b)(a + c)(b + c)}{abc} = \frac{3\sqrt[3]{9}a}{3a \cdot 3c} = \frac{\sqrt[3]{9}}{3c} = \frac{\sqrt[3]{9}}{3c} = \sqrt[3]{\frac{9}{3}c} = \sqrt[3]{3c} \geq \sqrt[3]{3}.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Equality in the AM-GM inequality holds if and only if \(a = b = c\). Therefore, the minimum value of \(\frac{(a + b)(a + c)(b + c)}{abc}\) is \(\sqrt[3]{3}\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The answer is
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \boxed{\sqrt[3]{3}}.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
