[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m First, we will use the sympy library to find the solutions to the cubic equation.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m ```python
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m import sympy as sp
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m # Define the variable and the equation
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m t = sp.symbols('t')
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m equation = t**3 - t**2 + 9*t - 7
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m # Solve the equation
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m solutions = sp.solve(equation, t)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m print(solutions)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m ```
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m ```output
