[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m We can use the fact that \(a\) and \(b\) are roots of the polynomial \(x^5 - x^4 + x^3 - x^2 + x - 1 = 0\). This polynomial can be related to the Dirichlet L-function associated with the Riemann zeta function, and specifically to the form given by the product of the roots of unity.
