[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To express the quotient \(1023_4 \div 11_4\) in base 4, we will follow these steps:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. Convert the decimal numbers \(1023_4\) and \(11_4\) to base 10.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. Perform the division in base 10.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3. Convert the quotient back to base 4.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m ### Step 1: Convert \(1023_4\) to base 10
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The number \(1023_4\) can be expanded as follows:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1023_4 = 1 \cdot 4^3 + 0 \cdot 4^2 + 2 \cdot 4^1 + 3 \cdot 4^0
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Calculating each term:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1 \cdot 4^3 = 1 \cdot 64 = 64
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 0 \cdot 4^2 = 0 \cdot 16 = 0
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2 \cdot 4^1 = 2 \cdot 4 = 8
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3 \cdot 4^0 = 3 \cdot 1 = 3
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Adding these values together gives:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 64 + 0 + 8 + 3 = 75
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m So, \(1023_4 = 75_{10}\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m ### Step 2: Convert \(11_4\) to base 10
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The number \(11_4\) can be expanded as follows:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
