[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To solve the expression \(1 - 3 + 5 - 7 + 9 - \cdots - 43 + 45 - 47 + 49\) step by step, we first observe that it resembles the alternating sum of the first \(n\) odd numbers. The general form of the sequence alternating between positive and negative terms, starting from 1, can be written as:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
