[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Here, \(n\) is a positive integer. Now, let's analyze the sequence:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. The first odd number is 1, so \(1\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. The second odd number is 3, so \(1 - 3\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3. The third odd number is 5, so \(1 - 3 + 5\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 4. The fourth odd number is 7, so \(1 - 3 + 5 - 7\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 5. And so on...
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Notice that the sequence alternates between positive and negative terms, starting with positive terms. To simplify the expression, we can group the terms in pairs:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ (1 - 3) + (5 - 7) + (9 - 11) + \cdots + (4n - 4n+1) + (4n+1) \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Each pair \((2k-1) - (2k+1)\) simplifies to \(-2\), so we have:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m (1 - 3) + (5 - 7) + \cdots + (4n - 4n+1) + (4n+1) = -2 + 2 - 2 + 2 - \cdots + 2 - 2
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m If \(n\) is even, there are an even number of terms, so they all simplify to \(-2\). If \(n\) is odd, there is an odd number of terms, so the last term is \(-2\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - If \(n\) is even, it simplifies to \(-2 + 2 - 2 + 2 - \cdots + 2 - 2 = -2\) (since there are \(n/\dfrac{1}{2} = 2n\) terms).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - If \(n\) is odd, it simplifies to \(-2 + 2 - 2 + 2 - \cdots + 2 - 2 = 0\) (since there is 1 term).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
