[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To compute the matrix product \(\begin{pmatrix} 2 & - 1 \\ - 3 & 4 \end{pmatrix} \begin{pmatrix} 3 \\ - 1 \end{pmatrix}\), we need to multiply each row of the first matrix by each column of the second matrix and then sum the results.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Let's denote the first matrix as \(A\) and the second matrix as \(B\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ A = \begin{pmatrix} 2 & -1 \\ -3 & 4 \end{pmatrix}, \quad B = \begin{pmatrix} 3 \\ -1 \end{pmatrix} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The product \(AB\) is calculated as follows:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ AB = \begin{pmatrix} 2 & -1 \\ -3 & 4 \end{pmatrix} \begin{pmatrix} 3 \\ -1 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 2 \cdot 3 + (-1) \cdot (-1) \\ -3 \cdot 3 + 4 \cdot (-1) \end{pmatrix} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Now, we compute each element of the resulting matrix:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ 2 \cdot 3 + (-1) \cdot (-1) = 6 + 1 = 7 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ -3 \cdot 3 + 4 \cdot (-1) = -9 - 4 = -13 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m So, the resulting matrix is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ AB = \begin{pmatrix} 7 \\ -13 \end{pmatrix} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Therefore, the final answer is:
