[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Now, we need to find out how many years it takes for a tree that is currently 12 feet to grow to become \(3 \text{ feet}\). The tree grows at a rate of 18 inches per year, which is equivalent to \(18/12 = 1.5\) feet per year. To find the number of years (\(t\)) it takes to grow from 12 feet to 3 feet, we divide the total inch growth (3 feet) by the growth rate (1.5 feet per year):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ t = \frac{3 \text{ feet}}{1.5 \text{ feet/year}} = 2 \text{ years} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
