[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To determine the total number of canoes built by BoatsRUs by the end of May, we need to calculate the number of canoes built in each month from January to May and then sum them up.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. **January:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    BoatsRUs built 7 canoes.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. **February:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    Each month, they built twice the number of canoes they had built in the previous month.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - February 2023: \( 2 \times 7 = 14 \) canoes
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - March: \( 2 \times 14 = 28 \) canoes
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - April: \( 2 \times 28 = 56 \) canoes
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - May: \( 2 \times 56 = 112 \) canoes
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3. **Total number of canoes by the end of May:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    Sum the number of canoes built each of the four months:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    7 + 14 + 28 + 56 = 105
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Thus, the total number of canoes built by BoatsRUs by the end of May is \(\boxed{105}\).<|endoftext|>
