[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To determine how many different positive two-digit integers can be formed using the digits 2, 4, and 7 without repeating any digit, we need to consider the number of possible permutations of these three digits. Since we are forming two-digit numbers and not two-digit integers (e.g., 26 or 74), we will calculate the number of permutations of the three digits.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The number of permutations of three distinct digits is given by the factorial of 3, which is calculated as follows:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
