[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To find the distance between the points \((-5, 5)\) and \((5, -5)\), we can use the distance formula. The distance formula is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m d = \sqrt{(x_2 - x_1)^2 + (y_2 - y_1)^2}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Here, \((x_1, y_1) = (-5, 5)\) and \((x_2, y_2) = (5, -5)\). Substituting these coordinates into the formula, we get:
