[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Find the greatest common divisor of 9,009 and 14,014.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To find the greatest common divisor (GCD) of \( 9009 \) and \( 14014 \), we will use the Euclidean algorithm. The Euclidean algorithm involves repeated division and taking remainders until we reach a remainder of 0. The last non-zero remainder is the GCD.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Let's start by applying the algorithm.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. Divide \( 14014 \) by \( 9009 \).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    14014 \div 9009 = 1 \quad \text{(quotient)}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    14014 - 9009 \times 1 = 5005
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    So, the remainder is \( 5005 \).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. Now, divide \( 9009 \) by \( 5005 \).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    9009 \div 5005 = 1 \quad \text{(quotient)}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    9009 - 5005 \times 1 = 4004
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    So, the remainder is \( 4004 \).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3. Divide \( 5005 \) by \( 4004 \).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    5005 \div 4004 = 1 \quad \text{(quotient)}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    5005 - 4004 \times 1 = 1001
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    So, the remainder is \( 1001 \).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 4. Divide \( 4004 \) by \( 1001 \).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    4004 \div 1001 = 4 \quad \text{(quotient)}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    4004 - 1001 \times 4 = 0
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    So, the remainder is \( 0 \).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Since the remainder is now \( 0 \), the last non-zero remainder is the GCD. Therefore, the GCD of \( 9009 \) and \( 14014 \) is \( 1001 \).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Thus, the greatest common divisor of \( 9009 \) and \( 14014 \) is \(\boxed{1001}\).<|endoftext|>
