[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2^2 &= 4 \quad \text{(units digit is 4)} \\
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2^3 &= 8 \quad \text{(units digit is 8)} \\
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2^4 &= 16 \quad \text{(units digit is 6)} \\
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2^5 &= 32 \quad \text{(units digit is 2)} \\
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \end{aligned}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m We can see that the units digits repeat every 4 powers: 2, 4, 8, 6. This is because the units digits of the powers of 2 cycle through 2, 4, 8, 6 in a repeating pattern every 4 terms.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To find the units digit of \( 2^{67^{17}} \), we need to determine the position of 67 in the repeating cycle. We do this by finding the remainder when 67 is divided by 4:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 67 \div 4 = 16 \text{ remainder } 3
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m This means that \( 67^{17} \) is the same as \( 3^{17} \) in terms of the repeating pattern. Now we need to find the units digit of \( 3^3 \):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3^3 = 27
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The units digit of 27 is 7. Therefore, the units digit of \( 2^{67^{17}} \) is the same as the units digit of \( 2^7 \), which is 12. Since the units digit is a possible value (1 or 2, 4 or 8), and in this case, it is 1, we conclude that the units digit of \( 2^{67^{17}} \) is 1.
