[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To solve the problem, we need to determine the total number of stamps on the first 4 complete books under Jenny's new stamp collection system. Let's break it down step by step.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m First, calculate the number of stamps in each of the 8 stamp books. Each book contains 42 pages, and each page contains 6 stamps.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 42 \text{ pages/book} \times 6 \text{ stamps/page} = 252 \text{ stamps/book}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Since there are 8 books in total, the number of stamps in all the books is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 8 \text{ books} \times 252 \text{ stamps/book} = 2016 \text{ stamps}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Next, determine the number of stamps in the remaining pages of the 4 books. Each book now contains 42 pages, and each page now contains 10 stamps.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 42 \text{ pages/book} \times 10 \text{ stamps/page} = 420 \text{ stamps/book}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Since there are 4 books in total, the number of stamps in all the books is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 4 \text{ books} \times 420 \text{ stamps/book} = 1680 \text{ stamps}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Now, calculate the total number of stamps in all 4 complete books:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1680 \text{ stamps} + 2016 \text{ stamps} = 3696 \text{ stamps}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To find the number of stamps on the last page, we need to determine how many stamps are in the remaining pages of the non-last book. The total number of pages in the 4 non-last books is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 4 \text{ books} \times 42 \text{ pages/book} = 168 \text{ pages}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Each page in the non-last book contains 8 new stamps (since 10 original stamps plus the 1 remaining stamp"), so:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 8 \text{ pages/non-last book} \times 10 \text{ stamps/page} = 80 \text{ stamps/non-last book}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The total number of stamps in the non-last book is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 168 \text{ pages/non-last book} \times 80 \text{ stamps/page} = 13440 \text{ stamps/non-last book}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The firstbook has 8 new stamps per page, so the total number of stamps in the first book is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 8 \text{ pages/book} \times 10 \text{ stamps/page} = 80 \text{ stamps/book}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The last page will contain the same number of new stamps as the first book, which is 80 stamps.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Despite the increased capacity of the books, the total number of stamps collected remains the same. Therefore, the number of stamps on the last page of the fifth book is:
