[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m This is because the angle between a vector and its negative is the internal angle between the original vector and the adjacent vector. So:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ \text{Angle between } \mathbf{a} \text{ and } -\mathbf{a} = 180^\circ - 43^\circ = 137^\circ. \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Putting this in our final answer:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
