[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To find the units digit of the sum \(3^1 + 3^3 + 3^5 + 3^7 + \ldots + 3^{2009}\), we first need to observe the units digit of each term in the sum. The units digits of the powers of 3 repeat every 4 terms. Let's list the first few powers of 3 to identify the pattern:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \begin{aligned}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3^1 & = 3 \quad \text{(units digit is 3)} \\
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3^2 & = 9 \quad \text{(units digit is 9)} \\
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3^3 & = 27 \quad \text{(units digit is 7)} \\
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3^4 & = 81 \quad \text{(units digit is 1)} \\
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3^5 & = 243 \quad \text{(units digit is 3)} \\
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3^6 & = 729 \quad \text{(units digit is 9)} \\
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3^7 & = 2187 \quad \text{(units digit is 7)} \\
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \end{aligned}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m We can see that the units digits repeat every 4 terms: 3, 9, 7, 1. Therefore, we need to find the units digit of the sum \(3 + 9 + 7 + 1 + 3 + 9 + 7 + 1 + \ldots + 3^{2009}\). This is an arithmetic series where the first term \(a = 3\) and the common difference \(d = 2\) with 2010 terms in total. The sum of the first \(n\) terms of an arithmetic series is given by the formula:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m S_n = \frac{n}{2} (2a + (n-1)d)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Here, \(n = 2010\), \(a = 3\), and \(d = 2\). Plugging in these values, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m S_{2010} = \frac{2010}{2} (2 \cdot 3 + (2010-1) \cdot 2) = 1005 (6 + 4018) = 1005 \cdot 4024 = 4049240
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The units digit of 4049240 is 0. Therefore, the units digit of the 2010th term (3rd term) of the sum is the same as the units digit of 3, which is 3.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Thus, the units digit of the sum \(3^1 + 3^3 + 3^5 + 3^7 + \ldots + 3^{2009}\) is \(\boxed{3}\).<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
