[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To factor the expression \(2x(x-3) + 3(x-3)\), we will follow these steps:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. **Identify the common factor:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    Both terms in the expression \(2x(x-3) + 3(x-3)\) have a common factor of \((x-3)\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. **Factor out the common factor:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    We can factor \((x-3)\) out of each term:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    2x(x-3) + 3(x-3) = (x-3)(2x) + (x-3)(3)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3. **Remove the common factor:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    Since \((x-3)\) is a common factor in both terms, we can factor it out:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    (x-3)(2x) + (x-3)(3) = (x-3)(2x + 3)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Thus, the factored form of the expression \(2x(x-3) + 3(x-3)\) is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \boxed{(x-3)(2x+3)}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m [Ground Truth]
