[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Now, we complete the square for the \(y\) terms. We take half of \(-16\) (the coefficient of \(y\)) and square it (which gives \(-8^2 = 64\)). We add and subtract 64 inside the equation:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
