[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To determine how many minutes less a 450-mile trip would take compared to a 475-mile trip at a steady speed of 50 miles per hour, we need to follow these steps:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. **Calculate the total time for a 475-mile trip:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \text{Time} = \frac{\text{Distance}}{\text{Speed}} = \frac{475 \text{ miles}}{50 \text{ miles per hour}} = 9.5 \text{ hours}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. **Calculate the total time for a 450-mile trip:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \text{Time} = \frac{\text{Distance}}{\text{Speed}} = \frac{450 \text{ miles}}{50 \text{ miles per hour}} = 9 \text{ hours}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3. **Determine the difference in time between the two trips:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \text{Difference} = 9 \text{ hours} - 9.5 \text{ hours} = -0.5 \text{ hours}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    The negative sign indicates that the time for the 450-mile trip is 0.5 hours less than the 475-mile trip.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 4. **Convert the difference into minutes:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \text{Difference in minutes} = 0.5 \text{ hours} \times 60 \text{ minutes per hour} = 30 \text{ minutes}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Therefore, a 450-mile trip would take \boxed{30} minutes less than a 475-mile trip.<|endoftext|>
