[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To determine the height of the second cylinder, we first need to find the height of the first cylinder using its given radius and volume. The volume \( V \) of a cylinder is given by the formula:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ V = \pi r^2 h \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m where \( r \) is the radius and \( h \) is the height. For the first cylinder, the radius \( r \) is 6 inches and the volume is 2304 cubic inches. Substituting these values into the formula, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ 2304 = \pi (6)^2 h \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ 2304 = 36\pi h \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ h = \frac{2304}{36\pi} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ h = \frac{56}{\pi} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m So the height of the first cylinder is \( \frac{56}{\pi} \) inches. Next, we use this height to find the height of the second cylinder, which has a radius of 8 inches. Let \( h_2 \) be the height of the second cylinder. Again, we use the volume formula:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ V = \pi (8)^2 h_2 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ 2304 = \pi (8)^2 h_2 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ 2304 = 64\pi h_2 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ h_2 = \frac{2304}{64\pi} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ h_2 = \frac{36}{\pi} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m So the height of the second cylinder is \( \frac{36}{\pi} \) inches. To express this as a mixed number, we perform the division and take the integer part of the quotient:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ \frac{36}{\pi} \approx 11.3137 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The integer part is 11, so we can write the height of the second cylinder as:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ 11 \frac{5}{\pi} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Therefore, the number of inches in the height of the second cylinder is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ \boxed{11 \frac{5}{\pi}} \]<|endoftext|>
