[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. **Determine the Coordinates:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - Place the center of the larger circle \(A\) at the origin \((0, 0)\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - The coordinates of \(B\) will be \((3, 0)\) since \(B\) is on the circumference of the larger circle and its center is at \(3\) inches from \(A\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - The coordinates of \(C\) will be \((0, 3)\) since \(C\) is 3 inches from \(A\) and its center is at \(\frac{3}{2}\) feet from \(A\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3. **Calculate the Area of the Shaded Region:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - The shaded region is the area of the smaller circle with center \(A\) and radius 3 inches minus the area of the larger circle with center \(B\) and radius 6 inches.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - The area of each circle is given by the formula \(A = \pi r^2\).
