[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 4. **Calculate the Area of the Larger Circle:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \text{Area}_{B} = \pi \times 6^2 = 36\pi
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 5. **Calculate the Area of the Smaller Circle:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \text{Area}_{A} = \pi \times 3^2 = 9\pi
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 6. **Subtract the Areas to Find the Shaded Region:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \text{Area}_{\text{shaded}} = \text{Area}_{B} - \text{Area}_{A} = 36\pi - 9\pi = 27\pi
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Therefore, the area of the shaded region is \(\boxed{27\pi}\).<|endoftext|>
