[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To calculate \(\left(\dfrac{3}{4}\right)^5\), we need to raise \(\dfrac{3}{4}\) to the power of 5. This can be done by multiplying \(\dfrac{3}{4}\) by itself five times:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \left(\dfrac{3}{4}\right)^5 = \dfrac{3}{4} \times \dfrac{3}{4} \times \dfrac{3}{4} \times \dfrac{3}{4} \times \dfrac{3}{4}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Let's perform the multiplication step by step:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \left(\dfrac{3}{4}\right)^5 = \dfrac{3^5}{4^5}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m First, calculate \(3^5\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3^5 = 3 \times 3 \times 3 \times 3 \times 3 = 243
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Next, calculate \(4^5\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 4^5 = 4 \times 4 \times 4 \times 4 \times 4 = 1024
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Now, divide the two results:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \left(\dfrac{3}{4}\right)^5 = \dfrac{243}{1024}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m So, the final answer is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \boxed{\dfrac{243}{1024}}
