[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To find the sum of \(\left(\dfrac{1}{3}\right) + \left(\dfrac{1}{3}\right)^2 + \left(\dfrac{1}{3}\right)^3 + \left(\dfrac{1}{3}\right)^4\), we need to compute each term individually and then add them together.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m First, let's compute each term:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \left(\dfrac{1}{3}\right) = \dfrac{1}{3}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \left(\dfrac{1}{3}\right)^2 = \left(\dfrac{1}{3}\right) \times \left(\dfrac{1}{3}\right) = \dfrac{1}{3} \cdot \dfrac{1}{3} = \dfrac{1}{9}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \left(\dfrac{1}{3}\right)^3 = \dfrac{1}{3} \times \dfrac{1}{3} \times \dfrac{1}{3} = \dfrac{1}{27}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \left(\dfrac{1}{3}\right)^4 = \dfrac{1}{3} \times \dfrac{1}{3} \times \dfrac{1}{3} \times \dfrac{1}{3} = \dfrac{1}{81}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Now, we add these terms together:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \left(\dfrac{1}{3}\right) + \left(\dfrac{1}{3}\right)^2 + \left(\dfrac{1}{3}\right)^3 + \left(\dfrac{1}{3}\right)^4 = \dfrac{1}{3} + \dfrac{1}{9} + \dfrac{1}{27} + \dfrac{1}{81}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To add these fractions, we need a common denominator. The least common multiple of 3, 9, 27, and 81 is 81. We convert each fraction to have this common denominator:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \dfrac{1}{3} = \dfrac{27}{81}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \dfrac{1}{9} = \dfrac{9}{81}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \dfrac{1}{27} = \dfrac{3}{81}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \dfrac{1}{81} = \dfrac{1}{81}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Now we add these fractions:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \dfrac{27}{81} + \dfrac{9}{81} + \dfrac{3}{81} + \dfrac{1}{81} = \dfrac{27 + 9 + 3 + 1}{81} = \dfrac{40}{81}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Therefore, the sum is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \boxed{\dfrac{40}{81}}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
