[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To solve for the scalars \( p \) and \( q \) in the equation \(\mathbf{M}^2 = p \mathbf{M} + q \mathbf{I}\), we will follow these steps:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. Compute \(\mathbf{M}^2\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. Identify the coefficients \( p \) and \( q \) using the form \( p \mathbf{M} + q \mathbf{I} \).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m First, let's compute \(\mathbf{M}^2\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \mathbf{M}^2 = \mathbf{M} \cdot \mathbf{M}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Given:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \mathbf{M} = \begin{pmatrix} 0 & -5 \\ -2 & 4 \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \mathbf{M}^2 = \begin{pmatrix} 0 & -5 \\ -2 & 4 \end{pmatrix} \cdot \begin{pmatrix} 0 & -5 \\ -2 & 4 \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The element in the first row and first column of \(\mathbf{M}^2\) is obtained by:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m (-5)(0) + (-2)(-5) = 0 + 10 = 10
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The element in the first row and second column of \(\mathbf{M}^2\) is obtained by:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m (-5)(-5) + (-2)(4) = 25 - 8 = 17
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The element in the second row and first column of \(\mathbf{M}^2\) is obtained by:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m (-2)(0) + (4)(-5) = 0 - 20 = -20
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The element in the second row and second column of \(\mathbf{M}^2\) is obtained by:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m (-2)(-5) + (4)(4) = 10 + 16 = 26
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Thus, we have:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \mathbf{M}^2 = \begin{pmatrix} 10 & 17 \\ -20 & 26 \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Next, we expand the equation \(\mathbf{M}^2 = p \mathbf{M} + q \mathbf{I}\) to find \( p \) and \( q \):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \begin{pmatrix} 10 & 17 \\ -20 & 26 \end{pmatrix} = p \begin{pmatrix} 0 & -5 \\ -2 & 4 \end{pmatrix} + q \begin{pmatrix} 1 & 0 \\ 0 & 1 \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m This gives us the system of equations:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 10p + q = 10 \quad \text{(1)}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 17p + 0q = 17 \quad \text{(2)}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m -20p + 0q = -20 \quad \text{(3)}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m -26p + 1q = 26 \quad \text{(4)}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Let's solve system (1) and (2) for \( p \) and \( q \):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m From Equation (2):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 17p = 17 \implies p = 1
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Substitute \( p = 1 \) into Equation (1):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 10(1) + q = 10 \implies 10 + q = 10 \implies q = 0
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Thus, the ordered pair \((p, q)\) is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
