[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To determine how much greater than \(19^2\) is \(31^2\), we will first calculate the squares of 19 and 31, and then find the difference between the two.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m First, calculate \(19^2\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 19^2 = 19 \times 19 = 361
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Next, calculate \(31^2\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 31^2 = 31 \times 31 = 961
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Now, find the difference between \(31^2\) and \(19^2\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 961 - 361 = 600
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Thus, \(31^2\) is \(\boxed{600}\) greater than \(19^2\).<|endoftext|>
