[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To find the modulo 4 residue of \(121 \cdot 122 \cdot 123\), we need to compute the product \(121 \cdot 122 \cdot 123 \mod 4\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m First, let's find the remainder when each of the numbers \(121\), \(122\), and \(123\) is divided by 4:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 121 \div 4 = 30 \text{ remainder } 1 \quad \Rightarrow \quad 121 \equiv 1 \mod 4
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 122 \div 4 = 30 \text{ remainder } 2 \quad \Rightarrow \quad 122 \equiv 2 \mod 4
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 123 \div 4 = 30 \text{ remainder } 3 \quad \Rightarrow \quad 123 \equiv 3 \mod 4
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Next, we multiply these remainders together modulo 4:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 121 \cdot 122 \cdot 123 \equiv 1 \cdot 2 \cdot 3 \mod 4
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Now, perform the multiplication:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1 \cdot 2 = 2
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2 \cdot 3 = 6
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 6 \mod 4 = 2
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Thus, the modulo 4 residue of \(121 \cdot 122 \cdot 123\) is \(\boxed{2}\).<|endoftext|>
