[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m There is a game in which n people, numbered 1 through n, are arranged in an inverse decreasing order of their opinion on some problem. At each step, one person dies, and the player whose opinion is lowest is declared a winner and paid with coins equal to his/her opinion. Determine the number of coins that need to be paid at the beginning of the game so as to make the expected value of the game zero. In this case, the person who did not die wins nothing and receives no coins.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m If all n people have the same opinion, then, of course, none of them will be given any coins in expectation. Turn the problem around! Determine the number of coins that must be paid at the beginning of the game so as to make the expected value of the game zero.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To determine the number of coins that must be paid at the beginning of the game so as to make the expected value of the game zero, let's break down the problem mathematically.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
