[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To solve the given problem, we first need to analyze the roots $s_1, s_2, \ldots, s_{70}$ of the polynomial \(x^{70} + x^{69} + x^{68} + \cdots + x^2 + x + 1 = 0\). This polynomial is the 70th cyclotomic polynomial, which can be factored as:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[x^{70} + x^{69} + x^{68} + \cdots + x^2 + x + 1 = \prod_{\substack{n = 1 \\ n \nmid 70}}^{70} (x - e^{2\pi i k/n}) \prod_{1 \leq j < k < 70} (x - e^{2\pi i (k-j)/2}).\]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The roots of the polynomial are the 70th roots of unity excluding 1 and -1, so the roots $s_i$ are the vertices of a regular hexagon inscribed in the unit circle in the complex plane.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
