[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[s_1 + s_2 + \cdots + s_{70} = -1.\]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Thus, the expression \(\frac{s_1}{s_2 + s_3 + \cdots + s_{70}} + \frac{s_2}{s_1 + s_3 + \cdots + s_{70}} + \cdots + \frac{s_{39}, s_{40}, \cdots, s_{70}}\) can be written as:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[\frac{s_1}{s_2 + s_3 + \cdots + s_{70}} + \frac{s_2}{s_1 + s_3 + \cdots + s_{70}} + \cdots + \frac{s_{39}}{s_{40} + \cdots + s_{70}} = \left(\frac{s_1}{-1}\right) + \left(\frac{s_2}{-1}\right) + \cdots + \left(\frac{s_{39}}{-1}\right) = -\sum
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
