[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m It appears that the code attempted to access an index that does not exist. This could be due to a misunderstanding of the roots of the polynomial. For a higher-degree polynomial like this one, the real roots are typically isolated and straightforward to find.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Since the polynomial \(x^4 - 80x - 36 = 0\) is quadratic (degree 4) and has no real roots, we can directly use the fact that the sum of the roots (taken one at a time) for a polynomial of even degree with real coefficients is zero. This is because the coefficients are all real.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Let's verify this by manually assuming the non-real roots because we know the polynomial is real and the only possible real roots are ones we can identify straightforwardly. The sum of the real roots must be zero, as the absolute value of the real roots is the same as the absolute value of the complex roots, and their sum is zero.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The sum of the roots (counting multiplicities) of the polynomial \(x^4 - 80x - 36 = 0\) is \(\boxed{0}\).<|endoftext|>
