[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To solve the given problem, we need to use the properties of dot products and cross products. Given that \(\mathbf{a},\) \(\mathbf{b},\) and \(\mathbf{c}\) are unit vectors such that \(\mathbf{a} \cdot \mathbf{b} = \mathbf{a} \cdot \mathbf{c} = 0\) and the angle between \(\mathbf{b}\) and \(\mathbf{c}\) is \(\frac{\pi}{4}\), we can denote \(\mathbf{a} \cdot \mathbf{b} = \mathbf{a} \cdot \mathbf{c} = 0\) and \(\theta = \cos^{-1}\left(\mathbf{b} \cdot \mathbf{c}\right) = \frac{\pi}{4}\). Since \(\mathbf{b}\) and \(\mathbf{c}\) are unit vectors, \(\mathbf{b} \cdot \mathbf{c} = \cos\theta = \frac{1}{\sqrt{2}}\).
