[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m We need to find the possible value of \(k\) such that \(\mathbf{a} = k (\mathbf{b} \times \mathbf{c})\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m First, let's express \(\mathbf{b} \times \mathbf{c}\) in terms of its components:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \mathbf{b} \times \mathbf{c} = \begin{vmatrix} \mathbf{i} & \mathbf{j} & \mathbf{k} \\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\ 0 & 1 & 0 \end{vmatrix} = \mathbf{i} \begin{vmatrix} 0 & 0 \\ 1 & 0 \end{vmatrix} - \mathbf{j} \begin{vmatrix} 1 & 0 \\ 0 & 0 \end{vmatrix} + \mathbf{k} \begin{vmatrix} 1 & 0 \\ 0 & 1 \end{vmatrix} = \mathbf{i} \cdot 0 - \mathbf{j} \cdot 0 + \mathbf{k} \cdot 1 = \mathbf{k} \mathbf{i} + \mathbf{k} \mathbf{j}.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Thus, we have:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \mathbf{a} = k (\mathbf{b} \times \mathbf{c}) = k (\mathbf{k} \mathbf{i} + \mathbf{k} \mathbf{j}) = (k, k, k).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m This means there is no constant \(k\) such that \(\mathbf{a} = k (\mathbf{b} \times \mathbf{c})\) separately. However, if we consider the cross product \((\mathbf{b} \times \mathbf{c})\) in terms of its magnitude, we can find a relationship between \(k\) and \(\mathbf{a}\):
