[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Therefore, the orientation of \(\mathbf{a}\) is such that it can be expressed as \(k (\mathbf{b} \times \mathbf{c})\). The magnitude of \(\mathbf{a}\) is \(k\).
