[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To find the smallest positive angle \(\theta\) such that \(\cos \theta = \sin 60^\circ + \cos 42^\circ - \sin 12^\circ - \cos 6^\circ\), we start by using trigonometric identities. Recall the following double-angle identities:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
