[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Since \(\cos 12^\circ\) and \(\cos 6^\circ\) are not simple values, we will approximate their magnitudes and see if we can find a simplification. However, we can directly use the identity that \(\cos \theta = \sin(90^\circ - \theta)\), so we can test temperatures or angles that might simplify our calculations.
