[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m What is the sum of $\left(\dfrac{1}{3}\right) + \left(\dfrac{1}{3}\right)^2 + \left(\dfrac{1}{3}\right)^3 + \left(\dfrac{1}{3}\right)^4$?
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To find the sum of \(\left(\dfrac{1}{3}\right) + \left(\dfrac{1}{3}\right)^2 + \left(\dfrac{1}{3}\right)^3 + \left(\dfrac{1}{3}\right)^4\), we will calculate each term individually and then sum them up.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. \(\left(\dfrac{1}{3}\right)\)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \left(\dfrac{1}{3}\right) = \dfrac{1}{3}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. \(\left(\dfrac{1}{3}\right)^2\)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \left(\dfrac{1}{3}\right)^2 = \dfrac{1}{3} \times \dfrac{1}{3} = \dfrac{1}{9}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3. \(\left(\dfrac{1}{3}\right)^3\)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \left(\dfrac{1}{3}\right)^3 = \dfrac{1}{3} \times \dfrac{1}{3} \times \dfrac{1}{3} = \dfrac{1}{27}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 4. \(\left(\dfrac{1}{3}\right)^4\)
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \left(\dfrac{1}{3}\right)^4 = \dfrac{1}{3} \times \dfrac{1}{3} \times \dfrac{1}{3} \times \dfrac{1}{3} = \dfrac{1}{81}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Now, we sum these values:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \left(\dfrac{1}{3}\right) + \left(\dfrac{1}{3}\right)^2 + \left(\dfrac{1}{3}\right)^3 + \left(\dfrac{1}{3}\right)^4 = \dfrac{1}{3} + \dfrac{1}{9} + \dfrac{1}{27} + \dfrac{1}{81}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To add these fractions, we need a common denominator. The least common multiple of 3, 9, 27, and 81 is 81. We convert each fraction to have this common denominator:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \dfrac{1}{3} = \dfrac{27}{81}, \quad \dfrac{1}{9} = \dfrac{9}{81}, \quad \dfrac{1}{27} = \dfrac{3}{81}, \quad \dfrac{1}{81} = \dfrac{1}{81}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Adding these fractions together:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \dfrac{27}{81} + \dfrac{9}{81} + \dfrac{3}{81} + \dfrac{1}{81} = \dfrac{27 + 9 + 3 + 1}{81} = \dfrac{40}{81}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Thus, the sum is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \boxed{\dfrac{40}{81}}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
