[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. **Identify the first term and the common difference:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - The first term (\(a\)) is \(2.5\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - The common difference (\(d\)) is \(3.0\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. **Find the general form of the \(n\)-th term of the sequence:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    The \(n\)-th term of an arithmetic sequence is given by:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    a_n = a + (n-1)d
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    Plugging in the values for \(a\) and \(d\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
