[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m A quadrilateral in the plane has vertices $(1, 3)$, $(1, 1)$, $(2, 1)$ and $(2006, 2007)$. How many square units is the area of the quadrilateral?
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To find the area of the quadrilateral with vertices \((1, 3)\), \((1, 1)\), \((2, 1)\), and \((2006, 2007)\), we can use the Shoelace Theorem (also known as Gauss's area formula). The Shoelace Theorem states that for a polygon with vertices \((x_1, y_1), (x_2, y_2), \ldots, (x_n, y_n)\), the area \(A\) is given by:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m A = \frac{1}{2} \left| \sum_{i=1}^{n-1} (x_i y_{i+1} - y_i x_{i+1}) + (x_n y_1 - y_n x_1) \right|
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m For our quadrilateral, the vertices are \((1, 3)\), \((1, 1)\), \((2, 1)\), and \((2006, 2007)\). We can list the coordinates in order and apply the Shoelace Theorem:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m A = \frac{1}{2} \left| 1 \cdot 1 + 1 \cdot 1 + 2 \cdot 2007 + 2006 \cdot 3 - (3 \cdot 1 + 1 \cdot 2 + 1 \cdot 2006 + 2007 \cdot 1) \right|
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Simplifying inside the absolute value:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m A = \frac{1}{2} \left| 1 + 1 + 4014 + 6018 - (3 + 2 + 2006 + 2007) \right|
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m A = \frac{1}{2} \left| 1 + 1 + 4014 + 6018 - (7018 + 2007) \right|
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m A = \frac{1}{2} \left| 1 + 1 + 4014 + 6018 - 9025 \right|
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m A = \frac{1}{2} \left| 10033 - 9025 \right|
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m A = \frac{1}{2} \left| 1008 \right|
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m A = \frac{1}{2} \times 1008 = 504
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Therefore, the area of the quadrilateral is \(\boxed{504}\) square units.<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
