[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. Evaluate \( q(2) \).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. Substitute the result from step 1 into \( p(x) \).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m First, let's evaluate \( q(2) \):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ q(x) = \frac{6}{x} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m So,
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ q(2) = \frac{6}{2} = 3 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Next, we need to evaluate \( p(q(2)) \), which means we first need to find \( p(3) \):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ p(x) = 2 - x^2 \]
