[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m In right triangle $BCD$ with $\angle D = 90^\circ$, we have $BC = 9$ and $BD = 4$.  Find $\sin B$.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To find \(\sin B\) in the right triangle \(BCD\) with \(\angle D = 90^\circ\), we need to determine the length of the side opposite to \(\angle B\), which is denoted as \(CD\). Here are the steps:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. Identify the given information:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - \(\angle D = 90^\circ\), so \(BD\) is the adjacent side to \(\angle B\), and \(BC\) is the opposite side to \(\angle B\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - \(BC = 9\) and \(BD = 4\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. Calculate the length of the adjacent side \(CD\) using the Pythagorean theorem:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    CD = \sqrt{BD^2 - BC^2} = \sqrt{4^2 - 9^2} = \sqrt{16 - 81} = \sqrt{16 - 81} = \sqrt{16 - 81} = \sqrt{16 - 81} = \sqrt{16 - 81}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3. Recognize that \(\sin B\) is the ratio of the length of the opposite side to the length of the adjacent side:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \sin B = \frac{\text{opposite}}{\text{adjacent}} = \frac{BC}{BD} = \frac{9}{4}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Therefore, the value of \(\sin B\) is \(\boxed{\frac{9}{4}}\).<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m [Ground Truth]
