[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Find the modulo 4 residue of $121 \cdot 122 \cdot 123$.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To find the modulo 4 residue of the product \(121 \cdot 122 \cdot 123\), we can use the Chinese Remainder Theorem (CRT). This theorem states that if \(p_1, p_2, \ldots, p_k\) are distinct primes that do not share any factors, then the product \(x = p_1 x_1 p_2 x_2 \cdots p_k x_k\) satisfies the congruence:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ x \equiv x_1 \pmod{p_1} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ x \equiv x_2 \pmod{p_2} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ \vdots \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ x \equiv x_k \pmod{p_k} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m where \(x_1, x_2, \ldots, x_k\) are the remainders when \(x\) is divided by \(p_1, p_2, \ldots, p_k\) respectively.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m In this case, the primes are 2, 11, and 41. We need to find \(121 \cdot 122 \cdot 123 \mod 4\). First, we find the product of the remainders when each number is divided by 4:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ 121 \equiv 1 \pmod{4} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ 122 \equiv 2 \pmod{4} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ 123 \equiv 3 \pmod{4} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m So, we need to find:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ 1 \cdot 2 \cdot 3 \pmod{4} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m First, calculate \(1 \cdot 2 \cdot 3\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ 1 \cdot 2 = 2 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ 2 \cdot 3 = 6 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Finally, find the remainder when 6 is divided by 4:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ 6 \div 4 = 1 \text{ remainder } 2 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m So,
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ 6 \equiv 2 \pmod{4} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Therefore,
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ 1 \cdot 2 \cdot 3 \equiv 2 \pmod{4} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m This means:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ 121 \cdot 122 \cdot 123 \equiv 2 \pmod{4} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Next, we need to find \(121 \cdot 122 \cdot 123 \mod 11\). Let's use the expression \(121 \equiv 1 \pmod{11}\), \(122 \equiv 2 \pmod{11}\), and \(123 \equiv 0 \pmod{11}\) (since \(123 - 120 = 3\) and \(3 \div 11 = 0\) remainder 3 when divided by 11). So,
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ 121 \cdot 122 \cdot 123 \equiv 1 \cdot 2 \cdot 0 \pmod{11} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Finally, find the remainder when 0 is divided by 11:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ 0 \div 11 = 0 \text{ remainder } 0 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m So,
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ 121 \cdot 122 \cdot 123 \equiv 0 \pmod{11} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m This means:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ 121 \cdot 122 \cdot 123 \equiv 0 \pmod{11} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Since \(121 \cdot 122 \cdot 123 \equiv 0 \pmod{11}\), we need to find the remainder when \(1 + 2 + 3 = 6\) is divided by 11:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ 6 \equiv 6 \pmod{11} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m So,
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ 121 \cdot 122 \cdot 123 \equiv 6 \pmod{11} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m This means:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ 121 \cdot 122 \cdot 123 \equiv 6 \pmod{11} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Finally, we reduce 6 modulo 4:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ 6 \div 4 = 1 \text{ remainder } 2 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m So,
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ 6 \equiv 2 \pmod{4} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Therefore,
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ 121 \cdot 122 \cdot 123 \equiv 2 \pmod{4} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Putting it all together, the final answer is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \boxed{2}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
