[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The volume of the parallelepiped generated by $\begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ 3 \\ 4 \end{pmatrix},$ $\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ k \\ 2 \end{pmatrix},$ and $\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ 2 \\ k \end{pmatrix}$ is 15.  Find $k,$ where $k > 0.$
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To find the value of \( k \) such that the volume of the parallelepiped generated by the vectors \(\begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ 3 \\ 4 \end{pmatrix}, \begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ k \\ 2 \end{pmatrix}, \begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ 2 \\ k \end{pmatrix}\) is 15, we need to calculate the absolute value of the volume determinant of the matrix formed by these vectors.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The volume of the parallelepiped is given by the absolute value of the determinant of the matrix formed by these vectors. The matrix is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \begin{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2 & 1 & 1 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3 & k & 2 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 4 & 2 & k
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The volume determinant is calculated as follows:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \text{Volume} = \left| \begin{vmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2 & 1 & 1 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3 & k & 2 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 4 & 2 & k
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \end{vmatrix} \right|
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m We can expand this determinant along the first row:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \text{Volume} = 2 \left| \begin{vmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m k & 2 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2 & k
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \end{vmatrix} \right| - 1 \left| \begin{vmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3 & 2 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 4 & k
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \end{vmatrix} \right| + 1 \left| \begin{vmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3 & k \\
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 4 & 2
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \end{vmatrix} \right|
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Now, we calculate each of the 2x2 determinants:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \left| \begin{vmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m k & 2 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2 & k
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \end{vmatrix} \right| = k \cdot k - 2 \cdot 2 = k^2 - 4
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \left| \begin{vmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3 & 2 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 4 & k
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \end{vmatrix} \right| = 3 \cdot k - 2 \cdot 4 = 3k - 8
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \left| \begin{vmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3 & k \\
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 4 & 2
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \end{vmatrix} \right| = 3 \cdot 2 - k \cdot 4 = 6 - 4k
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Substituting these back into the volume determinant expression, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \text{Volume} = 2(k^2 - 4) - (3k - 8) + (6 - 4k) = 2k^2 - 8 - 3k + 8 + 6 - 4k = 2k^2 - 7k + 6
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m We know that the volume is 15, so we set up the equation:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2k^2 - 7k + 6 = 15
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Simplifying this equation, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2k^2 - 7k - 9 = 0
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m We solve this quadratic equation using the quadratic formula \(k = \frac{-b \pm \sqrt{b^2 - 4ac}}{2a}\), where \(a = 2\), \(b = -7\), and \(c = -9\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m k = \frac{-(-7) \pm \sqrt{(-7)^2 - 4 \cdot 2 \cdot (-9)}}{2 \cdot 2} = \frac{7 \pm \sqrt{49 + 72}}{4} = \frac{7 \pm \sqrt{121}}{4} = \frac{7 \pm 11}{4}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m This gives us two solutions:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m k = \frac{7 + 11}{4} = \frac{18}{4} = \frac{9}{2} \quad \text{and} \quad k = \frac{7 - 11}{4} = \frac{-4}{4} = -1
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Since \(k > 0\), we have \(k = \frac{9}{2}\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Thus, the value of \(k\) is \(\boxed{\frac{9}{2}}\).<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
