[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To calculate the product \(\frac{1}{4} \cdot \frac{2}{5} \cdot \frac{3}{6} \cdot \frac{4}{7} \cdots \frac{49}{52} \cdot \frac{50}{53}\), we start by identifying the general form of the terms in the product. The \(n\)-th term of the product is \(\frac{n+3}{n+4}\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m So, the product can be written as:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \frac{1}{4} \cdot \frac{2}{5} \cdot \frac{3}{6} \cdot \frac{4}{7} \cdots \frac{49}{52} \cdot \frac{50}{53}
