[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1 \cdot 3 \cdot 5 \cdot 7 \cdot \cdots \cdot 50
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m In the denominator, we can see that the \(52!\) terms cancel out, leaving us with:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 4 \cdot 6 \cdot 8 \cdot 10 \cdots 53
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Notice that all the odd numbers from 1 to 49 in the denominator will cancel out with all the even numbers from 4 to 52 in the numerator. So, we are left with:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1 \cdot 50 = 50
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Therefore, the product is:
