[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To determine the probability that the product of the results of the two spins will be an even number, we first need to understand when the product of two numbers is even. The product of two numbers is even if at least one of the numbers is even.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m ### Step 1: Identify the possible outcomes for each spinner
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Each spinner is divided into three sections (numbers 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, and 7) out of a total of 7 possible outcomes.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m ### Step 2: Calculate the probability of each outcome
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The probability that the product of the results of the two spins is even depends on the individual probabilities of the outcomes for each spinner:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - The spinner with the numbers 2, 4, 6, and 8 has an odd probability of 2/3.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - The spinner with the numbers 3, 5, and 7 has an even probability of 3/3 = 1 (since it will always result in an even number).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m ### Step 3: Determine the total number of favorable outcomes
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To have an even product, the two spins must both result in even numbers. Therefore, we need to calculate the number of outcomes where both spins produce even numbers.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - The spinner with the numbers 2, 4, 6, and 8 has 4 even numbers out of 7 possible outcomes.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m - The spinner with the numbers 3, 5, and 7 has 3 even numbers out of 7 possible outcomes.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The total number of favorable outcomes is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[4 \times 3 = 12\]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m ### Step 4: Calculate the probability
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The probability that the product of the results of the two spins is even is the number of favorable outcomes divided by the total number of possible outcomes:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \frac{12}{7 \times 7} = \frac{12}{49}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Thus, the probability that the product of the results of the two spins will be an even number is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \boxed{\frac{12}{49}}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m [Ground Truth]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \frac{2}{3}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
