[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To determine the real numbers \(x\) that are not in the domain of the function \(f(x) = \frac{1}{1 + \frac{1}{1 + \frac{1}{x}}}\), we need to ensure that the denominator \(1 + \frac{1}{x}\) is undefined. The function is undefined when the denominator is zero. Therefore, we need to find the values of \(x\) that make \(1 + \frac{1}{x} = 0\).
