[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To determine the change in the area of the square after its length and width are altered, we need to calculate the original area, the new area, and then find the difference between the new area and the original area.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. **Calculate the original area:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - The original length is \( \text{length}_{\text{original}} = 3491 \) units.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - The original width is \( \text{width}_{\text{original}} = 3491 \) units.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - The original area \( A_{\text{original}} \) is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      A_{\text{original}} = \text{length}_{\text{original}} \times \text{width}_{\text{original}} = 3491 \times 3491 = 12183081
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 2. **Calculate the new area:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - The new length is \( \text{length}_{\text{new}} = 3491 - 60 = 3421 \) units.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - The new width is \( \text{width}_{\text{new}} = 3491 + 60 = 3551 \) units.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - The new area \( A_{\text{new}} \) is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      A_{\text{new}} = \text{length}_{\text{new}} \times \text{width}_{\text{new}} = 3421 \times 3551
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - To find \( 3421 \times 3551 \), we can use the distributive property:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      3421 \times 3551 = 3421 \times (3500 + 50) = 3421 \times 3500 + 3421 \times 50 = 11933500 + 171050 = 12004550
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - Therefore, the new area is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      A_{\text{new}} = 12004550
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 3. **Calculate the change in area:**
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    - The change in area is:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      \text{Change in area} = A_{\text{new}} - A_{\text{original}} = 12004550 - 12183081 = -178431
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m      \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Thus, the area changes by \(\boxed{-178431}\).<|endoftext|>
