[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To find the units digit of the sum \(3^1 + 3^3 + 3^5 + 3^7 + \ldots + 3^{2009}\), we can use properties of modular arithmetic to simplify the calculation.
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m First, observe that:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ 3^1 = 3 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ 3^3 = 27 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ 3^5 = 243 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ 3^7 = 2187 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[ \vdots \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m We can see that each term in the series can be written as \(3^{2k+1}\) for \(k = 0, 1, 2, \ldots, 998\). The units digit of \(3^n\) depends on the value of \(n \mod 4\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 1. For \(n \equiv 1 \pmod{4}\):
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m    \[ 3^{2k+1} = 3 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
