[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m To find the value of \( y \) given that \(\text{proj}_{\mathbf{w}} \mathbf{v} = \begin{pmatrix} -6 \\ -2 \end{pmatrix}\), we need to calculate the projection of the vector \(\mathbf{v}\) onto the vector \(\mathbf{w}\).
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m The projection of \(\mathbf{v}\) onto \(\mathbf{w}\) is given by the formula:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \text{proj}_{\mathbf{w}} \mathbf{v} = \frac{\mathbf{v} \cdot \mathbf{w}}{\mathbf{w} \cdot \mathbf{w}} \mathbf{w}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m We are given that \(\text{proj}_{\mathbf{w}} \mathbf{v} = \begin{pmatrix} -6 \\ -2 \end{pmatrix}\). This means:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \frac{\mathbf{v} \cdot \mathbf{w}}{\mathbf{w} \cdot \mathbf{w}} \mathbf{w} = \begin{pmatrix} -6 \\ -2 \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m Let \(\mathbf{w} = \begin{pmatrix} 9 \\ 3 \end{pmatrix}\) and \(\mathbf{v} = \begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ y \end{pmatrix}\). The dot products \(\mathbf{v} \cdot \mathbf{w}\) and \(\mathbf{w} \cdot \mathbf{w}\) are calculated as follows:
[36m(main_task pid=1419827)[0m \[
